msgid "whish."
msgstr "frufrú"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "less than nothing"
msgstr "menos que nada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "less than nothing"
msgid "There is nothing here.  Not even time or space."
msgstr "No hay nada aquí. Ni siquiera espacio o tiempo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "impaled officer"
msgstr "oficial empalado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "impaled officer"
msgid ""
"A dead body encased in high-tech armor hanging in the air.  Their form seems "
"twisted and refracted in the light of the strange glowing crystal that has "
"seeped out of the ground and impaled their body."
msgstr ""
"El cuerpo muerto enfundado en una armadura de alta tecnología en el aire. Su "
"forma parece estar torcida y refractada en la luz de un extraño cristal "
"brillante que ha salido del suelo y empalado su cuerpo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "an absence of sound."
msgstr "una ausencia de sonido."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "impaled mercenary"
msgstr "mercenario empalado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "impaled mercenary"
msgid ""
"A dead body encased in military armor hanging in the air.  Their form seems "
"twisted and refracted in the light of the strange glowing crystal that has "
"seeped out of the ground and impaled their body."
msgstr ""
"El cuerpo muerto enfundado en una armadura militar en el aire. Su forma "
"parece estar torcida y refractada en la luz de un extraño cristal brillante "
"que ha salido del suelo y a empalado su cuerpo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "empty spike"
msgstr "pica vacía"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "empty spike"
msgid ""
"A strange otherworldly spike that refracts light in strange ways.  The body "
"no longer rests on it."
msgstr ""
"Un extraño pico de otro mundo que refracta la luz de formas extrañas. El "
"cuerpo ya no descansa sobre él."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-alien.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_MISSING_BODY" in furniture "empty
#. spike"'s examine action
msgid "The body is gone but it can't have gone far, you need to destroy it."
msgstr "El cuerpo ya no esta pero no puede haber ido muy lejos, necesitas destruirlo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cooling unit"
msgstr "unidad de refrigeración"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cooling unit"
msgid ""
"A large, blocky appliance encased in sheet metal.  This commonplace fixture "
"is used for cooling large indoor areas."
msgstr ""
"Un aparato grande, en forma de bloque, revestido de chapa. Este aparato tan "
"habitual se utiliza para refrigerar grandes superficies interiores."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "central air filter"
msgstr "filtro de aire central"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "central air filter"
msgid ""
"A large synthetic membrane used to filter out dust, smoke, mites, and other "
"contaminants from air that passes through it."
msgstr ""
"Una gran membrana sintética utilizada para filtrar el polvo, el humo, los "
"ácaros y otros contaminantes del aire que la atraviesa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dishwasher"
msgid ""
"A large, boxy machine that uses hot water and soap to efficiently clean "
"batches of dishes.  Now that it's sat powerless for a while, a putrid scent "
"of rot is leaking from inside."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina grande y cuadrada que utiliza agua caliente y jabón para limpiar "
"eficientemente grandes cantidades de platos. Ahora que lleva un tiempo sin "
"funcionar, de su interior se desprende un pútrido olor a podrido."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dryer"
msgstr "secadora"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dryer"
msgid ""
"A common household appliance used to quickly dry large batches of clothing "
"after they have been washed."
msgstr ""
"Un electrodoméstico común utilizado para secar rápidamente grandes cantidades "
"de ropa después de haberla lavado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "furnace"
msgstr "horno industrial"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "furnace"
msgid ""
"A gas-powered forced-air central heating unit, with an internal fan to push "
"the air through a building's ventilation system to keep it warm."
msgstr ""
"Una unidad de calefacción central de aire forzado a gas, con un ventilador "
"interno para empujar el aire a través del sistema de ventilación de un "
"edificio para mantenerlo caliente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#: data/json/items/vehicle/utilities.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "washing machine"
msgid_plural "washing machines"
msgstr[0] "lavadora"
msgstr[1] "lavadoras"
msgstr[2] "lavadoras"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "washing machine"
msgid ""
"An appliance used to clean laundry.  It needs to be plugged into a grid that "
"provides it with electricity and large amounts of water to be used."
msgstr ""
"Un aparato utilizado para lavar la ropa. Necesita enchufarse a una red que le "
"proporcione electricidad y grandes cantidades de agua para su uso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "oven"
msgid ""
"A standard electric convection-based oven, commonly used for heating and "
"cooking food.  It can safely contain a fire, although it's not adequately "
"ventilated.  You could disconnect it and plug it into a working power grid, "
"or power it with a UPS."
msgstr ""
"Un horno eléctrico estándar basado en la convección, utilizado habitualmente "
"para calentar y cocinar alimentos. Puede contener un fuego con seguridad, "
"aunque no está adecuadamente ventilado. Podrías desconectarlo y enchufarlo a "
"una red eléctrica que funcione, o alimentarlo con un SEU."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "gas oven"
msgstr "horno de gas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "gas oven"
msgid ""
"A standard gas-powered oven, commonly used for heating and cooking food.  "
"With the state of nearby gas lines unknown, it's best not to put any fire "
"near it."
msgstr ""
"Un horno de gas estándar, utilizado habitualmente para calentar y cocinar "
"alimentos. Dado que se desconoce el estado de las tuberías de gas cercanas, "
"es mejor no encender fuego cerca de él."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "gas oven and microwave combo"
msgstr "combo de horno de gas y microondas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "gas oven and microwave combo"
msgid ""
"A standard gas-powered oven, commonly used for heating and cooking food.  "
"This one has an attached microwave.  With the state of nearby gas lines "
"unknown, it's best not to put any fire near it.  You could disassemble the "
"shelving holding them together and pull the microwave out."
msgstr ""
"Un horno de gas estándar, utilizado habitualmente para calentar y cocinar "
"alimentos. Éste tiene un microondas adjunto. Dado que se desconoce el estado "
"de las tuberías de gas cercanas, es mejor no encender fuego cerca de él. "
"Podrías desmontar la estantería que los sujeta y sacar el microondas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "blacksmith bellows"
msgstr "fuelles de herrero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "blacksmith bellows"
msgid ""
"An old device for pushing air into a blacksmith's forge to strengthen the "
"fire and maintain a high temperature.  Useless in its current state, but good "
"for parts."
msgstr ""
"Antiguo dispositivo para introducir aire en la fragua del herrero para "
"reforzar el fuego y mantener una temperatura elevada. Inútil en su estado "
"actual, pero bueno para partes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "blacksmith drop hammer"
msgstr "martillo pilón de herrero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "blacksmith drop hammer"
msgid ""
"An anvil with a large metal hammer suspended above it in a metal framework.  "
"It would be useful for shaping softened metal plates, or you could use the "
"anvil by itself."
msgstr ""
"Un yunque con un gran martillo de metal suspendido sobre él en un armazón "
"metálico. Sería útil para dar forma a placas de metal reblandecido, o podrías "
"utilizar el yunque por sí solo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "document shredder"
msgstr "trituradora de documentos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "document shredder"
msgid ""
"A simple electronic device mounted to a large basket.  It is designed to "
"efficiently destroy paper documents with sensitive information.  Good for "
"parts, as identity theft and corporate espionage probably aren't big concerns "
"anymore."
msgstr ""
"Un sencillo dispositivo electrónico montado en una gran papelera. Está "
"diseñado para destruir eficazmente los documentos en papel con información "
"sensible. Es bueno para las partes, ya que el robo de identidad y el "
"espionaje corporativo probablemente ya no son grandes preocupaciones."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "server stack"
msgstr "pila de servidores"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "server stack"
msgid ""
"A large rack of specialized computers for storing and transmitting "
"information.  Powerless and largely useless for its intended purpose, the "
"laptops mounted inside can still be used if removed."
msgstr ""
"Un gran bastidor de ordenadores especializados para almacenar y transmitir "
"información. Sin energía y en gran medida inútil para su propósito, los "
"ordenadores portátiles montados en su interior pueden seguir utilizándose si "
"se extraen."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "supercomputer"
msgstr "superordenador"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "supercomputer"
msgid ""
"Hanging platters assembled into an inverted cone, their positions kept stable "
"by dense threading of copper cabling."
msgstr ""
"Discos colgantes ensamblados en un cono invertido, con sus posiciones  "
"estables gracias a un cableado de cobre denso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "large satellite dish"
msgstr "gran antena parabólica"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "large satellite dish"
msgid ""
"A large, concave metal panel with simple electronics used to receive signals "
"from satellites.  While the hundreds of expensive machines orbiting the "
"planet will likely continue to function indefinitely, their various purposes "
"have all been lost."
msgstr ""
"Un gran panel metálico cóncavo con una electrónica sencilla que sirve para "
"recibir señales de los satélites. Aunque es probable que los cientos de "
"costosas máquinas que orbitan el planeta sigan funcionando indefinidamente, "
"sus diversos propósitos se han perdido."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mounted polycrystalline solar panel"
msgstr "panel solar policristalino montado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mounted polycrystalline solar panel"
msgid ""
"A set of photovoltaic power generators, which turns solar radiation into "
"useable electricity.  While useful before the Cataclysm, they have become "
"priceless tools, invaluable to any survivor.  This one uses less efficient "
"polycrystalline solar panels."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de generadores de energía fotovoltaica, que convierte la "
"radiación solar en electricidad utilizable. Aunque eran útiles antes del "
"Cataclismo, se han convertido en herramientas inestimables, de valor "
"incalculable para cualquier superviviente. Este utiliza paneles solares "
"policristalinos menos eficientes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mounted monocrystalline solar panel"
msgstr "panel solar monocristalino montado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mounted monocrystalline solar panel"
msgid ""
"A set of photovoltaic power generators, which turns solar radiation into "
"useable electricity.  While useful before the Cataclysm, they have become "
"priceless tools, invaluable to any survivor.  This one uses more efficient "
"monocrystalline solar panels."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de generadores de energía fotovoltaica, que convierte la "
"radiación solar en electricidad utilizable. Aunque eran útiles antes del "
"Cataclismo, se han convertido en herramientas inestimables, de valor "
"incalculable para cualquier superviviente. Este utiliza paneles solares "
"monocristalinos más eficientes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "oxygen concentrator"
msgid ""
"A machine capable of generating pure oxygen from the air.  It needs power to "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Una maquina capaz de generar oxigeno puro del aire. Necesita electricidad "
"para funcionar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-appliances.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "high pressure compressor unit"
msgid ""
"A machine designed to compress an input gas to a very high pressure.  It "
"needs large amounts of power to function."
msgstr ""
"Una maquina diseñada para comprimir un gas de entrada a una alta presión. "
"Necesita grandes cantidades de energía para funcionar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "road barricade"
msgstr "barricada de camino"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "road barricade"
msgid ""
"A large wooden blockade used to block passage through a road.  It is lined "
"with reflective tape to increase visibility.  Despite the name, it does "
"little to stop a moving car."
msgstr ""
"Es un gran obstáculo de madera que se usa para bloquear el tránsito de una "
"calle. Está bordeado con cinta adhesiva reflectante para incrementar su "
"visibilidad. A pesar de su nombre, no logra mucho para detener a un vehículo "
"en movimiento."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "gravelbag barricade"
msgstr "barricada de sacos de grava"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "gravelbag barricade"
msgid ""
"A low wall made of stacked gravelbags, uncommonly used to catch bullets and "
"block flooding."
msgstr ""
"Un muro bajo hecho de sacos de grava apilados, no comunmente utilizado para "
"atrapar balas y bloquear inundaciones."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "rrrip!"
msgstr "¡rrrip!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "gravelbag wall"
msgstr "muro de sacos de grava"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "gravelbag wall"
msgid "A wall of stacked gravelbags, a bit taller than an average adult."
msgstr "Un muro de sacos de grava apilados, un poco más alto que un adulto medio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "earthbag barricade"
msgstr "Barricada de sacos de tierra"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "earthbag barricade"
msgid ""
"A low wall made of stacked earthbags, commonly used to catch bullets and "
"block flooding."
msgstr ""
"Un muro bajo hecho de sacos de tierra apilados, comúnmente utilizado para "
"atrapar balas y bloquear inundaciones."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "earthbag wall"
msgstr "muro de bolsas de tierra"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "earthbag wall"
msgid "A wall of stacked earthbags, a bit taller than an average adult."
msgstr "Un muro de sacos de tierra apilados, un poco más alto que un adulto medio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "lane guard"
msgstr "guardarraíl"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "lane guard"
msgid "A simple wooden post to mark the separation between street lanes."
msgstr "Un muro de sacos de tierra apilados, un poco más alto que un adulto medio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sandbag barricade"
msgstr "barricada de bolsas de arena"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sandbag barricade"
msgid ""
"A low wall made of canvas sacks filled with sand, commonly used to catch "
"bullets and prevent flooding."
msgstr ""
"Muro bajo hecho con sacos de lona rellenos de arena, comúnmente utilizado "
"para atrapar balas y evitar inundaciones."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sandbag wall"
msgstr "muro de bolsas de arena"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sandbag wall"
msgid "A wall of stacked sandbags, a bit taller than an average adult."
msgstr "Un muro de sacos de arena apilados, un poco más alto que un adulto medio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "show jump"
msgstr "obstáculo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "show jump"
msgid ""
"A show jump made of a long pole, suitable for showing off your equestrian "
"skills."
msgstr ""
"Un salto de exhibición hecho con una poste largo, adecuado para mostrar tus "
"habilidades ecuestres."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-barriers.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "show jump"
msgid "The end of a show jump made of planks."
msgstr "La parte final de un obstáculo hecho con tablas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-beach.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "scattered seaweed"
msgstr "algas marinas dispersas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-beach.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "scattered seaweed"
msgid "Seaweed and other detritus, scattered along the high water line of the beach."
msgstr ""
"Algas y otros detritus, esparcidos a lo largo de la línea de pleamar de la "
"playa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-beach.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "driftwood log"
msgstr "leño de madera traido por la marea"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-beach.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "driftwood log"
msgid "A small log, bleached white by sun and salt."
msgstr "Un pequeño leño, blanqueado por el sol y la sal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-beach.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken boat"
msgstr "restos de barco roto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-beach.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken boat"
msgid ""
"A section of old, sun-bleached boat, half-buried in the ground.  There's no "
"restoring it, but parts could be salvaged."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de un viejo barco, decolorado por el sol, semienterrado en el "
"suelo. No se puede restaurar, pero se podría rescatar alguna parte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/decorative.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "standing mirror"
msgid_plural "standing mirrors"
msgstr[0] "espejo de pie"
msgstr[1] "espejos de pie"
msgstr[2] "espejos de pie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "standing mirror"
msgid ""
"A full-length mirror mounted in a sleek aluminum frame.  You can easily see "
"all of the dirt and blood on your clothes, and the weariness in your eyes."
msgstr ""
"Un espejo de cuerpo entero montado en un elegante marco de aluminio. Puedes "
"ver fácilmente toda la suciedad y la sangre en tu ropa, y el agotamiento en "
"tus ojos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken standing mirror"
msgstr "espejo de pie roto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken standing mirror"
msgid ""
"An aluminum frame for a full-length mirror, with most of the mirror missing.  "
"What remains in the frame are large, dangerous-looking shards of fractured "
"glass."
msgstr ""
"Un marco de aluminio para un espejo de cuerpo entero, al que le falta la "
"mayor parte del espejo. Lo que queda en el marco son grandes fragmentos de "
"cristal fracturado de aspecto peligroso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bitts"
msgstr "bolardo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bitts"
msgid ""
"A pair of vertical iron posts mounted on a wharf, pier, or other form of "
"dock.  They are used to secure mooring lines, ropes, and similar."
msgstr ""
"Un par de postes verticales de hierro montados en un muelle, embarcadero u "
"otra forma de muelle. Se utilizan para asegurar cabos de amarre, cuerdas y "
"similares."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cleat"
msgstr "cala"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cleat"
msgid ""
"A small horn cleat with two \"horns\" extending parallel to the deck or the "
"axis of the spar, and resembling a small anvil.  They are used to secure "
"mooring lines, ropes, and similar."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña cornamusa con dos \"cuernos\" que se extienden paralelos a la "
"cubierta o al eje del larguero y se asemejan a un pequeño yunque. Se utilizan "
"para sujetar cabos de amarre, sogas y similares."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "manacles"
msgstr "esposas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "manacles"
msgid "A pair of metal shackles with heavy chains mounted to a wall or floor."
msgstr ""
"Un par de grilletes metálicos con pesadas cadenas montados en un muro/pared o "
"en el suelo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "crack."
msgstr "crack."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "statue"
msgstr "estatua"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "statue"
msgid ""
"A massive block of stone that has been carefully carved into a work of "
"timeless art."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme bloque de piedra que ha sido cuidadosamente tallado en una obra de "
"arte intemporal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-decorative.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
