" If examined closely, you can read what's on the screen and perform any "
"allowed functions.  It might even be possible to hack it, given the skills."
msgstr ""
"Un terminal informático normal, cuya pantalla brilla con una tenue luz "
"artificial. Si se examina de cerca, se puede leer lo que aparece en la "
"pantalla y realizar cualquier operación permitida. Incluso es posible "
"piratearlo, si se poseen los conocimientos necesarios."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/expansion/recipe_modular_workshop/version_2/recipe_modular_workshop_common.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmw_2_common_1"
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "fbmw_2_common_smithy_2"
msgid "forge"
msgstr "forja"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "forge"
msgid "A metalworking station typically used in combination with an anvil."
msgstr ""
"Una estación para trabajar los metales, comúnmente utilizada en combinación "
"con un yunque."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Cody's forge"
msgstr "Forja de Cody"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Cody's forge"
msgid ""
"A metalworking station typically used in combination with an anvil.  You can "
"see pipes running into the walls."
msgstr ""
"Una estación de trabajo del metal que suele utilizarse en combinación con un "
"yunque. Se pueden ver tuberías que atraviesan las paredes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "anvil"
msgid ""
"A heavy block of oddly-shaped metal with a pritchel hole and hardy hole.  "
"It's used for metalworking."
msgstr ""
"Un bloque pesado de metal de forma extraña con un orificio de pritchel y otro "
"de hardy. Se utiliza para trabajar el metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze anvil"
msgid_plural "bronze anvils"
msgstr[0] "yunque de bronce"
msgstr[1] "yunques de bronce"
msgstr[2] "yunques de bronce"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bronze anvil"
msgid ""
"A heavy block of oddly-shaped bronze with a pritchel hole and hardy hole.  "
"It's used for metalworking."
msgstr ""
"Un bloque pesado de bronce de forma extraña con un agujero pritchel y un "
"agujero hardy. Se utiliza para trabajar el metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "heavy anvil"
msgid_plural "heavy anvils"
msgstr[0] "yunque pesado"
msgstr[1] "yunques pesados"
msgstr[2] "yunques pesados"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy anvil"
msgid ""
"An enormously heavy block of oddly-shaped metal with all the accoutrements a "
"blacksmith could ask for.  It's used for heavy-duty metalworking."
msgstr ""
"Un pesado bloque de metal de forma extraña con todos los accesorios que un "
"herrero podría pedir. Se utiliza para trabajos pesados en metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/metalworking.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "small anvil"
msgid_plural "small anvils"
msgstr[0] "yunque pequeño"
msgstr[1] "yunques pequeños"
msgstr[2] "yunques pequeños"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "small anvil"
msgid "A small, handcrafted anvil."
msgstr "Un yunque pequeño hecho a mano."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "makeshift anvil"
msgstr "yunque improvisado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "makeshift anvil"
msgid ""
"A steel ingot mounted into a heavy log to make a suitable anvil.  Smaller "
"steel pieces serve as shaping surfaces."
msgstr ""
"Un lingote de acero montado en un leño pesado para hacer un yunque adecuado. "
"Las piezas de acero más pequeñas sirven como superficies de moldeado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "scavenged anvil"
msgstr "yunque recuperado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "scavenged anvil"
msgid ""
"An old machinery part, cut and smoothed to make a serviceable anvil, and "
"mounted to a heavy log stand."
msgstr ""
"Una vieja pieza de maquinaria, cortada y alisada para convertirla en un "
"yunque útil, y montada en un pesado soporte de leños."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "still"
msgid_plural "stills"
msgstr[0] "destilador"
msgstr[1] "destiladores"
msgstr[2] "destiladores"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "still"
msgid ""
"An essential component for brewing and chemistry that allows for refining "
"liquid mixtures."
msgstr ""
"Es un componente esencial para la destilación y procesos químicos. Permite "
"refinar mezclas de líquidos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "screw press"
msgid_plural "screw presses"
msgstr[0] "prensa de tornillo"
msgstr[1] "prensas de tornillo"
msgstr[2] "prensas de tornillo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "screw press"
msgid ""
"A large screw press for manually pressing oil out of fruit or seed paste.  "
"The paste is placed in wetted bags and pressed down by the force of the screw "
"mechanism."
msgstr ""
"Una gran prensa con el propósito de extraer aceite manualmente de pasta de "
"fruta o semillas. La pasta se pone en bolsas mojadas y se presiona con la "
"fuerza del mecanismo de tornillo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "charcoal kiln"
msgstr "horno de carbón vegetal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled charcoal kiln"
msgid ""
"A primitive rock kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into "
"charcoal in the absence of oxygen.  It isn't especially efficient compared to "
"a modern metal variant."
msgstr ""
"Un primitivo horno de piedra diseñado para quemar madera y materia orgánica y "
"convertirla en carbón vegetal en ausencia de oxígeno. No es especialmente "
"eficiente comparado con una variante metálica moderna."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled charcoal kiln"
msgstr "horno de carbón vegetal lleno"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "horno de carbón de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled metal charcoal kiln"
msgid ""
"A metal kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into charcoal in the "
"absence of oxygen.  Much more efficient than its archaic rock counterpart."
msgstr ""
"Una horno de carbón de metal diseñado para convertir la madera y la materia "
"orgánica en carbón en ausencia de oxígeno. Mucho mas eficiente que su arcaica "
"contraparte de rocas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "horno de carbón de metal lleno"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "arc furnace"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled arc furnace"
msgid ""
"An arc furnace designed to burn a powdery mix of coke and limestone to create "
"calcium carbide."
msgstr ""
"Un horno de arco diseñado para quemar una mezcla polvorienta de coque y "
"piedra caliza para crear carburo de calcio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled arc furnace"
msgstr "horno de arco lleno"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "smoking rack"
msgstr "ahumador"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "smoking rack"
msgid ""
"A wooden rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  "
"Works as a charcoal smoker in crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Un estante de madera diseñado para ahumar los alimentos y mejorar su "
"conservación y sabor. Funciona como ahumador de carbón en recetas artesanales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "spinning wheel"
msgid_plural "spinning wheels"
msgstr[0] "máquina de hilar"
msgstr[1] "máquinas de hilar"
msgstr[2] "máquinas de hilar"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "spinning wheel"
msgid ""
"A large wooden device with a mechanical wheel used to combine fibers together "
"into a stronger material."
msgstr ""
"Un gran dispositivo de madera con una rueda mecánica que se utiliza para "
"combinar fibras y obtener un material más resistente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stationary scutcher"
msgid_plural "stationary scutchers"
msgstr[0] "mostradores estacionarios"
msgstr[1] "mostradores estacionarios"
msgstr[2] "vendedores estacionarios"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "stationary scutcher"
msgid ""
"A bulky, simple-hinged wooden device to break up the hard parts of fiber "
"plants, with nail combs on the back for separating them out."
msgstr ""
"Un aparato voluminoso de madera con bisagras simples para romper las partes "
"duras de las plantas de fibra, con peines de clavos en la parte posterior "
"para separarlas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active smoking rack"
msgstr "ahumador activo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active smoking rack"
msgid ""
"A wooden rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  It "
"is lit and smoking."
msgstr ""
"Una rejilla de madera diseñada para ahumar alimentos y mejorar su "
"conservación y sabor. Esta encendida y ahumando."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal smoking rack"
msgid_plural "metal smoking racks"
msgstr[0] "ahumador de metal"
msgstr[1] "ahumadores de metal"
msgstr[2] "ahumadores de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal smoking rack"
msgid ""
"A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  Works "
"as a charcoal smoker in crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Una rejilla metálica diseñada para ahumar alimentos y mejorar su conservación "
"y sabor. Funciona como ahumador de carbón en recetas de fabricación."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active metal smoking rack"
msgstr "ahumador de metal activo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active metal smoking rack"
msgid "A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste."
msgstr ""
"Una rejilla metálica diseñada para ahumar los alimentos y mejorar su "
"conservación y sabor."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "rock forge"
msgstr "forja de piedra"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "rock forge"
msgid ""
"A metalworking station made of rock, typically used in combination with an "
"anvil.  Works as a charcoal forge in crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Una estación de trabajo del metal hecha de roca, que suele utilizarse en "
"combinación con un yunque. Funciona como forja de carbón en las recetas de "
"fabricación."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "clay kiln"
msgstr "horno de arcilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "clay kiln"
msgid "A kiln designed to bake clay pottery and bricks."
msgstr "Un horno fabricado para cocer ladrillos y hacer alfarería."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden stepladder"
msgid_plural "wooden stepladders"
msgstr[0] "escalera de madera"
msgstr[1] "escaleras de madera"
msgstr[2] "escaleras de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden stepladder"
msgid ""
"A short, foldable wooden ladder.  Can help you climb to a rooftop, or maybe "
"slow something down."
msgstr ""
"Una escalera de madera corta y plegable. Puede ayudarte a subir a un tejado o "
"a frenar algo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "aluminum stepladder"
msgid_plural "aluminum stepladders"
msgstr[0] "escalera de aluminio"
msgstr[1] "escaleras de aluminio"
msgstr[2] "escaleras de aluminio"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "aluminum stepladder"
msgid ""
"A short, foldable aluminum ladder.  Can help you climb to a rooftop, or maybe "
"slow something down."
msgstr ""
"Una escalera de aluminio corta y plegable. Puede ayudarte a subir a un tejado "
"o a frenar algo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Beverly shear"
msgid_plural "Beverly shears"
msgstr[0] "cizalla Beverly"
msgstr[1] "cizallas Beverly"
msgstr[2] "cizallas Beverly"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Beverly shear"
#. ~ Description of "Beverly shear"
msgid ""
"A massive bench-mounted device with a short guillotine blade mounted to a "
"long lever.  Designed for making straight or curved cuts through sheet metal "
"up to 3 millimeters thick."
msgstr ""
"Un dispositivo muy grande montado en un banco con una cuchilla de guillotina "
"corta montada en una palanca larga. Diseñado para realizar cortes rectos o "
"curvos en chapa de hasta 3 milímetros de grosor."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "drill press"
msgid ""
"A powerful drill mounted on a slide that lets it drop precisely down.  Useful "
"in all kinds of projects from industrial fabrication to home woodworking.  "
"You can take this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un potente taladro montado sobre una corredera que le permite descender con "
"precisión. Útil en todo tipo de proyectos, desde la fabricación industrial "
"hasta la carpintería doméstica. Puedes desmontarlo y conectarlo a tu propia "
"red eléctrica para utilizarlo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "firefly terrarium"
msgstr "terrario de luciérnaga"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "firefly terrarium"
msgid ""
"While many survivors would have focused on trying to bring back electric "
"lights, whoever lives here has apparently decided to make use of the changes "
"wrought by the Cataclysm to provide light.  This vivarium contains soil, "
"strange plants you don't recognize immediately, and most strikingly, a giant "
"mutant firefly."
msgstr ""
"Mientras muchos supervivientes se enfocaron en intentar recuperar la luz "
"mediante electricidad, quien sea que vivía aquí aparentemente decidió hacer "
"uso de los cambios que trajo el Cataclismo para producir luz. Este vivero "
"contiene tierra, plantas extrañas que no reconoces y, lo que es más "
"impresionante, una luciérnaga mutante gigante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "table saw"
msgid ""
"A rotating sawblade set into a large, flat table, for making straight "
"measured cuts.  It's a key tool in any carpenter's arsenal.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Una hoja de sierra giratoria colocada en una gran mesa plana, para hacer "
"cortes rectos medidos, una herramienta clave en el arsenal de cualquier "
"carpintero. Puedes desmontarla y conectarla a tu propia red eléctrica para "
"utilizarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mitre saw"
msgid ""
"A circular sawblade on an arm that can slide and rotate in several "
"directions, this is a staple tool for nearly any carpentry.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Una hoja de sierra circular en un brazo que puede deslizarse y girar en "
"varias direcciones, es una herramienta básica para casi cualquier "
"carpintería. Puedes desmontarla y conectarla a tu red eléctrica para "
"utilizarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "band saw"
msgid ""
"A ribbonlike sawblade runs in a single direction in this tool, allowing "
"precise cuts at almost any angle.  You can take this down and plug it into "
"your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Una hoja de sierra en forma de cinta corre en una sola dirección en esta "
"herramienta, lo que permite cortes precisos en casi cualquier ángulo. Puedes "
"desmontarla y conectarla a tu red eléctrica para utilizarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "router table"
msgid ""
"This table has an inset router, a rotating motor with an exchangeable blade "
"head for cutting specific profiles and grooves and stuff.  You can take this "
"down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Esta mesa tiene una fresadora de inserción, un motor giratorio con un cabezal "
"de cuchilla intercambiable para cortar perfiles específicos y ranuras y esas "
"cosas. Puedes desmontarla y enchufarla a tu red eléctrica para utilizarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "planer"
msgid ""
"A hefty tool that will take in a board and cut it smooth and flat to a "
"specific width, particularly great if working with raw lumber stock, but also "
"good just for shaving wood down to size.  You can take this down and plug it "
"into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta robusta que toma una tabla y la reduce a una anchura "
"específica, especialmente si se trabaja con madera en bruto, pero también es "
"buena para reducir el tamaño de la madera. Puedes desmontarla y conectarla a "
"tu red eléctrica para utilizarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "jointer"
msgid ""
"A table-shaped tool with a rotating blade that will cut down, smooth out, and "
"square off a board to make it very smooth and nice indeed.  You can take this "
"down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta en forma de mesa con una cuchilla giratoria que cortará, "
"alisará y escuadrará una tabla para dejarla muy suave y bonita. Puedes "
"desmontarla y conectarla a tu red eléctrica para utilizarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "disconnected catalytic cracking reactor"
msgstr "reactor de craqueo catalítico desconectado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "disconnected catalytic cracking reactor"
msgid ""
"A makeshift extraction system, or as makeshift as you can consider something "
"that was purpose-built in a laboratory by a group of experts.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un sistema de extracción improvisado. Tan improvisado como puedas considerar "
"algo que fue construido precisamente en un laboratorio por un grupo de "
"expertos. Puedes desarmarlo y conectarlo a tu red eléctrica para usarlo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "hydraulic press"
msgid ""
"If you really want to squash something a lot, this would be exactly the right "
"industrial tool for you.  You can take this down and plug it into your own "
"power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Si realmente quieres aplastar algo mucho, esta sería exactamente la "
"herramienta industrial adecuada para ti. Puedes desmontarla y conectarla a tu "
"red eléctrica para utilizarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "power lathe"
msgid_plural "power lathes"
msgstr[0] "torno eléctrico"
msgstr[1] "tornos eléctricos"
msgstr[2] "tornos eléctricos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "power lathe"
msgid ""
"An industrial-grade lathe, for turning chunks of metal and other hard things "
"into round chunks of metal and other hard things."
msgstr ""
"Un torno de calidad industrial, para convertir trozos de metal y otras cosas "
"duras en trozos redondos de metal y otras cosas duras."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "air compressor"
msgid ""
"This durable tank is topped with a motor that will cram as much air into the "
"tank as possible.  You can take this down and plug it into your own power "
"grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Este depósito resistente está provisto de un motor que introduce la mayor "
"cantidad de aire posible dentro. Puedes desmontarla y conectarlo a tu red "
"eléctrica para utilizarlo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "manual tire changer"
msgid_plural "manual tire changers"
msgstr[0] "desmontador manual de llantas"
msgstr[1] "desmontadoras manuales de llantas"
msgstr[2] "desmontadoras manuales de llantas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "manual tire changer"
msgid ""
"This floor-mounted machine contains all the levers, clamps and mounts "
"required to remove or fit a tire, plus an integrated foot pump to inflate it."
msgstr ""
"Esta máquina montada en el suelo contiene todas las palancas, abrazaderas y "
"soportes necesarios para desmontar o montar un neumático, además de una bomba "
"de pie integrada para inflarlo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fermenting vat"
msgstr "tanque de fermentación"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fermenting vat"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled fermenting vat"
msgid "A sealable 50-liter vat for fermenting vinegar and various alcoholic brews."
msgstr ""
"Una cuba de 50 litros sellada para fermentar vinagre y varios brebajes "
"alcohólicos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled fermenting vat"
msgstr "tanque de fermentación lleno"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wooden fermenting vat"
msgstr "tanque de fermentación de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden fermenting vat"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled wooden fermenting vat"
msgid ""
"A sealable 50-liter wooden vat for fermenting vinegar and various alcoholic "
"brews."
msgstr ""
"Un tanque de madera de 50 litros sellada para fermentar vinagre y varios "
"brebajes alcohólicos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled wooden fermenting vat"
msgstr "tanque de fermentación de madera lleno"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "anaerobic digester"
msgstr "digestor anaeróbico"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "anaerobic digester"
msgid "A 1000 L anaerobic digester."
msgstr "Un digestor anaeróbico de 1000L."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled anaerobic digester"
msgstr "digestor anaeróbico lleno"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled anaerobic digester"
msgid "A 1000L anaerobic digester."
msgstr "Un digestor anaeróbico de 1000L."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "butchering rack"
msgstr "estantería de descuartizado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "butchering rack"
msgid "A wooden butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air."
msgstr ""
"Un estante de descuartizado de madera diseñado para colgar un cadáver en el "
"aire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal butchering rack"
msgid_plural "metal butchering racks"
msgstr[0] "estanteria de descuartizado de metal"
msgstr[1] "estanterias de descuartizado de metal"
msgstr[2] "estanterias de descuartizado de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal butchering rack"
msgid ""
"A metal butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air.  It can be "
"deconstructed and folded for easy transportation."
msgstr ""
"Una estantería de descuartizado de metal diseñada para colgar un cadáver en "
"el aire. Puede ser deconstruido y doblado para facilitar el transporte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "hanging meathook"
msgstr "gancho de carne colgante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "hanging meathook"
msgid "A hefty hook suspended from a chain for stringing up corpses."
msgstr "Un gran gancho suspendido de una cadena para colgar cadáveres."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wind mill"
msgid_plural "wind mills"
msgstr[0] "molino de viento"
msgstr[1] "molinos de viento"
msgstr[2] "molinos de viento"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wind mill"
msgid "A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño molino de viento que puede convertir productos con almidón en "
"harina."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active wind mill"
msgstr "molino de viento activo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active wind mill"
msgid ""
"A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Its "
"brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño molino de viento que puede convertir productos con almidón en "
"harina. Se le ha quitado el freno y está girando."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "water mill"
msgid_plural "water mills"
msgstr[0] "molino de agua"
msgstr[1] "molinos de agua"
msgstr[2] "molinos de agua"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "water mill"
msgid "A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr "Un pequeño molino de agua que puede convertir productos con almidón en harina."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active water mill"
msgstr "molino de agua activo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active water mill"
msgid ""
"A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Its "
"brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño molino de agua que puede convertir productos con almidón en "
"harina. Se le ha quitado el freno y está girando."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "automated gas console"
msgstr "consola automática de gases"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "automated gas console"
msgid "An automated gas flow control console."
msgstr "Una consola automatizada de control del flujo de gas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken automated gas console"
msgstr "consola automática de gases rota"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken automated gas console"
msgid ""
"An automated gas flow control console.  It's broken.  This is not a good "
"thing."
msgstr ""
"Una consola automatizada de control de flujo de gas. Está rota. Esto no es "
"bueno."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "reinforced vending machine"
msgstr "máquina expendedora reforzada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced vending machine"
msgid ""
"A bit tougher to crack open than a regular vending machine.  That just makes "
"it all the sweeter of a target, doesn't it?"
msgstr ""
"Un poco más difícil de abrir que una máquina expendedora normal. Eso hace que "
"sea un objetivo aún más dulce, ¿no?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "reinforced vending machine (off)"
msgstr "máquina expendedora reforzada (apag.)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced vending machine (off)"
msgid ""
"A bit tougher to crack open than a regular vending machine.  Out of order, "
"for lack of power.  That just makes it all the sweeter of a target, doesn't "
"it?"
msgstr ""
"Un poco más difícil de abrir que una máquina expendedora normal. Fuera de "
"servicio, por falta de energía. Eso lo hace un blanco más dulce, ¿no?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "vending machine"
msgstr "máquina expendedora"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "vending machine"
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  The goods inside can be "
"yours if you have money on a cash card."
msgstr ""
"Un armario metálico vertical con una puerta transparente. La mercancía que "
"hay dentro puede ser tuya si tienes dinero en una tarjeta de caja."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "vending machine (off)"
msgstr "máquina expendedora (apag.)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "vending machine (off)"
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  Out of order, for lack of "
"power."
msgstr ""
"Un armario metálico vertical con una puerta transparente. Fuera de servicio, "
"por falta de energía."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken vending machine"
msgstr "máquina expendedora rota"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken vending machine"
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  It's smashed open, so you "
"can take whatever you want for free."
msgstr ""
"Un armario metálico vertical con una puerta transparente. Está destrozado, "
"así que puedes llevarte lo que quieras gratis."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "grappling hook"
msgid_plural "grappling hooks"
msgstr[0] "gancho de escalada"
msgstr[1] "ganchos de escalada"
msgstr[2] "ganchos de escalada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "grappling hook"
msgid ""
"A dangling piece of rope, hooked securely to something above you.  You could "
"climb up or take it down."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza de soga colgando, asegurada firmemente a algo encima tuyo. Podrías "
"usarla para subir o retirarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "vine leading up"
msgstr "enredadera que sube"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "vine leading up"
msgid ""
"A thick vine is rigidly anchored to something above you.  It looks quite "
"alive.  You could climb up or tear it down."
msgstr ""
"Una gruesa enredadera está rígidamente anclada a algo por encima de ti. "
"Parece bastante viva. Podrías trepar por ella o derribarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "twang."
msgstr "twang."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "web leading up"
msgstr "red para subir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "web leading up"
msgid ""
"A thick, dangling strand of slightly sticky web, the other end is tied "
"securely to something above you.  You could use it to climb up."
msgstr ""
"Una hebra gruesa y colgante de telaraña ligeramente pegajosa, el otro extremo "
"está atado firmemente a algo por encima de ti. Podrías usarla para trepar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "rope hoist"
msgstr "polipasto de soga"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "rope hoist"
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, using a sturdy horizontal support as a basic "
"pulley.  While crude, it gives you some mechanical advantage for lifting "
"things."
msgstr ""
"Aquí cuelga un lazo de soga, utilizando un soporte horizontal resistente como "
"polea básica. Aunque rudimentario, te da cierta ventaja mecánica para "
"levantar cosas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "rope and tackle hoist"
msgstr "polipasto de soga y aparejo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "rope and tackle hoist"
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, looped through a quality tackle to give a "
"significant mechanical advantage while lifting heavy objects."
msgstr ""
"Aquí cuelga un lazo de soga, enlazado a través de un aparejo de calidad para "
"proporcionar una ventaja mecánica significativa al levantar objetos pesados."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "chain hoist"
msgstr "aparejo a cadena"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chain hoist"
msgid ""
"A sturdy chain and heavy tackle hang well-supported from the ceiling here, "
"ready to lift most heavy items you could think of using mechanical advantage."
msgstr ""
"Una cadena resistente y un aparejo fuerte que cuelgan del techo, preparada "
"para levantar los objetos más pesados que puedas imaginar utilizando su "
"ventaja mecánica."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "illuminating plant bulb"
msgstr "bulbo de planta iluminada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "illuminating plant bulb"
msgid ""
"A small plant grows among the roots here, its green, onion-like bulb "
"illuminating the area around it."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña planta crece entre las raíces y su bulbo verde, como una cebolla, "
"ilumina la zona que la rodea."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "brambles"
msgstr "zarzas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "brambles"
msgid ""
"A wall of tangled roots blocks the path here, you'd have destroy it to get "
"past."
msgstr ""
"Un muro de raíces enmarañadas bloquea el camino aquí, tendrías que destruirlo "
"para pasar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "composting midden"
msgstr "basurero de compostaje"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "composting midden"
msgid ""
"A hole has been dug into the roots here, and a pretty unpleasant smell emits "
"from it."
msgstr ""
"Un agujero ha sido cavado en las raíces aquí, y un olor bastante desagradable "
"emana de él."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active backup generator"
msgstr "generador de reserva activo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active backup generator"
msgid ""
"A ubiquitous piece of compact machinery meant for running anything from the "
"bathroom lights to electric stoves and other necessities when grid "
"electricity is unavailable.  This one is currently running.  You can hear it "
"humming slightly when you are very close."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza omnipresente de maquinaria compacta pensada para hacer funcionar "
"cualquier cosa, desde luces de baño a cocinas eléctricas y otras necesidades "
"cuando una red eléctrica no esta disponible. Este esta encendido ahora. "
"Puedes oír un ligero ronroneo cuando te acercas mucho."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "portable generator"
msgstr "generador portátil"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "portable generator"
msgid "A small, portable generator, one that people buy for a camp."
msgstr "Un generador pequeño y portátil, de los que se compran para un campamento."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "diesel generator"
msgid "Big and powerful generator, used for street works."
msgstr "Generador grande y potente, utilizado para trabajos en la calle."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "military diesel generator"
msgid "Big and powerful generator, painted in camo."
msgstr "Generador grande y potente, pintado con camuflaje."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "powerful gasoline generator"
msgid "Big and powerful, yet portable generator."
msgstr "Generador grande y potente, pero portátil."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_military.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "M224 mortar"
msgstr "mortero M224"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_military.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "M224 mortar"
msgid ""
"Deployed and ready to be used 60 mm mortar.  You are lucky you don't need to "
"scavenge actual firing tables, as they are clipped tightly to the mortar "
"itself.  However you can use it only for indirect fire, with a substantial "
"precision loss."
msgstr ""
"Mortero de 60mm desplegado y listo para ser utilizado. Tienes suerte de no "
"tener que rebuscar en las mesas de tiro reales, ya que están firmemente "
"enganchadas al propio mortero. Sin embargo, sólo se puede utilizar para fuego "
"indirecto, con una pérdida sustancial de precisión."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_military.json
#. ~ Message when furniture "M224 mortar"'s examine action fails its condition
msgid "You have absolutely no idea how to use this mortar."
msgstr "No tienes ni idea de cómo usar este mortero."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ATM"
msgstr "cajero automático"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_misc.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ATM"
msgid ""
"For your banking convenience, this Automated Teller Machine is fully capable "
"of operating autonomously in the event of complete network failure.  You can "
"deposit funds from cash cards and migrate all of your inflation-adjusted "
"earnings to a single card.  This thing has seen better days; there's been a "
"run on the bank, and this machine has the dents and cracks to prove it."
msgstr ""
"Para tu comodidad bancaria, este cajero automático es totalmente capaz de "
"funcionar de forma autónoma en caso de fallo total de la red. Puede depositar "
"fondos de tarjetas de efectivo y migrar todas tus ganancias ajustadas a la "
"inflación a una sola tarjeta. Esta cosa ha visto días mejores; ha habido una "
"carrera en el banco, y esta máquina tiene las abolladuras y grietas para "
"probarlo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_misc.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ATM"
msgid ""
"Designed to withdraw money from your bank account, this machine is completely "
"dead now, both from having no more power, and having no internet connection "
"to do any withdraws.  While you can deconstruct it, it's effectively just a "
"big pile of metal."
msgstr ""
"Diseñada para retirar dinero de tu cuenta bancaria, esta máquina está "
"completamente inactiva, tanto por no tener más energía como por no tener una "
"conexión a Internet para realizar retiradas. Aunque se puede desmontar, no es "
"más que un montón de metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "decaying tube"
msgstr "tubo en descomposición"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "decaying tube"
msgid "A decomposing fleshy stalagmite extends from the ceiling to the floor."
msgstr ""
"Una estalagmita carnosa en descomposición se extiende desde el techo hasta el "
"suelo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "glowing decaying tube"
msgstr "tubo en descomposición brillante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "glowing decaying tube"
msgid ""
"A decomposing fleshy stalagmite extends from the ceiling to the floor.  "
"Countless glowing spores weft from within, coating everything nearby."
msgstr ""
"Una estalagmita carnosa en descomposición se extiende desde el techo hasta el "
"suelo. De su interior brotan innumerables esporas brillantes que cubren todo "
"lo que hay cerca."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "beautiful nether lily"
msgstr "lirio del inframundo bonito"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "beautiful nether lily"
msgid ""
"A very tall, mesmerizing blood red flower.  Its beautiful, pristine form is "
"rooted firmly on the innards of the beast.  The flesh around it is decayed, "
"being consumed to feed its ornate, magnanimous body.  You feel an urge to sit "
"and admire this priceless miracle of life."
msgstr ""
"Una flor muy alta, hipnotizante, de color rojo sangre. Su bella y prístina "
"forma está firmemente enraizada en las entrañas de la bestia. La carne a su "
"alrededor está descompuesta, consumiéndose para alimentar su ornamentado y "
"magnánimo cuerpo. Sientes el impulso de sentarte y admirar este inapreciable "
"milagro de la vida."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "a chilling scream!"
msgstr "¡un grito escalofriante!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_floraxeno.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_floraxeno.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "squish!"
msgstr "¡Squish!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You admire the lily.  Isn't it beautiful?"
msgstr "Admiras el lirio. ¿No es hermoso?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You worship the lily, and feel truly fulfilled."
msgstr "Adoras el lirio y te sientes realmente realizado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You bow to the lily, and gain immense satisfaction in having done so."
msgstr ""
"Te inclinas ante el lirio y obtienes una inmensa satisfacción por haberlo "
"hecho."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You focus on the lily and realize it truly is perfection *incarnate*."
msgstr "Te concentras en el lirio y te das cuenta de que es la perfección *encarnada*."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nether grass"
msgstr "hierba del inframundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nether grass"
msgid ""
"A bed of waist high segmented blue plants that remind you of grass.  As you "
"wade past, they react to your movement and always swivel to face you."
msgstr ""
"Un lecho de plantas azules segmentadas a la altura de la cintura que "
"recuerdan a la hierba. Al pasar, reaccionan a tus movimientos y giran siempre "
"hacia ti."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "tall nether grass"
msgstr "hierba alta del inframundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "tall nether grass"
msgid ""
"A clump of tall, segmented blue plants that remind you of grass.  As you "
"approach, they bend towards you, hugging your body and making movement "
"difficult."
msgstr ""
"Un grupo de plantas altas, segmentadas y azules que recuerdan a la hierba. Al "
"acercarte, se inclinan hacia ti, abrazando tu cuerpo y dificultando el "
"movimiento."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nether patchwork"
msgstr "retazos del inframundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nether patchwork"
msgid ""
"A peculiar plant that is hard to distinguish, resembling a tangled mess of "
"different terrestrial flowers and weeds firmly wedged into the monstrous "
"flesh.  It pulses rhythmically as it rearranges its form into even weirder "
"shapes."
msgstr ""
"Una planta peculiar difícil de distinguir, que se asemeja a un enredo de "
"diferentes flores terrestres y malas hierbas firmemente encajadas en la carne "
"monstruosa. Late rítmicamente mientras reorganiza su forma en formas aún más "
"extrañas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nether lichen"
msgstr "liquen del inframundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nether lichen"
msgid ""
"A bed of orange, flowering lichen, covering the surface of the yellow ichor.  "
"Every now and then, a flower disappears into the liquid, but seems to "
"reappear the moment you look away."
msgstr ""
"Un lecho de líquenes anaranjados en flor cubre la superficie de icor "
"amarillo. De vez en cuando, una flor desaparece en el líquido, pero parece "
"volver a aparecer en cuanto apartas la mirada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "refrigerator"
msgstr "nevera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "refrigerator"
msgid ""
"A standard household refrigerator.  If powered, it will cool its contents to "
"extend the time before they spoil.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it "
"to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Una nevera doméstica normal. Si recibe energía, enfriará su contenido para "
"prolongar su conservación. Desmóntala si quieres conectarla a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "minifridge"
msgid ""
"A small fridge, often used in places where full-size fridge would be too big "
"or too much a hassle to transport, or when you only need a small amount of "
"items chilled.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Una nevera pequeña, que suele utilizarse en lugares donde un frigorífico de "
"tamaño normal sería demasiado grande o demasiado molesto de transportar, o "
"cuando sólo se necesita refrigerar una pequeña cantidad de objetos. "
"Desmóntala si quieres conectarla a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "single glass door fridge"
msgid ""
"A modern refrigerator with a thick sheet of glass for a door, used in stores "
"to show off the goods while keeping them cool.  Deconstruct it if you want to "
"connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Una nevera moderna con una gruesa hoja de cristal como puerta, que se utiliza "
"en las tiendas para mostrar la mercancía mientras se mantiene fría. "
"Desmóntala si quieres conectarla a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "double glass door fridge"
msgid ""
"A modern refrigerator with two glass doors, to fit twice as much goods for "
"consumers.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Una nevera moderna con dos puertas de cristal, para que quepan el doble de "
"productos para los consumidores. Desmóntala si quieres conectarla a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy-duty fridge"
msgid ""
"A heavy, bulky refrigerator, used in professional kitchens.  Deconstruct it "
"if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Una nevera pesada y voluminosa, utilizada en cocinas profesionales. "
"Desmóntala si quieres conectarla a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "display fridge"
msgid ""
"A big glass chamber, designed to display different food in multiple rows, "
"while cooling it at the same time.  Looks gorgeous, but has nothing good to "
"show to you.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Una gran cámara de cristal, diseñada para exponer distintos alimentos en "
"varias filas, al tiempo que los enfría. Tiene un aspecto precioso, pero no "
"tiene nada que ofrecerte. Desmóntala si quieres conectarla a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "minifreezer"
msgid ""
"A small upright freezer, used to store a small amount of perishables long "
"term.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño congelador vertical, utilizado para almacenar una pequeña cantidad "
"de productos perecederos a largo plazo. Desmóntalo si quieres conectarlo a la "
"red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chest minifreezer"
msgid ""
"A small chest freezer, used to store a small amount of perishables for a long "
"time, if you're willing to dig them out each time that is.  Deconstruct it if "
"you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño arcón congelador, que sirve para almacenar una pequeña cantidad de "
"productos perecederos durante mucho tiempo, si estás dispuesto a sacarlos "
"cada vez, claro. Desmóntalo si quieres conectarlo a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chest freezer"
msgid ""
"A chest freezer.  Big and power efficient, this is the dream for every "
"Cataclysm survivor.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Un arcón congelador. Grande y de gran eficiencia energética, es el sueño de "
"todo superviviente del Cataclismo. Desmóntalo si quieres conectarlo a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy-duty freezer"
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty upright freezer, one that is used in a professional kitchen.  "
"Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Un congelador vertical muy resistente, de los que se usan en una cocina "
"profesional. Desmóntalo si quieres conectarlo a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "glass door freezer"
msgid ""
"A commercial upright freezer, used to show ice creams, frozen veggies, pizza, "
"or anything else a consumer may want frozen and preserved.  Deconstruct it if "
"you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Un congelador vertical comercial, utilizado para mostrar helados, verduras "
"congeladas, pizza o cualquier otra cosa que un consumidor pueda querer "
"congelar y conservar. Desmóntalo si quieres conectarlo a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "display chest freezer"
msgstr "arcón congelador expositor"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "display chest freezer"
msgid ""
"A commercial chest freezer, used to show off ice creams, frozen veggies, "
"pizza, or anything else a consumer may want frozen and preserved.  "
"Conveniently tall enough for any curious child to gaze in at the sweets.  "
"Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""
"Un arcón congelador comercial, utilizado para mostrar helados, verduras "
"congeladas, pizza o cualquier otra cosa que un consumidor pueda querer "
"congelar y conservar. Convenientemente alto para que cualquier niño curioso "
"pueda mirar los dulces. Desmóntalo si quieres conectarlo a la red."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass figure"
msgstr "figura de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of a someone frozen halfway through falling backwards, "
"and suspended on a single leg."
msgstr ""
"Una figura de cristal negro de alguien congelado a medio camino cayendo hacia "
"atrás y suspendido sobre una sola pierna."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "tink."
msgstr "tink."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid "A black glass figure of a person covering their face with their hands."
msgstr "Una figura de cristal negro de una persona que se cubre la cara con las manos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of a child.  It is difficult to make out their facial "
"features, but it seems as if they are smiling."
msgstr ""
"Figura de cristal negro de un niño. Es difícil distinguir sus rasgos "
"faciales, pero parece como si sonriera."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid "A black glass figure of someone kneeling in prayer."
msgstr "Figura de cristal negro de alguien arrodillado rezando."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone in a firing posture.  Their jagged fingers "
"are frozen squeezing a trigger that isn't there."
msgstr ""
"Una figura de cristal negro de alguien en una posición de disparo. Sus dedos "
"dentados están congelados apretando un gatillo que no está ahí."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone leaning into the space to their right, their "
"fingers bent as if interlaced with someone else's."
msgstr ""
"Una figura de cristal negro de alguien inclinado en el espacio a su derecha, "
"sus dedos doblados como entrelazados con los de otra persona."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone clutching at their neck.  A delicate spray of "
"connected glass droplets emerges between their fingers."
msgstr ""
"Una figura de cristal negro de alguien agarrándose el cuello. Un delicado "
"rocío de gotas de vidrio conectadas surge entre sus dedos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"Most of a black glass human figure.  The face and much of the head is "
"missing, as if scooped out, and the inner surface is perfectly smooth."
msgstr ""
"La mayor parte de una figura humana de vidrio negro. Falta la cara y gran "
"parte de la cabeza, como si la hubieran sacado con cuchara, y la superficie "
"interior es perfectamente lisa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid "A black glass figure of someone doubled over in laughter."
msgstr "Una figura de cristal negro de alguien partiéndose de risa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure.  Their features are too jagged to make out clearly, but "
"they remind you of someone you knew."
msgstr ""
"Una figura de cristal negro. Sus rasgos son demasiado irregulares para "
"distinguirlos con claridad, pero te recuerdan a alguien conocido."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone in a fighting stance, their face twisted with "
"howls of rage and anger.  They're gripping some sort of weapon that isn't "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Una figura de cristal negro de alguien en postura de combate, con la cara "
"retorcida por los aullidos de rabia e ira. Está empuñando un arma que no "
"existe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bed"
msgstr "cama de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bed"
msgid ""
"A black glass sculpture of a bed.  The rumpled covers are jagged, and "
"splinter at the touch."
msgstr ""
"Una cama esculpida en cristal negro. Las fundas arrugadas son irregulares y "
"se astillan al tacto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clink."
msgstr "clink."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bathtub"
msgstr "bañera de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bathtub"
msgid ""
"A tub made from black glass, with a frozen column of onyx pouring from the "
"tap."
msgstr ""
"Una bañera de cristal negro, con una columna helada de ónice que mana del "
"grifo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "glass shattering!"
msgstr "¡cristal rompiéndose!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clink!"
msgstr "¡clink!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass dresser"
msgstr "vestidor de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dresser"
msgid ""
"A black glass cabinet with its doors slightly ajar.  Inside is a row of "
"hangers bearing neatly folded and entirely rigid clothing."
msgstr ""
"Un armario de cristal negro con las puertas ligeramente entreabiertas. Dentro "
"hay una hilera de perchas con ropa perfectamente doblada y rígida."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass refrigerator"
msgstr "frigorífico de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass refrigerator"
msgid ""
"A black glass refrigerator, its door hanging open.  Inside is a seamless "
"surface with protrusions resembling fresh fruit and plastic bottles."
msgstr ""
"Un frigorífico de cristal negro, con la puerta abierta. Dentro hay una "
"superficie sin juntas con protuberancias que parecen fruta fresca y botellas "
"de plástico."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass armchair"
msgstr "sillón de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass armchair"
msgid ""
"An armchair that was presumably once very plush and comfortable.  Now the "
"overstuffed cushions are hard, cold, and slippery."
msgstr ""
"Un sillón que presumiblemente fue una vez muy afelpado y cómodo. Ahora los "
"cojines son duros, fríos y resbaladizos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass chair"
msgstr "silla de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass chair"
msgid ""
"A simple glass chair.  The seat is very thin, and crunches ominously under "
"any weight."
msgstr ""
"Una simple silla de cristal. El asiento es muy delgado, y cruje ominosamente "
"bajo cualquier peso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass desk"
msgstr "escritorio de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass desk"
msgid ""
"A glass desk.  There are a handful of shapes atop it that suggest pens, "
"paper, and miscellaneous knickknacks that are too jagged to identify."
msgstr ""
"Un escritorio de cristal. Encima hay un puñado de formas que sugieren "
"bolígrafos, papel y diversos cachivaches demasiado irregulares para "
"identificarlos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass locker"
msgstr "taquilla de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass locker"
msgid ""
"A tall glass cabinet.  Whatever was inside will stay that way; the door is "
"seamless with the frame."
msgstr ""
"Una vitrina de cristal alta. Lo que hubiera dentro se quedará así; la puerta "
"no tiene juntas con el marco."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "glass crunching!"
msgstr "¡cristal rompiéndose!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass oven"
msgstr "horno de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass oven"
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a gas oven.  Bristling from the burner is a crown of "
"jagged shards in the rough shape of an uncontrolled fire."
msgstr ""
"Una escultura de cristal de un horno de gas. Del quemador sale una corona de "
"fragmentos irregulares con la forma tosca de un fuego incontrolado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass mailbox"
msgstr "buzón de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass mailbox"
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a mailbox.  The door is open; inside is a pile of "
"envelopes, all razor-edged."
msgstr ""
"Una escultura de cristal de un buzón. La puerta está abierta; dentro hay una "
"pila de sobres, todos afilados."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass display rack"
msgstr "expositor de cristal negro "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass display rack"
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a shelving unit.  The angled shelves are covered in "
"jagged miscellany, most of which is firmly fused in place."
msgstr ""
"Una escultura de cristal de una estantería. Los estantes en ángulo están "
"cubiertos de una miscelánea dentada, la mayor parte de la cual está "
"firmemente fundida en su lugar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass sink"
msgstr "fregadero de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass sink"
msgid ""
"A glass basin and tap.  The inside stops halfway down in sheet of concentric "
"ripples, with the tiny spire of a splashing droplet at the center "
msgstr ""
"Un lavabo y un grifo de cristal. El interior se detiene a mitad de camino en "
"una lámina de ondulaciones concéntricas, con la diminuta aguja de una gota "
"que salpica en el centro. "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass toilet"
msgstr "inodoro de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass toilet"
msgid "A toilet made of black glass.  The lid, perhaps mercifully, is fused shut."
msgstr "Un inodoro de cristal negro. La tapa, quizás por suerte, está fundida."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass cupboard"
msgstr "armario de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass cupboard"
msgid ""
"A black glass cupboard.  The doors are fused shut, but it presumably contains "
"glasses."
msgstr ""
"Un armario de cristal negro. Las puertas están cerradas, pero se supone que "
"contiene vasos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass garden"
msgstr "jardín de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass garden"
msgid ""
"A planter of dark glass.  Sharp, twisting glass sprouts emerge from the black "
"soil within."
msgstr ""
"Una maceta de cristal oscuro. Brotes afilados y retorcidos de cristal emergen "
"de la tierra negra de su interior."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass flower"
msgstr "flor de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass flower"
msgid ""
"A delicate little thing; a wispy stem slightly bowed under the weight of "
"translucent petals.  The tiny barbs that line it are almost impossible to "
"see, until it crumbles in your fingers."
msgstr ""
"Una cosita delicada; un tallo delgado ligeramente inclinado bajo el peso de "
"pétalos translúcidos. Las diminutas púas que lo recubren son casi imposibles "
"de ver, hasta que se deshace entre los dedos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "tinkle."
msgstr "tintineo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "plink."
msgstr "plink."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bench"
msgstr "banco de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bench"
msgid ""
"A long, low slab of black glass.  You can't tell if the fissures here and "
"there on the surface are natural cracks, or carved names."
msgstr ""
"Una losa larga y baja de cristal negro. No se sabe si las fisuras aquí y allá "
"en la superficie son grietas naturales, o nombres tallados."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass washer"
msgstr "lavadora de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass washer"
msgid ""
"A glass washing machine.  The inside is completely filled with black sand, "
"some of which has spilled onto the floor."
msgstr ""
"Una lavadora de cristal. El interior está completamente lleno de arena negra, "
"parte de la cual se ha derramado por el suelo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass dryer"
msgstr "secadora de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dryer"
msgid ""
"A mechanical dryer of black glass.  The door hangs open, and inside, you can "
"see a jumble of what might once have been clothes, now smashed to pieces."
msgstr ""
"Una secadora mecánica de cristal negro. La puerta cuelga abierta y, dentro, "
"se ve un revoltijo de lo que podría haber sido ropa, ahora hecha pedazos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bookcase"
msgstr "estantería de libros de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bookcase"
msgid ""
"A heavy bookshelf, laden with books fused into the shelves and each other.  "
"You can make out titles on the spines, but the alphabet they're written in is "
"unfamiliar."
msgstr ""
"Una pesada estantería, cargada de libros fundidos en las estanterías y entre "
"sí. Se distinguen los títulos en los lomos, pero el alfabeto en el que están "
"escritos es desconocido."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass counter"
msgstr "mostrador de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass counter"
msgid ""
"A thick cube of black glass.  On the surface, fused in place, are statues of "
"utensils and miscellany."
msgstr ""
"Un grueso cubo de vidrio negro. En la superficie, fundidas en su sitio, hay "
"estatuas de utensilios y miscelánea."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass table"
msgstr "mesa de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass table"
msgid ""
"A slab of smooth black glass on four stout legs.  In a few places, there is "
"shallowly rounded mass, like liquid spilled on the surface."
msgstr ""
"Una losa de vidrio negro liso sobre cuatro patas robustas. En algunos lugares "
"hay una masa poco profunda y redondeada, como líquido derramado en la "
"superficie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass birdbath"
msgstr "pajarera de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass birdbath"
msgid ""
"A glass pedestal and bowl.  Inside, frozen in the midst of washing itself in "
"the black sand, is the delicate figure of a bird."
msgstr ""
"Un pedestal y un cuenco de cristal. En su interior, congelada en medio del "
"lavado en la arena negra, está la delicada figura de un pájaro."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clunk."
msgstr "clunk."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass shower"
msgstr "ducha de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass shower"
msgid ""
"From the head of this shower descend a dozen streams of thin black glass, "
"with frozen droplets strung from them like pearls."
msgstr ""
"De la cabeza de esta ducha descienden una docena de chorros de fino cristal "
"negro, con gotas heladas ensartadas en ellos como perlas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass water heater"
msgstr "calentador de agua de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass water heater"
msgid ""
"A cylinder of thick black glass.  The top has burst apart, and rivulets of "
"black sand run down the side."
msgstr ""
"Un cilindro de grueso cristal negro. La parte superior ha estallado y por el "
"lateral corren riachuelos de arena negra."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass fireplace"
msgstr "chimenea de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass fireplace"
msgid ""
"A fireplace of pitted glass bricks.  The fire inside has been frozen in glass "
"at the moment it began to leap beyond the grate."
msgstr ""
"Una chimenea de ladrillos de vidrio picados. El fuego interior se ha "
"congelado en vidrio en el momento en que empezó a saltar más allá de la "
"rejilla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ring of black stones"
msgstr "anillo de piedras negras"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ring of black stones"
msgid ""
"A circle of smooth glass pebbles.  Inside are frozen tendrils of fire, "
"slightly translucent.  It seems colder as you approach."
msgstr ""
"Un círculo de guijarros de vidrio liso. En su interior hay zarcillos de fuego "
"congelados, ligeramente translúcidos. Parece más frío a medida que te acercas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass lantern"
msgstr "linterna de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass lantern"
msgid ""
"A tall glass pole with a translucent shade atop it.  You know it could not "
"possibly turn on, but in the corner of your eye, you think you might see a "
"soft glow."
msgstr ""
"Un poste alto de cristal con una pantalla translúcida encima. Sabes que es "
"imposible que se encienda, pero con el rabillo del ojo te parece ver un suave "
"resplandor."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "tink!"
msgstr "¡tink!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass box"
msgstr "caja de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass box"
msgid "A box of thin black glass.  Its edges are glisteningly sharp."
msgstr "Una caja de fino cristal negro. Sus bordes son brillantes y afilados."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass sofa"
msgstr "sofa de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass sofa"
msgid "A long bench, padded with cold glass cushions."
msgstr "Un banco largo, acolchado con cojines de cristal frío."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass dishwasher"
msgstr "lavavajillas de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dishwasher"
msgid ""
"A glass dishwasher, its door hanging open.  Inside, glass plates and utensils "
"are half buried in black sand."
msgstr ""
"Un lavavajillas de cristal, con la puerta abierta. Dentro, platos y "
"utensilios de cristal están semienterrados en arena negra."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "incomplete plush doll"
msgstr "muñeco de peluche incompleto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "incomplete plush doll"
msgid "A soft plush torso, empty of features, is lying on this sofa."
msgstr "Un suave torso de felpa, vacío de rasgos, yace en este sofá."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bookcase"
msgid "This bookcase is missing a book."
msgstr "A esta estantería de libros le falta un libro."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rocky coastline"
msgstr "costa rocosa"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rocky coastline"
msgid ""
"This is a section of eroded natural stone formations along the beach, the "
"water lapping and splashing at the edges."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una sección de formaciones de piedra natural erosionadas a lo largo "
"de la playa, con el agua chapoteando y salpicando en los bordes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tide pool"
msgstr "poza de marea"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tide pool"
msgid "A shallow pool of salt water, often filled with interesting life."
msgstr "Una piscina poco profunda de agua salada, a menudo llena de vida interesante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "walkway"
msgstr "acera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "walkway"
msgid ""
"A metallic bridge commonly used in industrial settings to meet specified "
"safety standards."
msgstr ""
"Es un puente metálico comúnmente utilizado en industrias para cumplir con las "
"reglas de seguridad establecidas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_recreational.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain_light_blue.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "dock"
msgstr "muelle"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow bridge"
msgid "A wooden platform held by a support made of logs dug into the ground."
msgstr ""
"Una plataforma de madera sostenida por un soporte hecho de leños excavados en "
"el suelo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "deep dock pile"
msgstr "postes de muelle profundos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of wood extending all the way to the riverbed.  A frame "
"will be required to support a surface."
msgstr ""
"Una pila robusta de madera que se extiende hasta el lecho del río. Se "
"necesitará una estructura para soportar una superficie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "deep dock frame"
msgstr "estructura de muelle profundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
msgid ""
"A log frame secured atop a wooden pile.  Adding a wood surface will make this "
"into a proper dock section."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura de leños asegurado sobre una pila de madera. Añadiendo una "
"superficie de madera, esto se convertirá en una sección de muelle apropiada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "deep dock"
msgstr "muelle profundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
msgid ""
"A wooden platform held by a tall wooden pile that extend to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr ""
"Una plataforma de madera sostenida por una alta pila de madera que se "
"extiende hasta el lecho del río. Muy robusta, y es probable que dure más que "
"tú."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shallow bridge"
msgstr "puente poco profundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "pontoon bridge"
msgstr "puente flotante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "pontoon bridge"
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over still water, like the ones armies used to "
"make to cross lakes."
msgstr ""
"Un puente temporal flotante sobre aguas tranquilas, como los que hacían los "
"ejércitos para cruzar los lagos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "river bridge"
msgstr "puente de río"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "river bridge"
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over flowing water, like the ones armies used to "
"make to cross rivers."
msgstr ""
"Un puente temporal flotante sobre el agua que fluye, como los que los "
"ejércitos solían hacer para cruzar los ríos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bridge pavement"
msgstr "pavimento puente"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge pavement"
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal."
msgstr "Una sección del puente hecha de hormigón y metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "concrete cracking and metal screeching!"
msgstr "¡rotura de hormigón y chirrido de metal!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bridge yellow pavement"
msgstr "pavimento amarillo puente"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge yellow pavement"
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal.  It's painted yellow."
msgstr "Un tramo de puente hecho de hormigón y metal. Está pintado de amarillo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bridge sidewalk"
msgstr "acera del puente"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge sidewalk"
msgid "The sidewalk section of a concrete bridge."
msgstr "La sección de la acera de un puente de hormigón."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
msgid "A metal platform held by a support made of concrete set into the ground."
msgstr ""
"Una plataforma metálica sostenida por un soporte de hormigón incrustado en el "
"suelo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of poured concrete extending all the way to the riverbed.  "
"A metal frame will be required to support a surface."
msgstr ""
"Un robusto pilar de hormigón vertido que se extiende hasta el lecho del río. "
"Se necesitará una estructura metálica para soportar una superficie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
msgid ""
"A metal frame secured atop a concrete pile.  Adding a metal surface will make "
"this into a proper dock section."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura metálica fijada sobre un pilar de hormigón. Si se añade una "
"superficie metálica, se convertirá en una sección de muelle propiamente dicha."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
msgid ""
"A metal platform held by a tall metal pile that extends to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr ""
"Una plataforma metálica sostenida por una alta pila de metal que se extiende "
"hasta el lecho del río. Muy resistente, y es probable que dure más que tú."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal floating dock"
msgstr "muelle flotante de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floating dock"
msgid "A floating temporary dock, anchored to keep it from drifting away."
msgstr "Un muelle temporal flotante, anclado para evitar que se vaya a la deriva."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed laminated glass door"
msgstr "puerta cerrada de cristal laminado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed laminated glass door"
msgid ""
"A closed laminated glass door, composed of layers of glass and plastic held "
"together by an interlayer."
msgstr ""
"Puerta cerrada de cristal laminado, compuesta por capas de cristal y plástico "
"unidas por una capa intermedia."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open laminated glass door"
msgstr "abrir la puerta de cristal laminado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open laminated glass door"
msgid ""
"A laminated glass door, composed of layers of glass and plastic held together "
"by an interlayer.  It's open."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de cristal laminado, compuesta por capas de cristal y plástico "
"unidas por una capa intermedia. Está abierta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed ballistic glass door"
msgstr "puerta de cristal antibalas cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed ballistic glass door"
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass."
msgstr "Una puerta de cristal antibalas, formada por capas de cristal laminado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open ballistic glass door"
msgstr "puerta de cristal antibalas abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open ballistic glass door"
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass.  It's open."
msgstr "Un cristal antibalas, que consiste en capas de cristal laminado. Está abierto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed reinforced glass door"
msgstr "puerta de cristal reforzada cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced glass door"
msgid ""
"A closed glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but "
"practical pattern."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta cerrada de cristal reforzada con alambres de acero tejidos en un "
"patrón elegante, pero práctico."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open reinforced glass door"
msgstr "abrir la puerta de cristal reforzado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced glass door"
msgid ""
"A glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but practical "
"pattern.  It's open."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de cristal reforzada con alambres de acero entretejidos en un "
"patrón elegante pero práctico. Está abierta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wood door"
msgstr "puerta de madera cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de madera estándar que no parece muy resistente. Probablemente "
"también se quemaría fácilmente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
msgid "You notice the door is unlocked, so you simply open it."
msgstr ""
"Te das cuenta de que la puerta no está cerrada con llave, así que simplemente "
"la abres."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
msgstr "puerta de madera cerrada con cerradura electrónica"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt electronic lock, so it's likely locked. "
" You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock "
"the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de madera estándar que no parece muy resistente. Probablemente "
"también se quemaría fácilmente. Ésta tiene un cerrojo electrónico, así que "
"probablemente esté cerrada. Podrías hacer palanca para abrirla, adivinar el "
"código es impensable, o desbloquear el cerrojo desde dentro."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid "You pry open the door."
msgstr "Abres la puerta a la fuerza."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid "You pry, but can't pry open the door."
msgstr "Haces palanca, pero no puedes abrir la puerta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This one "
"has a deadbolt numpad, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open, "
"guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock the deadbolt from the "
"inside."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta normal de madera corriente, pero con mirilla. Si la examinaras más "
"de cerca, serías capaz de mirar a través del agujero. Esta tiene un teclado "
"numérico de cerrojo, así que probablemente esté cerrada. Podrías abrirla "
"haciendo palanca, adivinar el código es impensable, o desbloquear el cerrojo "
"desde dentro."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has an electronic keypad, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de madera estándar que no parece muy resistente. Probablemente "
"también se quemaría fácilmente. Esta tiene un teclado electrónico, así que "
"probablemente esté cerrada. Podrías abrirla haciendo palanca, adivinar el "
"código es impensable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wood door"
msgstr "puerta de madera abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one is wide open."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de madera estándar que no parece muy resistente. Probablemente "
"también se quemaría fácilmente. Esta está abierta de par en par."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "damaged wood door"
msgstr "puerta dañada de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door"
msgid ""
"A trashed wooden door, with a large hole in the middle that you can see right "
"through.  The doorknob is so messed up that it can't be opened anymore.  It "
"could be fixed up with a few planks."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de madera rota, con un gran agujero en el medio por el que puedes "
"ver. El pomo esta tan maltrecho que no se puede abrir. Se podría arreglar con "
"unos cuantos tablones."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "empty door frame"
msgstr "marco vacío de puerta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "empty door frame"
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made from planks and nails.  A variety of doors could be "
"constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Un marco de puerta vacío hecho con tablones y clavos. Aquí se podría "
"construir una variedad de puertas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed glass door"
msgstr "puerta de cristal cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed glass door"
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door, clear enough that an animal or a particularly dumb "
"person could slam right into it.  This one is closed, so don't hurt yourself."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta corredera de cristal, lo suficientemente despejada como para que "
"un animal o una persona especialmente tonta se estrelle contra ella. Esta "
"está cerrada, así que no te hagas daño."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open glass door"
msgstr "puerta de cristal abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open glass door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open frosted glass door"
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door that has been left open for all manner of things to "
"travel through."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta corrediza de cristal que ha sido dejada abierta para que todo tipo "
"de cosas viajen a través de ella.Una puerta corrediza de cristal que ha sido "
"dejada abierta para que todo tipo de cosas viajen a través de ella."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgstr "sección de lente de faro con bisagras cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be "
"visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is on hinges and can "
"be opened for maintenance."
msgstr ""
"Una intrincada disposición de cristales, diseñada para enfocar la luz desde "
"el interior y ser visible a larga distancia. Esta sección de la lente tiene "
"bisagras y puede abrirse para su mantenimiento."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgstr "sección de lente de faro con bisagras abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be "
"visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is hinged and is "
"currently open."
msgstr ""
"Una intrincada disposición de cristales, diseñada para enfocar la luz desde "
"el interior y ser visible a larga distancia. Esta sección de la lente tiene "
"bisagras y actualmente está abierta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wood door with peephole"
msgstr "puerta de madera cerrada con mirilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta normal de madera ordinaria, excepto que ésta tiene una mirilla. Si "
"la examinaras más de cerca, podrías ver a través del agujero."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "damaged wood door with peephole"
msgstr "puerta dañada de madera con mirilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door with peephole"
msgid ""
"The bad news is that the peephole is broken and you can't use it to look "
"through the door.  The good news is that the door is nearly broken down, so "
"there's nothing blocking the view.  Also, the doorknob is so messed up that "
"it can't be opened anymore.  A few planks, nails, and the right tools could "
"patch up all the damage."
msgstr ""
"La mala noticia es que la mirilla está rota y no puedes usarla para mirar a "
"través de la puerta. La buena noticia es que la puerta está casi rota, así "
"que no hay nada que bloquee la vista. Además, el pomo de la puerta está tan "
"destrozado que ya no se puede abrir. Unos cuantos tablones, clavos y las "
"herramientas adecuadas podrían arreglar todos los desperfectos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wood door with peephole"
msgstr "puerta de madera abierta con mirilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  No need "
"right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta normal de madera ordinaria, excepto que tiene una mirilla. Si la "
"examinas más de cerca, puedes ver a través de la mirilla. Aunque, no "
"necesitas mirar a través de ella ya que la puerta está abierta de todos modos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed reinforced wood door"
msgstr "puerta de madera reforzada cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced wood door"
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks "
"and an additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but it's "
"still susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""
"Igual que otras puertas de madera, excepto que ésta tiene capas de tablones "
"clavados y una bisagra adicional como refuerzo. Puede estar reforzada, pero "
"aún así es susceptible al fuego."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "damaged reinforced wood door"
msgstr "puerta dañada de madera reforzada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged reinforced wood door"
msgid ""
"Despite someone's best efforts at reinforcing this door, there are "
"splintering planks and visible holes in the wood, it could soon be smashed "
"apart completely if not repaired.  The doorknob is all messed up and the door "
"can't be opened until it's fixed."
msgstr ""
"A pesar de los esfuerzos de alguien por reforzar esta puerta, hay tablones "
"astillados y agujeros visibles en la madera, pronto podría romperse por "
"completo si no se repara. El pomo está destrozado y la puerta no se puede "
"abrir hasta que la reparen."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open reinforced wood door"
msgstr "puerta de madera reforzada abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced wood door"
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks "
"for reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but it's still susceptible to "
"fire.  It's open, so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr ""
"Igual que otras puertas de madera, excepto que ésta tiene capas de tablones "
"clavados como refuerzo. Puede estar fortificada, pero sigue siendo "
"susceptible al fuego. Está abierta, así que no detiene nada ahora mismo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta común de madera que no parece muy resistente. Y probablemente, "
"se prenda fuego fácil, también. Esta tiene otra cerradura más, así que más "
"que seguro que está cerrada. Podrías intentar forzar la cerradura."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain ""
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the door opens."
msgstr "Con un satisfactorio click, la cerradura de la puerta se abre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta común de madera que no parece muy resistente. Y probablemente, "
"se prenda fuego fácil, también. Esta tiene una cerradura de seguridad, así "
"que debe estar cerrada. Podrías intentar abrirla o forzar la cerradura, o "
"abrir la cerradura de seguridad desde adentro."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This one "
"has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or pick "
"the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta normal de madera ordinaria, excepto que ésta tiene una mirilla. Si "
"la examinaras más de cerca, podrías ver a través del agujero. Esta tiene una "
"cerradura con cerrojo, así que es probable que esté cerrada. Podrías abrirla "
"o forzar la cerradura, o desbloquear el cerrojo desde el interior."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed door curtain"
msgstr "puerta de cortina cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed door curtain"
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr ""
"Cortinas reutilizadas de una ventana que cubren el marco de una puerta. "
"Podrían desmontarse fácilmente para llevar suministros o colocarse en otro "
"lugar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed makeshift door"
msgstr "puerta improvisada cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed makeshift door"
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"vertically from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and "
"re-purposed."
msgstr ""
"Una mampara improvisada formada por tablones atados con una soga, que cuelga "
"verticalmente de la parte superior de la puerta. Podría desmontarse "
"fácilmente y reutilizarse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "wham."
msgstr "zas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open door curtain"
msgstr "puerta de cortina abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open door curtain"
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, "
"bundled, and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr ""
"Cortinas reutilizadas de una ventana que cubren el marco de una puerta. "
"Podrían desmontarse fácilmente para llevar suministros o colocarse en otro "
"lugar. Las cortinas están abiertas, liadas y atadas junto a la puerta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed grass curtain"
msgstr "cortina cerrada de pasto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed grass curtain"
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr ""
"Hojas de hilo de hierba cubriendo el marco de una puerta. Podría desmontarse "
"fácilmente para recoger suministros o colocarse en otro lugar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open grass curtain"
msgstr "cortina abierta de pasto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open grass curtain"
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, bundled, and tied "
"next to the doorway."
msgstr ""
"Hojas de hilo de hierba cubriendo el marco de una puerta. Podrían desmontarse "
"fácilmente para recoger suministros o colocarse en otro lugar. Las cortinas "
"están abiertas, liadas y atadas junto a la puerta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open makeshift door"
msgstr "puerta improvisada abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open makeshift door"
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-purposed.  "
"The planks have been rolled up and attached to the top of the doorway, "
"allowing free movement through."
msgstr ""
"Una mampara improvisada formada por tablones atados con soga, que cuelga de "
"la parte superior de la puerta. Podría desmontarse fácilmente y reutilizarse. "
"Los tablones se han enrollado y atado a la parte superior de la puerta, "
"permitiendo la libre circulación."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "empty metal door frame"
msgstr "marco de metal vacío de puerta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal door frame"
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made of steel and assorted metal.  A variety of doors "
"could be constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Un marco de puerta vacío hecho de acero y metal variado. Una variedad de "
"puertas podrían ser construidas aquí."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "empty metal window frame"
msgstr "marco de metal vacío de ventana"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal window frame"
msgid ""
"An empty window frame constructed from assembled metal and carefully braced "
"with various hardware."
msgstr ""
"Un marco de ventana vacío construido con metales ensamblados y cuidadosamente "
"apuntalados."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up door"
msgstr "puerta tapiada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that has several planks across it, nailed down to "
"board it up and increase its durability.  It's still flammable, though."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de madera estándar que tiene varios tablones a lo largo, clavados "
"para entablarla y aumentar su durabilidad. Pero sigue siendo inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgid "You pry the boards from the door."
msgstr "Sacas las tablas de la puerta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up damaged door"
msgstr "puerta tapiada dañaha"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
msgid ""
"A boarded up wooden door, except that some of the planks are fractured or "
"coming loose.  Without repairs, it could be broken down easily."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de madera tapiada, salvo que algunas de las tablones están "
"fracturadas o se están soltando. Si no se repara, podría romperse fácilmente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up door with peephole"
msgstr "puerta tapiada con mirilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A boarded up door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, you could still look through the "
"peephole if you were close enough."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta tapiada de madera normal, pero con una mirilla. Aunque está "
"cubierta de tablones, aún se puede mirar por la mirilla si se está lo "
"suficientemente cerca."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up reinforced door"
msgstr "puerta entablada reforzada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
msgid ""
"An additionally reinforced door of layered planks that has been boarded up "
"with more wood to prevent it from opening.  It's still susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta adicionalmente reforzada de tablones estratificados que ha sido "
"tapiada con más madera para evitar que se abra. Sigue siendo susceptible al "
"fuego."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
msgstr "puerta dañada con tablas reforzada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
msgid ""
"A battered and torn reinforced door with planks bursting from the joints.  "
"The boarded up planks are fragmented and in pieces, this doesn't look like an "
"easy repair."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta reforzada bastante golpeada y rota, con tablones de madera "
"sobresaliendo. Los entablados de tablones están fragmentados en trozos, esto "
"no parece fácil de reparar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgstr "puerta dañada con tablas con mirilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A wrecked door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole and some "
"partly-splintered boards nailed across it.  The peephole is damaged and can't "
"be used to see through."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta destrozada hecha de madera normal, excepto que ésta tiene una "
"mirilla y algunas tablas parcialmente astilladas clavadas a través de ella. "
"La mirilla está dañada y no se puede ver a través de ella."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_doors.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed metal door"
msgstr "puerta de metal cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente hecha de acero variado, tallada y "
"golpeada en su forma."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed corrugated metal door"
msgstr "puerta de metal corrugada cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed corrugated metal door"
msgid "A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame."
msgstr "Una fina puerta de acero corrugado sujeto a un marco."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal wall"
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned and joined "
"seamlessly with perimeter sealant, this wall is capable of resisting extreme "
"elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely "
"fire-retardant, breaching it will require specialized tools or an industrial "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Una gruesa plancha fabricada industrialmente, cuidadosamente colocada y unida "
"a la perfección con sellante perimetral, este muro/pared es capaz de resistir "
"elementos extremos, así como fuerzas hostiles. Clasificado para soportar "
"explosiones y extremadamente ignífugo, para romperlo se necesitan "
"herramientas especializadas o un vehículo industrial."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open secret door"
msgstr "abrir puerta secreta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of metal wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr ""
"Este trozo de muro/pared de metal parecía normal pero se ha abierto para "
"revelar un pasaje secreto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de hormigón"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
msgid ""
"A faux concrete wall positioned and joined seamlessly with the wall, this "
"wall is capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  "
"Blast load rated and extremely fire-retardant, breaching it will require "
"specialized tools or an industrial vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un muro/pared de hormigón de imitación colocado y unido a la perfección, este "
"muro es capaz de resistir elementos extremos así como fuerzas hostiles. "
"Clasificado para soportar explosiones y extremadamente ignífugo, para "
"romperlo se necesitan herramientas especializadas o un vehículo industrial."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of concrete wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr ""
"Este segmento aparentemente normal de muro/pared de hormigón se ha abierto "
"para revelar un pasaje secreto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "thwack!"
msgstr "¡track!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "electronic locked metal door"
msgstr "puerta de metal cerrada electrónica"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "electronic locked metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It is locked by an electronic keypad."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente hecha de acero variado, tallada y "
"golpeada en su forma. Está cerrada mediante un teclado electrónico."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open metal door"
msgstr "puerta de metal abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente hecha de acero variado, tallada y "
"golpeada en su forma. Está abierta, así que no se necesitan herramientas para "
"entrar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open corrugated metal door"
msgstr "puerta de metal corrugada abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open corrugated metal door"
msgid ""
"A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame.  It's open, so no tools "
"are needed to break in."
msgstr ""
"Una fina puerta de acero corrugado sujeta a un marco. Está abierta, por lo "
"que no se necesitan herramientas para entrar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed metal door with peephole"
msgstr "puerta de metal cerrada con mirilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door with peephole"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente hecha de acero variado, tallado y "
"golpeado para darle forma. Si la examinaras más de cerca, serías capaz de "
"asomarte por la mirilla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open metal door with peephole"
msgstr "puerta de metal abierta con mirilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door with peephole"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole.  No need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente hecha de acero variado, tallado y "
"golpeado para darle forma. Si la examinaras más de cerca, podrías mirar por "
"la mirilla. Pero ahora no hace falta, ya que la puerta está abierta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid ""
"A galvanized steel door, forged to withstand punishment and impede anyone or "
"anything.  Typically used in conjunction with automated electronic locking "
"mechanisms that require an external source to unlock."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta de acero galvanizado, forjada para soportar cualquier castigo y "
"impedir el paso de todo. Comúnmente se utiliza en conjunto con un mecanismo "
"de cerradura electrónica que requieren un elemento externo para poder abrirse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain ""
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid "You pry open the metal door."
msgstr "Abres la puerta de metal a la fuerza."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain ""
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid "The metal door is too thick."
msgstr "La puerta de metal es muy gruesa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could "
"probably pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente hecha de acero variado, tallada y "
"golpeada en su forma. Esta tiene un ojo de cerradura extra, así que es "
"probable que esté cerrada. Probablemente podrías forzar la cerradura."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed bar door"
msgstr "puerta de bar cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism doesn't appear to be engaged."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de detención hecha de barras de acero inoxidable entrecruzadas. El "
"mecanismo de cierre no parece estar activado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_spaceship.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_spaceship.json
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed bar door"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "open wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "chain link fence"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal post"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "railroad track"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "recessed railroad track"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "rebar cage"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "armored boarded up window"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window frame with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars and curtains"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal grate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal grate and curtains"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "prison grating"
msgid "You finish cutting the metal."
msgstr "Terminaste de cortar el metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open bar door"
msgstr "puerta de bar abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open bar door"
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's wide "
"open.  Freedom!"
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de detención hecha de barras entrecruzadas de acero inoxidable. "
"Está abierta. ¡Libertad!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism appears to be engaged.  You could pick it open with enough skill."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de seguridad formada por barras de acero inoxidable entrecruzadas. "
"El mecanismo de cierre parece estar activado. Podrías abrirla con suficiente "
"habilidad."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed bar door"
msgid "The door swings open…"
msgstr "La puerta se abre..."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed frosted glass door"
msgstr "puerta cerrada de cristal mate"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed frosted glass door"
msgid "A sliding door of frosted white glass."
msgstr "Una puerta de cristal mate corrediza."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open frosted glass door"
msgstr "puerta abierta de cristal mate"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed bulkhead door"
msgstr "puerta de mamparo cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bulkhead door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight and opened "
"using the fly wheel."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente de metal fundido, es estanca y se abre "
"mediante un volante de inercia."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open bulkhead door"
msgstr "puerta de mamparo abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open bulkhead door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight, or would be "
"if it was closed."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta extremadamente resistente de metal fundido, es estanca, o lo sería "
"si estuviera cerrada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brick wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de ladrillos con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brick wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach weapons "
"against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr ""
"Este muro/pared de ladrillos tiene una tronera que te permite disparar y "
"utilizar armas de alcance contra los enemigos del exterior, a la vez que te "
"protege."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "adobe wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de adobe con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "adobe wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This adobe brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr ""
"Este muro/pared de adobe tiene una tronera que te permite disparar y utilizar "
"armas de alcance contra los enemigos del exterior, a la vez que te protege."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "stone wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de piedra con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "stone wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"The small opening on this stone wall allows you to shoot and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the other side, while also providing cover for you."
msgstr ""
"La pequeña abertura de esta pared de piedra te permite disparar y utilizar "
"armas de alcance, a la vez que te garantiza una buena cobertura."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de madera con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This wooden wall has a hole that lets you shoot and use reach weapons against "
"enemies on the other side.  Highly flammable."
msgstr ""
"Esta pared de madera tiene un agujero que te permite disparar y usar armas de "
"alcance contra los enemigos del otro lado. Altamente inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "muro/pare de madera con una amplia apertura"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with a wide opening"
msgid ""
"This wooden wall previously had an embrasure, but the hole has been smashed "
"wide enough that you can climb through it, rendering it kind of pointless.  "
"Highly flammable."
msgstr ""
"Este muro/pared de madera tenía antes una tronera, pero el agujero se ha "
"hecho tan grande que se puede trepar por él, por lo que carece de sentido. "
"Altamente inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "log wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de leños con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This timber wall has a hole that lets you shoot through and use reach weapons "
"against enemies on the other side, while also protecting you.  Quite "
"flammable."
msgstr ""
"Esta pared de leños tiene un agujero que te permite disparar a través de ella "
"y utilizar armas de alcance, a la vez que te protege. Bastante inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "log wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "muro/pared de leño con una amplia apertura"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with a wide opening"
msgid ""
"This timber wall previously had an embrasure, but now the hole is so big that "
"you can climb through it, rendering it kind of pointless.  Quite flammable."
msgstr ""
"Esta pared de leños tenía antes una tronera, pero ahora el agujero es tan "
"grande que se puede atravesar. Bastante inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "palisade wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de empalizada con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"An age-old type of fortification consisting of hefty lumber staked into the "
"ground and cabled together.  This section in particular has an embrasure, so "
"you can shoot or use reach weapons through it while staying safe."
msgstr ""
"Un tipo de fortificación ancestral que consiste en maderos gruesos clavados "
"en el suelo y unidos por cables. Esta sección en particular tiene una "
"tronera, por lo que puedes disparar o usar armas de alcance a través de ella "
"mientras te mantienes a salvo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de hormigón simple con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"A durable and uniform concrete wall.  This one has an embrasure, so you can "
"shoot or use reach weapons through it while staying safe."
msgstr ""
"Una pared de hormigón durable e uniforme. Esta tiene una tronera, que permite "
"disparar o usar armas de alcance a través de ella de forma segura."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "muro/pared de hormigón armado con tronera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"A section of wall with a nice small hole, letting you shoot your machine gun "
"from the safety of your reinforced bunker."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de pared con un bonito y pequeño agujero, que te permite disparar "
"tu ametralladora desde la seguridad de tu búnker reforzado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "palisade gate"
msgstr "verja empalizada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade gate"
msgid ""
"A large doorway consisting of long logs cabled together, best used as part of "
"a longer wall.  Can act as a door if some type of pulley system were rigged "
"on an adjacent palisade wall."
msgstr ""
"Una gran puerta formada por troncos largos unidos por cables, que se utiliza "
"mejor como parte de un muro más largo. Puede actuar como puerta si se monta "
"algún tipo de sistema de poleas en un muro de empalizada adyacente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open palisade gate"
msgstr "abrir la puerta de la empalizada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open palisade gate"
msgid ""
"A hanging palisade gate, hoisted by a nearby pulley system.  You probably "
"shouldn't be underneath when it comes down."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de empalizada colgante, levantada por un sistema de poleas "
"cercano. Probablemente no debería estar debajo cuando baje."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "makeshift portcullis"
msgstr "compuerta improvisada de rejas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "makeshift portcullis"
msgid ""
"An immense gateway cobbled together from various bits of steel and metal "
"scraps."
msgstr ""
"Una inmensa puerta de entrada desguazada junto con varios restos de acero y "
"metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "locked wire gate"
msgstr "verja de alambre cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "locked wire gate"
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence.  This one has a locked padlock on the latch "
"system.  With the right tools, you could cut the metal fence or pick the "
"lock.  You could also examine the fence to see if it looks climbable."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de una valla de tela metalica. Esta tiene un candado cerrado en el "
"sistema de cierre. Con las herramientas adecuadas, podrías cortar la valla "
"metálica o forzar el candado. También podrías examinar la valla para ver si "
"parece escalable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "locked wire gate"
msgid "Gachunk!"
msgstr "¡Gachunk!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the gate opens."
msgstr "¡Con un clic satisfactorio, la cerradura de la puerta se abre!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wire gate"
msgstr "verja de alambre cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wire gate"
msgid "A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""
"Es la puerta de una verja de alambre con un sistema de cerrojos para "
"mantenerla cerrada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wire gate"
msgstr "verja de alambre abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wire gate"
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch "
"is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr ""
"Es la puerta de una verja de alambre con un sistema de cerrojos para "
"mantenerla cerrada. El pestillo no está terminado, así que se abre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "locked retractable gate"
msgstr "verja retráctil cerrada con llave"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "locked retractable gate"
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate.  The latch on this one is locked.  With the "
"right tools, you could cut the metal fence or disable the lock."
msgstr ""
"Una verja retráctil de seguridad. El cerrojo está cerrado. Con las "
"herramientas apropiadas, podrías cortar la valla de metal o inutilizar la "
"cerradura."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed retractable gate"
msgstr "verja retráctil cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed retractable gate"
msgid "A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""
"Una verja retráctil de seguridad con un sistema de cerrojos para mantenerla "
"cerrada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open retractable gate"
msgstr "abrir verja retráctil"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open retractable gate"
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch is "
"undone, so the gate has retracted up."
msgstr ""
"Una verja retráctil de seguridad con un sistema de cerrojos para mantenerla "
"cerrada. El cerrojo está abierto así que la verja se ha retraído."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wooden gate"
msgstr "verja de madera cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden split rail gate"
msgid "A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system."
msgstr "Es una verja de calidad comercial hecha de madera con un sistema de cerrojos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wooden gate"
msgstr "verja de madera abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden privacy gate"
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  The gate is wide "
"open, allowing anything to travel through."
msgstr ""
"Es una verja de calidad comercial hecha de madera con un sistema de cerrojos. "
"Está abierta, lo que permite pasar por ahí."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed screen door"
msgstr "puerta de pantalla cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed screen door"
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh."
msgstr "Una simple puerta de madera con malla de protección."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "rattle!"
msgstr "¡traqueteo!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open screen door"
msgstr "abrir la puerta pantalla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open screen door"
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh.  The door is open."
msgstr "Una simple puerta de madera con malla de protección. La puerta esta abierta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed chickenwire gate"
msgstr "puerta cerrada de alambre de gallinero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed chickenwire gate"
msgid "A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta para una cerca de alambre de gallinero con un simple sistema de "
"cierre para permanecer cerrada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open chickenwire gate"
msgstr "abrir la puerta del gallinero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open chickenwire gate"
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed.  "
"The latch is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta para una cerca de alambre de gallinero con un simple sistema de "
"cierre para permanecer cerrada. El pestillo está desabrochado, así que la "
"puerta se ha abierto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "picket fence"
msgstr "valla de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "picket fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wood, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""
"Es una barrera hecha de madera, nada muy complicado que digamos. Sugiere "
"tibiamente por dónde no habría que pasar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "picket fence"
msgid "You pry out the fence post."
msgstr "Sacas a la fuerza el poste de la valla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "woven wattle fence"
msgstr "valla de palos tejidos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "woven wattle fence"
msgid "A flimsy barrier made of woven sticks.  Suitable for small animals."
msgstr "Una barrera endeble hecha de palos tejidos. Adecuada para pequeños animales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "narrow fence posts"
msgstr "postes de vallas finos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "narrow fence posts"
msgid "A set of narrow wooden posts for a woven wattle fence."
msgstr "Un conjunto de postes de madera finos para usar en una valla de palos tejidos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chain link fence"
msgstr "valla metálica"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chain link fence"
msgid ""
"A tall fence made of woven wires.  There aren't any gaps big enough for you "
"to fit through, so you'll have to cut it, climb it, or find a way around."
msgstr ""
"Una valla alta hecha de alambres tejidos. No hay huecos por los que puedas "
"pasar, así que tendrás que cortarla, trepar por ella o encontrar una forma de "
"evitarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal post"
msgstr "poste de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal post"
msgid "A set of metal posts that can hold more serious fences."
msgstr "Un conjunto de postes metálicos que pueden sostener vallas más serias."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chickenwire fence"
msgstr "la valla de alambre de gallinero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence"
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy fence made of planks and woven wire, suitable for "
"containing small livestock like chickens."
msgstr ""
"Una valla alta y más bien endeble hecha de tablones y alambre trenzado, "
"adecuada para contener animales pequeños como las gallinas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "metal rattling!"
msgstr "¡traqueteo metálico!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "screen mesh wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de malla de pantalla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "screen mesh wall"
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy wall made of planks and screen mesh, suitable for "
"keeping the bugs out."
msgstr ""
"Un muro alto y más bien endeble hecho de tablones y malla metálica, adecuado "
"para mantener alejados a los insectos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chickenwire fence post"
msgstr "poste de la cerca de alambre de gallinero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence post"
#. ~ Description of terrain "fence post"
msgid ""
"A couple of posts that can support a fence.  They look lonely without the "
"fence."
msgstr ""
"Un par de postes que pueden soportar una valla. Parecen solitarios sin la "
"valla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "fence post"
msgstr "poste"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wire fence"
msgstr "alambrado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wire fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wire, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""
"Es una barrera hecha de alambre, nada muy complicado que digamos. Sugiere "
"tibiamente por dónde no habría que pasar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "barbed wire fence"
msgstr "alambrado de púas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "barbed wire fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of sharp barbed wire.  The more persuasive brother of the wire "
"fence."
msgstr ""
"Una barrera hecha de alambre de espino afilado. El hermano más persuasivo de "
"la alambrada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rope fence"
msgstr "valla de soga"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rope fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of rope, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr "Una barrera hecha de soga, nada complicada. Sugiere ligeramente a dónde no ir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "split rail fence"
msgstr "valla de rieles divididos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "split rail fence"
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, suitable for containing "
"livestock like horses, cows and pigs."
msgstr ""
"Una valla bastante robusta hecha de tablones y postes, adecuada para contener "
"el ganado como caballos, vacas y cerdos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "puerta cerrada de madera de rieles divididos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "abrir la puerta de madera del carril dividido"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal fence"
msgstr "valla metálica"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal fence"
msgid "A simple metal fence."
msgstr "Una simple valla de metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed metal gate"
msgstr "puerta metálica cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal gate"
msgid "A closed metal gate."
msgstr "Una puerta de metal cerrada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open metal gate"
msgstr "abrir la puerta de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal gate"
msgid "An open metal gate."
msgstr "Una puerta de metal abierta.Una puerta de metal abierta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden privacy fence"
msgstr "valla de privacidad de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden privacy fence"
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, it is tall enough to "
"prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr ""
"Una valla bastante robusta hecha de tablones y postes, lo suficientemente "
"alta como para impedir que la gente vea tu jardín."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "puerta de privacidad de madera cerrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden privacy gate"
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  It is tall "
"enough to prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de valla comercial de calidad hecha de madera con un sistema de "
"pestillo. Es alta y evita que la gente vea tu patio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "puerta de privacidad de madera abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railing"
msgstr "pasamanos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railing"
msgid "A section of wooden railing."
msgstr "Una sección de barandilla de madera."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "glass railing"
msgstr "barandilla de cristal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "glass railing"
msgid "A section of railing made out of glass."
msgstr "Una sección de la barandilla hecha de cristal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "glass braking!"
msgstr "¡cristal haciendose añicos!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "ker-rash!"
msgstr "¡ker-rash!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal railing"
msgstr "barandilla de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal railing"
msgid "A section of metal railing."
msgstr "Una sección de la barandilla de metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete railing"
msgstr "barandilla de hormigón"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete railing"
msgid "A section of cemented concrete railing."
msgstr "Una sección de barandilla de hormigón cementado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "guard rail"
msgstr "guardarraíl"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "guard rail"
msgid ""
"A section of metal railing, put in place to prevent people from falling or "
"taking the easy way out."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de barandilla metálica, colocada para evitar que la gente se "
"caiga o tome la salida fácil."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "lowered boom barrier"
msgstr "barrera de pluma bajada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "lowered boom barrier"
msgid "A lowered boom barrier."
msgstr "Una barrera de pluma bajada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "cattle feeder"
msgstr "comedero para ganado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "cattle feeder"
msgid ""
"A section of tall steel with a solid base and feed spaces above to allow "
"livestock to reach the contained food."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de acero alta con una base sólida y espacios de alimentación por "
"encima para permitir que el ganado alcance la comida contenida."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "overgrown floor"
msgstr "piso recubierto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "overgrown floor"
msgid ""
"A bare concrete floor, almost completely covered by twitching filaments of "
"gray flesh."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de hormigón desnudo, cubierto casi por completo por filamentos "
"crispados de carne gris."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/json/snippets/snippets.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
#. ~ Snippet in category "<random_sound>"
msgid "SMASH!"
msgstr "¡CLONC!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "overgrown wall"
msgstr "muro recubierto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "overgrown wall"
msgid "A concrete wall overgrown by a grotesque grid of veins and knotted flesh."
msgstr ""
"Una pared de hormigón recubierta por un grotesco entramado de venas y carne "
"anudada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor that can support a roof, could still insulate "
"from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls are "
"broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de hormigón desnudo y frío que puede soportar un techo/tejado , "
"todavía se podría aislar del exterior, pero el colapso del techo/tejado es "
"posible si los muros/paredes de soporte se derrumban."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of yellow paint, could still "
"insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls "
"are broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de hormigón desnudo y frío con una raya de pintura amarilla, todavía "
"podría aislar del exterior, pero el colapso del techo/tejado es posible si "
"los muros/paredes de soporte se derrumban."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of red paint, could still "
"insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls "
"are broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de hormigón desnudo y frío con una raya de pintura roja, todavía "
"podría aislar del exterior, pero el colapso del techo/tejado es posible si "
"los muros/paredes de soporte se derrumban."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with painted stripes of black and yellow, "
"could still insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if "
"supporting walls are broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de hormigón desnudo y frío, con rayas pintadas de negro y amarillo, "
"podría seguir aislando del exterior, pero el derrumbe del techo/tejado es "
"posible si se derriban los muros/paredes de soporte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of yellow paint and a "
"still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above, could still insulate "
"from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls are "
"broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de hormigón desnudo y frío, con una mancha de pintura amarilla y una "
"luz que aún funciona pegada al techo, podría seguir aislando del exterior, "
"pero el colapso del techo/tejado es posible si se rompen los muros/paredes de "
"soporte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete floor, overhead light"
msgstr "suelo de hormigón, luz en la parte superior"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a still-functioning light attached to the "
"ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de hormigón frío y desnudo con una luz funcionando, puesta arriba, "
"en el techo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden floor, overhead light"
msgstr "piso de madera, luz en la parte posterior"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"Interlocking wooden tiles that are more than likely treated against fire, "
"with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Tejas de madera entrelazadas, más que probablemente tratadas contra el fuego, "
"con una luz que sigue funcionando fijada al techo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brick floor"
msgstr "suelo de ladrillo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brick floor"
msgid "A relatively flat area made of tightly placed bricks.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Un área relativamente plana hecha de ladrillos bien colocados. Puede soportar "
"un techo/tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dirt floor, overhead light"
msgstr "suelo de tierra, luz de arriba"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"A floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down, with a "
"still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de tierra finamente mezclada y apisonada, con una luz que aún "
"funciona fijada al techo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal floor, with overhead light"
msgstr "piso de metal, luz en la parte posterior"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor, with overhead light"
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls, with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Suelo metálico a cuadros resistente y de alta calidad para reducir el riesgo "
"de resbalones y caídas, con una luz que sigue funcionando sujeta al techo por "
"encima."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "strong concrete floor, overhead light"
msgstr "suelo fuerte de hormigón, luz en la parte superior"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "strong concrete floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient floor made from carefully placed rebar and poured "
"concrete, with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo extremadamente resistente hecho de barras corrugadas cuidadosamente "
"colocadas y hormigón vertido, con una luz que aún funciona sujeta al techo "
"por encima."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "gray linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgstr "suelo de linóleo gris, luz en la parte superior"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "gray linoleum floor, overhead light"
#. ~ Description of terrain "white linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"Linoleum flooring with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling "
"above."
msgstr "Es un piso de linóleo con una luz todavia funcionando en el techo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "white linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgstr "suelo de linóleo blanco, luz en la parte superior"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "small rebar roof cage"
msgstr "techo/tejado de pequeña jaula de barras corrugadas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "small rebar roof cage"
msgid ""
"A series of structural supports crafted from rebar in order to allow the "
"pouring of concrete for a more stable floor and roof support."
msgstr ""
"Una serie de soportes estructurales elaborados con barras corrugadas para "
"permitir el vertido de hormigón para un suelo y un techo/tejado más estables."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "SCRRRASH!"
msgstr "¡SCRRRASH!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "reinforced concrete floor"
msgstr "suelo de hormigón armado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete floor"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient floor made from carefully placed rebar and poured "
"concrete, capable of providing protection from the elements.  It can support "
"a roof, but that still requires supporting walls, otherwise it may very well "
"cave in."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo extremadamente resistente hecho de barras corrugadas cuidadosamente "
"colocadas y hormigón vertido, capaz de proteger de los elementos. Puede "
"soportar un techo/tejado, pero sigue necesitando muros/paredes de soporte, "
"pues de lo contrario podría derrumbarse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "fractured concrete floor"
msgstr "suelo de hormigón fracturado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "fractured concrete floor"
msgid ""
"Thin strands of violet light shimmer in the air above this concrete floor, "
"like cracks upon a pane of glass.  It can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Finas hebras de luz violeta brillan en el aire sobre este suelo de hormigón, "
"como grietas en un panel de cristal. Puede soportar un techo/tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rebar roof cage"
msgstr "techo/tejado de jaula de barras corrugadas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rebar roof cage"
msgid ""
"A network of architecturally sound rebar in order to support a floor and roof "
"support, looks like it's missing the poured concrete."
msgstr ""
"Una red de barras de refuerzo arquitectónicas para sostener un suelo y un "
"soporte de techo/tejado, parece que le falta el hormigón vertido."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "half-built reinforced concrete floor"
msgstr "suelo de hormigón armado a medio construir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "half-built reinforced concrete floor"
msgid ""
"An unfinished construction of rebar and poured concrete; the floor hasn't "
"been smoothed and the roof support isn't quite filled in yet."
msgstr ""
"Una construcción sin terminar de barras corrugadas y hormigón vertido; el "
"suelo no se ha alisado y el soporte del techo/tejado aún no se ha rellenado "
"del todo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rock floor"
msgstr "suelo de piedra"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rock floor"
msgid ""
"A relatively flat area of rock and stone.  Looks stable enough to be mined "
"with the proper mining gear.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Una zona relativamente plana de roca y piedra. Parece lo bastante estable "
"para ser explotada con el equipo minero adecuado. Puede soportar un "
"techo/tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "marble floor"
msgstr "suelo de mármol"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "marble floor"
msgid ""
"A smooth and flat flooring made of marble tiles.  Beautiful and expensive.  "
"Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo liso y plano de baldosas de mármol. Bonito y caro. Puede soportar un "
"techo/tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "warped stone floor"
msgstr "suelo de piedra deformado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "warped stone floor"
msgid ""
"A rough stone floor.  Its patterns constantly shift as if your mind can't "
"quite understand what it's really seeing.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de piedra tosca. Sus patrones cambian constantemente como si tu "
"mente no pudiera entender lo que realmente está viendo. Puede soportar un "
"techo/tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal floor"
msgstr "suelo de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Suelo metálico ajedrezado de alta calidad y resistencia para reducir el "
"riesgo de resbalones y caídas. Puede soportar un techo/tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
