msgid "resin wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de resina"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin wall"
msgid ""
"A wall made of a glistening, nearly opaque, plastic-like substance.  Deep "
"within, you can barely see a network of pulsating green conduits, snaking "
"through it like blood vessels.  The material is hard, warm to the touch, and "
"slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Una pared hecha de una sustancia brillante, casi opaca, parecida al plástico. "
"En lo profundo del material que lo compone, apenas se puede ver una red de "
"conductos verdes pulsantes, serpenteando como vasos sanguíneos a través de "
"ella. El material es duro, cálido al tacto y ligeramente húmedo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alienciv.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alienciv.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "boom!"
msgstr "¡Boom!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin cage"
msgstr "jaula de resina"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin cage"
msgid ""
"A resin wall that opens into a series of small honeycomb-like hexagons, "
"allowing the passage of air and light.  While still made of the same sturdy "
"material, it is thinner and more delicate in appearance."
msgstr ""
"Esta pared de resina se abre en una serie de pequeños hexágonos en forma de "
"panal, permitiendo el paso del aire y la luz. Aunque sigue siendo del mismo "
"material resistente, es más delgado y más delicado en apariencia."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin floor"
msgstr "suelo de resina"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin floor"
msgid ""
"A nearly opaque, plastic-like floor.  It has a gentle curve from wall to "
"wall, but in the central areas is quite flat.  The material is hard, warm to "
"the touch, and slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Este suelo casi opaco, parecido al plástico, tiene una suave curva de pared a "
"pared, pero en las zonas centrales es bastante plano. El material es duro, "
"cálido al tacto y ligeramente húmedo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin floor"
msgid ""
"A nearly opaque, plastic-like floor that is smooth and flat.  The material is "
"hard, warm to the touch, and slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo casi opaco, parecido al plástico que es liso y plano. El material es "
"duro, cálido al tacto y ligeramente húmedo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de resina"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin roof"
msgid ""
"A wide, domed section of nearly opaque, plastic-like material.  When the "
"light hits it, a network of multicolored conduits like blood vessels can be "
"seen snaking through its glistening interior."
msgstr ""
"Una amplia sección abovedada de material casi opaco, parecido al plástico. "
"Cuando la luz la golpea, se puede ver una red de conductos multicolores como "
"vasos sanguíneos serpenteando por su brillante interior."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed resin portal"
msgstr "portal de resina cerrado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed resin portal"
msgid ""
"A tricuspid hatch of some sort of damp, flexible, resinous material.  This "
"one is closed tightly, but it looks like a firm push would cause it to snap "
"open."
msgstr ""
"Una escotilla tricúspide de algún tipo de material resinoso, flexible y "
"húmedo. Esta está cerrada herméticamente, pero parece que un empujón firme "
"haría que se abriera."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open resin portal"
msgstr "portal abierto de resina"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open resin portal"
msgid ""
"A tricuspid hatch of some sort of damp, flexible, resinous material.  This "
"one is open, the flaps held out by some sort of stringy mucus-like substance."
msgstr ""
"Una escotilla tricúspide de algún tipo de material resinoso, flexible y "
"húmedo. Esta está abierta, las aletas están sostenidas por una especie de "
"sustancia fibrosa parecida al moco."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin-lined hole"
msgstr "agujero forrado de resina"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin-lined hole"
msgid "An open hole in the resin wall, large enough for you to crawl through."
msgstr ""
"Un agujero abierto en la pared de resina, lo suficientemente grande como para "
"que reptes a través de él."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass"
msgstr "cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass"
msgid ""
"An endless expanse of black glass.  It perfectly reflects the darkness around "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Una extensión infinita de cristal negro. Refleja perfectamente la oscuridad a "
"su alrededor"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "perfect basalt wall"
msgstr "muro/pared perfecta de basalto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "perfect basalt wall"
msgid ""
"Hexagonal columns of basalt spring from the dark floor.  Each a perfect copy "
"of the next."
msgstr ""
"Columnas hexagonales de basalto brotan del suelo oscuro. Cada una es una "
"copia perfecta de la siguiente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "gravel"
msgstr "gravilla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "gravel"
msgid ""
"An area of small, uniformly-sized stones.  Often used for roads, as railroad "
"ballast, and in many other applications."
msgstr ""
"Un área de pequeñas piedras uniformes. Suelen utilizarse a menudo para hacer "
"las carreteras, como balastro ferroviario y en muchas otras aplicaciones."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railroad track"
msgstr "vía de ferrocarril"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad track"
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks stand unused in the "
"face of the Cataclysm.  You could probably reclaim lengths of the track "
"itself with a metalcutting tool like a hacksaw."
msgstr ""
"Los trenes solían circular por ellas. Estas vías de ferrocarril están "
"inutilizadas por el Cataclismo. Probablemente puedas recuperar tramos de vía "
"con una herramienta para cortar metal, como una sierra para metales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railroad tie"
msgstr "enlace ferroviario"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad tie"
msgid "A crosstie, used to support train rails."
msgstr "Una traviesa que se utiliza para apoyar los rieles de tren."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad track"
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks stand unused in the "
"face of the Cataclysm.  A crosstie sits underneath, supporting the rails.  "
"You could probably reclaim lengths of the track itself with a metalcutting "
"tool like a hacksaw."
msgstr ""
"Los trenes solían circular por ellas. Estas vías de ferrocarril están "
"inutilizadas por el Cataclismo. Una traviesa se asienta debajo, soportando "
"los raíles. Probablemente puedas recuperar tramos de vía con una herramienta "
"para cortar metal, como una sierra para metales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "buffer stop"
msgstr "parachoques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "buffer stop"
msgid ""
"A tiny blockade on the train tracks, meant to signify the end of a track, or "
"mark a 'no-go' zone for trains."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño bloqueo en las vías del tren, que significa el final de una vía, o "
"una marca de una zona \"prohibida\" para los trenes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railroad crossing signal"
msgstr "señal del cruce de trenes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad crossing signal"
msgid ""
"Traffic lights meant to light and make noise when a train approaches, to "
"prevent people from turning into meaty mush while they cross the tracks.  "
"Won't stop people from turning into meaty mush by other means, though."
msgstr ""
"Los semáforos están pensados para iluminar y hacer ruido cuando se aproxima "
"un tren, para evitar que la gente se convierta en papilla mientras cruza las "
"vías. Sin embargo, no impedirá que la gente se convierta en papilla por otros "
"medios."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plants.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clang."
msgstr "clonc."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "crossbuck"
msgstr "cruce de vias"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "crossbuck"
msgid ""
"A traffic sign intended to indicate a level railway crossing.  If the trains "
"were still running."
msgstr ""
"Una señal de tráfico destinada a indicar un cruce de ferrocarril a nivel. Si "
"los trenes aún estuvieran en marcha."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "small railroad track"
msgid_plural "small railroad tracks"
msgstr[0] "pequeña vía de ferrocarril"
msgstr[1] "pequeñas vías de ferrocarril"
msgstr[2] "pequeñas vías de ferrocarril"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "small railroad track"
msgid ""
"Like a railroad track, only smaller.  You could probably run a small vehicle "
"on this."
msgstr ""
"Como una vía férrea, sólo que más pequeña. Probablemente podrías hacer "
"funcionar un pequeño vehículo en esto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "recessed railroad track"
msgstr "vía de ferrocarril empotrada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "recessed railroad track"
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks sit flush with the "
"road.  You could probably reclaim lengths of the track itself with a "
"metalcutting tool like a hacksaw."
msgstr ""
"Los trenes solían circular por ellas. Estas vías están al ras de la "
"carretera. Probablemente podrías recuperar tramos de vía con una herramienta "
"para cortar metal, como una sierra para metales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "sandbox"
msgstr "arenero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sandbox"
msgid ""
"Children used to play in this sandbox.  The population of lice probably "
"diminished considerably now that they no longer do."
msgstr ""
"Los niños solían jugar en este arenero. La población de piojos probablemente "
"disminuyó considerablemente ahora que ya no lo hacen."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "slide"
msgstr "tobogán"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "slide"
msgid "A children's slide.  It's too small for you to slide on comfortably."
msgstr "Un tobogán para niños. Demasiado pequeño para deslizarte cómodamente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "monkey bars"
msgstr "pasamanos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "monkey bars"
msgid ""
"A set of monkey bars to be used by children to train their arm strength, or, "
"in happier days, to just have fun."
msgstr ""
"Un juego de barras para que los niños entrenen la fuerza de sus brazos o, en "
"tiempos más felices, simplemente se diviertan."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "backboard"
msgstr "tablero"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "backboard"
msgid "A basketball backboard."
msgstr "Un tablero de baloncesto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "backboard"
msgid "A metal backboard."
msgstr "Una tabla de metal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rain gutter"
msgstr "canalón de lluvia"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rain gutter"
msgid "Channels water from the roof towards the ground, it looks flimsy."
msgstr "Canaliza el agua desde el techo/tejado hacia el suelo, se ve endeble."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "gutter drop"
msgstr "caída de la canaleta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "gutter drop"
msgid ""
"A spot in the gutter where the water flows into a downspout.  It looks "
"flimsy.  You may be able to climb down here."
msgstr ""
"Un punto en el canalón donde el agua desemboca en un bajante. Parece frágil. "
"Puede que puedas bajar por aquí."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "downspout"
msgstr "bajante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "downspout"
msgid ""
"A length of gutter running from the roof to the ground, you could place a "
"container underneath it to collect rainwater.  It looks flimsy.  You may be "
"able to climb up here."
msgstr ""
"Un tramo de canalón que va desde el tejado hasta el suelo, se podría colocar "
"un recipiente debajo para recoger el agua de lluvia. Parece endeble. Es "
"posible que puedas trepar por aquí."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "flat roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado plano"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
msgid "A flat, gray section of rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección plana y gris del tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tar paper flat roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado plano de papel alfaltado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tar paper flat roof"
msgid "A flat, gray section of rooftop covered with tar paper."
msgstr "Una sección plana y gris de techo/tejado cubierto con papel asfaltado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shingle flat roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado plano de tejas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shingle flat roof"
msgid "A flat section of rooftop covered with shingles."
msgstr "Una sección plana del techo/tejado cubierto de tejas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "thatched roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de paja"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "thatched roof"
msgid "A section of roof made out of straw."
msgstr "Una sección del techo/tejado hecho de paja."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal flat roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado plano de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal flat roof"
msgid "A section of flat, sheet metal rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección del techo/tejado plano, de chapas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tile flat roof"
msgstr "techo plano de baldosas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tile flat roof"
msgid "A section of flat, tiled rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección del techo/tejado plano de baldosas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "skylight"
msgstr "Tragaluz"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "skylight"
msgid "A giant sheet of glass inserted into the roof to let light pass through."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina gigante de cristal insertada en el techo/tejado que deja pasar la "
"luz."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rock roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de roca"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rock roof"
msgid "A section of flat natural rock."
msgstr "Una sección de roca natural plana."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "warped roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado deformado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "warped roof"
msgid ""
"A section of flat, stone-like rooftop.  It is patterned with grooves and "
"lines that constantly shift."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de techo@tejado de piedra plana. Su patrón de ranuras y líneas "
"cambia constantemente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
msgid "A flat surface made of ambiguous pulpy matter, covered in sticky wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Una superficie plana hecha de materia pulposa imprecisa, cubierta de saliva "
"pegajosa de avispa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
msgid ""
"A flat surface made of hardened, ambiguous pulpy matter, covered in sticky "
"wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Una superficie plana hecha de materia pulposa endurecida e imprecisa, "
"cubierta de saliva pegajosa de avispa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de hormigón"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete roof"
msgid "A flat section of concrete rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección plana de techo/tejado de hormigón."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "wooden roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden roof"
msgid "A flat section of wooden rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección plana de techo/tejado de madera."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "treated wooden roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de madera tratada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "treated wooden roof"
msgid "A flat section of flame-resistant wooden rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección plana de techo/tejado de madera resistente al fuego."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal roof"
msgid "A high-quality and sturdy section of metallic rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección de techo/tejado metálico resistente de alta calidad."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "red metal roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de metal rojo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "red metal roof"
msgid ""
"A sturdy section of metallic rooftop, painted red for visibility and weather "
"resistance."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta sección de techo/tejado metálico, pintado de rojo para mayor "
"visibilidad y resistencia a la intemperie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "sod roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de césped"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sod roof"
msgid "A section of rooftop made out of sod."
msgstr "Una sección de techo/tejado hecho de césped."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brick roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de ladrillos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brick roof"
msgid "A section of brick rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección del techo/tejado hecho de ladrillos."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "canvas roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de lona"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "canvas roof"
msgid "A section of canvas rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección del techo/tejado de lona."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "treetop"
msgstr "copa de árbol"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "treetop"
msgid "The upper branches of a tree.  There's just enough room to perch here."
msgstr "Las ramas superiores de un árbol. Con suficiente espacio para subirse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dead treetop"
msgstr "copa de árbol muerto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dead treetop"
msgid ""
"The bare upper branches of a dead tree.  There's just enough room to perch "
"here."
msgstr ""
"Las desnudas ramas superiores de un árbol muerto. Con suficiente espacio para "
"subirse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "giant fern top"
msgstr "copa de helecho gigante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "giant fern top"
msgid ""
"The top of some unearthly gigantic fern.  There is enough room to perch up "
"here, but only just."
msgstr ""
"La copa de un helecho sobrenatural gigantesco. Con suficiente espacio para "
"subirse, pero por poco."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shallow pit"
msgstr "pozo poco profundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow pit"
msgid ""
"A pit that could be dug even deeper or filled up.  Also useful as a starting "
"foundation for some constructions."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo que podría ser cavado aún más profundo o llenado. También es útil "
"como base de partida para algunas construcciones."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "pit"
msgid ""
"A steep hole that could seriously injure something if it fell in, potentially "
"fatal if it was filled with sharp and dangerous things.  Deep enough for more "
"advanced construction projects, and possibly to reach groundwater if "
"constructed properly."
msgstr ""
"Un agujero empinado que podría herir seriamente algo si se cae, "
"potencialmente mortal si se llena con cosas afiladas y peligrosas. "
"Suficientemente profundo para proyectos de construcción más avanzados, y "
"posiblemente para llegar al agua subterránea si se construye adecuadamente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "corpse filled pit"
msgstr "pozo lleno de cadáveres"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "corpse filled pit"
msgid ""
"A giant trench full of corpses, maybe even a mass graveyard.  The bodies "
"could be dug out, but nothing in here looks remotely usable."
msgstr ""
"Una zanja gigante llena de cadáveres, tal vez alguna especie de cementerio. "
"Los cuerpos podrían ser sacados, pero ninguno parece ni remotamente útil para "
"algo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "covered pit"
msgstr "pozo cubierto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "covered pit"
msgid ""
"A deep pit with a plank placed across it, looks sturdy enough to cross "
"safely.  The plank could be removed to make it dangerous again."
msgstr ""
"Un foso profundo con un tablón colocado sobre él, parece lo suficientemente "
"resistente como para cruzarlo con seguridad. El tablón podría retirarse para "
"que volviera a ser peligroso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "spiked pit"
msgid "A narrow trench full of very pointy things that would easily puncture a body."
msgstr ""
"Es una zanja angosta llena de cosas muy puntiagudas que fácilmente podrían "
"herir el cuerpo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "covered spiked pit"
msgstr "pozo con púas cubierto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "covered spiked pit"
msgid ""
"Menacing with sharp spears along the bottom, this pit has a plank across it "
"to allow someone or something to cross safely.  The plank could be removed to "
"make it dangerous again."
msgstr ""
"Este foso, amenazador por sus afiladas lanzas en el fondo, está atravesado "
"por un tablón para que alguien o algo pueda cruzarlo con seguridad. El tablón "
"puede retirarse para que vuelva a ser peligroso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "glass pit"
msgid ""
"Looks like a ton of broken glass was dumped into this pit.  Might not fatal "
"to fall in, but it wouldn't be pleasant to try to crawl out."
msgstr ""
"Parece que una tonelada de cristales rotos fueron arrojados a este pozo. "
"Puede que no sea fatal caer dentro, pero no sería agradable intentar salir "
"reptando."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "covered glass pit"
msgstr "pozo con cristales cubierto"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "covered glass pit"
msgid ""
"A plank has been placed carefully to allow traversal over this ditch full of "
"large glass shards.  The plank could be removed to make it dangerous again."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera se puso cuidadosamente sobre este pozo lleno de grandes "
"trozos de cristal. El tablón puede ser sacado para que no pueda ser cruzado "
"con seguridad."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dead drop pit"
msgstr "foso con caída "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dead drop pit"
msgid ""
"A seemingly innocuous shallow pit.  Careful inspection reveals a black "
"canister half-buried in the exposed soil."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo aparentemente inofensivo y poco profundo. Una inspección cuidadosa "
"revela un recipiente negro semienterrado en el suelo expuesto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_BEM_human_sample_deliver" in terrain
#. "dead drop pit"'s examine action
msgid "You prepare the drop as instructed"
msgstr "Preparas el gotero según las instrucciones"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_BEM_human_sample_deliver" in
#. terrain "dead drop pit"'s examine action
msgid "You don't have anything to deliver."
msgstr "No tienes nada que entregar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "small den"
msgstr "cubil pequeño"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "small den"
msgid "A small den that burrowing animals such as groundhogs or hares call home."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña madriguera en la que viven animales de madriguera como las "
"marmotas o las liebres."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "large den"
msgstr "cubil grande"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "large den"
msgid "A large den that burrowing animals such as bears and foxes call home."
msgstr ""
"Una gran madriguera a la que llaman hogar animales de madriguera como osos y "
"zorros."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#: data/json/monsters/slimes.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "slime"
msgid_plural "slimes"
msgstr[0] "légamo"
msgstr[1] "légamos"
msgstr[2] "légamos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "slime"
msgid ""
"A disgusting, slippery mess.  Could be used to stash things, because who'd "
"want to touch it?"
msgstr ""
"Un desastre asqueroso y resbaladizo. Podría usarse para esconder cosas, "
"porque ¿quién querría tocarlo?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "solid bark wall"
msgstr "muro sólida de corteza"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "solid bark wall"
msgid ""
"A solid wall of bark, enclosing the trunk of a massive tree.  It will "
"probably burn quite well."
msgstr ""
"Un sólido muro de corteza, que encierra el tronco de un enorme árbol. "
"Probablemente arderá bastante bien."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chipped bark wall"
msgstr "muro astillado de corteza"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chipped bark wall"
msgid ""
"A solid wall of bark enclosing the trunk of a massive tree.  Some of it has "
"been broken away."
msgstr ""
"Un sólid muro de corteza que encierra el tronco de un enorme árbol. Parte de "
"ella se ha roto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "broken bark wall"
msgstr "muro roto de corteza"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "broken bark wall"
msgid ""
"A formerly solid wall of bark, now almost completely destroyed and waiting to "
"collapse."
msgstr ""
"Un muro de corteza antes sólido, ahora casi completamente destruido y a punto "
"de derrumbarse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "solid wood wall"
msgstr "muro sólido de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "solid wood wall"
msgid "A solid wall of naturally grown wood.  Likely very flammable."
msgstr "Un muro sólido de madera cultivada naturalmente. Probablemente muy inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bark"
msgstr "corteza"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bark"
msgid "A solid piece of bark covers the floor here."
msgstr "Una pieza sólida de corteza cubre el suelo aquí."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "branches with leaves"
msgstr "ramas con hojas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "branches with leaves"
msgid "Thin branches emerge here, covered with thick, large leaves."
msgstr "De aquí surgen ramas finas, cubiertas de hojas gruesas y grandes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "root floor"
msgstr "suelo de raíces"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "root floor"
msgid "A dirt floor covered with roots."
msgstr "Un suelo de tierra cubierto de raíces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "downward root slope"
msgstr "pendiente de raíces descendente"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "downward root slope"
msgid "A downward-facing slope of root-covered dirt."
msgstr "Una pendiente descendente de tierra cubierta de raíces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "upward root slope"
msgstr "pendiente de raíces ascendente"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "upward root slope"
msgid "An upward-facing slope of root-covered dirt."
msgstr "Una pendiente ascendente de tierra cubierta de raíces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed bramble roots"
msgstr "raíces espinosas cerradas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bramble roots"
msgid "A bramble of roots covering a large hole.  They could easily be pulled apart."
msgstr "Una zarza de raíces cubriendo un gran agujero. Se podrían separar fácilmente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open bramble roots"
msgstr "raíces espinosas abiertas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open bramble roots"
msgid "A bramble of roots, pulled apart to reveal a hole."
msgstr "Una zarza de raíces, separada para revelar un agujero."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wall"
msgstr "pared"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wall"
msgid ""
"A standard wall consisting of a wooden support structure filled with "
"insulation and drywalled.  Painted a neutral off-white or cream color, it "
"could use some more vibrant paint.  Looks flammable."
msgstr ""
"La típica pared con estructura de soporte de madera rellena de aislamiento y "
"con muros de yeso. El trabajo de pintura es demasiado común y de color blanco "
"roto neutro o crema, aunque podría usar una pintura más vibrante. Parece "
"inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "half-built wall"
msgstr "muro/pared a medio construir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "half-built wall"
msgid ""
"An incomplete wall of refined wood, dotted with carefully placed nails to "
"provide proper support.  It requires some more planks and nails before it'd "
"be considered a suitable wall."
msgstr ""
"Un muro/pared incompleto de madera refinada, salpicado de clavos "
"cuidadosamente colocados para proporcionar un soporte adecuado. Necesita "
"algunos tablones y clavos más para considerarse un muro/pared adecuado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "pony wall"
msgstr "muro de poni"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "pony wall"
msgid ""
"A short divider wall consisting of a wooden support structure with drywall.  "
"Painted an all-too-common and neutral off-white or cream color.  Looks "
"flammable."
msgstr ""
"Una corta pared divisoria con una estructura de soporte de madera con paneles "
"de yeso. El trabajo de pintura es demasiado común y de color blanco neutro o "
"crema. Parece como si el material fuera inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de madera"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall"
msgid ""
"A finished wall of planks and support beams, capable of supporting an upper "
"level or roof.  Highly flammable."
msgstr ""
"Una pared terminada de tablones y vigas de soporte, capaz de soportar un "
"nivel superior o techo/tejado. Altamente inflamable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
msgid ""
"An aesthetically pleasing design with simple lines, this type of concrete was "
"used with a weaker chemical mixture in order to have faster setting times.  "
"Not ideal for multi-story buildings, but still capable of supporting a roof."
msgstr ""
"Un diseño estético con líneas simples, este tipo de hormigón se utilizó con "
"una mezcla química más débil para tener tiempos de fraguado más rápidos. No "
"es ideal para edificios de varios pisos, pero aún así es capaz de soportar un "
"techo/tejado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "simple concrete wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de hormigón común"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "simple concrete wall"
msgid ""
"A durable and uniform concrete wall, quite drab without decoration.  More "
"than capable of supporting a roof, as well as keeping out most anything, save "
"for vehicles."
msgstr ""
"Un muro/pared de hormigón duradero y uniforme, bastante monótono sin "
"decoración. Más que capaz de soportar un techo/tejado, así como de mantener "
"fuera casi todo, excepto los vehículos."

