msgid "The upper end of a railroad ramp leading up."
msgstr "El extremo superior de una rampa de vias de tren que va hacia arriba."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railroad ramp up (low end)"
msgstr "rampa de vias de tren hacia arriba (extremo inferior)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad ramp up (low end)"
msgid "The lower end of a railroad ramp leading up."
msgstr "El extremo inferior de una rampa de vias de tren que va hacia arriba."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete ramp down (high end)"
msgstr "rampa de hormigón hacia abajo (extremo superior)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete ramp down (high end)"
msgid "The upper end of a concrete ramp leading down."
msgstr "El extremo superior de una rampa de hormigón que baja."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete ramp down (low end)"
msgstr "rampa de hormigón hacia abajo (extremo inferior)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete ramp down (low end)"
msgid "The lower end of a concrete ramp leading down."
msgstr "El extremo inferior de una rampa de hormigón que baja."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete ramp up (high end)"
msgstr "rampa de hormigón hacia arriba (extremo superior)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete ramp up (high end)"
msgid "The upper end of a concrete ramp leading up."
msgstr "El extremo superior de una rampa de hormigón que sube"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete ramp up (low end)"
msgstr "rampa de hormigón hacia arriba (extremo inferior)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-zlevel-transitions.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete ramp up (low end)"
msgid "The lower end of a concrete ramp leading up."
msgstr "El extremo inferior de una rampa de hormigón que sube"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bone floor"
msgstr "suelo de hueso"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bone floor"
msgid ""
"An impossibly hard, impregnable bone structure covers the internals of the "
"beast."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura ósea imposiblemente dura e inexpugnable cubre las entrañas de "
"la bestia."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bone wall"
msgstr "pared de hueso"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bone wall"
msgid ""
"An amazingly durable, impregnable wall of bone stands before you, forming the "
"outer shell of the eldritch monster."
msgstr ""
"Un muro de hueso increíblemente duradero e inexpugnable se alza ante ti, "
"formando la coraza exterior del monstruo eldritch."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "monster teeth"
msgid_plural "monster teeth"
msgstr[0] "diente de monstruo"
msgstr[1] "dientes de monstruo"
msgstr[2] "dientes de monstruo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "monster teeth"
msgid ""
"A fractal array of uncountable, bristling teeth that seem impossibly sharp, "
"even at a conceptual level.  An iridescent haze surrounds it, as if light "
"itself cannot help but be separated in their presence.  You surmise you could "
"extract some for your own use, if you had an appropriate tool to remove them "
"from the wall they're imbedded in."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto fractal de incontables dientes erizados que parecen "
"imposiblemente afilados, incluso a nivel conceptual. Una neblina iridiscente "
"los rodea, como si la luz misma no pudiera evitar separarse en su presencia. "
"Supones que podrías extraer algunos para tu propio uso, si tuvieras una "
"herramienta adecuada para sacarlos de la muro/pared en la que están "
"incrustados."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "flesh floor"
msgstr "suelo de carne"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh floor"
msgid ""
"Walking over the innards of this monstrous beast, you can still feel movement "
"underneath your feet."
msgstr ""
"Caminando sobre las entrañas de esta bestia monstruosa, aún puedes sentir "
"movimiento bajo tus pies."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#: data/json/monsters/zed_fusion.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "flesh wall"
msgid_plural "flesh walls"
msgstr[0] "muro de carne"
msgstr[1] "muros de carne"
msgstr[2] "muros de carne"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh wall"
msgid "Warm to the touch, the tainted flesh of this monstrous being still twitches."
msgstr "Cálida al tacto, la carne mancillada de este ser monstruoso aún se estremece."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh wall"
msgid ""
"A thick wall of fleshy cartilage.  With the proper tools, you could smash "
"right through it."
msgstr ""
"Una gruesa pared de cartílago carnoso. Con las herramientas adecuadas, "
"podrías atravesarla."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh wall"
msgid ""
"This section of flesh seems hollowed out.  You can see silky, translucent "
"larvae wriggling inside, consuming flesh at a prodigious pace."
msgstr ""
"Esta sección de carne parece ahuecada. Se pueden ver larvas sedosas y "
"translúcidas retorciéndose en su interior, consumiendo carne a un ritmo "
"prodigioso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "monster hemolymph"
msgstr "hemolinfa monstruosa"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "monster hemolymph"
msgid ""
"A shallow stream of glowing yellow ichor streaks through the beast.  Peering "
"into it, you can see dark shadows moving under the surface."
msgstr ""
"Una corriente poco profunda de ichor amarillo brillante atraviesa a la "
"bestia. Al mirar dentro, se ven sombras oscuras moviéndose bajo la superficie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "cartilage"
msgstr "cartílago"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "cartilage"
msgid "A thin, transparent cartilage webbing."
msgstr "Una membrana cartilaginosa fina y transparente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "Riiiiip!"
msgstr "¡Riiiiip!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "nether brain"
msgstr "cerebro del inframundo"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "nether brain"
msgid "An oozing pile of wrinkled, decomposing flesh."
msgstr "Un montón rezumante de carne arrugada y en descomposición."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass ground"
msgstr "suelo de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass ground"
msgid ""
"A patch of black glass, roughly textured and entirely solid.  The little of "
"it you can see through reveals larger, darker pebbles underneath."
msgstr ""
"Un trozo de cristal negro, de textura rugosa y totalmente sólido. Lo poco que "
"se puede ver a través de él revela guijarros más grandes y oscuros debajo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black grass"
msgstr "hierba negra"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black grass"
msgid "A patch of thick, luxuriant midnight black grass.  Every blade is a razor."
msgstr ""
"Una mancha de hierba espesa, exuberante y negra como la medianoche. Cada hoja "
"es una navaja."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass floor"
msgstr "suelo de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass floor"
msgid ""
"A floor of black glass, textured with the knots and whorls of old and "
"well-loved wood boards."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo de cristal negro, texturizado con los nudos y espirales de tablas de "
"madera viejas y bien cuidadas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass floor"
msgid "A black glass floor formed from tessellated octagonal tiles."
msgstr "Un suelo de cristal negro formado por baldosas octogonales teseladas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass wall"
msgstr "pared de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass wall"
msgid ""
"A heavy wall of black glass, textured with the knots and whorls of old and "
"well-loved wood boards."
msgstr ""
"Un muro/pared pesada de cristal negro, texturizada con los nudos y espirales "
"de tablas de madera viejas y bien cuidadas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "edge of a vastness"
msgstr "borde a la inmensidad"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "edge of a vastness"
msgid ""
"Beyond this point stretches an endless expanse of smooth black.  You are so "
"small, in comparison.  And why would you even want to leave?"
msgstr ""
"Más allá de este punto se extiende una interminable extensión de negro liso. "
"Eres tan pequeño, en comparación. ¿Y por qué querrías irte?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass door"
msgstr "puerta de cristal negra"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass door"
msgid ""
"A door made from black glass, fused shut on useless hinges.  If you look very "
"closely, you can see the tiny ridges of fingerprints on the knob."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de cristal negro, fundida sobre bisagras inútiles. Si te fijas "
"bien, puedes ver las diminutas marcas de huellas dactilares en el pomo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black fiberglass fence"
msgstr "valla negra de fibra de vidrio"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black fiberglass fence"
msgid ""
"A network of delicate glass threads strung between thicker posts.  The wind "
"blowing across them produces a faint, eerie whine."
msgstr ""
"Una red de delicados hilos de cristal ensartados entre postes más gruesos. El "
"viento que sopla a través de ellos produce un débil y espeluznante gemido."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "sharp tinkling!"
msgstr "¡Tintineo agudo!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "resonant tinkling!"
msgstr "¡Tintineo resonante!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "spined glasswire fence"
msgstr "valla de cristal espinada"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "spined glasswire fence"
msgid ""
"Rolling coils of thin black glass covered in delicate barbs.  It's "
"reminiscent of snowflakes."
msgstr ""
"Rollos de fino cristal negro cubiertos de delicadas púas. Recuerda a los "
"copos de nieve."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "translucent black glass wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de cristal negro translúcido"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "translucent black glass wall"
msgid ""
"An area of black glass translucent enough to allow murky shapes to be seen "
"through it."
msgstr ""
"Una superficie de cristal negro lo suficientemente translúcida como para "
"permitir ver a través de ella formas turbias."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass dust"
msgstr "polvo de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass dust"
msgid ""
"A pile of glass ground so finely that the slightest breeze bears it aloft "
"into mesmerizing clouds."
msgstr ""
"Un montón de cristal molido tan finamente que la más leve brisa lo eleva en "
"nubes hipnotizadoras."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass curtains"
msgstr "cortinas de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass curtains"
msgid ""
"The shape of a window and trim, covered in drapings of black glass.  "
"Presumably it was once transparent; now the opaque curtains are solid and "
"immobile."
msgstr ""
"La forma de una ventana y su marco, cubiertos con cortinas de cristal negro. "
"Es de suponer que una vez fue transparente; ahora las cortinas opacas son "
"sólidas e inmóviles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "jagged glass aperture"
msgstr "apertura dentada de cristal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "jagged glass aperture"
msgid ""
"A ragged hole smashed through a thin portion of black glass.  The biggest "
"shards could probably be snapped off to make it safer to pass through."
msgstr ""
"Un agujero irregular atravesó una fina porción de cristal negro. Los "
"fragmentos más grandes podrían romperse para hacer más seguro el paso."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass pole"
msgstr "poste de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass pole"
msgid ""
"A spar of glass fused into the ground, still bearing the jagged edges of the "
"structure it once supported."
msgstr ""
"Una viga de cristal se fundió en el suelo, aún con los bordes dentados de la "
"estructura que una vez soportó."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass well"
msgstr "pozo de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass well"
msgid ""
"This was formerly a well shaft and pump mechanism; it is now so obscured with "
"bubbles of black glass that only a faint outline of the original shape can be "
"seen."
msgstr ""
"Antiguamente era el pozo y el mecanismo de bombeo; ahora está tan oculto por "
"las burbujas de vidrio negro que sólo puede verse un tenue contorno de la "
"forma original."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass bars"
msgstr "barras de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass bars"
msgid "Thick spars of black glass extending from floor to ceiling."
msgstr "Gruesas palos de cristal negro que se extienden desde el suelo hasta el techo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "a tremendous shattering!"
msgstr "¡un tremendo estruendo!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clonk!"
msgstr "¡clonk!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass column"
msgstr "columna de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass column"
msgid "A tremendous spar of black glass."
msgstr "Una tremenda columna de cristal negro."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shallow black pool"
msgstr "piscina negra poco profunda"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow black pool"
msgid ""
"At first glance, this looks like a smooth pool of black water.  Closer "
"examination reveals it to be fine glass dust."
msgstr ""
"A primera vista, parece un charco liso de agua negra. Un examen más detenido "
"revela que se trata de fino polvo de vidrio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tree of glass apples"
msgstr "árbol de manzanas de cristal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tree of glass apples"
msgid ""
"A flourishing tree, its branches heavy with apples.  Every black leaf is "
"razor-edged; every heavy fruit turns to dust at the touch."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol floreciente, sus ramas cargadas de manzanas. Cada hoja negra tiene "
"el filo de una navaja; cada fruto pesado se convierte en polvo al tocarlo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass tree"
msgstr "árbol de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass tree"
msgid "The glass skeleton of a once-leafy tree.  It looks more like coral, now."
msgstr ""
"El esqueleto de cristal de un árbol que una vez tuvo hojas. Ahora se parece "
"más al coral."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass bush"
msgstr "arbusto de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass bush"
msgid ""
"What was once a small shrub has grown wild, each of its branches twisting "
"into delicate glass spirals."
msgstr ""
"Lo que antes era un pequeño arbusto ha crecido de forma salvaje, y cada una "
"de sus ramas se retuerce en delicadas espirales de cristal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass stairs"
msgstr "escaleras de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass stairs"
msgid ""
"A set of smooth glass stairs, with countless years of bare footprints worn "
"into them."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de escaleras de cristal liso, con innumerables años de huellas "
"desgastadas en ellas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass downspout"
msgstr "bajante de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass downspout"
msgid ""
"A drainpipe of black glass.  There are holes down its length, from which "
"occasionally trickle little dustings of black sand."
msgstr ""
"Un desagüe de vidrio negro. Hay agujeros a lo largo de su longitud, de los "
"que de vez en cuando gotean pequeños polvillos de arena negra."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass roof"
msgid ""
"A roof of black glass tiles.  They are very smooth, and some break away at "
"the touch."
msgstr ""
"Un techo/tejado de baldosas de vidrio negro. Son muy lisas, y algunas se "
"rompen al tacto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass drain"
msgstr "desague de cristal negro"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass drain"
msgid "A funnel of smooth glass, filled almost to the brim with sand."
msgstr "Un embudo de cristal liso, lleno casi hasta el borde de arena."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow black pool"
msgid ""
"At first glance, this looks like a rippling pool of black water.  Closer "
"examination reveals it to be fine glass dust, blown in slow waves by the "
"breeze."
msgstr ""
"A primera vista, parece un charco ondulante de agua negra. Un examen más "
"detenido revela que se trata de fino polvo de vidrio, soplado en lentas ondas "
"por la brisa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "soft glass soil"
msgstr "tierra de cristal suave"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/json/npcs/EOC_talkers/vitrified_farm.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "soft glass soil"
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This little mound of soil is unlike the jagged dirt around it.  It is smooth, "
"welcoming, and pleasant to the touch."
msgstr ""
"Este pequeño montículo de tierra no se parece a la tierra irregular que lo "
"rodea. Es suave, acogedora y agradable al tacto."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_any.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "swirling mist"
msgstr "remolinos de niebla"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_any.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "swirling mist"
msgid ""
"A swirling, exotic pattern of shapes, floating in an ill-defined darkness.  "
"Staring at it too long hurts your brain."
msgstr ""
"Un remolino de formas exóticas que flota en una oscuridad mal definida. "
"Mirarlo demasiado tiempo daña el cerebro."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_any.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sparkling chasm"
msgid ""
"At a glance this just looks like darkness.  Then, gazing deeper, you think it "
"might be full of stars.  Still deeper, perhaps those stars are eyes?"
msgstr ""
"A primera vista parece oscuridad. Luego, mirando más profundamente, piensas "
"que podría estar lleno de estrellas. Aún más profundo, ¿quizás esas estrellas "
"sean ojos?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk0"
msgstr "Obelico 0"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk0"
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk1"
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk2"
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk3"
msgid "Obelisk"
msgstr "Obelisco"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_0_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk0"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Thief's Pass.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr "Ya conoces la clave del Ladrón. El obelisco está inerte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_0_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk0"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a tall, olive green, metallic pillar covered in swirling patterns.  "
"As you focus on it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  You have "
"learned the Thief's Passcode."
msgstr ""
"Ves un pilar alto, verde oliva, metálico y cubierto de remolinos. Cuando te "
"concentras en él, sientes un ardor en la piel. Has aprendido la clave del "
"Ladrón."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_0_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk0"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a tall, olive green, metallic pillar covered in swirling patterns.  "
"As you focus on it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  "
"<ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of your own face, smirking; it's the "
"'Thief's Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""
"Ves un pilar alto, verde oliva, metálico y cubierto de remolinos. Cuando te "
"concentras en él, sientes un ardor en la piel.<ls_obelisk_firsttime1>un "
"tatuaje de tu propia cara, sonriendo; es la 'Clave del "
"Ladrón'.<ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk1"
msgstr "Obelisco 1"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_1_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk1"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Circle of Wings Passcode.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr "Ya conoces la clave del Círculo de las Alas. El obelisco está inerte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_1_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk1"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a squat, angry-looking, indigo metallic pillar covered carved in "
"relief with the image of flying birds.  As you focus on it, you feel a "
"burning sensation on your skin.  You have learned the Circle of Wings "
"Passcode."
msgstr ""
"Ves un pilar metálico de color índigo, achaparrado y de aspecto amenazador, "
"cubierto con relieves que representan pájaros volando. Al concentrarte en él, "
"sientes una sensación de ardor en la piel. Has aprendido la contraseña del "
"Círculo de las Alas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_1_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk1"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a squat, angry-looking, indigo metallic pillar covered carved in "
"relief with the image of flying birds.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you "
"feel a burning sensation on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of "
"wings in a circle, running into themselves like an ouroboros; it's the "
"'Circle of Wings Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""
"Ves un pilar metálico de color índigo, achaparrado y de aspecto amenazador, "
"cubierto con relieves que representan pájaros volando. Mientras tus ojos se "
"sienten atraídos por él, sientes una sensación de ardor en la piel. "
"<ls_obelisk_firsttime1>Un tatuaje de alas en círculo, entrelazadas como un "
"ouroboros; es lo 'Contraseña del Círculo de Alas'."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk2"
msgstr "Obelisco 2"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_2_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk2"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Hard Nails Passcode.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr "Ya conoces la contraseña de Uñas Duras. El obelisco está inerte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_2_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk2"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a thick, powerful, gold-burnished pillar covered in what look like "
"deep fingernail scratches.  As you focus on it, you feel a burning sensation "
"on your skin.  You have learned the Hard Nails Passcode."
msgstr ""
"Ves un pilar grueso, poderoso y bruñido en oro, cubierto de lo que parecen "
"profundos arañazos de uñas. Al concentrarte en él, sientes una sensación de "
"ardor en la piel. Has aprendido la contraseña 'Uñas duras'."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_2_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk2"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a thick, powerful, gold-burnished pillar covered in what look like "
"deep fingernail scratches.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning "
"sensation on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of a hand clawing "
"down a sheet of metal; it's the 'Hard Nails Passcode'.  "
"<ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""
"Ves un pilar grueso, poderoso y bruñido en oro cubierto de lo que parecen "
"profundos arañazos de uñas. A medida que tus ojos se sienten atraídos por él, "
"sientes una sensación de ardor en la piel. <ls_obelisk_firsttime1>Un tatuaje "
"de una mano arañando una lámina de metal; es la 'Contraseña de las Uñas "
"Duras'<ls_obelisk_firsttime2>."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk3"
msgstr "Obelisco 3"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_3_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk3"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Laughing Man Passcode.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr "Ya conoces la contraseña del Hombre Riendo. El obelisco está inerte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_3_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk3"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a beautiful pillar the color of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in "
"its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation "
"on your skin.  You have learned the Laughing Man Passcode."
msgstr ""
"Ves una hermosa columna del color de las rosas o de la sangre, absolutamente "
"perfecta en sus proporciones. A medida que tus ojos se sienten atraídos por "
"ella, sientes una sensación de ardor en la piel. Has aprendido la contraseña "
"del Hombre Riendo."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_3_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk3"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a beautiful pillar the color of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in "
"its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation "
"on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of a handsome man laughing.  "
"At first glance it appears charming and friendly, but the longer you examine "
"it, the more it appears to be inhumanly cold and cruel; it's the 'Laughing "
"Man Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""
"Ves una hermosa columna del color de las rosas o la sangre, absolutamente "
"perfecta en sus proporciones. A medida que tus ojos se sienten atraídos por "
"ella, sientes una sensación de ardor en la piel. <ls_obelisk_firsttime1>Un "
"tatuaje de un hombre guapo riendo. A primera vista parece encantador y "
"amistoso, pero cuanto más lo examinas, más parece ser inhumanamente frío y "
"cruel; es la 'Contraseña del Hombre Riendo'.<ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "mysterious closed door"
msgstr "puerta cerrada misteriosa"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "mysterious closed door"
msgid ""
"A dark door of twisted metal, etched with symbols and writing that you can't "
"piece together."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta oscura de metal retorcido, grabada con símbolos y escritos que no "
"puedes descifrar."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "mysterious closed door"
msgid "With great effort, you pry open the door."
msgstr "Con gran esfuerzo, logras abrir la puerta."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "mysterious closed door"
msgid "You pry, but it seems like your tools will give out before the door does."
msgstr ""
"Intentas apalancarla, pero parece que tus herramientas se romperán antes de "
"que la puerta ceda."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "mysterious open door"
msgstr "misteriosa puerta abierta"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "mysterious open door"
msgid ""
"A dark door of twisted metal, etched with symbols and writing that you can't "
"piece together.  It has been swung open."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta oscura de metal retorcido, grabada con símbolos y escritos que no "
"puedes descifrar. Ha sido abierta de par en par."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metallic wall"
msgstr "muro/pared metálico"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metallic wall"
msgid ""
"A durable wall of ordinary looking sheet metal, at first.  Staring closer, "
"the welds and joins seem to form strange fractal patterns."
msgstr ""
"A primera vista, un muro/pared resistente de chapa metálica de aspecto "
"corriente. Al observarla más de cerca, las soldaduras y uniones parecen "
"formar extraños patrones fractales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "metal wailing!"
msgstr "¡Metal aullando!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "scrap metal wall"
msgstr "muro/pared de restos de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "scrap metal wall"
msgid ""
"A relatively simple wall made of cobbled-together scrap metal.  The wires and "
"bolts holding it together seem to be in just slightly different "
"configurations whenever you look back at it."
msgstr ""
"Un muro/pared relativamente sencillo hecha con restos de metal improvisados. "
"Los cables y tornillos que la mantienen unida parecen tener una configuración "
"ligeramente diferente cada vez que la miras."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "metal crying!"
msgstr "¡El metal gime!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metallic floor"
msgstr "piso metálico"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metallic floor"
msgid ""
"Diamond-treaded metallic flooring.  Something seems off about the diamond "
"tread; you keep imagining that the bumps spell out words, but when you look "
"closer they're in very ordinary patterns."
msgstr ""
"Suelo metálico con relieve en forma de rombos. Hay algo que no cuadra en el "
"relieve en forma de rombos; no dejas de imaginar que las protuberancias "
"forman palabras, pero cuando te fijas mejor ves que son patrones muy comunes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "broken metal floor"
msgid ""
"Something has cratered this metal flooring.  It will be difficult to move "
"things across.  Through the cracks and dents emanates a faint eery glow."
msgstr ""
"Algo ha hecho cráteres en este suelo metálico. Será difícil mover cosas por "
"él. A través de las grietas y abolladuras emana un tenue y espeluznante "
"resplandor."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "scrap metal floor"
msgstr "piso de restos de metal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "scrap metal floor"
msgid ""
"A floor assembled from various scraps of metal.  Though their placement seems "
"random, you keep seeing spots where they form faces."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo ensamblado a partir de diversos restos de metal. Aunque su "
"colocación parece aleatoria, se siguen viendo puntos en los que forman caras."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "catwalk"
msgstr "pasarela"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "catwalk"
msgid "This catwalk extends over a deep chasm of swirling shadow."
msgstr "Esta pasarela se extiende sobre un profundo abismo de sombras arremolinadas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "swirling metal roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado metálico ondulado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "swirling metal roof"
msgid ""
"A section of sturdy metal roofing that seems to swirl and twist with an "
"unfamiliar, ever-shifting pattern."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de techo metálico resistente que parece girar y retorcerse con un "
"patrón desconocido y siempre cambiante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brown laminate floor"
msgstr "suelo laminado marrón"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brown laminate floor"
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, smooth material, colored in an "
"atrocious mottled brown."
msgstr ""
"Un sección de suelo de un material resistente y liso, coloreado de un atroz "
"marrón moteado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bullet trailer roof"
msgstr "techo/tejado de trailer bala"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bullet trailer roof"
msgid "A smooth roof of gleaming chrome, slightly dusty from the road."
msgstr ""
"Un techo/tejado liso de cromo reluciente, ligeramente polvoriento por la "
"carretera."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bullet trailer exterior wall"
msgstr "muro exterior de trailer bala"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bullet trailer exterior wall"
msgid "A smooth wall of gleaming chrome, slightly dusty from the road."
msgstr "Un muro liso de cromo brillante, ligeramente polvorienta por el camino."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bullet trailer interior wall"
msgstr "pared interior de trailer bala"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bullet trailer interior wall"
msgid "A simple wall paneled in a coarsely textured gray laminate of some sort."
msgstr "Una simple pared revestida con algún tipo de laminado gris de textura gruesa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_bullettrailer_table_top"
msgid "A small trailer table, designed to convert into a bed when not in use."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña mesa de remolque, diseñada para convertirse en cama cuando no se "
"utiliza."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer cabinets"
msgstr "armarios de trailer"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer cabinets"
msgid ""
"Cramped trailer cabinets, with some inbuilt appliances taking up even more of "
"the limited space."
msgstr ""
"Armarios de remolque estrechos, con algunos electrodomésticos incorporados "
"que ocupan aún más del limitado espacio."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer sink"
msgstr "fregadero del remolque"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer sink"
msgid "A tiny metal sink and connected cabinet."
msgstr "Un pequeño lavabo de metal y un armario conectado."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mini desk"
msgstr "miniescritorio"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mini desk"
msgid "A small wooden desk with a little attached bookshelf."
msgstr "Un pequeño escritorio de madera con una pequeña estantería adosada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "trailer bathroom door"
msgstr "puerta de baño de remolque"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "trailer bathroom door"
msgid ""
"A gray textured door, rimmed in chrome, like a very tacky version of a ship's "
"hatch."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta de textura gris, bordeada de cromo, como una versión muy hortera "
"de la escotilla de un barco."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "travel toilet"
msgid_plural "travel toilets"
msgstr[0] "inodoro portátil"
msgstr[1] "inodoros portátiles"
msgstr[2] "inodoros portátiles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "travel toilet"
msgid ""
"A tiny plastic toilet for use in a travel trailer.  Unlike a normal toilet, "
"it doesn't store water locally for you to siphon out."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño inodoro de plástico para su uso en una caravana de viaje. A "
"diferencia de los inodoros normales, no almacena agua para que puede ser "
"transvasada."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "plastic cracking!"
msgstr "¡plástico haciendo crack!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer sofa"
msgstr "sofa de remolque"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer sofa"
msgid ""
"A folding trailer sofa with a durable, somewhat comfortable weave of coarse "
"red fabric."
msgstr ""
"Un sofá plegable de remolque con un tejido duradero y algo cómodo de tela "
"roja gruesa."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer bed"
msgstr "cama de remolque"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer bed"
msgid "A small but comfy-looking double bed."
msgstr "Una cama doble pequeña pero cómoda."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "plywood sign for 'Dana's Bakery'"
msgstr "Cartel de madera contrachapada 'Panadería de Dana'."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "plywood sign for 'Dana's Bakery'"
msgid "A spraypainted plywood sign reads 'Dana's Bakery' in red letters."
msgstr ""
"Un letrero de madera contrachapada pintado con aerosol reza 'Panadería Dana' "
"en letras rojas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged aisle"
msgstr "pasillo inundado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged aisle"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged aisle.  It has started to degrade after some time spent "
"underwater.  Absolutely unrecoverable."
msgstr ""
"Un pasillo inundado. Ha comenzado a deteriorarse tras pasar algún tiempo bajo "
"el agua. Absolutamente irrecuperable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged board"
msgstr "tablero inundado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged board"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged metal wall.  Keeps zombies outside the vehicle and prevents "
"people from seeing through it.  It has started to degrade after some time "
"spent underwater.  Absolutely unrecoverable."
msgstr ""
"Un muro/pared metálica empapada. Mantiene a los zombis fuera del vehículo e "
"impide que la gente vea a través de ella. Ha comenzado a degradarse tras "
"pasar algún tiempo sumergida. Absolutamente irrecuperable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged quarterpanel"
msgstr "panel lateral trasero inundado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged quarterpanel"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged half-height metal wall.  Keeps zombies outside the vehicle but "
"allows people to see over it.  It has started to degrade after some time "
"spent underwater.  Absolutely unrecoverable."
msgstr ""
"Un muro/pared metálica de media altura empapada. Mantiene a los zombis fuera "
"del vehículo, pero permite ver a la gente que está al otro lado. Ha comenzado "
"a deteriorarse tras pasar algún tiempo sumergida. Absolutamente irrecuperable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged windshield"
msgstr "parabrisas inundado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged windshield"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged sheet of glass that lets you see outside the vehicle.  It has "
"started to degrade after some time spent underwater.  Absolutely "
"unrecoverable."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de cristal inundada que permite ver el exterior del vehículo. Ha "
"comenzado a degradarse tras pasar algún tiempo sumergida en agua. "
"Absolutamente irrecuperable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged frame"
msgstr "chasis inundado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged frame"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on "
"it, and it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  "
"It has started to degrade after some time spent underwater.  Absolutely "
"unrecoverable."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura metálica inundada. Otros componentes de vehículo pueden ser "
"montado sobre ella, y puede ser unido a otros chasis para incrementar el "
"tamaño de un vehículo. Ha comenzado a degradarse tras pasar algún tiempo "
"sumergida en el agua. Absolutamente irrecuperable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "waterlogged bucket seat"
msgstr "asiento de butaca inundado"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "waterlogged bucket seat"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged soft upholstered car seat, contoured to hold one person.  It "
"has started to degrade after some time spent underwater.  Absolutely "
"unrecoverable."
msgstr ""
"Un asiento de coche tapizado, blando e inundado, con forma anatómica para una "
"persona. Ha comenzado a degradarse tras pasar algún tiempo sumergido en agua. "
"Absolutamente irrecuperable."

