#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "butternut husks"
msgid_plural "butternut husks"
msgstr[0] "cáscaras de nueces de nogal blanco"
msgstr[1] "cáscaras de nueces de nogal blanco"
msgstr[2] "cáscaras de nueces de nogal blanco"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "butternut husks"
msgid "A handful of husks from a butternuts, emptied of their meat."
msgstr "Un puñado de cáscaras de una nuez de nogal blanco, vacía de su carne."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sewage water"
msgid_plural "sewage water"
msgstr[0] "agua de alcantarillado"
msgstr[1] "aguas de alcantarillado"
msgstr[2] "aguas de alcantarillado"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sewage water"
msgid "Turbid liquid from the sewers with an awful stench."
msgstr "Líquido turbio proveniente de las alcantarillas con un hedor horrible."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "detergent"
msgid_plural "detergent"
msgstr[0] "detergente"
msgstr[1] "detergentes"
msgstr[2] "detergentes"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "detergent"
msgid "A popular pre-Cataclysm washing powder."
msgstr "Un detergente en polvo muy popular pre-Cataclismo."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "soap flakes"
msgid_plural "soap flakes"
msgstr[0] "escamas de jabón"
msgstr[1] "escamas de jabón"
msgstr[2] "escamas de jabón"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "soap flakes"
msgid ""
"A handful of flakes shaved off a bar of soap, suitable for use in a washing "
"machine."
msgstr "Un puñado de escamas de una pastilla de jabón, aptas para lavadora."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "lye"
msgid_plural "lye"
msgstr[0] "sosa caústica"
msgstr[1] "sosa caústica"
msgstr[2] "sosa caústica"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "lye"
msgid "A liquid form of sodium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with care."
msgstr ""
"Una forma líquida de hidróxido de sodio. Es altamente corrosiva; manipular "
"con precaución"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "potassium lye"
msgid_plural "potassium lye"
msgstr[0] "lejía potásica"
msgstr[1] "lejía potásica"
msgstr[2] "lejía potásica"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "potassium lye"
msgid ""
"A liquid form of potassium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with "
"care."
msgstr ""
"Una forma líquida de hidróxido de potasio. Es altamente corrosiva; manipular "
"con precaución."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nanomaterial canister"
msgid_plural "nanomaterial canisters"
msgstr[0] "contenedor de nanomaterial"
msgstr[1] "contenedores de nanomaterial"
msgstr[2] "contenedores de nanomaterial"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "nanomaterial canister"
msgid ""
"A steel canister containing carbon, iron, titanium, copper, and other "
"elements in specifically engineered atomic-scale configurations.  A "
"nanofabricator can assemble them into usable items."
msgstr ""
"Un recipiente de acero que contiene carbono, hierro, titanio, cobre y otros "
"elementos en configuraciones específicamente diseñadas a escala atómica. Un "
"nanofabricador puede ensamblar estos elementos en objetos útiles."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wood ashes"
msgid_plural "wood ashes"
msgstr[0] "cenizas de madera"
msgstr[1] "cenizas de madera"
msgstr[2] "cenizas de madera"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "wood ashes"
msgid ""
"A handful of almost-weightless residue left after the burning of some "
"substance."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de un residuo casi sin peso dejado después de quemar alguna "
"sustancia."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "corpse ashes"
msgid_plural "corpse ashes"
msgstr[0] "cenizas de cadáver"
msgstr[1] "cenizas de cadáveres"
msgstr[2] "cenizas de cadáveres"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "corpse ashes"
msgid "The burnt remains of a person or animal."
msgstr "Los restos quemados de una persona o animal."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ether"
msgid_plural "ether"
msgstr[0] "éter"
msgstr[1] "éter"
msgstr[2] "éter"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ether"
msgid ""
"A useful industrial solvent, and the first inhalative anesthetic in "
"widespread use.  Its uncomfortable side effects and tendency to explode "
"caused it to fall out of favor decades ago in the developed world.  If you "
"can't get the good stuff, however, it might make a passable substitute."
msgstr ""
"Un disolvente industrial útil, y el primer anestésico inhalatorio de uso "
"generalizado. Sus incómodos efectos secundarios y su tendencia a explotar "
"hicieron que cayera en desgracia hace décadas en el mundo desarrollado. Si no "
"puedes conseguir uno bueno, sin embargo, puede ser un sustituto pasable."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgid_plural "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgstr[0] "dimetilsulfóxido"
msgstr[1] "dimetilsulfóxido"
msgstr[2] "dimetilsulfóxido"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgid ""
"Dimethyl sulfoxide, or DMSO, is a common and important aprotic solvent, "
"capable of dissolving a huge range of things.  It has the unusual property of "
"being absorbed very quickly through the skin, causing a garlic flavor in the "
"mouth, even if it touched your arm."
msgstr ""
"El dimetilsulfóxido, o DMSO, es un disolvente aprótico común e importante, "
"capaz de disolver una enorme variedad de cosas. Tiene la insólita propiedad "
"de absorberse muy rápidamente a través de la piel, provocando un sabor a ajo "
"en la boca, aunque te haya tocado el brazo."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "chloroform"
msgid_plural "chloroform"
msgstr[0] "cloroformo"
msgstr[1] "cloroformo"
msgstr[2] "cloroformo"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "chloroform"
msgid ""
"Famous for its properties as an illicit sedative, this substance is also a "
"very good solvent.  In particular, it's used a lot in nuclear magnetic "
"resonance spectroscopy."
msgstr ""
"Famosa por su capacidad como sedante ilícito, esta sustancia es también un "
"muy buen disolvente. En particular, se usa mucho en la espectroscopia de "
"resonancia magnética nuclear."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "phenol"
msgid_plural "phenol"
msgstr[0] "fenol"
msgstr[1] "fenol"
msgstr[2] "fenol"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "phenol"
msgid ""
"A useful and potent solvent with a wide range of reactive applications.  It "
"can be used to make a huge number of plastics and polymers, it can be an "
"antiseptic, it can strip paint and break down epoxy, and it can burn your "
"skin away like tissue paper under a heat gun.  Wear gloves."
msgstr ""
"Un disolvente útil y potente con una amplia gama de aplicaciones reactivas. "
"Se puede utilizar para fabricar un gran número de plásticos y polímeros, "
"puede ser un antiséptico, puede decapar la pintura y descomponer el epoxi, y "
"puede quemar la piel como papel de seda bajo una pistola de calor. Utiliza "
"guantes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "benzene"
msgid_plural "benzene"
msgstr[0] "benceno"
msgstr[1] "benceno"
msgstr[2] "benceno"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "benzene"
msgid ""
"A colorless, highly flammable liquid with a sweet odor, one of the elementary "
"petrochemicals.  Being used primarily as a precursor to the manufacture of "
"chemicals with more complex structure, it's a major industrial chemical, but "
"finds limited use in consumer items because of its toxicity."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido incoloro, muy inflamable y de olor dulce, uno de los productos "
"petroquímicos elementales. Se utiliza principalmente como precursor para la "
"fabricación de productos químicos con una estructura más compleja, es un "
"producto químico industrial importante, pero encuentra un uso limitado en "
"artículos de consumo debido a su toxicidad."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "toluene"
msgid_plural "toluene"
msgstr[0] "tolueno"
msgstr[1] "tolueno"
msgstr[2] "tolueno"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "toluene"
msgid ""
"A colorless, toxic, and highly flammable liquid which smells like paint "
"thinner.  It's predominantly used as an industrial feedstock and a solvent, "
"and is also used as an intoxicative inhalant in a manner unintended by "
"manufacturers."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido incoloro, tóxico y altamente inflamable que huele a disolvente de "
"pintura. Se utiliza principalmente como materia prima industrial y "
"disolvente, y también como inhalante estupefaciente de forma no intencionada "
"por los fabricantes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "glycerol"
msgid_plural "glycerol"
msgstr[0] "glicerol"
msgstr[1] "glicerol"
msgstr[2] "glicerol"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "glycerol"
msgid ""
"Also called glycerin, this clear, odorless liquid is both a handy skin "
"moisturizer and an ingredient necessary to make dynamite."
msgstr ""
"También llamado glicerina, este líquido claro e inodoro es a la vez un "
"práctico humectante para la piel y un ingrediente necesario para fabricar "
"dinamita."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "peptone water powder"
msgid_plural "peptone water powder"
msgstr[0] "polvos de agua de peptona"
msgstr[1] "aguas de peptona en polvo"
msgstr[2] "aguas de peptona en polvo"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "peptone water powder"
msgid "A pre-mixed salty solution of protein and sugar meant for bacteria to eat."
msgstr ""
"Una solución salada premezclada de proteínas y azúcar destinada a ser "
"ingerida por las bacterias."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "agar"
msgid_plural "agar"
msgstr[0] "agar"
msgstr[1] "agar"
msgstr[2] "agar"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "agar"
msgid ""
"Clear flakes of processed seaweed that can be dissolved in boiling water to "
"create a very sturdy, temperature-resistant gel.  Not only is it good for "
"making gels to separate molecules by size, but it's a great cheat ingredient "
"to make sure your jellies set properly."
msgstr ""
"Copos transparentes de algas procesadas que pueden disolverse en agua "
"hirviendo para crear un gel muy sólido y resistente a la temperatura. No solo "
"sirve para hacer geles para separar moléculas por tamaño, sino que es un "
"ingrediente trampa estupendo para que tus gelatinas cuajen bien."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acrylamide"
msgid_plural "acrylamide"
msgstr[0] "acrilamida"
msgstr[1] "acrilamida"
msgstr[2] "acrilamida"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acrylamide"
msgid ""
"A handful of highly carcinogenic white powder that can be readily polymerized "
"into a whole bunch of useful water-soluble gels."
msgstr ""
"Un puñado de polvo blanco altamente cancerígeno que puede polimerizarse "
"fácilmente en un montón de útiles geles solubles en agua."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "steel grille"
msgid_plural "steel grilles"
msgstr[0] "rejilla de acero"
msgstr[1] "rejillas de acero"
msgstr[2] "rejillas de acero"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "steel grille"
msgid "A metal grille.  It can be used as a framework for making a chemical catalyst."
msgstr ""
"Una rejilla de metal. Puede ser usada como estructura para hacer un "
"catalizador químico."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "cobalt-60 pellet"
msgid_plural "cobalt-60 pellets"
msgstr[0] "perdigón de cobalto 60"
msgstr[1] "perdigones de cobalto 60"
msgstr[2] "perdigones de cobalto 60"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "cobalt-60 pellet"
msgid ""
"A piece of unshielded radioactive material that used to be a part of some "
"nuclear industry equipment.  You have yet to find some use for it, and you "
"probably shouldn't stand near it."
msgstr ""
"Un trozo de material radiactivo sin blindaje que solía formar parte de "
"algunos equipos de la industria nuclear. Aún no le has encontrado ninguna "
"utilidad y probablemente no deberías acercarte a él."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden bead"
msgid_plural "wooden beads"
msgstr[0] "cuenta de madera"
msgstr[1] "cuentas de madera"
msgstr[2] "cuentas de madera"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "wooden bead"
msgid ""
"A wooden bead.  It can be used to craft inscribable jewelry or create a "
"beaded curtain door."
msgstr ""
"Una cuenta de madera. Se puede utilizar para fabricar joyas inscribibles o "
"crear una puerta de cortina de cuentas."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "rosin"
msgid_plural "rosin"
msgstr[0] "colofonia"
msgstr[1] "colofonias"
msgstr[2] "colofonias"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "rosin"
msgid "A chunk of yellowish rosin, usable as a flux for soldering."
msgstr "Un trozo de resina amarillenta, utilizable como fundente para soldar."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acetylene"
msgid_plural "acetylene"
msgstr[0] "acetileno"
msgstr[1] "acetileno"
msgstr[2] "acetileno"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acetylene"
msgid ""
"A flammable gas that explodes under pressure.  Combined with oxygen, "
"acetylene makes a great welding gas."
msgstr ""
"Un gas inflamable que explota bajo presión. Combinado con el oxígeno, el "
"acetileno es un gran gas para soldar."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "formic acid"
msgid_plural "formic acid"
msgstr[0] "ácido fórmico"
msgstr[1] "ácido fórmico"
msgstr[2] "ácido fórmico"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "formic acid"
msgid ""
"Common in nature as an insect venom, this substance has a number of "
"industrial uses such as preservation and manufacturing."
msgstr ""
"Común en la naturaleza como veneno de insecto, esta sustancia tiene una serie "
"de usos industriales como la preservación y la fabricación."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "latex"
msgid_plural "latex"
msgstr[0] "latex"
msgstr[1] "latex"
msgstr[2] "latex"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "latex"
msgid "A liquid precursor to rubber found in some plants."
msgstr "Un precursor líquido del plastico que se encuentra en algunas plantas."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "citric acid"
msgid_plural "citric acid"
msgstr[0] "ácido cítrico"
msgstr[1] "ácido cítrico"
msgstr[2] "ácido cítrico"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "citric acid"
msgid ""
"A manufactured form of citric acid that is commonly used as an additive in "
"food, cleaning agents, and nutritional supplements."
msgstr ""
"Una forma manufacturada de ácido cítrico que se utiliza comúnmente como "
"aditivo en alimentos, agentes de limpieza y suplementos nutricionales."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wasp venom gland"
msgid_plural "wasp venom glands"
msgstr[0] "glándula de veneno de avispa"
msgstr[1] "glándulas de veneno de avispa"
msgstr[2] "glándulas de veneno de avispa"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "wasp venom gland"
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of wasp "
"venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with the right "
"know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un órgano frágil y ligeramente tembloroso para la producción y almacenamiento "
"del veneno de avispas. Se podrían extraer algunos productos químicos muy "
"útiles de él con los conocimientos adecuados, pero sólo si te das prisa."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bee venom gland"
msgid_plural "bee venom glands"
msgstr[0] "glándula de veneno de abeja"
msgstr[1] "glándulas de veneno de abeja"
msgstr[2] "glándulas de veneno de abeja"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "bee venom gland"
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of "
"honeybee venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with "
"the right know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un órgano frágil y ligeramente tembloroso para la producción y almacenamiento "
"del veneno de las abejas de miel. Se podrían extraer algunos productos "
"químicos muy útiles de él con los conocimientos adecuados, pero sólo si te "
"das prisa."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sac of paralytic venom"
msgid_plural "sacs of paralytic venom"
msgstr[0] "saco de veneno paralizante"
msgstr[1] "sacos de veneno paralizante"
msgstr[2] "sacos de veneno paralizante"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sac of paralytic venom"
msgid ""
"A grayish, flexible vesicle filled to the brim with the potent paralytic "
"agent the triffids use to subdue still-moving fertilizer such as yourself.  "
"If you know your way around poisons you might be able to find a use for it."
msgstr ""
"Una vesícula grisácea y flexible llena hasta el borde del potente agente "
"paralizante que los trífidos utilizan para someter a los fertilizantes en que "
"todavia se mueven como tú. Si conoces bien los venenos, quizá puedas "
"encontrarle un uso."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sac of triffid fungicide"
msgid_plural "sacs of triffid fungicide"
msgstr[0] "saco trífido con fungicida"
msgstr[1] "sacos de fungicida trífido"
msgstr[2] "sacos de fungicida trífido"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sac of triffid fungicide"
msgid ""
"A triffid sac filled with what appears to be a triffid-produced antifungal "
"agent.  It will likely already work as an antifungal compound for more "
"offensive applications, but requires further refining before it can be used "
"as a medical drug."
msgstr ""
"Un saco de trífido lleno de lo que parece ser un agente antifúngico producido "
"por el trífido. Es probable que ya funcione como compuesto antifúngico para "
"aplicaciones más ofensivas, pero requiere un mayor refinamiento antes de que "
"pueda utilizarse como fármaco médico."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "concentrated venom"
msgid_plural "concentrated venom"
msgstr[0] "veneno concentrado"
msgstr[1] "veneno concentrado"
msgstr[2] "veneno concentrado"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "concentrated venom"
msgid ""
"A transparent, lightly greenish liquid, refined from the venom of bees and "
"wasps.  Active ingredients include (nor-)adrenaline, dopamine, histamine, and "
"protein toxins.  It is now relatively stable, but will require further "
"separation to be useful for anything other than killing you."
msgstr ""
"Un líquido transparente, ligeramente verdoso, refinado a partir del veneno de "
"abejas y avispas. Los ingredientes activos incluyen (nor-)adrenalina, "
"dopamina, histamina y toxinas proteínicas. Ahora es relativamente estable, "
"pero requerirá una mayor separación para ser útil para otra cosa que no sea "
"matarte."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "concentrated paralytic"
msgid_plural "concentrated paralytic"
msgstr[0] "concentrado paralizante"
msgstr[1] "concentrado paralizante"
msgstr[2] "concentrado paralizante"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "concentrated paralytic"
msgid ""
"A concentrated paralytic agent, originally from a triffid.  Given your "
"experience with its effects (chiefly gathered while sourcing this batch) and "
"their striking similarity to earthly flora, you figure it's related to "
"curarines.  Might come in handy in crafting more useful things."
msgstr ""
"Un agente paralizante concentrado, originario de un trífido. Dada tu "
"experiencia con sus efectos (recopilada principalmente mientras conseguías "
"esta remesa) y su sorprendente similitud con la flora terrestre, supones que "
"está relacionado con las curarinas. Podría ser útil para fabricar cosas más "
"útiles."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "rocuronium"
msgid_plural "rocuronium"
msgstr[0] "rocuronio"
msgstr[1] "rocuronio"
msgstr[2] "rocuronio"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "rocuronium"
msgid ""
"Rocuronium bromide, a fast-acting muscle relaxant.  Used primarily in "
"emergency medicine because of its relative stability, it can serve as a "
"component of a balanced anesthesia in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Bromuro de rocuronio, un relajante muscular de acción rápida. Utilizado "
"principalmente en la medicina de emergencia por su relativa estabilidad, "
"puede servir como componente de una anestesia balanceada en caso de necesidad."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "red phosphorous"
msgid_plural "red phosphorous"
msgstr[0] "fósforo rojo"
msgstr[1] "fósforo rojo"
msgstr[2] "fósforo rojo"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "red phosphorous"
msgid ""
"An allotrope of the element phosphorous.  It's what you use to light matches, "
"but can also be used in the synthesis of methamphetamine.  You could use it "
"to make bombs, and if you were truly desperate you might even be able to use "
"it in small portions as a propellant for bullets."
msgstr ""
"Alótropo del elemento fósforo. Es lo que se utiliza para encender cerillas, "
"pero también se puede emplear en la síntesis de la metanfetamina. Se puede "
"utilizar para fabricar bombas y, si se está realmente desesperado, incluso se "
"puede utilizar en pequeñas porciones como propelente para balas."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "small portion of red phosphorous"
msgid_plural "small portion of red phosphorous"
msgstr[0] "pequeña porción de fósforo rojo"
msgstr[1] "pequeñas porciones de fósforo rojo"
msgstr[2] "pequeñas porciones de fósforo rojo"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "small portion of red phosphorous"
msgid ""
"An allotrope of the element phosphorous.  It's what you use to light matches, "
"but can also be used in the synthesis of methamphetamine.  You could use it "
"to make bombs, and if you were truly desperate you might even be able to use "
"it as a propellant for bullets."
msgstr ""
"Un alótropo del elemento del fósforo. Es lo que usas con las cerillas, pero "
"que también se puede usar para hacer metanfetaminas. Lo podrías usar para "
"hacer bombas, y si estuvieras verdaderamente desesperado podrías usarlo como "
"propelente para balas."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
