#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "EOD jacket"
msgid_plural "EOD jackets"
msgstr[0] "chaqueta de desactivador de bombas"
msgstr[1] "chaquetas de desactivador de bombas"
msgstr[2] "chaquetas de desactivador de bombas"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "EOD jacket"
msgid ""
"A thick armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for "
"use by explosive ordnance disposal technicians.  It features a central pocket "
"for a large plate, and near complete coverage in fragmentation resistant "
"materials.  Aside from the plate, it offers insufficient protection from "
"ballistic threats."
msgstr ""
"Una chaqueta blindada gruesa fabricada con Kevlar, Nomex y relleno de espuma, "
"usada por los técnicos en desactivación de explosivos. Presenta un bolsillo "
"central para una placa grande de materiales resistentes a la fragmentación "
"con una cobertura casi completa. Al margen de la placa, ofrece una protección "
"insuficiente contra las amenazas balísticas."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "EOD jacket"
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid "Pocket for a huge armor plate."
msgstr "Bolsillo para una enorme placa de armadura."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid_plural "tactical EOD jackets"
msgstr[0] "chaqueta táctica EOD"
msgstr[1] "chaquetas tácticas EOD"
msgstr[2] "chaquetas tácticas EOD"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid ""
"An armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for use "
"by explosive ordnance disposal technicians in 'non-permissive environments'.  "
"It is lighter than normal EOD armor to allow for wearing a plate carrier "
"beneath it.  It features two pockets in the arms covering the deltoids for "
"additional optional protection."
msgstr ""
"Una chaqueta blindada fabricada con Kevlar, Nomex y relleno de espuma usada "
"por técnicos en desactivación de explosivos en 'entornos no permisivos'. Es "
"más ligero que el blindaje EOD normal para poder llevar un portaplacas "
"debajo. Presenta dos bolsillos en los brazos que cubren los deltoides para "
"una protección adicional opcional."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "tactical EOD jacket"
msgid "Pockets for deltoid armor plates."
msgstr "Bolsillos para placas de armaduras de deltoide."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "EOD fragmentation plate"
msgid_plural "EOD fragmentation plates"
msgstr[0] "placa de fragmentación EOD"
msgstr[1] "placas de fragmentación EOD"
msgstr[2] "placas de fragmentación EOD"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "EOD fragmentation plate"
msgid ""
"A polygonal fragmentation plate with a slightly concave profile, made of thin "
"layers of steel, UHMW polyethylene, foam, and Kevlar.  Though certified to "
"provide protection from fragmentation, it will not provide much protection "
"from firearms.  This is intended to be inserted into an EOD suit, and can't "
"be worn on its own."
msgstr ""
"Una placa de fragmentación poligonal con un perfil ligeramente cóncavo, "
"fabricada con finas capas de acero, polietileno UHMW, espuma y Kevlar. Aunque "
"está certificada para ofrecer protección contra la fragmentación, no ofrece "
"mucha protección contra las armas de fuego. Está pensada para ser insertada "
"en un traje EOD, y no puede llevarse sola."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ESAPI ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "ESAPI ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "placa antibalas ESAPI"
msgstr[1] "placas antibalas ESAPI"
msgstr[2] "placas antibalas ESAPI"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "ESAPI ballistic plate"
msgid ""
"A polygonal ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile, made of ceramic. "
" Its inner surface is coated with UHMW polyethylene and is labeled \"TOP\", "
"while the outer surface is labeled \"STRIKE FACE\".  This is intended to be "
"worn in a ballistic vest, and can withstand several high-energy rifle rounds "
"before breaking."
msgstr ""
"Una placa antibalas poligonal de perfil ligeramente cóncavo, fabricada en "
"cerámica. Su superficie interior está recubierta de polietileno UHMW y lleva "
"la etiqueta \"TOP\", mientras que la superficie exterior lleva la etiqueta "
"\"STRIKE FACE\". Está pensada para ser llevada en un chaleco antibalas, y "
"puede soportar varios disparos de fusil de alta energía antes de romperse."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "soft stab panel"
msgid_plural "soft stab panels"
msgstr[0] "panel antipuñalada"
msgstr[1] "paneles antipuñalada"
msgstr[2] "paneles antipuñalada"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "soft stab panel"
msgid ""
"A soft armor insert designed to protect against stab wounds.  While it's not "
"great protection, it incurs no additional encumbrance.  This is intended to "
"be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be worn on its own."
msgstr ""
"Una armadura blanda diseñada para proteger contra las puñaladas. Aunque no es "
"una gran protección, no supone un incomodidad adicional. Está pensada para "
"ser insertada en un chaleco antibalas, y no puede llevarse sola."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "steel ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "steel ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "placa de acero antibalas"
msgstr[1] "placas de acero antibalas"
msgstr[2] "placas de acero antibalas"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic plate"
msgid ""
"A concave ballistic plate made of hard steel, designed to stop small-caliber "
"rounds.  \"NIJ III A PROTECTION\" is etched into the back of the plate.  This "
"is intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be worn on its "
"own."
msgstr ""
"Una placa antibalas cóncava hecha de acero duro, diseñada para detener balas "
"de pequeño calibre. \"NIJ III A PROTECTION\" está grabado en la parte "
"posterior de la placa. Está pensada para ser insertada en un chaleco "
"antibalas, y no puede llevarse sola."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "heavy steel ballistic plate"
msgid_plural "heavy steel ballistic plates"
msgstr[0] "placa de acero pesado antibalas"
msgstr[1] "placas de acero pesado antibalas"
msgstr[2] "placas de acero pesado antibalas"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "heavy steel ballistic plate"
msgid ""
"A heavy concave ballistic plate made of tempered steel, designed to stop "
"small-caliber rounds.  \"NIJ III PROTECTION\" is etched into the back of the "
"plate.  This is intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be "
"worn on its own."
msgstr ""
"Una pesada placa antibalas cóncava de acero templado, diseñada para detener "
"balas de pequeño calibre. \"NIJ III PROTECTION\" está grabado en la parte "
"posterior de la placa. Está pensada para ser insertada en un chaleco "
"antibalas, y no puede llevarse sola."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "scrap ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "scrap ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "placa ESAPI desechada"
msgstr[1] "placas ESAPI desechadas"
msgstr[2] "placas ESAPI desechadas"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "scrap ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"A flat piece of salvaged steel, crudely cut and bent into the shape of an "
"ESAPI ballistic plate.  It's wrapped in rags to cover the sharp edges.  "
"Better than nothing, but it's heavier than the real thing, and not very "
"strong.  This is intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be "
"worn on its own."
msgstr ""
"Un trozo plano de acero reciclado, toscamente cortado y doblado en forma de "
"placa antibalas ESAPI. Está envuelta en trapos para cubrir los bordes "
"afilados. Mejor que nada, pero es más pesada que la real, y no es muy fuerte. "
"Está pensada para ser insertada en un chaleco antibalas, y no puede llevarse "
"sola."

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "mild ESAPI plate"
msgid_plural "mild ESAPI plates"
msgstr[0] "placa de acero dulce ESAPI"
msgstr[1] "placas de acero dulce ESAPI"
msgstr[2] "placas de acero dulce ESAPI"

#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
#. ~ Description of "mild ESAPI plate"
msgid ""
"Mild steel forged into a ballistic plate.  While it is more professionally "
"done than scrap plates, it still has a fair amount of jerry-rigging."
msgstr ""
"Acero dulce forjado en una placa antibalas. Si bien es más profesional que "
"las placas de chatarra, todavía tiene tiene bastantes apaños."

