#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
#. ~ Description of gun "IWI Tavor X95"
#. ~ Description of "IWI Tavor X95"
msgid ""
"The Tavor is an Israeli series of bullpup rifles designed and produced by "
"Israel Weapon Industries.  This is the Tavor X95, a civilian-legal rifle "
"lacking any full-auto capability, and sporting a 16.5\" barrel.  Chambered in "
"5.56/.223, this rifle feeds from STANAG magazines."
msgstr ""
"El Tavor es una serie israelí de rifles bullpup diseñados y fabricados por "
"Israel Weapon Industries. Este es el Tavor X95, un rifle legal para uso civil "
"que carece de capacidad totalmente automática y cuenta con un cañón de 42cm. "
"Con recámara para 5,56/.223, este rifle se alimenta con cargadores STANAG."

#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "sporter AR rifle"
msgid_plural "sporter AR rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle AR deportivo"
msgstr[1] "rifles AR deportivos"
msgstr[2] "rifles AR deportivos"

#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
#. ~ Description of gun "sporter AR rifle"
#. ~ Description of "sporter AR rifle"
msgid ""
"A lightweight AR-15 platform rifle, capable of feeding standard AR magazines. "
" Unlike the military versions, it has no threaded barrel or collapsing stock."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle ligero basado en la plataforma AR-15, capaz de alimentarse con "
"cargadores AR estándar. A diferencia de las versiones militares, no tiene "
"cañón roscado ni culata plegable."

#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "sporter AR rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "sporter AR rifle"
msgid "M&P 15"
msgid_plural "M&P 15s"
msgstr[0] "M&P 15"
msgstr[1] "M&P 15s"
msgstr[2] "M&P 15s"

#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
#. ~ Description of variant "sporter AR rifle" of gun "M&P 15"
#. ~ Description of variant "M&P 15" of item "sporter AR rifle"
msgid ""
"S&Ws version of the AR-15, the M&P-15 is a very common rifle.  Despite being "
"very similar to an AR-15 in both form and function, the receivers and uppers "
"are incompatible."
msgstr ""
"La versión de S&W del AR-15, el M&P-15, es un rifle muy común. A pesar de ser "
"muy similar al AR-15 tanto en forma como en función, los receptores y las "
"partes superiores son incompatibles."

#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "bolt-action hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de caza de cerrojo"
msgstr[1] "rifles de caza de cerrojo"
msgstr[2] "rifles de caza de cerrojo"

#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Description of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Description of "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid ""
"Featuring a handsome set of wooden furnishings, a classic design, and a no "
"nonsense .270 caliber chambering, this is a powerful hunting rifle.  With a "
"tried and proven pedigree dating back over 60 years, millions of such rugged "
"arms have been made, exported, and used throughout the United States and the "
"world at large.  Where hunting is concerned, this is a highly capable and "
"well proven weapon in all respects.  Fortunate, given that your prey in these "
"dark days may turn out to be a little bit more feisty than typical "
"White-Tailed deer, moose, and black bears."
msgstr ""
"Este poderoso rifle de caza posee un elegante conjunto de accesorios de "
"madera, un diseño clásico y un entendible calibre .270. Con un linaje probado "
"de más de 60 años, millones de estas robustas armas han sido fabricadas, "
"exportadas y utilizadas a lo largo de Estados Unidos y el mundo entero. En "
"cuanto a la caza se refiere, este es un rifle muy capaz y bien probado en "
"todos sus aspectos. Y eso es una suerte, ya que en estos días oscuros tu "
"presa puede resultar un poco más peleadora que los típicos ciervos de cola "
"blanca, alces y osos negros."

#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid "Remington 700 .270 Win rifle"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .270 Win rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[1] "rifles Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[2] "rifles Remington 700 .270 Win"

#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Description of variant "bolt-action hunting rifle" of gun "Remington 700
#. .270 Win rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Remington 700 .270 Win rifle" of item "bolt-
#. action hunting rifle"
msgid ""
"A classic bolt-action rifle chambered for .270 Winchester, very popular among "
"hunters.  This is a CDL SF model with a forged, fluted, 416 stainless steel "
"barrel threaded into the receiver and a recessed bolt face.  It has checkered "
"walnut furniture and a recoil pad to reduce perceived recoil."
msgstr ""
"Un clásico rifle de cerrojo con recámara para Winchester .270, muy popular "
"entre los cazadores. Este es un modelo CDL SF con un cañón de acero "
"inoxidable 416 forjado y estriado, roscado en el cañón y con una cara del "
"cerrojo empotrada. Tiene armazones de nogal a cuadros y una almohadilla de "
"retroceso para reducir el retroceso percibido."

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M2010 ESR"
msgid_plural "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[0] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[1] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[2] "M2010 ESR"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "M2010 ESR"
#. ~ Description of "M2010 ESR"
msgid ""
"A bolt-action, box-magazine-fed sniper rifle chambered in the powerful .300 "
"Winchester Magnum round.  The M2010 had completely replaced the M24 rifle "
"series by 2017."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de francotirador de cerrojo con recámara para el potente proyectil "
".300 Winchester Magnum. En 2017, el M2010 había sustituido por completo a la "
"serie de fusiles M24."

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Weatherby Mark V"
msgid_plural "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[0] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[1] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[2] "Weatherby Mark V"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Weatherby Mark V"
#. ~ Description of "Weatherby Mark V"
msgid ""
"The Weatherby Mark V is one of the world's finest bolt-action rifles.  "
"Designed in 1955 by Roy Weatherby and Fred Jennie, it has a strong action "
"designed to safely fire high-pressure cartridges.  These rifles were "
"presented to celebrities as part of a marketing campaign."
msgstr ""
"El Weatherby Mark V es uno de los mejores rifles de cerrojo del mundo. "
"Diseñado en 1955 por Roy Weatherby y Fred Jennie, tiene una potente acción "
"diseñada para disparar con seguridad cartuchos de alta presión. Estos rifles "
"se regalaron a celebridades como parte de una campaña de marketing."

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Winchester Model 70"
msgid_plural "Winchester Model 70s"
msgstr[0] "winchester Model 70"
msgstr[1] "winchesters Model 70"
msgstr[2] "winchesters Model 70"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Winchester Model 70"
#. ~ Description of "Winchester Model 70"
msgid ""
"The Winchester Model 70 is a bolt-action sporting rifle.  It has an iconic "
"place in American sporting culture and has been held in high regard by "
"shooters since it was introduced in 1936."
msgstr ""
"El Winchester Model 70 es un rifle de cerrojo para tiro deportivo. Ocupa un "
"lugar icónico en la cultura deportiva estadounidense, y ha sido tenido en "
"gran consideración por los tiradores desde que fue presentada en 1936."

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Ruger Precision Rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger Precision Rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de Precisión Ruger"
msgstr[1] "rifles de Precisión Ruger"
msgstr[2] "rifles de Precisión Ruger"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Precision Rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Ruger Precision Rifle"
msgid ""
"Originally introduced to the Ruger gun corporation's family of high-end "
"marksman rifles in 2015, the Ruger Precision Rifle is a modern and highly "
"modular long-range bolt-action weapon.  By incorporating a unique in-line "
"recoil path that manages recoil from the rear of the receiver to the "
"buttstock, as opposed to traditional bedding, the rifle offers maximal "
"accuracy potential, while the arm's additional bells and whistles, an "
"incorporated marksman's trigger, muzzle brake, and this particular rifle's "
"powerhouse chambering of .300 Win Mag, help to make the most from any "
"long-range engagement."
msgstr ""
"Originalmente introducido en 2015 en la familia de rifles de alta gama de la "
"corporación Ruger, el Ruger Precision Rifle es un arma de cerrojo moderna y "
"altamente modular de largo alcance. Al incorporar un retroceso en linea único "
"que maneja el retroceso de la parte trasera del receptor de la culata, al "
"contrario a lo tradicional, el rifle ofrece un potencial máximo de precisión, "
"con añadidos adicionales, como un gatillo de competición incorporado, freno "
"de boca y este en particular, con el calibre .300 Win Mag, que ayudan a sacar "
"el máximo partido en cualquier enfrentamiento a larga distancia."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "BLR lever-action hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de caza de palanca BRL"
msgstr[1] "rifles de caza de palanca BRL"
msgstr[2] "rifles de caza de palanca BRL"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Description of "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
msgid ""
"A highly accurate lever-action hunting rifle chambered for the powerful "
".30-06 round.  Notable for using a detachable magazine instead of a "
"traditional tube."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de caza de acción de palanca, con muy buena precisión y calibre para "
"la poderosa .30-06. Conocido por utilizar un cargador extraíble en lugar de "
"la tradicional cámara."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
msgid "Browning BLR"
msgid_plural "Browning BLRs"
msgstr[0] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[1] "Browning BLRs"
msgstr[2] "Browning BLRs"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "BLR lever-action hunting rifle" of gun "Browning
#. BLR"
#. ~ Description of variant "Browning BLR" of item "BLR lever-action hunting
#. rifle"
msgid ""
"The Browning BLR is notable for being a lever-action rifle, chambered in "
"calibers with spitzer bullets.  This is unusual for lever-actions, as a "
"spitzer bullet risks setting off other cartridges in a typical tube magazine. "
" The BLR gets around this issue by utilizing box magazines instead, making it "
"quite unique among other lever-action rifles.  This one is chambered for "
"30-06."
msgstr ""
"El Browning BLR destaca por ser un rifle de palanca, recamarado en calibres "
"con balas spitzer. Esto es inusual en los rifles de palanca, ya que una bala "
"spitzer corre el riesgo de disparar otros cartuchos en un cargador de tubo "
"típico. El BLR evita este problema utilizando cargadores de caja, lo que lo "
"hace único entre los rifles de palanca. Este rifle tiene recámara para 30-06."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Garand battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Garand battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de batalla Garand"
msgstr[1] "rifles de batalla Garand"
msgstr[2] "rifles de batalla Garand"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Garand battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Garand battle rifle"
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic .30-06 battle rifle, developed to replace the M1903 "
"Springfield.  It didn't completely supplant the older bolt-action until after "
"World War II."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de combate semiautomático de calibre .30-06, desarrollado para "
"reemplazar el M1903 Springfield. No llegó a reemplazarlo completamente hasta "
"después de la Segunda Guerra Mundial."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Garand battle rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Garand battle rifle"
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M1 Garand"
msgid_plural "M1 Garand"
msgstr[0] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[1] "M1s Garand"
msgstr[2] "M1s Garand"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Garand battle rifle" of gun "M1 Garand"
#. ~ Description of variant "M1 Garand" of item "Garand battle rifle"
msgid ""
"The M1 Garand is a widely celebrated battle rifle, being one of the most "
"mass-produced battle rifles in the world.  It saw widespread use in the US "
"military, being used extensively in WW2 and the Korean War.  While its "
"military use has dwindled down, being out of US service for more than 50 "
"years, some of its mechanical influence still remains through rifles such as "
"AKs or M14s.  It still sees widespread use in civilian spaces as an accurate "
"competition or hunting rifle."
msgstr ""
"El M1 Garand es un famoso rifle de combate, uno de los de mayor producción en "
"serie del mundo. Se utilizó ampliamente en el ejército estadounidense en la "
"Segunda Guerra Mundial y en la Guerra de Corea. Aunque su uso militar ha "
"disminuido, ya que hace más de 50 años que dejó de estar en servicio en "
"EE.UU., aún se conserva parte de su influencia mecánica en rifles como el AK "
"o el M14. Todavía se utiliza mucho en el ámbito civil como rifle de "
"competición de gran precisión o como rifle de caza."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Springfield rifle"
msgid_plural "Springfield rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle Springfield"
msgstr[1] "rifles Springfield"
msgstr[2] "rifles Springfield"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Springfield rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Springfield rifle"
msgid ""
"A powerful military rifle chambered in .30-06, developed to replace the US "
"Army's older Krag rifle.  It served as the main American rifle in World War "
"I, was used alongside the M1 Garand in World War II, and was used as a sniper "
"rifle as late as the Vietnam War."
msgstr ""
"Un poderoso rifle militar calibre .30-06, desarrollado para reemplazar el "
"viejo rifle Krag del ejército de Estados Unidos. Fue el arma principal de los "
"estadounidenses durante la Primera Guerra Mundial, usado junto al M1 Garand "
"durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial, y llegó a ser usado como rifle de "
"francotirador incluso en la guerra de Vietnam."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Springfield rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Springfield rifle"
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M1903 Springfield"
msgid_plural "M1903 Springfields"
msgstr[0] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[1] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[2] "M1903 Springfield"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Springfield rifle" of gun "M1903 Springfield"
#. ~ Description of variant "M1903 Springfield" of item "Springfield rifle"
msgid ""
"A powerful military rifle originally chambered in .30-03 Springfield, "
"developed to replace the US Army's older Krag rifle.  It was quickly "
"rechambered into the .30-06 caliber with its spitzer bullet.  While an "
"American rifle produced and developed around WW1, manufacturing couldn't keep "
"up with demand, and saw service alongside the M1917 Enfield, a British rifle "
"rechambered for the American 30-06.  It saw service as a sniper rifle up to "
"the Vietnam War, but nowadays is mainly used by civilians, either as hunting "
"rifles or in collections."
msgstr ""
"Un potente rifle militar originalmente con recámara en .30-03 Springfield, "
"desarrollado para sustituir al antiguo rifle Krag del ejército "
"estadounidense. Fue rápidamente adaptado al calibre .30-06 con su bala "
"spitzer. Aunque era un rifle estadounidense producido y desarrollado en torno "
"a la Primera Guerra Mundial, la fabricación no pudo seguir el ritmo de la "
"demanda, y entró en servicio junto con el M1917 Enfield, un rifle británico "
"con recamara para el 30-06 estadounidense. Estuvo en servicio como rifle de "
"francotirador hasta la guerra de Vietnam, pero hoy en día es utilizado "
"principalmente por civiles, ya sea como rifle de caza o en colecciones."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "BAR rifle"
msgid_plural "BAR rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle BAR"
msgstr[1] "rifles BAR"
msgstr[2] "rifles BAR"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "BAR rifle"
#. ~ Description of "BAR rifle"
msgid ""
"This heavy rifle was designed near the end of World War I, and provided fire "
"support for the US Army from World War II all the way to the Vietnam War.  "
"Too much firepower to serve as a battle rifle, but not enough to be an ideal "
"light machine gun, it still found a niche on the battlefield."
msgstr ""
"Este rifle pesado fue diseñado cerca del final de la Primera Guerra Mundial, "
"y proporcionó fuego de apoyo al Ejército de EE.UU. desde la Segunda Guerra "
"Mundial hasta la Guerra de Vietnam. Demasiada potencia de fuego para servir "
"como rifle de combate, pero no la suficiente para ser una ametralladora "
"ligera ideal, aun así encontró un hueco en el campo de batalla."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "BAR rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "BAR rifle"
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Browning Automatic Rifle"
msgid_plural "Browning Automatic Rifles"
msgstr[0] "Rifle Automático Browning"
msgstr[1] "Rifles Automáticos Browning"
msgstr[2] "Rifles Automáticos Browning"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "BAR rifle" of gun "Browning Automatic Rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Browning Automatic Rifle" of item "BAR rifle"
msgid ""
"Designed near the end of World War I, the BAR provided fire support for the "
"US Army from World War II all the way to the Vietnam War.  Originally "
"developed to fill a now outdated role as an \"automatic rifle\", it was "
"pushed into service for use as a light machine gun.  Despite being heavy and "
"cumbersome, without filling its designed role, it saw service for over 50 "
"years.  While newer models have a slow and fast fully automatic setting, this "
"one is an older one, with just semi and full auto."
msgstr ""
"Diseñado cerca del final de la Primera Guerra Mundial, el BAR proporcionó "
"apoyo de fuego al Ejército de EE.UU. desde la Segunda Guerra Mundial hasta la "
"Guerra de Vietnam. Originalmente desarrollado para desempeñar un papel ya "
"obsoleto como 'rifle automático', fue empujado al servicio para su uso como "
"ametralladora ligera. A pesar de ser pesada e incómoda, sin cumplir la "
"función para la que fue diseñada, estuvo en servicio durante más de 50 años. "
"Mientras que los modelos más nuevos tienen un ajuste lento y rápido "
"completamente automático, éste es uno más antiguo, con sólo semi y "
"completamente automático."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Remington 700 .30-06 rifle"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .30-06 rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[1] "rifles Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[2] "rifles Remington 700 .30-06"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Remington 700 .30-06 rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Remington 700 .30-06 rifle"
msgid ""
"A very popular and durable hunting or sniping rifle.  Popular among SWAT and "
"US Marine snipers.  Highly damaging, but perhaps not as accurate as the "
"competing Browning BLR."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de caza o francotirador muy popular y duradero. Popular entre los "
"francotiradores de SWAT y de la Marina de Estados Unidos. Causa mucho daño, "
"pero tal vez no sea tan preciso como su competidor, el Browning BLR."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Ruger Guide rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger Guide rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle Ruger Guide"
msgstr[1] "rifles Ruger Guide"
msgstr[2] "rifles Ruger Guide"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Guide rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Ruger Guide rifle"
msgid ""
"This is a popular and sturdy long-range rifle that has been in production by "
"the Ruger gun company for several decades.  Using a bolt-action feed system, "
"the rifle features a four round capacity of .30-06 cartridges and has the "
"capability to dispatch said rounds with a level of accuracy that would make "
"comparable hunting rifles blush."
msgstr ""
"Este es un rifle de largo alcance popular y robusto que ha sido producido por "
"la empresa de armas Ruger durante décadas. Usando un sistema de carga de "
"cerrojo, el rifle tiene una capacidad de cuatro cartuchos .30-06 y tiene la "
"capacidad de soltarlos con un nivel de precisión que hacen palidecer a rifles "
"de caza parecidos. "

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Ruger Guide rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Ruger Guide rifle"
msgid "Ruger M77 Hawkeye rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger M77 Hawkeye rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle Ruger M77 Hawkeye"
msgstr[1] "rifles Ruger M77 Hawkeye"
msgstr[2] "rifles Ruger M77 Hawkeye"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Ruger Guide rifle" of gun "Ruger M77 Hawkeye
#. rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Ruger M77 Hawkeye rifle" of item "Ruger Guide
#. rifle"
msgid ""
"A popular bolt-action hunting rifle first introduced in 2006, the Ruger M77 "
"was originally intended to be a modernized Mauser 98-style long gun.  To this "
"end, the weapon features a Mauser-type fixed blade extractor and an angled "
"large screw that tightly beds the action into the stock.  This particular "
"rifle is a variant with additional features, a smoother trigger, and a "
"recontoured buttstock."
msgstr ""
"Un popular rifle de caza de cerrojo introducido por primera vez en 2006, el "
"Ruger M77 fue pensado originalmente para ser un arma larga modernizada estilo "
"Mauser 98. Para ello, el arma cuenta con un extractor de cuchilla fija tipo "
"Mauser y un tornillo grande en ángulo que encaja firmemente la acción en la "
"culata. Este rifle en particular es una variante con características "
"adicionales, un gatillo más suave y una culata remodelada."

#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgid_plural "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[0] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgstr[1] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[2] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"

#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
#. ~ Description of gun "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
#. ~ Description of "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgid ""
"A gas-operated rifle, with a short 5.5 inch barrel, built-in thin folding "
"stock, and full rail mount on the upper receiver.  This particular one is a "
"select-fire military version."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de cañón corto operado por gas, con un cañón de 14cm (5.5 pulgadas), "
"culata plegable delgada incorporada y montaje de riel completo en el receptor "
"superior. Esta en concreto es una versión militar con fuego selectivo."

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Enfield battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Enfield battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de combate Enfield"
msgstr[1] "rifles de combate Enfield"
msgstr[2] "rifles de combate Enfield"

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Enfield battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Enfield battle rifle"
msgid ""
"An iconic weapon of both the First and Second World Wars, this bolt-action "
"rifle has seen deployment in the hands of Commonwealth troops across Europe "
"and beyond.  Firing the .303-caliber cartridge and making use of 10-round "
"Enfield magazines, the firearm's reputation precedes it."
msgstr ""
"Un arma icónica tanto de la Primera como de la Segunda Guerra Mundial, este "
"rifle de cerrojo ha estado en manos de las tropas de la Commonwealth en toda "
"Europa y más allá. Dispara el cartucho de calibre .303 y utiliza cargadores "
"Enfield de 10 balas, por lo que su reputación le precede."

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Enfield battle rifle"
