#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
#. ~ Description of "tempered steel bladed tepoztopili"
msgid ""
"This is a redesigned version of the Mesoamerican tepoztopili.  It has an "
"elliptical piece of carved wood lined with sharp tempered steel blades, "
"firmly attached to a stout spear shaft.  It's a weapon worthy of being "
"wielded by Huitzilopochtli himself."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una versión rediseñada del tepoztopili mesoamericano. Tiene una pieza "
"elíptica de madera tallada forrada con afiladas hojas de acero templado, "
"firmemente unidas a una robusto asta de lanza. Un arma digna de ser empuñada "
"por el mismísimo Huitzilopochtli."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/weapon_copy_extensions.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "2-by-sword"
msgid_plural "2-by-swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de madera"
msgstr[1] "espadas de madera"
msgstr[2] "espadas de madera"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "2-by-sword"
msgid ""
"A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point.  Not much good for slashing, "
"but much better than your bare hands."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón con un mango y una punta afilada. No sirve para acuchillar, pero es "
"mucho mejor que las manos desnudas."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/weapon_copy_extensions.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "zweitimber"
msgid_plural "zweitimbers"
msgstr[0] "tablonazo"
msgstr[1] "tablonazos"
msgstr[2] "tablonazos"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "zweitimber"
msgid ""
"A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point, left large enough to require "
"two hands.  Still not much good for slashing, but far better than the plank "
"on its own."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón con un mango y una punta recortada, lo suficientemente grande como "
"para necesitar las dos manos. No sirve para acuchillar, pero es mucho mejor "
"que el tablón por sí solo."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nord"
msgid_plural "nords"
msgstr[0] "clavespada"
msgstr[1] "clavespadas"
msgstr[2] "clavespadas"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "nord"
msgid ""
"A nail sword, or nord for short.  This wooden sword has a dozen nails "
"sticking out at jagged angles from the edge of the blade, making it much "
"better at chopping than slashing."
msgstr ""
"Una espada de clavos, o clavespada para abreviar. Esta espada de madera tiene "
"una docena de clavos que sobresalen en ángulos irregulares del filo de la "
"cuchilla, por lo que es mucho mejor para cortar que para acuchillar."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "scrap sword"
msgid_plural "scrap swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de chatarra"
msgstr[1] "espadas de chatarra"
msgstr[2] "espadas de chatarra"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "scrap sword"
msgid ""
"Several bits of thin scrap metal crudely beat into the semblance of an edge "
"over a wooden sword.  The added weight is unbalanced, but the jagged edge "
"offers a good bit of slashing power."
msgstr ""
"Varios trocitos de restos de metal finos golpeados para darle un parecido de "
"filo a una espada de madera. El peso agregado está desbalanceado, pero el "
"filo dentado brinda una buena cantidad daño cortante."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "scrap greatsword"
msgid_plural "scrap greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande de chatarra"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes de chatarra"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes de chatarra"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "scrap greatsword"
msgid ""
"A large wooden sword with scrap metal hammered over it into something "
"pretending to be an edge.  The extra weight almost completely front-loads the "
"balance, and it hurts your wrists just to wield."
msgstr ""
"Una gran espada de madera con restos de metal martillados sobre ella en algo "
"que simula ser un filo. El peso extra afecta casi por completo al equilibrio, "
"y duele en las muñecas sólo de empuñarla."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "welded sword"
msgid "welded sword"
msgid_plural "welded swords"
msgstr[0] "espada soldada"
msgstr[1] "espadas soldadas"
msgstr[2] "espadas soldadas"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "welded sword"
#. ~ Description of variant "welded sword" of item "welded sword"
msgid ""
"A vicious single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered twice over "
"itself then welded together.  It's not as robust as a proper forged sword, "
"but the edge is wickedly sharp."
msgstr ""
"Una feroz espada de un solo filo fabricada con chapas superpuestas y "
"soldadas. No es tan robusta como una espada forjada, pero el filo esta "
"tremendamente afilado."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "welded sword"
msgid "bolted sword"
msgid_plural "bolted swords"
msgstr[0] "espada atornillada"
msgstr[1] "espadas atornilladas"
msgstr[2] "espadas atornilladas"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of variant "bolted sword" of item "welded sword"
msgid ""
"A vicious single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered twice over "
"itself then bolted together.  It's not quite a katana made from steel folded "
"a thousand times over, but it has a certain industrial charm to it."
msgstr ""
"Una espada despiadada de filo simple hecha con dos chapas atornilladas "
"juntas. No es como una katana que está hecha de acero doblado cientos de "
"veces, pero tiene cierto encanto industrial."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "welded greatsword"
msgid "welded greatsword"
msgid_plural "welded greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande soldada"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes soldadas"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes soldadas"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "welded greatsword"
#. ~ Description of variant "welded greatsword" of item "welded greatsword"
msgid ""
"A long-handled single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered thrice over "
"itself then welded together.  The extra length and weight makes it a tad "
"awkward, but gives it a lot of slashing power."
msgstr ""
"Una espada de un solo filo y mango largo fabricada con chapas superpuestas "
"tres veces y soldadas entre sí. Su longitud y peso adicionales la hacen un "
"poco incómoda, pero le confieren una gran potencia de corte."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "welded greatsword"
msgid "bolted greatsword"
msgid_plural "bolted greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande atornillada"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes atornilladas"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes atornilladas"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of variant "bolted greatsword" of item "welded greatsword"
msgid ""
"A long-handled single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered thrice over "
"itself then bolted together.  It vaguely resembles a Japanese nagamaki if you "
"squint."
msgstr ""
"Una espada de un solo filo y mango largo hecha de chapas colocadas tres veces "
"sobre sí mismas y atornilladas. Se parece vagamente a una nagamaki japonesa "
"si entrecierras los ojos."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal sword"
msgid_plural "metal swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de metal"
msgstr[1] "espadas de metal"
msgstr[2] "espadas de metal"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "metal sword"
msgid ""
"An imitation of a true sword forged by someone who knows what swords look "
"like, at least.  Made from whatever scrap metal was on hand, it has the "
"general shape of a sword, and it is sharp, but it is a bit heavier than it "
"should be and the balance isn't quite right."
msgstr ""
"La imitación de una espada real forjada por alguien que sabe cómo es la "
"apariencia de una espada, por lo menos. Está hecha con la restos de metal  "
"que había disponible, tiene la forma general de una espada y está afilada "
"pero es un poco más pesada de lo que debería y su equilibrio no es el "
"adecuado."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal greatsword"
msgid_plural "metal greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande de metal"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes de metal"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes de metal"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "metal greatsword"
msgid ""
"A large, crudely-forged blade.  It's too big to be called a sword.  Too "
"massive, too thick, too heavy, and far too rough."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla grande, toscamente forjada. Es demasiado grande para llamarla "
"espada. Demasiado maciza, demasiado gruesa, demasiado pesada y demasiado "
"basta."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal fencing sword"
msgid_plural "metal fencing swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de esgrima de metal"
msgstr[1] "espadas de esgrima de metal"
msgstr[2] "espadas de esgrima de metal"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "metal fencing sword"
msgid ""
"Calling this a rapier is a stretch.  It's robust and very pointy, but more "
"akin to a long metal spike with a handguard than the elegant swords of the "
"Renaissance."
msgstr ""
"Llamar a esto espada ropera es exagerado. Es robusto y muy puntiagudo, pero "
"se parece más a un largo pincho metálico con guardamano que a las elegantes "
"espadas del Renacimiento."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "switchblade"
msgid "switchblade"
msgid_plural "switchblades"
msgstr[0] "navaja automática"
msgstr[1] "navajas automáticas"
msgstr[2] "navajas automáticas"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "switchblade"
#. ~ Description of variant "switchblade" of item "switchblade"
msgid ""
"A long, thin knife with a spring-loaded blade that rests inside the handle "
"while not in use."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo largo y delgado compuesto por una cuchilla accionada por resorte "
"que descansa dentro del mango cuando no se utiliza."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "switchblade"
msgid "balisong"
msgid_plural "balisongs"
msgstr[0] "navaja mariposa"
msgstr[1] "navajas mariposa"
msgstr[2] "navajas mariposa"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of variant "balisong" of item "switchblade"
msgid ""
"A flashy knife with hinged handles that completely conceal the blade while "
"folded.  Popular among movie gangbangers and people who thought fidget "
"spinners were too safe."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo llamativo con empuñadura plegable que guarda completamente la "
"hoja cuando está doblada. Es popular entre los pandilleros de las películas y "
"las personas que piensan que los fidget spinner eran demasiado seguros."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "folding knife"
msgid_plural "folding knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo plegable"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos plegables"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos plegables"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "folding knife"
msgid ""
"A small folding knife with a locking blade and a pocket clip.  Not as good a "
"weapon as a solid fixed-blade knife, but better than a penknife."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña navaja plegable con una cuchilla de bloqueo y clip de bolsillo. "
"No es tan buen arma como una navaja de hoja fija, pero es mejor que un "
"cortaplumas."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "utility folding knife"
msgid_plural "utility folding knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo plegable multiusos"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos plegables multiusos"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos plegables multiusos"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "utility folding knife"
msgid ""
"A 'Hideman' brand folding knife, this model includes extra utility options "
"such as a screwdriver, awl, and small pry bar."
msgstr ""
"Una navaja plegable de la marca 'Hideman', este modelo incluye opciones "
"adicionales de utilidad como un destornillador, un punzón y una pequeña "
"palanca."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Gun mod name
msgid "USMC bayonet"
msgid_plural "USMC bayonets"
msgstr[0] "bayoneta del USMC"
msgstr[1] "bayonetas del USMC"
msgstr[2] "bayonetas del USMC"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of gun mod "USMC bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "USMC bayonet"
msgid ""
"A modern bayonet in use with the US Marine Corps, adopted in an effort to "
"improve USMC hand-to-hand fighting capabilities.  The bayonet is optimized to "
"function as a fighting knife, sporting an ergonomic handle that will minimize "
"hand fatigue during combat.  The blade tip is sharper in profile than other "
"bayonets to assist in penetrating body armor, and also features a small "
"serrated section to provide for some utility."
msgstr ""
"Una bayoneta moderna en uso por el Cuerpo de Marines de EE.UU, adoptada en un "
"esfuerzo por mejorar las capacidades de combate cuerpo a cuerpo USMC. La "
"bayoneta está optimizada para funcionar como cuchillo de combate, con un "
"mango ergonómico que minimiza la fatiga en la mano durante el combate. La "
"punta de la cuchilla está más afilada que otras bayonetas para asistir en la "
"penetración de armaduras corporales, y también tiene una pequeña sección "
"serrada para otros usos."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Gun mod name
msgid "Bayonet"
msgid_plural "Bayonets"
msgstr[0] "Bayoneta"
msgstr[1] "Bayonetas"
msgstr[2] "Bayonetas"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Description of variant "Army bayonet"of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "Bayonet"
#. ~ Description of variant "Army bayonet" of item "Bayonet"
msgid ""
"The current issue Army bayonet, before the Cataclysm anyways.  It is thick, "
"heavy, and surprisingly sharp.  This bayonet also functions as a wire cutter, "
"and a mediocre saw for cutting through aircraft fuselage.  That the handle "
"and tang can be completely disassembled from the blade is surely a fact of "
"great comfort to the soldier, survivalist, and you."
msgstr ""
"La actual bayoneta del ejercito, antes del Cataclismo. Es gruesa, pesada y "
"sorprendentemente afilada. La bayoneta M9 también funciona como cortalambres, "
"una mediocre sierra y un destornillador difícil de sujetar. El hecho de poder "
"desmontar completamente el mango y la espiga de la cuchilla es seguramente un "
"gran alivio para el soldado, el supervivencialista, y para ti."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Bayonet"
msgid "Army bayonet"
msgid_plural "Army bayonets"
msgstr[0] "bayoneta del ejercito"
msgstr[1] "bayonetas del ejercito"
msgstr[2] "bayonetas del ejercito"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Bayonet"
msgid "AK bayonet"
msgid_plural "AK bayonets"
msgstr[0] "bayoneta AK"
msgstr[1] "bayonetas AK"
msgstr[2] "bayonetas AK"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of variant "AK bayonet"of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Description of variant "AK bayonet" of item "Bayonet"
msgid ""
"A 6H4 bayonet for Kalashnikov pattern rifles, usually imported military "
"surplus from eastern bloc countries.  The blade is made of stainless steel "
"and the handle of a lightweight and durable plastic.  It features a middling "
"metal saw on the spine of the blade, and can function as a wire cutter as "
"well.  Though it is quite sturdy, it can't hold an edge very well."
msgstr ""
"Un bayoneta 6H4 para rifles de patrón Kalashnikov, generalmente importados "
"como excedentes militares de países del bloque del este. La hoja está hecha "
"de acero inoxidable y el mango de un plástico ligero y duradero. Cuenta con "
"una sierra de metal mediana en el lomo de la hoja y también puede funcionar "
"como un cortador de alambre. Aunque es bastante resistente, no puede mantener "
"un filo muy bien."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Bayonet"
msgid "L-backswerda"
msgid_plural "L-backswerdas"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of variant "L-backswerda"of gun mod "Bayonet"
#. ~ Description of variant "L-backswerda" of item "Bayonet"
msgid ""
"A bayonet, although not of any model you're familiar with.  Despite "
"differences in appearance it seems analogous to any other bayonet - The "
"chrome shaded blade is worn but well-maintained, with a grooved edge on its "
"back to act as a sawing implement.  The handle and guard have some additional "
"mechanisms installed to help affix it to a variety of firearms."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Gun mod name
msgid "National Guard bayonet"
msgid_plural "National Guard bayonets"
msgstr[0] "bayoneta de La Guardia Nacional"
msgstr[1] "bayonetas de La Guardia Nacional"
msgstr[2] "bayonetas de La Guardia Nacional"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of gun mod "National Guard bayonet"
#. ~ Description of "National Guard bayonet"
msgid ""
"A Cold War era Army bayonet that has only partially been replaced by newer "
"models.  It has an apocalypse-proof full-tang, double-edged high steel blade "
"terminating in a spear point.  The no-frills design makes for both a good "
"fighting knife and bayonet, a fact that was appreciated when reserve stocks "
"of these were issued out to National Guardsmen."
msgstr ""
"Una bayoneta del ejército de la guerra fría que ha sido parcialmente "
"reemplazada por modelos más nuevos. Tiene una espiga a prueba de apocalipsis, "
"hoja de acero alto en carbono de doble filo que acaba en una punta de lanza. "
"Su sencillo diseño lo convierte en un buen cuchillo de combate y bayoneta, un "
"hecho que fue apreciado cuando las reservas almacenadas de estas fueron "
"entregadas a la Guardia Nacional."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hunting knife"
msgid_plural "hunting knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de caza"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de caza"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de caza"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "hunting knife"
msgid ""
"Commonly used by hunters, this single-edged sheath knife is designed for "
"cutting and skinning game rather than combat."
msgstr ""
"Comúnmente utilizado por cazadores, este cuchillo de un solo filo está "
"diseñado para cortar y despellejar a los animales, no para el combate."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "KA-BAR knife"
msgid_plural "KA-BAR knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo KA-BAR"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos KA-BAR"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos KA-BAR"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "KA-BAR knife"
msgid ""
"The KA-BAR was developed by the United States Marine Corps in 1942 by "
"modifying hunting knife designs to be more soldier-proof.  The handle is made "
"of stacked leather washers, and the blade is made of easy to sharpen high "
"steel, making for a popular fighting, hunting and utility knife.  The blade "
"is marked 'USMC'."
msgstr ""
"El KA-BAR fue desarrollado por el Cuerpo de Marines de los Estados Unidos en "
"1942 modificando los diseños de los cuchillos de caza para hacerlos más "
"resistentes a los soldados. El mango está hecho de arandelas de cuero "
"apiladas, y la hoja está hecha de acero inoxidable fácil de afilar, por lo "
"que es un cuchillo popular de lucha, caza y utilidad. La hoja está marcada "
"'USMC'."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "survival knife"
msgid_plural "survival knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de supervivencia"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de supervivencia"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de supervivencia"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "survival knife"
msgid ""
"This massive knife features a hollow handle with a compass built into the "
"pommel and a row of fearsome-looking saw teeth along the back of its blade."
msgstr ""
"Este enorme cuchillo tiene una empuñadura hueca con una brújula incorporada "
"en el pomo y una hilera de dientes de sierra imponentes en la parte de atrás "
"de la hoja."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "mild steel survival knife"
msgid_plural "mild steel survival knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de supervivencia de acero dulce"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de supervivencia de acero dulce"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de supervivencia de acero dulce"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "mild steel survival knife"
msgid ""
"This massive knife features a hollow handle with a compass built into the "
"pommel and a row of fearsome-looking saw teeth along the back of its blade.  "
"It's custom-made of mild steel, you could probably find better in a hunting "
"store."
msgstr ""
"Este enorme cuchillo tiene un mango hueco con una brújula integrada en el "
"pomo y una hilera de temibles dientes de sierra en la parte posterior de la "
"hoja. Está hecho a medida con acero dulce, probablemente lo encontrarías "
"mejor en una tienda de caza."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "medium steel survival knife"
msgid_plural "medium steel survival knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de supervivencia de acero medio"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de supervivencia de acero medio"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de supervivencia de acero medio"

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of "medium steel survival knife"
msgid ""
"This massive knife features a hollow handle with a compass built into the "
"pommel and a row of fearsome-looking saw teeth along the back of its blade.  "
"Made of medium steel, this is about as good as store bought."
msgstr ""
"Este enorme cuchillo cuenta con un mango hueco con una brújula incorporada en "
"el pomo y una hilera de dientes de sierra de aspecto temible a lo largo de la "
"parte posterior de su hoja. Hecha de acero medio, es tan buena como las que "
"se compran en la tienda."

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "medium steel survival knife"
msgid "A hidden handle compartment.  Unscrew the compass to access."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
