"countdown starting."
msgstr ""
"Un artefacto explosivo de fabricación casera, consistente en una gran jarra "
"de plástico llena de explosivos militares y restos de metal. Su mecha se ha "
"encendido, comenzando su cuenta atrás."

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ "message" action message of item "homemade bomb"
msgid "You've already lit the fuse - run!"
msgstr "Ya has encendido la mecha - ¡CORRE!"

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "homemade demolition charge"
msgid_plural "homemade demolition charges"
msgstr[0] "carga de demolición casera"
msgstr[1] "cargas de demolición caseras"
msgstr[2] "cargas de demolición caseras"

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Description of "homemade demolition charge"
msgid ""
"An improvised demolition charge.  Use this item to light the fuse.  You will, "
"of course, need a lighter or matches in your inventory to do this.  20 "
"seconds after lighting the fuse, it will explode, so get away!"
msgstr ""
"Una carga de demolición improvisada. Usa este objeto para encender la mecha. "
"Por supuesto, necesitarás un mechero o cerillas en tu inventario. 20 segundos "
"después de encender la mecha, explotará, así que ¡aléjate!"

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "homemade demolition charge"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "acetylene lamp (off)"
#, c-format
msgid "You light the %s."
msgstr "Enciendes la %s."

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "homemade demolition charge (lit)"
msgid_plural "homemade demolition charges (lit)"
msgstr[0] "carga de demolición casera (encendida)"
msgstr[1] "cargas de demolición caseras (encendidas)"
msgstr[2] "cargas de demolición caseras (encendidas)"

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Description of "homemade demolition charge (lit)"
msgid ""
"The fuse on this primitive demolition charge is lit and hissing.  It'll "
"explode any moment now."
msgstr ""
"La mecha de esta primitiva carga de demolición está encendida y silbando. "
"Explotará en cualquier momento."

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "50 L barrel bomb"
msgid_plural "50 L barrel bombs"
msgstr[0] "barril bomba de 50L"
msgstr[1] "barriles bomba de 50L"
msgstr[2] "barriles bomba de 50L"

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Description of "50 L barrel bomb"
msgid ""
"A metal keg filled with stable explosives.  Contains a volatile explosive "
"core, so 100 seconds after the fuse has been lit the charge will detonate "
"completely, delivering its entire destructive power to everything in sight."
msgstr ""
"Un barril de metal lleno de explosivos estables. Contiene un núcleo explosivo "
"volátil, por lo que 100 segundos después de encender la mecha la carga "
"detonará por completo, descargando todo su poder destructivo sobre todo lo "
"que haya a la vista."

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "50 L barrel bomb"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "100 L barrel bomb"
msgid "Activate fuse"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "50 L barrel bomb"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "100 L barrel bomb"
msgid "You activate the fuse on the barrel bomb.  Clear the area!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "active 50 L barrel bomb"
msgid_plural "active 50 L barrel bombs"
msgstr[0] "barril bomba de 50L activado"
msgstr[1] "barriles bomba de 50L activados"
msgstr[2] "barriles bomba de 50L activados"

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Description of "active 50 L barrel bomb"
msgid ""
"A metal keg filled with stable explosives.  The fuse has been lit and once it "
"ignites the primary explosive, the bomb will detonate and rain fire and steel "
"on everything in sight."
msgstr ""
"Un barril de metal lleno de explosivos estables. La mecha se ha encendido y, "
"una vez que prenda el explosivo primario, la bomba detonará y hará llover "
"fuego y acero sobre todo lo que haya a la vista."

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "100 L barrel bomb"
msgid_plural "100 L barrel bombs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "active 100 L barrel bomb"
msgid_plural "active 100 L barrel bombs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "60 mm mortar propellant charge"
msgid_plural "60 mm mortar propellant charges"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#. ~ Description of "60 mm mortar propellant charge"
msgid ""
"Small explosive in a form of donut without a piece, this thing is designed to "
"be attached on the mortar shell tail, to increase the projectile velocity "
"and, therefore, its range.  Since the projectile it was connected to was "
"already shot, you can only cut it for its content."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "electric firestarter"
msgid_plural "electric firestarters"
msgstr[0] "magiclick"
msgstr[1] "magiclicks"
msgstr[2] "magiclicks"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "electric firestarter"
msgid ""
"A crudely-made electric firestarter, which can function as an inefficient "
"lighter."
msgstr ""
"Un simple encendedor eléctrico, que puede funcionar ineficazmente como un "
"mechero normal."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bow fire drill"
msgid_plural "bow fire drills"
msgstr[0] "arco de rodamiento"
msgstr[1] "arcos de rodamiento"
msgstr[2] "arcos de rodamiento"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "bow fire drill"
msgid ""
"A simple item for starting fires with friction between a notched plank and "
"wooden shaft.  The shaft is spun rapidly with a sawing motion by a bowstring "
"wrapped around it.  Very slow to acquire a usable ember."
msgstr ""
"Un sencillo objeto para encender fuego mediante la fricción entre un tablón "
"con muescas y un eje de madera. El eje se hace girar rápidamente con un "
"movimiento de sierra mediante una cuerda de arco enrollada alrededor de él. "
"Muy lento para obtener una brasa utilizable."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pump fire drill"
msgid_plural "pump fire drills"
msgstr[0] "taladro de bombeo para hacer fuego"
msgstr[1] "taladros de bombeo para hacer fuego"
msgstr[2] "taladros de bombeo para hacer fuego"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "pump fire drill"
msgid ""
"A simple item for starting fires by friction between a notched plank and "
"wooden shaft, with a flywheel attached.  The shaft is spun rapidly with a "
"pumping motion by a cord wrapped around it.  Slow to acquire a usable ember."
msgstr ""
"Un objeto sencillo para encender fuego por fricción entre un tablón  dentado "
"y un eje de madera, con un volante de inercia acoplado. El eje se hace girar "
"rápidamente con un movimiento de bombeo mediante una cuerda enrollada a su "
"alrededor. Lento para obtener una brasa utilizable."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "flint and steel"
msgid_plural "sets of flint and steel"
msgstr[0] "yesquero"
msgstr[1] "yesqueros"
msgstr[2] "yesqueros"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "flint and steel"
msgid ""
"A piece of flint paired with a hardened high carbon steel striker.  Use it to "
"spark a flame."
msgstr ""
"Un trozo de pedernal combinado con un percutor de acero de alto carbono "
"endurecido. Se utiliza para encender una llama."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "lighter"
msgid_plural "lighters"
msgstr[0] "mechero"
msgstr[1] "mecheros"
msgstr[2] "mecheros"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "lighter"
msgid ""
"A disposable plastic lighter, capable of creating a small flame with the "
"flick of a finger.  Allows you to use various drugs like cigarettes, light "
"explosives like Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Un mechero de plástico desechable, capaz de generar un pequeña llama con un "
"gesto de dedos. Puede usarse para consumir diversas drogas como los "
"cigarrillos, encender explosivos ligeros como los cócteles molotov, o para "
"prender fuego a otras cosas cercanas."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "magnifying glass"
msgid_plural "magnifying glasses"
msgstr[0] "lupa"
msgstr[1] "lupas"
msgstr[2] "lupas"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "magnifying glass"
msgid ""
"A magnifying glass, for closely examining fine details.  It can also be used "
"for starting fires if direct sunlight is available."
msgstr ""
"Una lupa, para examinar de cerca los detalles finos. También puede utilizarse "
"para encender fuego si se dispone de luz solar directa."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "crude glass lens"
msgid_plural "crude glass lenses"
msgstr[0] "lente de vidrio rústico"
msgstr[1] "lentes de vidrio rústico"
msgstr[2] "lentes de vidrio rústico"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "crude glass lens"
msgid ""
"A very low-quality focusing lens, made from non-optical-grade glass.  Useless "
"for building most optical devices, but you can start a fire with it if "
"sunlight is available."
msgstr ""
"Una lente de muy baja calidad fabricada con vidrio no óptico. No sirve para "
"construir dispositivos ópticos pero se puede usar para encender un fuego si "
"la luz del sol esta disponible."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fire piston"
msgid_plural "fire pistons"
msgstr[0] "pistón de fuego"
msgstr[1] "pistones de fuego"
msgstr[2] "pistones de fuego"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "fire piston"
msgid ""
"A firestarting tool of Southeast Asian origin, consisting of a thin, hollow "
"wooden cylinder sealed at one end and open at the other, and a wooden piston "
"forming an airtight circular seal with it, making use of rapid and adiabatic "
"air compression to ignite a piece of tinder.  It also comes with a tinder "
"container to keep tinder dry.  Use it to start a fire."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta para encender fuego originaria del sudeste asiático, que "
"consiste en un cilindro de madera delgado y hueco, sellado por un extremo y "
"abierto por el otro, y un pistón de madera que forma un sello circular "
"hermético con él, aprovechando la compresión rápida y adiabática del aire "
"para encender un trozo de yesca. También viene con un contenedor de yesca "
"para mantenerla seca. Usar para encender un fuego."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "matchbook"
msgid_plural "matchbooks"
msgstr[0] "librito de cerillas"
msgstr[1] "libritos de cerillas"
msgstr[2] "libritos de cerillas"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "matchbook"
msgid ""
"A small book of matches with a coarse strike surface on the outside flap for "
"lighting them.  Allows you to use various drugs like cigarettes, light "
"explosives like Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire.  Due to the "
"matches being lightly glued to the matchbook, they can be removed, but not "
"replaced on the book."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño librito de cerillas con una superficie rugosa en la solapa "
"exterior para encenderlas. Permite consumir diversas drogas, como "
"cigarrillos, encender explosivos, como cócteles Molotov, o prender fuego a "
"objetos cercanos. Debido a que las cerillas están ligeramente pegadas a la "
"caja de cerillas, pueden quitarse, pero no volver a colocarse en ella."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "survival match"
msgid_plural "survival matches"
msgstr[0] "cerilla de supervivencia"
msgstr[1] "cerillas de supervivencia"
msgstr[2] "cerillas de supervivencia"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "survival match"
msgid "A solid strike anywhere match.  One and done."
msgstr "Una cerilla que se enciende al rozar cualquier superficie. Una y listo."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "matchbox"
msgid_plural "matchboxes"
msgstr[0] "caja de fósforos"
msgstr[1] "cajas de fósforos"
msgstr[2] "cajas de fósforos"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "matchbox"
msgid ""
"A small box of matches with a coarse strike surface on the side for lighting "
"them.  Allows you to use various drugs like cigarettes, light explosives like "
"Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña caja de cerillas con una superficie de golpe gruesa en el lateral "
"para encenderlas. Permite consumir diversas drogas, como cigarrillos, "
"encender explosivos, como cócteles Molotov, o prender fuego a objetos "
"cercanos."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "refillable lighter"
msgid_plural "refillable lighters"
msgstr[0] "mechero recargable"
msgstr[1] "mecheros recargables"
msgstr[2] "mecheros recargables"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "refillable lighter"
msgid ""
"A stylish lighter featuring a flip-top cover and a refuelable tank, capable "
"of creating a small flame with the flick of a finger.  Allows you to use "
"various drugs like cigarettes, light explosives like Molotov cocktails, or "
"light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Un mechero con la tapa abatible y el depósito recargable. Puede usarse para "
"consumir diversas drogas como los cigarrillos, encender explosivos ligeros "
"como los cócteles molotov, o para prender fuego a otras cosas cercanas."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "refillable lighter"
msgid "You flick the lighter."
msgstr "Enciendes el mechero."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "refillable lighter"
msgid ""
"A stylish lighter featuring a flip-top cover and a refuelable tank.  It is "
"lit."
msgstr ""
"Un mechero estilizado con la tapa abatible y un depósito recargable. Está "
"encendido."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "refillable lighter"
msgid "You extinguish the lighter."
msgstr "Apagas el mechero."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "refillable butane lighter"
msgid_plural "refillable butane lighters"
msgstr[0] "mechero de butano recargable"
msgstr[1] "mecheros de butano recargables"
msgstr[2] "mecheros de butano recargables"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "refillable butane lighter"
msgid ""
"A large lighter with a trigger and a safety, reloaded by fitting a can of "
"butane inside the base.  Allows you to use various drugs like cigarettes, "
"light explosives like Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Un mechero grande con gatillo y seguro, que se recarga insertando una lata de "
"butano dentro de la base. Puede usarse para consumir diversas drogas como "
"cigarrillos, encender explosivos como cócteles molotov, o prender fuego a "
"objetos cercanos."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ember carrier"
msgid_plural "ember carriers"
msgstr[0] "braserito"
msgstr[1] "braseritos"
msgstr[2] "braseritos"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "ember carrier"
msgid ""
"A small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to provide a "
"controlled airflow.  It can nurture a smoldering ember for a long time, to "
"start fires without modern tools."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño recipiente para contener yesca, con agujeros perforados para "
"proporcionar un flujo de aire controlado. Puede alimentar una brasa latente "
"durante mucho tiempo, para encender fuego sin herramientas modernas."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "ember carrier"
msgid "You light the tinder."
msgstr "Enciendes la yesca."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "ember carrier"
msgid "The ember carrier is out of tinder."
msgstr "El portador de la brasa se ha quedado sin yesca."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ "need_fire_msg" action message of item "ember carrier"
msgid "You need a lighter or fire to light this."
msgstr "Necesitas un mechero o fuego para encenderla."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ember carrier (lit)"
msgid_plural "ember carriers (lit)"
msgstr[0] "braserito (encendido)"
msgstr[1] "braseritos (encendidos)"
msgstr[2] "braseritos (encendidos)"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "ember carrier (lit)"
msgid ""
"A small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to provide a "
"controlled airflow.  An ember is smoldering inside it, and can be used to "
"start a campfire."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño recipiente para contener yesca, con agujeros perforados para "
"proporcionar un flujo de aire controlado. En su interior arde una brasa que "
"puede utilizarse para encender una hoguera."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "ember carrier (lit)"
msgid "The ember is extinguished."
msgstr "Las brasas se extinguieron."

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "electric lighter"
msgid_plural "electric lighters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "electric lighter"
msgid "A rechargeable electric lighter."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "mini lighter"
msgid_plural "mini lighters"
msgstr[0] "minimechero"
msgstr[1] "minimechero"
msgstr[2] "minimecheros"

#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
#. ~ Description of "mini lighter"
msgid ""
"A miniature disposable plastic lighter, capable of creating a small flame "
"with the flick of a finger.  Allows you to use various drugs, like "
"cigarettes, light explosives like Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on "
"fire."
msgstr ""
"Un mechero de plástico desechable en miniatura, capaz de crear una pequeña "
"llama con sólo mover un dedo. Permite consumir diversas drogas, como "
"cigarrillos, encender explosivos como cócteles Molotov o prender fuego a "
"objetos cercanos."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "crash axe"
msgid_plural "crash axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de accidente"
msgstr[1] "hachas de accidentes"
msgstr[2] "hachas de accidentes"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "crash axe"
msgid ""
"A short, lightweight emergency tool with a quarter-circular blade, a short "
"pick opposite the blade, and an insulated handle.  Used on airplanes to chop "
"down or pry walls or cabinets to gain access in case of a fire."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta de emergencia corta y ligera con un cuarto de hoja circular, "
"un pico corto opuesto a la hoja y un mango aislado. Se utiliza en los aviones "
"para derribar o hacer palanca en paredes o armarios para acceder a ellos en "
"caso de incendio."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "large fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "large fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintor grande"
msgstr[1] "extintores grandes"
msgstr[2] "extintores grandes"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "large fire extinguisher"
msgid ""
"An emergency fire extinguisher containing five gallons of fire-retardant "
"foam.  Useful for putting out adjacent fires."
msgstr ""
"Un extintor de emergencia que contiene 18.9l (5 galones) de espuma retardante "
"contra el fuego. Útil para apagar fuegos cercanos."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fire axe"
msgid_plural "fire axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de bombero"
msgstr[1] "hachas de bombero"
msgstr[2] "hachas de bombero"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "fire axe"
msgid ""
"A large, two-handed pickhead axe normally used by firefighters.  It makes a "
"powerful melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings.  The "
"pickhead is for spiking into doors and glass and is not effective at hooking "
"limbs of opponents."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "fire axe"
msgid "Marrying strap for a Halligan bar."
msgstr "Correa para una barra Halligan."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Halligan bar"
msgid_plural "Halligan bars"
msgstr[0] "barra Halligan"
msgstr[1] "barras Halligan"
msgstr[2] "barras Halligan"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "Halligan bar"
msgid ""
"A heavy, multiple-use tool commonly carried by firefighters, law enforcement, "
"and military rescue units.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying "
"them or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash some heads "
"in."
msgstr ""
"Herramienta pesada de uso múltiple que suelen llevar los bomberos, las "
"fuerzas del orden y las unidades militares de rescate. Úsala para abrir "
"puertas cerradas sin destruirlas o para levantar tapas de alcantarilla. "
"También puedes empuñarla para romper cabezas."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "small fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "small fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintor pequeño"
msgstr[1] "extintores pequeños"
msgstr[2] "extintores pequeños"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "small fire extinguisher"
msgid ""
"A handheld fire extinguisher containing a liter of highly compressed CO2 gas. "
" Useful for putting out adjacent fires."
msgstr ""
"Un extintor portátil que contiene un litro de gas CO2 comprimido. Útil para "
"apagar fuegos cercanos."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "throwable fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintor arrojable"
msgstr[1] "extintores arrojables"
msgstr[2] "extintores arrojables"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid ""
"A fire extinguisher in grenade form.  While not as effective as a regular "
"fire extinguisher, you can use it from a farther distance.  It has a plastic "
"plug that can be pulled, but is primarily activated by heat, so just throw it "
"into the flames."
msgstr ""
"Un extintor en forma de granada. Aunque no es tan eficaz como un extintor "
"normal, se puede utilizar desde una distancia mayor. Tiene un tapón de "
"plástico del que se puede tirar, pero se activa principalmente con el calor, "
"así que basta con lanzarlo a las llamas."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid "Pull plug"
msgstr "Tirar del gancho de seguridad"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid "You pull the plug on the extinguisher grenade."
msgstr "Se tira del pin de la granada extintor."

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "active throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "active throwable fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintore arrojable activo"
msgstr[1] "extintores arrojables activos"
msgstr[2] "extintores arrojables activos"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "active throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid ""
"An active extinguisher grenade, likely to burst any second now.  Better throw "
"it!"
msgstr ""
"Una granada de extinción activa, es probable que estalle en cualquier "
"momento. ¡Mejor lánzala!"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pike pole"
msgid_plural "pike poles"
msgstr[0] "bichero"
msgstr[1] "bicheros"
msgstr[2] "bicheros"

#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
#. ~ Description of "pike pole"
msgid ""
"A durable tool consisting of a sturdy fiberglass shaft tipped with a small "
"steel hook."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta duradera que consiste en un robusto eje de fibra de vidrio "
"con un pequeño gancho de acero en la punta."

