"step above stone-age."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de cobre toscamente trabajado con un mango sencillo. Primitivo, "
"pero un paso por encima de la edad de piedra."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze knife"
msgid_plural "bronze knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de bronce"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de bronce"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de bronce"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "bronze knife"
msgid ""
"A cast bronze knife with a full tang, with a handle wrapped in cord and "
"leather, lovingly work-hardened and sharpened to a fine edge."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de bronce fundido con hoja de espiga completa, con mango envuelto "
"en cordón y cuero, templado con esmero y afilado hasta conseguir un filo fino."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "dive knife"
msgid_plural "dive knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de buzo"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de buzo"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de buzo"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "dive knife"
msgid ""
"A short, sturdy knife with a serrated edge for cutting lines and straps, and "
"a blunt tip for prying.  Used primarily by divers, this knife has been fitted "
"with cork to slow its descent if dropped underwater, so it takes up more "
"space than usual."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo corto y robusto con un filo dentado para cortar cabos, correas, y "
"una punta roma para hacer palanca. Utilizado principalmente por los "
"buceadores, este cuchillo ha sido dotado de corcho para ralentizar su "
"descenso si se deja caer bajo el agua, por lo que ocupa más espacio de lo "
"habitual."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "honey scraper"
msgid_plural "honey scrapers"
msgstr[0] "espátula para miel"
msgstr[1] "espátulas para miel"
msgstr[2] "espátulas para miel"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "honey scraper"
msgid ""
"A sharp, knife-like tool used for harvesting honey from beehives.  Makes a "
"passable melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta afilada parecida a un cuchillo, que se usa para sacar la miel "
"de las colmenas. También puede servir como arma c. a c."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pocket knife"
msgid_plural "pocket knives"
msgstr[0] "navaja"
msgstr[1] "navajas"
msgstr[2] "navajas"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "pocket knife"
msgid ""
"A small pocket knife.  It isn't great for combat, but it's better than "
"nothing.  It's sharp enough to butcher with."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña navaja de bolsillo. No es muy útil en combate, pero es mejor que "
"nada. Y esta bastante afilada como para usarla para descuartizar."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stone knife"
msgid_plural "stone knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de piedra"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de piedra"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de piedra"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "stone knife"
msgid ""
"A sharpened stone set into a hollowed handle.  Not nearly as usable as a "
"proper knife, but it's better than nothing."
msgstr ""
"Una piedra afilada colocada en un mango hueco. No es tan útil como un "
"cuchillo de verdad, pero es mejor que nada."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "boxcutter knife"
msgid_plural "boxcutter knives"
msgstr[0] "cutter"
msgstr[1] "cutters"
msgstr[2] "cutters"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "boxcutter knife"
msgid ""
"A small knife designed for opening boxes.  It could cause some damage, but it "
"really should be used against inanimate objects.  It is too small to "
"effectively butcher corpses with."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo pequeño, diseñado para abrir cajas. Puede causar algo de daño, "
"pero en realidad debería usarse contra objetos inanimados. Es demasiado "
"pequeño para descuartizar cadáveres."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stone chopper"
msgid_plural "stone choppers"
msgstr[0] "cortador de piedra"
msgstr[1] "cortadores de piedra"
msgstr[2] "cortadores de piedra"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "stone chopper"
msgid ""
"A rock with sharpened edges, produced by knapping.  Works as a crude cutting "
"and butchering tool, if nothing else is available."
msgstr ""
"Una piedra con bordes afilados, producida por el tallado lítico. Sirve como "
"herramienta rudimentaria de corte y descuartizado, si no se dispone de otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/weapon_copy_extensions.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "digging stick"
msgid_plural "digging sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo cavador"
msgstr[1] "palos cavadores"
msgstr[2] "palos cavadores"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "digging stick"
msgid ""
"A large stick with the end carved into a broad blade for digging.  It could "
"be used to dig shallow pits, but not deep ones."
msgstr ""
"Un palo grande con el extremo tallado en forma de hoja ancha para cavar. "
"Podía utilizarse para cavar fosas poco profundas, pero no profundas."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "trowel"
msgid_plural "trowels"
msgstr[0] "paleta"
msgstr[1] "paletas"
msgstr[2] "paletas"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "trowel"
msgid "A small, sharp gardening shovel, perfect for digging up grubs and worms."
msgstr "Una pequeña pala afilada de jardinería, perfecta para sacar larvas y gusanos."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hoe"
msgid_plural "hoes"
msgstr[0] "azada"
msgstr[1] "azadas"
msgstr[2] "azadas"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "hoe"
msgid ""
"A farming implement.  You can use it to turn tillable land into a "
"slow-to-cross pile of dirt, or dig a shallow pit."
msgstr ""
"Un apero de labranza. Se puede utilizar para convertir la tierra cultivable "
"en un montón de tierra que se arrastra lentamente o para cavar una fosa poco "
"profunda."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze hoe"
msgid_plural "bronze hoes"
msgstr[0] "azada de bronce"
msgstr[1] "azadas de bronce"
msgstr[2] "azadas de bronce"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "bronze hoe"
msgid ""
"A farming implement made from bronze.  The added heft and durability should "
"let you till soil for farming more easily as well."
msgstr ""
"Un apero de labranza fabricado en bronce. Su peso y durabilidad te permitirán "
"labrar la tierra con mayor facilidad."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden shovel"
msgid_plural "wooden shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala de madera"
msgstr[1] "palas de madera"
msgstr[2] "palas de madera"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "wooden shovel"
msgid ""
"A crude shovel with a shovelhead made from wood, historically used as an "
"alternative to metal shovels when metal was too expensive.  It works passably "
"well, but really can't compare to a metal shovel."
msgstr ""
"Una pala rudimentaria con cabeza de pala hecha de madera, utilizada "
"históricamente como alternativa a las palas de metal cuando éstas eran "
"demasiado caras. Funciona bastante bien, pero no se puede comparar con una "
"pala de metal."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal rake"
msgid_plural "metal rakes"
msgstr[0] "rastrillo de metal"
msgstr[1] "rastrillos de metal"
msgstr[2] "rastrillos de metal"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "metal rake"
msgid "A sturdy metal rake, a must-have during autumn."
msgstr "Un robusto rastrillo de metal, un obligatorio en otoño."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "plastic rake"
msgid_plural "plastic rakes"
msgstr[0] "rastrillo de plástico"
msgstr[1] "rastrillos de plástico"
msgstr[2] "rastrillos de plástico"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "plastic rake"
msgid ""
"A cheap plastic rake.  Will break quite quickly if used for anything other "
"than raking leaves."
msgstr ""
"Un rastrillo de plástico barato. Se romperá rápidamente si se utiliza para "
"otra cosa que no sea rastrillar hojas."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "scythe"
msgid_plural "scythes"
msgstr[0] "guadaña"
msgstr[1] "guadañas"
msgstr[2] "guadañas"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "scythe"
msgid ""
"An old-fashioned farming tool used to cut tall grass.  Despite being a giant "
"blade on the end of a stick, it is incredibly awkward to use for anything but "
"its intended purpose."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta agrícola anticuada utilizada para cortar la hierba alta. A "
"pesar de ser una cuchilla gigante en el extremo de un palo, es increíblemente "
"incómoda de usar para cualquier cosa que no sea su propósito previsto."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "scythe"
msgid ""
"A dull, cheaply-made replica of an old-fashioned farming tool used to cut "
"tall grass."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica aburrida y barata de un antiguo apero de labranza utilizado para "
"cortar la hierba alta."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_melee.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "grim reaper's scythe"
msgid_plural "grim reaper's scythes"
msgstr[0] "guadaña del ángel de la muerte"
msgstr[1] "guadañas del ángel de la muerte"
msgstr[2] "guadañas del ángel de la muerte"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "grim reaper's scythe"
msgid ""
"A long, crooked tool used to reap souls, with a skull engraved in its blade.  "
"Let the harvest begin."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta larga y curva que se utiliza para cosechar almas, tiene un "
"cráneo grabado en su cuchilla. Que comience la cosecha."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "shovel"
msgid_plural "shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala"
msgstr[1] "palas"
msgstr[2] "palas"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "shovel"
msgid "A digging tool.  Use it to dig pits adjacent to your location."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta de excavación. Úsala para cavar fosos adyacentes a tu "
"localización."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "snow shovel"
msgid_plural "snow shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala de nieve"
msgstr[1] "palas de nieve"
msgstr[2] "palas de nieve"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "snow shovel"
msgid ""
"A sturdy metal shovel used for picking up snow and moving it somewhere else.  "
"It was useful before the Cataclysm, but now it's useless."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "plastic snow shovel"
msgid_plural "plastic snow shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala de nieve de plástico"
msgstr[1] "palas de nieve de plástico"
msgstr[2] "palas de nieve de plástico"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "plastic snow shovel"
msgid ""
"A cheap plastic shovel used for picking up snow and moving it somewhere else. "
" It was useful before the Cataclysm, but now it's useless."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stone sickle"
msgid_plural "stone sickles"
msgstr[0] "hoz de piedra"
msgstr[1] "hoces de piedra"
msgstr[2] "hoces de piedra"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "stone sickle"
msgid ""
"A primitive tool for cutting grass.  The sharp, crescent-shaped stone at the "
"end of the handle is barely good enough for the job."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta primitiva para cortar hierba. La afilada piedra en forma de "
"media luna del extremo del mango apenas sirve para este trabajo."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json data/mods/MMA/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sickle"
msgid_plural "sickles"
msgstr[0] "hoz"
msgstr[1] "hoces"
msgstr[2] "hoces"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "sickle"
msgid ""
"An old-fashioned farming tool for cutting tall grass.  Despite being a "
"massive curved blade on a handle, it is incredibly awkward to use for "
"anything but its intended purpose."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta agrícola anticuada para cortar hierba alta. A pesar de ser "
"una enorme cuchilla curvada con mango, es increíblemente incómoda de usar "
"para cualquier cosa que no sea su propósito previsto."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze sickle"
msgid_plural "bronze sickles"
msgstr[0] "hoz de bronce"
msgstr[1] "hoces de bronce"
msgstr[2] "hoces de bronce"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "bronze sickle"
msgid ""
"A handheld grass-cutting tool with a cast bronze blade, fastened to a wood "
"handle wrapped with leather."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta manual para cortar hierba con una hoja de bronce fundido, "
"sujeta a un mango de madera envuelto en cuero."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bill"
msgid_plural "bills"
msgstr[0] "hocino"
msgstr[1] "hocinos"
msgstr[2] "hocinos"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "bill"
msgid ""
"A long, slightly curved and hooked steel blade on the end of a sturdy shaft.  "
"Could be used to thoroughly ruin something's day, or cut branches and small "
"trees."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla larga de acero levemente curvada con forma de gancho, con una "
"empuñadura resistente. Se puede usar para arruinarle el día a alguien o para "
"cortar ramas y arbustos."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze bill"
msgid_plural "bronze bills"
msgstr[0] "hocino de bronce"
msgstr[1] "hocinos de bronce"
msgstr[2] "hocinos de bronce"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "bronze bill"
msgid ""
"A long, slightly curved and hooked bronze blade on the end of a sturdy shaft. "
" Could be used to thoroughly ruin something's day, or cut branches and small "
"trees."
msgstr ""
"Una larga hoja de bronce ligeramente curvada y ganchuda en el extremo de un "
"mango robusto. Puede usarse para arruinarle el día a alguien o para cortar "
"ramas y árboles pequeños."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hedge trimmer (off)"
msgid_plural "hedge trimmers (off)"
msgstr[0] "cortasetos (off)"
msgstr[1] "cortasetos (off)"
msgstr[2] "cortasetos (off)"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "hedge trimmer (off)"
msgid ""
"A cordless, double-sided, gasoline-powered hedge trimmer.  A long line of "
"sharp-edged teeth extends from the engine; turning the trimmer on will make "
"them rapidly vibrate.  The poor man's chainsaw as far as the zombies are "
"concerned."
msgstr ""
"Un cortasetos a combustible, sin cable y de doble filo. Una larga línea de "
"dientes afilados se extienden desde el motor. Al encender el cortasetos hace "
"que vibren rápidamente. Es la motosierra del pobre, en cuanto a lo que "
"concierne a los zombis."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ value of variable 'success_message' in effect in EoC
#. "EOC_toolweapon_activate__trimmer" in use action of item "hedge trimmer
#. (off)"
msgid "With a roar, the hedge trimmer leaps to life!"
msgstr "¡Con un rugido, el cortasetos cobra vida!"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hedge trimmer (on)"
msgid_plural "hedge trimmers (on)"
msgstr[0] "cortasetos (on)"
msgstr[1] "cortasetos (on)"
msgstr[2] "cortasetos (on)"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "hedge trimmer (on)"
msgid ""
"A cordless, double-sided, gasoline-powered hedge trimmer.  It is currently "
"on, ready to do some zombie topiary; use this item to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"Un cortasetos a combustible, sin cable y de doble filo. Está encendido, listo "
"para podar artísticamente algún zombi. Usar para apagar."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ value of variable 'sound_message' in effect in EoC
#. "EOC_toolweapon_running__trimmer" in use action of item "hedge trimmer
#. (on)"
msgid "Your hedge trimmer rumbles."
msgstr "Tu cortasetos retumba."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "atomic lamp"
msgid_plural "atomic lamps"
msgstr[0] "lámpara atómica"
msgstr[1] "lámparas atómicas"
msgstr[2] "lámparas atómicas"

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Description of "atomic lamp"
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this very "
"expensive lamp will emit a small amount of light for at least a decade.  "
"Before the Cataclysm, it was mostly an expensive way to show off your "
"preparedness.  Now, it's actually really useful.  Use it to close the cover "
"and hide the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la desintegración nuclear y los LED de baja "
"energía, esta carísima lámpara emitirá una pequeña cantidad de luz durante al "
"menos una década. Antes del cataclismo, era sobre todo una forma cara de "
"presumir de estar preparado. Ahora, es realmente útil. Usar para cerrar la "
"tapa y ocultar la luz."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/items/tools/lighting.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic lamp"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "everglow matrix lamp (uncovered)"
msgid "You close the lamp's cover."
msgstr "Cierras la cubierta de la lámpara."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "atomic lamp (covered)"
msgid_plural "atomic lamps (covered)"
msgstr[0] "lámpara atómica (cubierta)"
msgstr[1] "lámparas atómicas (cubiertas)"
msgstr[2] "lámparas atómicas (cubiertas)"

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Description of "atomic lamp (covered)"
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this very "
"expensive lamp will emit a small amount of light for at least a decade.  "
"Before the Cataclysm, it was mostly an expensive way to show off your "
"preparedness.  Now, it's actually really useful.  The cover is closed.  Use "
"it to open the cover and show the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la desintegración nuclear y los LED de baja "
"energía, esta carísima lámpara emitirá una pequeña cantidad de luz durante al "
"menos una década. Antes del cataclismo, era sobre todo una forma cara de "
"presumir de estar preparado. Ahora, es realmente útil. La tapa está cerrada. "
"Usar para abrir la tapa y mostrar la luz."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/items/tools/lighting.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic lamp (covered)"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "everglow matrix lamp (covered)"
msgid "You open the lamp's cover."
msgstr "Abres la cubierta de la lámpara."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "atomic reading light"
msgid_plural "atomic reading lights"
msgstr[0] "luz atómica de lectura"
msgstr[1] "luces atómicas de lectura"
msgstr[2] "luces atómicas de lectura"

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Description of "atomic reading light"
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this extremely "
"expensive little light will provide just enough light to read by for at least "
"a decade.  It is also available with a cute cartoon bear cover to turn it "
"into a nightlight for a very wealthy child with a fear of the dark.  Use it "
"to close the cover and hide the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la descomposición nuclear y los LEDs de baja "
"energía, esta pequeña luz extremadamente cara proporcionará la luz suficiente "
"para leer durante al menos una década. También está disponible con una linda "
"cubierta de oso de dibujos animados para convertirla en una luz nocturna para "
"un niño muy rico con miedo a la oscuridad. Úsalo para cerrar la cubierta y "
"esconder la luz."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic reading light"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "magical reading light"
msgid "You close the nightlight's cover."
msgstr "Cierras la cubierta del velador."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "atomic reading light (covered)"
msgid_plural "atomic reading lights (covered)"
msgstr[0] "luz atómica de lectura (cubierta)"
msgstr[1] "luces atómicas de lectura (cubiertas)"
msgstr[2] "luces atómicas de lectura (cubiertas)"

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Description of "atomic reading light (covered)"
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this extremely "
"expensive little light will provide just enough light to read by for at least "
"a decade.  It is also available with a cute cartoon bear cover to turn it "
"into a nightlight for a very wealthy child with a fear of the dark.  The "
"cover is closed.  Use it to open the cover and show the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la descomposición nuclear y los LEDs de baja "
"energía, esta pequeña luz extremadamente cara proporcionará la luz suficiente "
"para leer durante al menos una década. También está disponible con una linda "
"cubierta de oso de dibujos animados para convertirla en una luz nocturna para "
"un niño muy rico con miedo a la oscuridad. La cubierta está cerrada. Úsala "
"para abrir la tapa y mostrar la luz."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic reading light (covered)"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "magical reading light (covered)"
msgid "You open the nightlight's cover."
msgstr "Abres la cubierta del lampara de noche."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "candle"
msgid_plural "candles"
msgstr[0] "vela"
msgstr[1] "velas"
msgstr[2] "velas"

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#. ~ Description of "candle"
msgid ""
"A thick wax candle.  It doesn't provide very much light, but it can burn for "
"quite a long time.  You'll need a lighter or matches to light it."
msgstr ""
"Una vela de cera gruesa. No proporciona mucha luz, pero puede arder durante "
"bastante tiempo. Necesitarás un mechero o cerillas para encenderla."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/caster_level_boosters.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "candle"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "small candle"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "kelvinist's candle (off)"
msgid "You light the candle."
msgstr "Enciendes la vela."

#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
