msgstr[2] "peces de dorados"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "goldfish"
msgid ""
"Yes, this is that common pet fish.  Though, given its size and the fact that "
"it's still alive, you can take a wild guess that this one is feral."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bowfin"
msgid_plural "bowfins"
msgstr[0] "amia calva"
msgstr[1] "amias calva"
msgstr[2] "amias calva"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bowfin"
msgid ""
"A bowfin.  These fish are related to gar but without the huge teeth, "
"skin-rending scales, and aggression."
msgstr ""
"Amia calva. Estos peces están relacionados con el gar pero sin los enormes "
"dientes, las escamas desgarradoras de la piel y la agresión."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "longnose gar"
msgid_plural "longnose gar"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "longnose gar"
msgid "A large ancient type of fish with a mean jaw and poisonous eggs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "burbot"
msgid_plural "burbots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "burbot"
msgid ""
"A relatively large fish that looks like a cross between a catfish and an eel, "
"and is the only freshwater fish from the order that cods hail from."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lake sturgeon"
msgid_plural "lake sturgeon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lake sturgeon"
msgid ""
"A very large armored bottom-feeder, the lake sturgeon is one of the largest "
"unmutated fish one can find in the freshwater regions of New England."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "shortnose sturgeon"
msgid_plural "shortnose sturgeon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "shortnose sturgeon"
msgid ""
"While the shortnose sturgeon is still large, it is nothing compared to its "
"cousin - the lake sturgeon.  What really sets it apart, however, is its "
"signature shorter snout."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fallfish"
msgid_plural "fallfish"
msgstr[0] "Semotilus corporalis"
msgstr[1] "semotilus corporalis"
msgstr[2] "semotilus corporalis"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fallfish"
msgid "A fallfish.  These fish are small cyprinids, related to carp."
msgstr "Un fallfish. Estos peces son pequeños ciprínidos, relacionados con las carpas."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lobster"
msgid_plural "lobsters"
msgstr[0] "langosta"
msgstr[1] "langostas"
msgstr[2] "langostas"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lobster"
msgid ""
"A dark greenish crustacean in its natural habitat.  These were once "
"considered pests barely worth eating, then some marketing genius started "
"selling them to people as a delicacy and they took off in popularity… and "
"price."
msgstr ""
"Un crustáceo de color verde oscuro en su hábitat natural. Antes se "
"consideraba una plaga que apenas merecía la pena comer, pero un genio de la "
"mercadotecnia empezó a venderlos como un manjar y su popularidad se "
"disparó... y su precio."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "crayfish"
msgid_plural "crayfish"
msgstr[0] "cangrejo de rio"
msgstr[1] "cangrejos de rio"
msgstr[2] "cangrejos de rio"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "crayfish"
msgid ""
"This crustacean looks like a tiny lobster, but is actually a completely "
"different species.  If you could get ahold of a bunch more of these, a hefty "
"pot of boiling water, and some spicy seasonings…"
msgstr ""
"Este crustáceo parece una langosta diminuta, pero en realidad es una especie "
"completamente diferente. Si pudieras conseguir un montón de ellas, una olla "
"grande de agua hirviendo y algunos condimentos picantes..."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "crustacean larva"
msgid_plural "crustacean larvae"
msgstr[0] "larva de crustáceo"
msgstr[1] "larvas de crustáceo"
msgstr[2] "larvas de crustáceo"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "crustacean larva"
msgid ""
"A minuscule half-translucent crustacean larva.  Impossible to identify which "
"species it belongs to."
msgstr ""
"Una larva de crustáceo minúscula y medio translucida. Imposible identificar a "
"que especie pertenece."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "American eel"
msgid_plural "American eels"
msgstr[0] "Anguila americana"
msgstr[1] "Anguilas americanas"
msgstr[2] "Anguilas americanas"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "American eel"
msgid ""
"An American eel.  They used to be quite common in these parts until the dams "
"were built.  They'll get a second chance now that those aren't running."
msgstr ""
"Una anguila americana. Solían ser bastante comunes en estas partes hasta que "
"se construyeron las presas. Tendrán una segunda oportunidad ahora que esas no "
"funcionan."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "oversized crayfish"
msgid_plural "oversized crayfish"
msgstr[0] "cangrejo de río de gran tamaño"
msgstr[1] "cangrejos de río de gran tamaño"
msgstr[2] "cangrejos de río de gran tamaño"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "oversized crayfish"
msgid ""
"A mutant crayfish the size of a dog, with a brown carapace, claws, and long "
"antennae."
msgstr ""
"Un cangrejo mutante del tamaño de un perro con un caparazón marrón, garras y "
"largas antenas."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant crayfish"
msgid_plural "giant crayfish"
msgstr[0] "cangrejo de rio gigante"
msgstr[1] "cangrejos de rio gigantes"
msgstr[2] "cangrejos de rio gigantes"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish"
msgid ""
"A mutant, terrestrial variety of crayfish, this massive crustacean resembles "
"a humongous lobster."
msgstr ""
"Una variedad mutante terrestre de cangrejo de río, este crustáceo masivo "
"parece una langosta gigantesca."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "colossal crayfish"
msgid_plural "colossal crayfish"
msgstr[0] "cangrejo de rio colosal"
msgstr[1] "cangrejos de rio colosales"
msgstr[2] "cangrejos de rio colosales"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "colossal crayfish"
msgid "An enormous mutated gray crayfish with pincer claws and long antennae."
msgstr "Un enorme cangrejo gris mutado con garras de pinza y largas antenas."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant crayfish larva"
msgid_plural "giant crayfish larvae"
msgstr[0] "larva de cangrejo de río gigante"
msgstr[1] "larvas de cangrejo de río gigante"
msgstr[2] "larvas de cangrejo de río gigante"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant crayfish larva"
msgid "A large crayfish larva already larger than non-mutated adults of its kind."
msgstr ""
"Una larva de cangrejo de río grande, ya más grande que los adultos no mutados "
"de su especie."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "razorclaw"
msgid_plural "razorclaws"
msgstr[0] "garracuchilla"
msgstr[1] "garracuchillas"
msgstr[2] "garracuchillas"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "razorclaw"
msgid ""
"A man-sized crustacean clad in iron-like chitin, capable of emitting horrible "
"shrieking noises.  Often spotted near shipwrecks or other dark, damp places, "
"which it uses as nesting grounds."
msgstr ""
"Crustáceo del tamaño de un hombre revestido de quitina similar al hierro, "
"capaz de emitir horribles chillidos. A menudo se le ve cerca de naufragios u "
"otros lugares oscuros y húmedos, que utiliza como lugar de anidación."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant carp"
msgid_plural "giant carps"
msgstr[0] "carpa gigante"
msgstr[1] "carpas gigantes"
msgstr[2] "carpas gigantes"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant carp"
msgid ""
"This thing looks like a carp, but huge and very, very angry.  Death is the "
"gift of the carp god."
msgstr ""
"Esta cosa parece una carpa, pero enorme y muy, muy enfadada. La muerte es el "
"regalo del dios carpa."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant salmon"
msgid_plural "giant salmon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant salmon"
msgid ""
"A mutated salmon roughly the size of a person.  Quite dangerous to the "
"inexperienced angler."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "huge salmon"
msgid_plural "huge salmon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "huge salmon"
msgid "A huge mutant salmon grown almost to the size of an alligator."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "leaper salmon"
msgid_plural "leaper salmon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "leaper salmon"
msgid ""
"A huge mutant salmon, one that outgrows even the other ones present.  On its "
"sides, beneath the fins, are visible two flesh-colored tubes which propel "
"water as it leaps."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "seweranha"
msgid_plural "seweranhas"
msgstr[0] "piraña de cloaca"
msgstr[1] "pirañas de cloaca"
msgstr[2] "pirañas de cloaca"

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "seweranha"
msgid ""
"A large, mutant variety of carp.  It has shimmering green scales and a mouth "
"lined with three jagged rows of razor-sharp teeth."
msgstr ""
"Una variedad mutada de una carpa grande. Tiene escamas verdes relucientes y "
"una boca con tres filas dentadas con dientes afilados como navajas."

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Atlantic mackerel"
msgid_plural "Atlantic mackerel"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic mackerel"
msgid "An Atlantic mackerel, known for its distinctive striped pattern."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "summer flounder"
msgid_plural "summer flounder"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "summer flounder"
msgid ""
"A flatfish, the summer flounder, also known as a fluke, likes to stay "
"camouflaged against the ocean floor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "black sea bass"
msgid_plural "black sea bass"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "black sea bass"
msgid ""
"A small, robust fish, the black sea bass is known for its dark, mottled color "
"and meaty texture."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "scup"
msgid_plural "scup"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "scup"
msgid ""
"Also known as porgy, the scup is a small fish commonly found in Atlantic "
"coastal waters, recognizable by its silver body with blue and purple tinges."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bluefish"
msgid_plural "bluefish"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bluefish"
msgid ""
"The bluefish, a moderately proportioned marine fish, is known for its "
"aggressive nature and sharp teeth.  It sports a distinct blue-green "
"coloration."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Atlantic cod"
msgid_plural "Atlantic cod"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic cod"
msgid ""
"A large, white-meat fish known for its mild flavor and flaky texture.  Highly "
"prized in both commercial and recreational fishing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "haddock"
msgid_plural "haddock"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "haddock"
msgid ""
"A popular food fish, the haddock is recognized by its dark lateral line and a "
"black blotch above the pectoral fin."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgid_plural "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgid ""
"One of the largest and fastest fish in the waters of New England, the bluefin "
"tuna is a streamlined predator with a dark blue back and silvery sides."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Atlantic halibut"
msgid_plural "Atlantic halibut"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic halibut"
msgid ""
"The largest flatfish in the ocean, known for its dense, firm texture and mild "
"flavor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pollock"
msgid_plural "pollock"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pollock"
msgid ""
"A member of the cod family, pollock is a versatile fish known for its white, "
"delicate meat and mild taste."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal blossom"
msgid_plural "fungal blossoms"
msgstr[0] "capullo fúngico"
msgstr[1] "capullos fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "capullos fúngicos"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal blossom"
msgid ""
"A broad fungus, looking much like a glowing blue sunflower.  It appears to "
"emit finer spores than the typical fungal emission."
msgstr ""
"Un hongo ancho, muy parecido a un brillante girasol azul. Parece emitir "
"esporas más finas que las que emiten típicamente los hongos."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal hedgerow"
msgid_plural "fungal hedgerows"
msgstr[0] "seto fúngico"
msgstr[1] "setos fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "setos fúngicos"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal hedgerow"
msgid ""
"Looking at first glance like a dull gray privet, this \"hedge\" is really a "
"mass of barbed fungal tendrils, defending the fungal tower."
msgstr ""
"A primera vista, parece un aburrido ligustro gris, pero este \"seto\" es en "
"realidad una masa de tentáculos fúngicos con púas, que defienden la torre "
"fúngica."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json data/json/monsters/misc.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/changeling.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/nightmares_and_chimeras.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "fungal hedgerow"
#. ~ Death message of monster "fungal wall"
#. ~ Death message of monster "spore cloud"
#. ~ Death message of monster "ancient red dragon"
#. ~ Death message of monster "vengeance spirit"
#. ~ Death message of monster "will-o-wisp"
#. ~ Death message of monster "will-o'-the-wisp"
#. ~ Death message of monster "flying shark"
#. ~ Death message of monster "endless snake"
#. ~ Death message of monster "swarm of teeth"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s disintegrates!"
msgstr "¡%s se desintegra!"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal tendril"
msgid_plural "fungal tendrils"
msgstr[0] "tentáculos fúngico"
msgstr[1] "tentáculos fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "tentáculos fúngicos"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal tendril"
msgid "A long and delicate-looking tendril with a sharp tip."
msgstr "Un zarcillo largo y aparentemente delicado, con la punta afilada."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal wall"
msgid ""
"A veritable wall of fungus, grown as a natural defense by the fungal spire.  "
"New spores erupt from the surface every few seconds, and tendrils constrict "
"around it, pulling new mass into its shape.  They move with an inexorable "
"strength that could snap limbs."
msgstr ""
"Un verdadero muro de hongos, cultivado como una defensa natural por la espira "
"de los hongos. Nuevas esporas salen de la superficie cada pocos segundos, y "
"los tentáculos se estrechan a su alrededor, atrayendo nueva masa a su forma. "
"Se mueven con una fuerza inexorable que podría romper las extremidades."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json data/mods/CrazyCataclysm/crazy_monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungaloid"
msgid_plural "fungaloids"
msgstr[0] "fungaloide"
msgstr[1] "fungaloides"
msgstr[2] "fungaloides"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungaloid"
msgid ""
"A pale white fungus, one meaty gray stalk supporting a bloom at the top.  "
"Spores are periodically expelled from its gills, and a few tendrils extend "
"from the base, allowing mobility and some basic means of defense."
msgstr ""
"Es un pálido hongo blanco, un tallo carnoso gris arriba del cual se apoya el "
"sombrero. De vez en cuando, algunas esporas son despedidas por sus branquias "
"y algunos tentáculos se extienden desde su base, lo que le permite moverse y "
"tener medios para defenderse."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungaloid shambler"
msgid_plural "fungaloid shamblers"
msgstr[0] "desastre fungaloide"
msgstr[1] "desastres fungaloides"
msgstr[2] "desastres fungaloides"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungaloid shambler"
msgid ""
"A large white fungus, a bulging gray stalk supporting a bloom at the top.  "
"Spores float from its gills and tendrils extend from the base.  Chunks of "
"rock, metal, bone, and wood are held by tendrils as a kind of armor."
msgstr ""
"Un gran hongo blanco, un tallo gris abultado que sostiene una floración en la "
"parte superior. Las esporas flotan desde sus branquias y los tentáculos se "
"extienden desde la base. Trozos de roca, metal, hueso y madera son sostenidos "
"por los tentáculos como una especie de armadura."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of special attack of monster "fungaloid shambler"
msgid "The fungaloid shambler throws a rock!"
msgstr "¡El desastre fungaloide lanza una piedra!"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal spire"
msgid_plural "fungal spires"
msgstr[0] "torre fúngica"
msgstr[1] "torres fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "torres fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal spire"
msgid ""
"An enormous fungal spire, towering over the ground.  It pulsates slowly, "
"continuously growing new defenses."
msgstr ""
"Es una enorme torre fúngica, que se eleva desde el cielo. Palpita lentamente "
"y está generando continuamente nuevas defensas."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant fungal blossom"
msgid_plural "giant fungal blossoms"
msgstr[0] "capullo fúngico gigante"
msgstr[1] "capullos fúngicos gigantes"
msgstr[2] "capullos fúngicos gigantes"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant fungal blossom"
msgid ""
"An immense fungal blossom, towering over its surroundings.  It pulses with a "
"soft blue glow, continuously pumping its spores into the air."
msgstr ""
"Un inmenso capullo fúngico, que sobresale en el paisaje. Palpita con un "
"brillo azul suave, y está continuamente tirando esporas en el aire."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_fungal.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain_pink.json
#. ~ Monster name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "fungal tower"
msgid_plural "fungal towers"
msgstr[0] "torre fúngica"
msgstr[1] "torres fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "torres fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal tower"
msgid ""
"An enormous fungal tower.  On closer inspection, its cap is supported by LOTS "
"of fungal tendrils of various thicknesses, emerging from yet more bristling "
"tendrils at ground level.  Between this redundancy and their noticeable "
"movement creating frequent gaps, it's tough to get a solid shot on the thing."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme torre fúngica. Mirando más de cerca, su parte de arriba está "
"apoyado en MUCHOS tentáculos de diferentes grosores, que emergen de más "
"tentáculos erizados que están en el suelo. Entre esta repetición y su "
"movimiento notable para crear grietas frecuentes, es difícil poder dispararle "
"a la cosa."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal sporeling"
msgid_plural "fungal sporelings"
msgstr[0] "espora fúngica"
msgstr[1] "esporas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "esporas fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal sporeling"
msgid ""
"A fungal stalk several feet in height.  Two vicious-looking tendrils extend "
"from its thorned and leathery exterior, and it moves about faster than the "
"larger fungaloids."
msgstr ""
"Un tallo de hongo de más de un metro de alto. Dos tentáculos de apariencia "
"feroz se extienden desde el curtido tallo que está lleno de espinas. Se mueve "
"un poco más rápido que los fungaloides más grandes."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "spore cloud"
msgid_plural "spore clouds"
msgstr[0] "nube de esporas"
msgstr[1] "nubes de esporas"
msgstr[2] "nubes de esporas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "spore cloud"
msgid "A mass of spores the size of a balled fist, wafting around in the air."
msgstr "Es una masa de esporas del tamaño de puños flotando por el aire."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal ant"
msgid_plural "fungal ants"
msgstr[0] "hormiga fúngica"
msgstr[1] "hormigas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "hormigas fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal ant"
msgid ""
"Pale, sickly gray in color, this giant ant's cracked exoskeleton is barely "
"held together by coils of fungus erupting from every joint in its body."
msgstr ""
"Esta hormiga gigante, pálida, de un gris enfermizo, tiene el exoesqueleto "
"roto y sus partes están sostenidos por espirales de hongos que salen por cada "
"articulación de su cuerpo."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal spider"
msgid_plural "fungal spiders"
msgstr[0] "araña fúngica"
msgstr[1] "arañas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "arañas fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal spider"
msgid ""
"The abdomen of this sickly-looking giant spider is now home to many lumps of "
"blooming fungi.  It leaves behind a trail of tainted secretions as it "
"struggles to drag itself along the ground."
msgstr ""
"El abdomen de esta araña gigante de aspecto enfermizo alberga ahora muchos "
"bultos de hongos en flor. Deja tras de sí un rastro de secreciones "
"contaminadas mientras se esfuerza por arrastrarse por el suelo."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal wasp"
msgid_plural "fungal wasps"
msgstr[0] "avispa fúngica"
msgstr[1] "avispas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "avispas fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal wasp"
msgid ""
"A huge wasp the size of a large cat.  It's bright yellow markings have faded "
"and ripped to show a disgusting mass of mold and rot beneath.  Her wings jut "
"into extremely odd angles, making flight impossible.  Even still, it chases "
"anything without any sense of self-preservation."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal wasp guard"
msgid_plural "fungal wasp guards"
msgstr[0] "avispa guardiana fúngica"
msgstr[1] "avispas guardianas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "avispas guardianas fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal wasp guard"
msgid ""
"A wasp worker split down the middle.  While it's condition looks fatal, it "
"doesn't seem to die, supposedly by the large mushroom growing from once it's "
"wings were.  It's emotionless face still seems to cry with pain and anger."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal wasp queen"
msgid_plural "fungal wasp queens"
msgstr[0] "avispa reina fúngica"
msgstr[1] "avispas reinas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "avispas reinas fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal wasp queen"
msgid ""
"A mutated wasp queen that has been consumed by a sickly gray mold covering "
"it's body.  Abandoning it's duty to laying eggs, it seemingly searches for "
"anything to attack, as a mist of spores emit from it's mandibles."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant fungal wasp"
msgid_plural "giant fungal wasps"
msgstr[0] "avispa gigante fúngica"
msgstr[1] "avispas gigantes fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "avispas gigantes fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant fungal wasp"
msgid ""
"A gigantic wasp worker, It's body now a host for a plethora of mushrooms and "
"spores.  Her abdomen glows faintly with a blue light, each pulse bringing a "
"new crack for fungal growths to escape from.  It's stinger seems to have a "
"soul of it's own, reaching out towards anything that isn't infested like "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"Una avispa obrera gigantesca, su cuerpo es ahora huésped de una plétora de "
"hongos y esporas. Su abdomen brilla débilmente con una luz azul, cada pulso "
"trae una nueva grieta por la que escapan los hongos. Su aguijón parece tener "
"alma propia, alcanzando todo lo que no esté infestado como él."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant fungal wasp guard"
msgid_plural "giant fungal wasp guards"
msgstr[0] "avispa guardiana gigante fúngica"
msgstr[1] "avispas guardianas gigantes fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "avispas guardianas gigantes fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant fungal wasp guard"
msgid ""
"A wasp worker which seems to move like a puppet on strings.  It ambles "
"backwards, its stinger, grotesquely swollen and pulsating, serving as a "
"perverse compass guiding it forward, seeking relentlessly for "
"something—anything—to pierce.  It periodically contracts and then abruptly "
"expands, ejecting a fine mist of spores into the surrounding air."
msgstr ""
"Un trabajador avispa que parece moverse como una marioneta con cuerdas. "
"Avanza lentamente hacia atrás, su aguijón, grotescamente hinchado y "
"palpitante, sirve como una brújula perversa que lo guía hacia adelante, "
"buscando incansablemente algo, cualquier cosa, para perforar. Periódicamente "
"se contrae y luego se expande abruptamente, expulsando una fina niebla de "
"esporas al aire circundante."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant fungal wasp queen"
msgid_plural "giant fungal wasp queens"
msgstr[0] "avispa reina gigante fúngica"
msgstr[1] "avispas reinas gigantes fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "avispas reinas gigantes fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant fungal wasp queen"
msgid ""
"The head of this colossal queen wasp appears to be attached by only a few "
"slender threads, wobbling precariously as additional tendrils sprout from the "
"silky white exoskeleton.  Her batch of eggs has decayed due to lack of proper "
"care, yet they seem to twitch, as if something within is attempting to break "
"free from the hardened shells."
msgstr ""
"La cabeza de esta colosal avispa reina parece estar unida solo por unos pocos "
"hilos delgados, tambaleándose precariamente mientras brotan nuevos tentáculos "
"del exoesqueleto blanco sedoso. Su remesa de huevos se ha deteriorado debido "
"a la falta de cuidado adecuado, sin embargo, parecen moverse, como si algo "
"dentro estuviera intentando liberarse de las cáscaras endurecidas."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal bee"
msgid_plural "fungal bees"
msgstr[0] "abeja fúngica"
msgstr[1] "abejas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "abejas fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal bee"
msgid ""
"A mutant bee the size of a small dog.  It's fur, once used to collect pollen "
"has been trapped with thousands of spores.  it moves erratically on the "
"ground, seemingly having great difficulty to keep any sense of coordination "
"as visible growths of mold worsen underneath the thin hairs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant fungal bee"
msgid_plural "giant fungal bees"
msgstr[0] "abeja gigante fúngica"
msgstr[1] "abejas gigantes fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "abejas gigantes fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant fungal bee"
msgid ""
"A sickly-sweet smelling gray goo pours from the mandibles of this dog-sized "
"insect, stirs an odd sense of hunger within you.  However, the writhing "
"syringe-looking needle and thick plumes of spores around quickly quell your "
"appetite."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "alpha fungal bee"
msgid_plural "alpha fungal bees"
msgstr[0] "abeja alfa fúngica"
msgstr[1] "abejas alfa fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "abejas alfa fúngicas"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "alpha fungal bee"
msgid ""
"This oversized insect's every move is coerced by a seemingly invisible "
"entity, like a puppet on strings.  Thousands of live spores fume from it's "
"mandibles, forming thick clouds.  A stark blue gel leaks from it's "
"splintering limbs, bubbling and sizzling, revealing soft, pulsing gray "
"material beneath."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "whispering fungi"
msgid_plural "whispering fungis"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "whispering fungi"
msgid ""
"Large, yellow, coral-like fungi grow from this spot, their spires riddled "
"with intersecting holes.  Despite lack of wind, it seems to wave at a set "
"rhythm, occasionally pulsing out spores.  A chorus of weak, whistly voices, "
"mixed with different accents and languages—some you recognize, others that "
"seem like meaningless gibberish—emanates from it."
msgstr ""

