msgstr[2] "cachorros de labrador"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Labrador puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Labrador puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult "
"dog."
msgstr ""
"Es un cachorrito de labrador, adorable e indefenso. Mucho más fácil de "
"domesticar que uno adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/json/snippets/home_pictures.json
#. ~ Monster name
#. ~ Snippet in category "<dog_breed>"
#. ~ Dog breeds, just grabbed a handful from our monster list.
msgid "bulldog"
msgid_plural "bulldogs"
msgstr[0] "bulldog"
msgstr[1] "bulldogs"
msgstr[2] "bulldogs"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bulldog"
msgid ""
"The American bulldog is a hardy, well-built dog that seems suited for "
"surviving the apocalypse."
msgstr ""
"El bulldog americano es un perro resistente y bien construido, que parece "
"adecuado para sobrevivir al apocalipsis."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bulldog puppy"
msgid_plural "bulldog puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de bulldog"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de bulldog"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de bulldog"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bulldog puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless American bulldog puppy.  Much safer to tame than an "
"adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de bulldog americano. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pit bull mix"
msgid_plural "pit bull mixes"
msgstr[0] "mezcla de pit bull"
msgstr[1] "mezclas de pit bull"
msgstr[2] "mezclas de pit bull"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pit bull mix"
msgid ""
"The oft-misunderstood pit bull is not actually a single breed but a label for "
"several kinds of terriers.  It has average abilities, and is well-known for "
"its 'lock jaw' - which isn't real, but its incredible determination is."
msgstr ""
"El a menudo incomprendido pit bull no es en realidad una sola raza, sino una "
"etiqueta para varios tipos de terrier. Tiene habilidades promedio, y es bien "
"conocido por su \"mandíbula de bloqueo\", que no es real, pero su increíble "
"determinación sí lo es."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pit bull puppy"
msgid_plural "pit bull puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de pit bull"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de pit bull"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de pit bull"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pit bull puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless pit bull puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult "
"dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de pit bull. Mucho más seguro de domesticar "
"que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/json/snippets/home_pictures.json
#. ~ Monster name
#. ~ Snippet in category "<dog_breed>"
#. ~ Dog breeds, just grabbed a handful from our monster list.
msgid "beagle"
msgid_plural "beagles"
msgstr[0] "beagle"
msgstr[1] "beagles"
msgstr[2] "beagles"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "beagle"
msgid ""
"An adorable beagle that has managed to survive the apocalypse.  Small and "
"agile, but not especially tough.  Generally attacks in packs."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable beagle que ha conseguido sobrevivir al apocalipsis. Pequeño y "
"ágil, pero no especialmente resistente. Suele atacar en manada."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "beagle puppy"
msgid_plural "beagle puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de beagle"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de beagle"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de beagle"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "beagle puppy"
msgid "An adorable, defenseless beagle puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de beagle. Mucho más seguro de domesticar "
"que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "border collie"
msgid_plural "border collies"
msgstr[0] "border collie"
msgstr[1] "border collies"
msgstr[2] "border collies"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "border collie"
msgid ""
"An athletic and hyperactive dog that loves to herd animals and jump, the "
"Border Collie is an agile attacker.  Although they can be easy to train, they "
"don't work well in packs."
msgstr ""
"Un perro atlético e hiperactivo al que le encanta arrear animales y saltar, "
"el Border Collie es un ágil atacante. Aunque pueden ser fáciles de entrenar, "
"no funcionan bien en manadas."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "border collie puppy"
msgid_plural "border collie puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de border collie"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de border collie"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de border collie"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "border collie puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Border Collie puppy.  Much safer to tame than an "
"adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de Border Collie. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "boxer mastiff"
msgid_plural "boxer mastiffs"
msgstr[0] "mastín boxer"
msgstr[1] "mastines boxer"
msgstr[2] "mastines boxer"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "boxer mastiff"
msgid ""
"An ordinary breed full of affection, the boxer mastiff doesn't otherwise "
"stand out among other dogs with its capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "boxer puppy"
msgid_plural "boxer puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de boxer"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de boxer"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de boxer"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "boxer puppy"
msgid "An adorable, defenseless boxer puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de boxer. Mucho más seguro de domesticar que "
"un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Chihuahua"
msgid_plural "Chihuahuas"
msgstr[0] "Chihuahua"
msgstr[1] "Chihuahuas"
msgstr[2] "Chihuahuas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Chihuahua"
msgid ""
"It's a tiny Chihuahua.  How it has managed to survive is a miracle, although "
"its small size and aggressive nature may have proven useful."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño Chihuahua. La forma en que ha logrado sobrevivir es un milagro, "
"aunque su pequeño tamaño y su naturaleza agresiva pueden haber sido útiles."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Chihuahua puppy"
msgid_plural "Chihuahua puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de chihuahua"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de chihuahua"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de chihuahua"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Chihuahua puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Chihuahua puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult "
"dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de chihuahua. Mucho más seguro de domesticar "
"que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "dachshund"
msgid_plural "dachshunds"
msgstr[0] "dachshund"
msgstr[1] "dachshunds"
msgstr[2] "dachshunds"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "dachshund"
msgid ""
"A wiener dog!  This awkward looking dog can be a useful watchdog, plus it "
"looks adorable as it bumbles around.  Needless to say, it doesn't make a good "
"attack dog."
msgstr ""
"Un perro salchicha. Este perro de aspecto torpe puede ser un útil perro "
"guardián, además de tener un aspecto adorable cuando va dando tumbos. No hace "
"falta decir que no es un buen perro de ataque."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "dachshund puppy"
msgid_plural "dachshund puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de dachshund"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de dachshund"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de dachshund"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "dachshund puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless dachshund puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult "
"dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de perro salchicha. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "German shepherd"
msgid_plural "German shepherds"
msgstr[0] "pastor alemán"
msgstr[1] "pastores alemanes"
msgstr[2] "pastores alemanes"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "German shepherd"
msgid ""
"The original K-9 breed.  An easily trained and powerful attack dog that will "
"defend its owner to the death, however they don't work well in packs."
msgstr ""
"La raza K-9 original. Un perro de ataque fácil de entrenar y poderoso que "
"defenderá a su dueño hasta la muerte, sin embargo no funcionan bien en "
"manadas."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "German shepherd puppy"
msgid_plural "German shepherd puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de pastor alemán"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de pastor alemán"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de pastor alemán"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "German shepherd puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless German Shepherd puppy.  Much safer to tame than an "
"adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de pastor alemán. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Great Pyrenees"
msgid_plural "Great Pyrenees"
msgstr[0] "Gran Pirineo"
msgstr[1] "Grandes Pirineos"
msgstr[2] "Grandes Pirineos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Great Pyrenees"
msgid ""
"A large and powerful breed, the Great Pyrenees has a beautiful, thick white "
"coat.  Originally bred to deter wolves and other predators, now faced with "
"protecting livestock from shambling hordes of undead."
msgstr ""
"Una raza grande y poderosa, el Gran Pirineo tiene un hermoso y grueso pelaje "
"blanco. Originalmente criado para disuadir a los lobos y otros depredadores, "
"ahora se enfrenta a la protección del ganado de las hordas de muertos "
"vivientes."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Great Pyrenees puppy"
msgid_plural "Great Pyrenees puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de gran pirineo"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de gran pirineo"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de gran pirineo"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Great Pyrenees puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Great Pyrenees puppy.  Much safer to tame than an "
"adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de Gran Pirineo. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "rottweiler"
msgid_plural "rottweilers"
msgstr[0] "rottweiler"
msgstr[1] "rottweilers"
msgstr[2] "rottweilers"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "rottweiler"
msgid ""
"A terrifying breed to face feral, Rottweilers are descended from Roman legion "
"mastiffs.  It's robust, vicious, and quite capable of mauling a human to "
"death."
msgstr ""
"Una raza aterradora para enfrentarse a lo salvaje, los Rottweilers descienden "
"de los mastines de la legión romana. Es robusto, feroz, y bastante capaz de "
"matar a un humano hasta la muerte."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "rottweiler puppy"
msgid_plural "rottweiler puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de rottweiler"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de rottweiler"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de rottweiler"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "rottweiler puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Rottweiler puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult "
"dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de Rottweiler. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "cattle dog"
msgid_plural "cattle dogs"
msgstr[0] "perro de ganado"
msgstr[1] "perros de ganado"
msgstr[2] "perros de ganado"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "cattle dog"
msgid ""
"An agile and sturdy breed that is welcome on any farm, the Australian cattle "
"dog is adept at leaping fences and herding livestock."
msgstr ""
"Es una raza resistente y ágil, bienvenida en cualquier granja. El perro "
"pastor australiano es capaz de saltar sobre cercos y pastorear ganado."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "cattle dog puppy"
msgid_plural "cattle dog puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de perro de ganado"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de perro de ganado"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de perro de ganado"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "cattle dog puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Australian cattle dog puppy.  Much safer to tame "
"than an adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de perro de ganado australiano. Mucho más "
"seguro de domesticar que un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Samoyed"
msgid_plural "Samoyeds"
msgstr[0] "samoyedo"
msgstr[1] "samoyedos"
msgstr[2] "samoyedos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Samoyed"
msgid ""
"A large, white, fluffy herding dog from Siberia.  Samoyeds are rarely "
"aggressive: Their smiley face doesn't help either.  They can be agile for "
"their size and can be taught to pull sleds."
msgstr ""
"Un perro de pastoreo grande, blanco y esponjoso de Siberia. Los samoyedos "
"rara vez son agresivos: Su cara sonriente tampoco ayuda. Pueden ser ágiles "
"para su tamaño y se les puede enseñar a tirar de los trineos."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Samoyed puppy"
msgid_plural "Samoyed puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de samoyedo"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de samoyedo"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de samoyedo"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Samoyed puppy"
msgid "An adorable, defenseless Samoyed puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro samoyedo. Mucho más seguro de domesticar que "
"un perro adulto."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Flat-coated Retriever"
msgid_plural "Flat-coated Retrievers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Flat-coated Retriever"
msgid ""
"A large, black retriever with a luxurious, glossy coat and almond-shaped "
"brown eyes that glitter with intelligence.  The Flat-coated Retriever has a "
"temperament that can only be described as 'superb', having the energy to "
"accompany humans who love physical activity, and the loyalty to lay around "
"with those that do not.  Flat-coated Retriever will often do little more than "
"bark at potential threats."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Flat-coated Retriever puppy"
msgid_plural "Flat-coated Retriever puppies"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Flat-coated Retriever puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Flat-coated Retriever puppy.  Much safer to tame "
"than an adult dog."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fox"
msgid_plural "foxes"
msgstr[0] "zorro"
msgstr[1] "zorros"
msgstr[2] "zorros"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fox"
msgid ""
"A small, omnivorous canine with almost cat-like mannerisms.  It is a solitary "
"hunter, and one of the only canids able to climb trees."
msgstr ""
"Un cánido pequeño y omnívoro, con un comportamiento casi felino. Es un "
"cazador solitario y uno de los únicos cánidos capaces de trepar a los árboles."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fox"
msgid ""
"The red fox, an omnivorous canine and largest of the true foxes, it is a wily "
"hunter with a combative, suspicious temperament."
msgstr ""
"Un zorro rojo, un canino omnívoro y el más grande de los zorros verdaderos. "
"Es un cazador astuto con un temperamento combativo y suspicaz."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "groundhog"
msgid_plural "groundhogs"
msgstr[0] "marmota"
msgstr[1] "marmotas"
msgstr[2] "marmotas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "groundhog"
msgid ""
"Also known as the woodchuck, this ground squirrel has no actual talent for "
"chucking wood."
msgstr "La marmota es una ardilla menos ágil, no la vas a ver trepando los árboles."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "snowshoe hare"
msgid_plural "snowshoe hares"
msgstr[0] "liebre americana"
msgstr[1] "liebres americanas"
msgstr[2] "liebres americanas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "snowshoe hare"
msgid ""
"A small grass-eater with a brown fur coat that changes to white in the "
"wintertime."
msgstr "Un pequeño herbívoro con pelaje marrón que cambia a blanco en invierno."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "snowshoe hare kit"
msgid_plural "snowshoe hare kits"
msgstr[0] "cria de liebre americana"
msgstr[1] "crias de liebre americana"
msgstr[2] "crias de liebre americana"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "snowshoe hare kit"
msgid "A tiny and very cute snowshoe hare kit."
msgstr "Una cria de liebre america diminuta y muy mona."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "foal"
msgid_plural "foals"
msgstr[0] "potrillo"
msgstr[1] "potrillos"
msgstr[2] "potrillos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "foal"
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and "
"powerful-looking muscles.  This one is still a juvenile; it'll take a while "
"before it can be ridden."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero herbívoro con pezuñas, melena, cola larga y músculos poderosos. "
"Este es todavía joven; pasará un tiempo antes de que se le pueda montar."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "horse"
msgid_plural "horses"
msgstr[0] "caballo"
msgstr[1] "caballos"
msgstr[2] "caballos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#: data/mods/Megafauna/monsters/mf_domestic.json
#. ~ Description of monster "horse"
#. ~ Description of monster "Scott's horse"
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and "
"powerful-looking muscles.  A stalwart companion to humans for longer than "
"recorded history, with some effort you should be able to get this one to "
"trust you enough to ride it."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero de pastoreo con pezuñas, pelo, cola y músculos poderosos. "
"Compañero incondicional de los humanos desde hace más tiempo que la historia, "
"con un poco de esfuerzo podrás conseguir que confíe en ti lo suficiente como "
"para montarlo."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mon_horse_police"
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and "
"powerful-looking muscles.  This one has been trained to have less of a fear "
"reaction in order to assist with riot control and standard police work.  With "
"some effort, you should be able to get this one to trust you enough to ride "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero herbívoro con pezuñas, melena, cola larga y músculos poderosos. "
"Se lo ha adiestrado para que reaccione con menos miedo, con el fin de ayudar "
"en el control de disturbios y en el trabajo policial habitual. Con un poco de "
"esfuerzo, conseguirás que confíe en ti lo suficiente como para montarlo."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lemming"
msgid_plural "lemmings"
msgstr[0] "lemming"
msgstr[1] "lemmings"
msgstr[2] "lemmings"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lemming"
msgid ""
"The Northern bog lemming, a small, predominantly vegetarian rodent that "
"spends its life in the murk of swamps and other wetlands.  Contrary to "
"popular belief, these creatures are not particularly hapless or suicidal, but "
"they can eat themselves into scarcity within a few generations."
msgstr ""
"Un lemming de las ciénagas del norte, es un roedor pequeño, predominantemente "
"vegetariano que pasa su vida en la oscuridad de los pantanos y otras zonas "
"húmedas. Al contrario de la creencia popular, estas criaturas no son "
"desgraciadas o suicidas, pero pueden volverse escasas en un par de "
"generaciones."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mink"
msgid_plural "minks"
msgstr[0] "visón"
msgstr[1] "visones"
msgstr[2] "visones"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mink"
msgid ""
"The American mink, a partially aquatic weasel, once factory-farmed for its "
"fur.  It is a capable fisher, but the presence of otters in these parts makes "
"it rely more on food from the land."
msgstr ""
"El visón americano, una comadreja parcialmente acuática, una vez cultivada en "
"fábrica por su piel. Es un pescador capaz, pero la presencia de nutrias en "
"estas partes hace que dependa más de la comida de la tierra."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "moose"
msgid_plural "moose"
msgstr[0] "alce"
msgstr[1] "alces"
msgstr[2] "alces"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "moose"
msgid ""
"The Eastern moose, the largest living species of deer.  While they aren't "
"typically aggressive unless provoked, the autumn mating season can make the "
"bulls quite ill-tempered."
msgstr ""
"El alce oriental, la mayor especie viva de ciervo. Aunque no suelen ser "
"agresivos a menos que se les provoque, la temporada de apareamiento de otoño "
"puede hacer que los machos sean bastante malhumorados."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "moose calf"
msgid_plural "moose calves"
msgstr[0] "cría de alce"
msgstr[1] "crías de alce"
msgstr[2] "crías de alce"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "moose calf"
msgid ""
"The baby moose is called a calf.  They can outrun a human within days of "
"birth and gain weight at an incredible pace."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "great tusked moose"
msgid_plural "great tusked moose"
msgstr[0] "gran alce colmilludo"
msgstr[1] "grandes alces colmilludos"
msgstr[2] "grandes alces colmilludos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "great tusked moose"
msgid ""
"A mutant variety of megafauna that evolved after the Cataclysm.  Easily "
"recognized by the underslung tusks off each side of the mouth, in addition to "
"an impressive rack of antlers.  Given the looks and how aggressive normal "
"moose are, you reckon you shouldn't test the patience of this one."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "tusked moose calf"
msgid_plural "tusked moose calves"
msgstr[0] "cría de alce colmilludo"
msgstr[1] "crías de alce colmilludo"
msgstr[2] "crías de alce colmilludo"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "tusked moose calf"
msgid ""
"The baby moose is called a calf and so are its mutant descendants.  They can "
"outrun a human within days of birth and gain weight at an incredible pace."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "muskrat"
msgid_plural "muskrats"
msgstr[0] "rata almizclera"
msgstr[1] "ratas almizcleras"
msgstr[2] "ratas almizcleras"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "muskrat"
msgid ""
"A large omnivorous rodent with a thick furry pelt, found in wetlands across "
"the Northern Hemisphere.  It marks its territory with a musky odor for which "
"it is named."
msgstr ""
"Un roedor omnívoro grande con un pelaje peludo y gruesoa, que se encuentra en "
"los humedales del hemisferio norte. Marca su territorio con un olor "
"almizclado por el que recibe su nombre."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "opossum"
msgid_plural "opossums"
msgstr[0] "zarigüeya"
msgstr[1] "zarigüeyas"
msgstr[2] "zarigüeyas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "opossum"
msgid ""
"The Virginia opossum, a small omnivorous marsupial native to North America.  "
"About the size of a cat, it is hardy and adaptive, and a fairly common sight "
"in urban areas."
msgstr ""
"Es la zarigüeya de Virginia, un pequeño marsupial omnívoro nativo de América "
"del Norte. Más o menos del tamaño de un gato, robusto y de fácil adaptación, "
"es común verlo en las zonas urbanas."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "skunk"
msgid_plural "skunks"
msgstr[0] "mofeta"
msgstr[1] "mofetas"
msgstr[2] "mofetas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "skunk"
msgid ""
"The common striped skunk, similar in size to opossum or domestic cats, these "
"mammals can often be smelled before they are seen."
msgstr ""
"La mofeta rayada común, de tamaño similar al de las zarigüeyas o los gatos "
"domésticos, estos mamíferos suelen olerse antes de verse."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "skunk"
msgid "A skunk raises its tail and squirts!"
msgstr "¡Una mofeta levanta la cola y lanza un chorro!"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "otter"
msgid_plural "otters"
msgstr[0] "nutria"
msgstr[1] "nutrias"
msgstr[2] "nutrias"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "otter"
msgid ""
"The North American river otter, a shy water-dwelling relative of the weasel "
"that lives in large families along the banks of streams.  It is an excellent "
"fisher and a resourceful survivor, using the abandoned dens of beavers and "
"other animals to raise its own young."
msgstr ""
"La nutria de río de Norte América es un tímido pariente de la comadreja que "
"vive en familias grandes a lo largo de las orillas de los arroyos. Es un "
"excelente pescador y un ingenioso superviviente, que utiliza las madrigueras "
"abandonadas de castores y otros animales para criar a sus propias crías."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "piglet"
msgid_plural "piglets"
msgstr[0] "lechón"
msgstr[1] "lechones"
msgstr[2] "lechones"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "piglet"
msgid ""
"A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and "
"inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral.  Unlike the fully "
"grown version, this juvenile can be tamed."
msgstr ""
"Un omnívoro domesticado descendiente del jabalí, inteligente e inquisitivo. "
"Dejado a su suerte, se ha vuelto salvaje. A diferencia de la versión "
"completamente desarrollada, puede ser domesticado."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pig"
msgid_plural "pigs"
msgstr[0] "cerdo"
msgstr[1] "cerdos"
msgstr[2] "cerdos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pig"
msgid ""
"A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and "
"inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral."
msgstr ""
"Un omnívoro domesticado que desciende del jabalí salvaje. Es inteligente y "
"curioso. Dejado a su propio cuidado, se ha vuelto salvaje."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "rabbit"
msgid_plural "rabbits"
msgstr[0] "conejo"
msgstr[1] "conejos"
msgstr[2] "conejos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "domestic rabbit"
msgid_plural "domestic rabbits"
msgstr[0] "conejo doméstico"
msgstr[1] "conejos domésticos"
msgstr[2] "conejos domésticos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "domestic rabbit"
msgid ""
"A small mammal with a cute wiggling nose, a cotton ball tail, and a body made "
"of delicious flesh."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño mamífero con una simpática nariz que se menea, una cola de bola de "
"algodón y un cuerpo hecho de deliciosa carne."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "domestic rabbit kit"
msgid_plural "domestic rabbit kits"
msgstr[0] "cria de conejo doméstico"
msgstr[1] "crias de conejos domésticos"
msgstr[2] "crias de conejos domésticos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "domestic rabbit kit"
msgid ""
"A tiny bunny with a cute wiggling nose, a cotton ball tail, and a body made "
"of delicious flesh."
msgstr ""
"Un conejito diminuto con una simpática nariz que se mueve, una cola de "
"algodón y un cuerpo de deliciosa carne."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "cottontail rabbit"
msgid_plural "cottontail rabbits"
msgstr[0] "conejo cola de algodón"
msgstr[1] "conejos cola de algodón"
msgstr[2] "conejos cola de algodón"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "cottontail rabbit"
msgid ""
"A brown-coated cottontail rabbit, with a fluffy white tail.  Its small size "
"and docile nature makes it easy prey for predators, at least the ones that "
"can catch it.  You can't tell which one of the two cottontail species from "
"the region this is."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "cottontail rabbit kit"
msgid_plural "cottontail rabbit kits"
msgstr[0] "cria de conejo cola de algodón"
msgstr[1] "crias de conejo cola de algodón"
msgstr[2] "crias de conejo cola de algodón"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "cottontail rabbit kit"
msgid "A tiny and very cute cottontail rabbit kit."
msgstr "Una pequeña y monísima cria de conejo de cola de algodón."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "raccoon"
msgid_plural "raccoons"
msgstr[0] "mapache"
msgstr[1] "mapaches"
msgstr[2] "mapaches"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "raccoon"
msgid ""
"A small mammal native to North America, distinctive for its dexterous paws "
"and facial markings.  It is resourceful and agile enough to open sealed "
"containers in search of food."
msgstr ""
"Pequeño mamífero originario de América del Norte, que se distingue por la "
"destreza de sus patas y sus marcas faciales. Es lo suficientemente ingenioso "
"y ágil como para abrir recipientes cerrados en busca de comida."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "brown rat"
msgid_plural "brown rats"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "brown rat"
msgid ""
"The brown rat is a worm-tailed rodent with long whiskers and beady eyes, "
"larger than its cousin, the black rat.  Widespread mostly wherever humans "
"are, they live off of foraging and will eat whatever they can find."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lamb"
msgid_plural "lambs"
msgstr[0] "cordero"
msgstr[1] "corderos"
msgstr[2] "corderos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lamb"
msgid ""
"A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever "
"domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero de pastoreo, tímido y con pezuñas, y uno de los primeros animales "
"domesticados. Su cuerpo está cubierto de una gruesa capa de lana."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "sheep"
msgid_plural "sheep"
msgstr[0] "oveja"
msgstr[1] "ovejas"
msgstr[2] "ovejas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "sheep"
msgid ""
"A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever "
"domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool, and the males "
"have long, spiraling horns."
msgstr ""
"Un tímido mamífero de pastoreo con pezuñas, y uno de los primeros animales "
"domesticados. Su cuerpo está cubierto de una gruesa capa de lana, y los "
"machos tienen largos cuernos en espiral."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "kid"
msgid ""
"A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything.  "
"The young are famously cute and cuddly."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero herbívoro con pezuñas conocido por trepar y comer casi cualquier "
"cosa. Las crías son adorables y cariñosas."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "goat"
msgid_plural "goats"
msgstr[0] "cabra"
msgstr[1] "cabras"
msgstr[2] "cabras"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "goat"
msgid ""
"A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything.  "
"Either gender can have horns."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero ramoneador con pezuñas conocido por trepar y comer casi cualquier "
"cosa. Ambos sexos pueden tener cuernos."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "squirrel"
msgid_plural "squirrels"
msgstr[0] "ardilla"
msgstr[1] "ardillas"
msgstr[2] "ardillas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "squirrel"
msgid ""
"A small granivorous rodent with a long bushy tail, often seen darting amid "
"the branches of trees.  A skittish varmint with an expression of unwavering "
"austerity, it is the mortal enemy of cat and dog alike."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño roedor granívoro con una cola larga y tupida, a menudo se la ve "
"corriendo a toda velocidad entre las ramas de los árboles. Una alimaña "
"asustadiza con expresión de austeridad inquebrantable. Es el enemigo mortal "
"de los gatos y los perros."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "squirrel"
msgid ""
"A tiny opportunistic rodent with a long bushy tail.  The pine squirrel is "
"clever and cute, and hunted by nearly everything in the woods with a taste "
"for meat."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño roedor oportunista con una cola larga y tupida. La ardilla de "
"pino es linda e inteligente, y es cazada por casi todo lo que anda por el "
"bosque que tenga ganas de comer carne."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "weasel"
msgid_plural "weasels"
msgstr[0] "comadreja"
msgstr[1] "comadrejas"
msgstr[2] "comadrejas"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "weasel"
msgid ""
"The long-tailed weasel, a small but ubiquitous predator whose range extends "
"across the continent.  It forms its den in small burrows, preferring to "
"occupy the nesting holes of its prey."
msgstr ""
"Es una comadreja de cola larga, es un depredador roedor pequeño pero que está "
"por todas partes del continente. Arma su nido en pequeñas madrigueras, y "
"prefiere ocupar las madrigueras de su presa."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/zombified_monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "wolf"
msgid_plural "wolfs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "wolf"
msgid ""
"A cunning pack predator, once extinct in the New England area, the wolf was "
"successfully reintroduced and their numbers reached record highs in the "
"decade before the Cataclysm.  Lucky you."
msgstr ""
"Un astuto depredador de manada, una vez extinguido en el área de Nueva "
"Inglaterra, el lobo fue reintroducido con éxito y su número alcanzó niveles "
"récord en la década anterior al Cataclismo. Qué suerte."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "wolf puppy"
msgid_plural "wolf puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de lobo"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de lobo"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de lobo"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "wolf puppy"
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless wolf pup that will, in time, grow into a "
"not-so-defenseless and debatably-adorable wolf.  Be careful of its parents, "
"who are sure to be around nearby!"
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de lobo que, con el tiempo, se convertirá en "
"un lobo no tan indefenso y discutiblemente adorable. Ten cuidado con sus "
"padres, que seguro que andan cerca."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "reindeer"
msgid_plural "reindeer"
msgstr[0] "reno"
msgstr[1] "renos"
msgstr[2] "renos"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer"
msgid ""
"Also known as the caribou, this deer is native to North America and parts of "
"Eurasia.  Although usually friendly, they can be aggressive during the autumn "
"and winter mating season as well as when hungry."
msgstr ""
"También conocido como caribú, este ciervo es originario de América del Norte "
"y partes de Eurasia. Aunque suele ser amistoso, puede ser agresivo durante la "
"época de apareamiento en otoño e invierno, así como cuando tiene hambre."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "reindeer fawn"
msgid_plural "reindeer fawns"
msgstr[0] "cervatillo de reno"
msgstr[1] "cervatillos de reno"
msgstr[2] "cervatillos de reno"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer fawn"
msgid ""
"A juvenile caribou, it is smaller than its adult counterparts, as well as "
"having shorter antlers."
msgstr ""
"Un caribú joven, es más pequeño que sus homólogos adultos, además de tener "
"una cornamenta más corta."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "llama calf"
msgid_plural "llama calfs"
msgstr[0] "ternero de llama"
msgstr[1] "terneros de llama"
msgstr[2] "terneros de llama"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "llama calf"
msgid ""
"A baby llama.  Unlike their parents, the calves tend to be more friendly in "
"demeanor."
msgstr ""
"Una cría de llama. A diferencia de sus padres, las crías suelen tener un "
"comportamiento más amistoso."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "llama"
msgid_plural "llamas"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "llama"
msgid ""
"A big and wooly herbivore domesticated by the Andean cultures of South "
"America.  Llamas and their kin are distant relatives to camels and are "
"adapted to mountain environments."
msgstr ""
"Un herbívoro grande y lanudo domesticado por las culturas andinas de "
"Sudamérica. Las llamas y sus congéneres son parientes lejanos de los camellos "
"y están adaptados a entornos montañosos."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "ferret"
msgid_plural "ferrets"
msgstr[0] "hurón"
msgstr[1] "hurones"
msgstr[2] "hurones"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "ferret"
msgid ""
"Domesticated from the European polecat, this sleek and energetic mammal was "
"commonly kept as a pet before the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"Domesticado a partir del hurón europeo, este mamífero esbelto y enérgico se "
"solía tener como mascota antes del Cataclismo."

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "ferret kit"
msgid_plural "ferret kits"
msgstr[0] "cría de hurón"
msgstr[1] "crías de hurón"
msgstr[2] "crías de hurón"

#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#. ~ Description of monster "ferret kit"
msgid "A young domesticated ferret, known as a kit."
msgstr "Un hurón doméstico joven, conocido como cría."

#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Marloss zealot"
msgid_plural "Marloss zealots"
msgstr[0] "fanático de Marloss"
msgstr[1] "fanáticos de Marloss"
msgstr[2] "fanáticos de Marloss"

#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Marloss zealot"
msgid ""
"Her eyes lie vacant and spittle foams in her mouth, as she recites from the "
"hymns in rapturous ecstasy."
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos están vacíos y escupe espuma en su boca, mientras recita los himnos "
"en un éxtasis extático."

#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Marloss zealot"
msgid ""
"His eyes lie vacant and spittle foams in his mouth, as he recites from the "
"hymns in rapturous ecstasy."
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos están vacíos y escupe espuma en su boca, mientras recita los himnos "
"en un éxtasis extático."

#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "X-03: 'Specter' Recon Mech"
msgid_plural "X-03: 'Specter' Recon Mechs"
msgstr[0] "X-03: Meca de Reconocimiento 'Espectro'"
msgstr[1] "X-03: Mecas de Reconocimiento 'Espectro'"
msgstr[2] "X-03: Mecas de Reconocimiento 'Espectro'"

#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "X-03: 'Specter' Recon Mech"
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo RMES (Recon Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be used in a "
"scout-recon-sniper role, due to its mobility, integrated laser sniper rifle, "
"and suite of optics for target designation and battlefield awareness.  It was "
"not deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a few prototypes in "
"the field.  You may be able to hack it to accept you as its pilot.  Like all "
"mech-suits, it can act as a UPS from its large battery."
msgstr ""
"El Boeing-Daewoo EMR (Exoesqueleto Mecánico de Reconocimiento), una "
"adquisición reciente del ejército de los Estados Unidos, fue diseñado para "
"ser utilizado en una función de explorador-reconocimiento-francotirador, "
"debido a su movilidad y a su rifle de francotirador láser integrado y al "
"conjunto de ópticas para la designación de objetivos y el conocimiento del "
"campo de batalla. No se desplegó antes del impacto del Cataclismo, aunque "
"había algunos prototipos en el campo. Es posible que puedas hackearlo para "
"que te acepte como su piloto. Como todos los trajes meca, puede actuar como "
"un SEU por su gran batería."

#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mech"
msgid_plural "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mechs"
msgstr[0] "X-02: Mecade Combate 'Grunt'"
msgstr[1] "X-02: Mecas de Combate 'Grunt'"
msgstr[2] "X-02: Mecas de Combate 'Grunt'"

#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mech"
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo CMES (Combat Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be used in a fire "
"support role, due to its fearsome integrated Gatling laser.  It was not "
"deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a few prototypes in the "
"field.  You may be able to hack it to accept you as its pilot.  Like all "
"mech-suits, it can act as a UPS from its large battery."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "X-01: 'Jack' Lifting Mech"
msgid_plural "X-01: 'Jack' Lifting Mechs"
msgstr[0] "X-01: Meca de Elevación 'Jack'."
msgstr[1] "X-01: Mecas de Elevación 'Jack'."
msgstr[2] "X-01: Mecas de Elevación 'Jack'."

#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "X-01: 'Jack' Lifting Mech"
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo LMES (Lifting Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be piloted by an "
"operator to load and unload heavy material, and for limited combat support "
"roles.  It was not deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a few "
"prototypes in the field.  You may be able to hack it to accept you as its "
"pilot.  Like all mech-suits, it can act as a UPS from its large battery."
msgstr ""
"El Boeing-Daewoo EME (Exoesqueleto Mecánico de Elevación), una reciente "
"adquisición del ejército de los EE.UU., fue diseñado para ser pilotado por un "
"operador para cargar y descargar material pesado, y para funciones limitadas "
"de apoyo al combate, no fue desplegado antes del impacto del Cataclismo, "
"aunque había unos pocos prototipos en el campo. Es posible que puedas "
"hackearlo para que te acepte como su piloto. Como todos los trajes meca, "
"puede actuar como un SEU por su gran batería."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go"
msgid_plural "mi-gos"
msgstr[0] "mi-go"
msgstr[1] "mi-gos"
msgstr[2] "mi-gos"

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json data/mods/MindOverMatter/monsters/mi_go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go"
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go lightbringer"
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go mindrender"
msgid ""
"An alien creature of uncertain origin.  Its shapeless pink body bears "
"numerous sets of paired appendages of unknown function, and a pair of ribbed, "
"membranous wings which seem to be quite useless.  Its odd, vaguely "
"pyramid-shaped head bristles with numerous wavering antennae, and it moves "
"with an uncanny fluidity on its many legs."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura alienígena de origen incierto. Su cuerpo rosado e amorfo está "
"provisto de numerosos apéndices emparejados de función desconocida y un par "
"de alas membranosas y estriadas que parecen bastante inútiles. Su extraña "
"cabeza, vagamente piramidal, está provista de numerosas antenas oscilantes y "
"se mueve con una fluidez extraña sobre sus numerosas patas."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go slaver"
msgid_plural "mi-go slavers"
msgstr[0] "esclavo mi-go"
msgstr[1] "esclavos mi-go"
msgstr[2] "esclavos mi-go"

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go slaver"
msgid ""
"An alien creature of uncertain origin.  Its shapeless pink body bears "
"numerous sets of paired appendages of unknown function, and a pair of ribbed, "
"membranous wings which seem to be quite useless.  Its odd, vaguely "
"pyramid-shaped head bristles with numerous wavering antennae, and it moves "
"with an uncanny fluidity on its many legs.  It is carrying an oblong object "
"that hums with an odd keening sound."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura alienígena de origen incierto. Su cuerpo rosa sin forma tiene "
"numerosos conjuntos de apéndices de función desconocida, y un par de alas "
"acanaladas y membranosas que parecen ser bastante inútiles. Su cabeza "
"extraña, vagamente en forma de pirámide, se eriza con numerosas antenas "
"vacilantes, y sus movimientos son fluidamente asombrosos en sus muchas "
"piernas. Lleva un objeto oblongo que zumba con un extraño sonido agudo."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go slaver"
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go guard"
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go myrmidon"
msgid "The mi-go's numerous antennae sync their movements for a brief moment."
msgstr ""
"Las numerosas antenas del mi-go sincronizan sus movimientos durante un breve "
"momento."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go surgeon"
msgid_plural "mi-go surgeons"
msgstr[0] "cirujano mi-go"
msgstr[1] "cirujanos mi-go"
msgstr[2] "cirujanos mi-go"

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go surgeon"
msgid ""
"This mi-go has a slender body with snaking carapace along it, and even more "
"paired clawed appendages.  Its claws are smaller and more delicate looking, "
"but that does not make them less unnerving."
msgstr ""
"Este mi-go tiene un cuerpo delgado con un caparazón serpenteante a lo largo "
"de él, e incluso más apéndices con garras emparejadas. Sus garras son más "
"pequeñas y de aspecto más delicado, pero eso no las hace menos inquietantes."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go guard"
msgid_plural "mi-go guards"
msgstr[0] "guardia mi-go"
msgstr[1] "guardias mi-go"
msgstr[2] "guardias mi-go"

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go guard"
msgid ""
"A more heavily armored version of the common mi-go.  Its trunk is a shapeless "
"mass of strange flesh encased in an iridescent carapace, from which sprout "
"several appendages terminating in what appear to be devices of some sort.  "
"Its pyramidal head is encrusted in barnacle-like armor, aside from the "
"bristling antennae that serve as its - you assume - sensory devices and mouth."
msgstr ""
"Una versión más blindada del mi-go común. Su tronco es una masa informe de "
"carne extraña envuelta en un caparazón iridiscente, del que brotan varios "
"apéndices que terminan en lo que parecen ser dispositivos de algún tipo. Su "
"cabeza piramidal está incrustada en una armadura parecida a la de los "
"percebes, aparte de las antenas erizadas que le sirven,supones, como "
"dispositivos sensoriales y boca."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go myrmidon"
msgid_plural "mi-go myrmidons"
msgstr[0] "mirmidón mi-go"
msgstr[1] "mirmidones mi-go"
msgstr[2] "mirmidones mi-go"

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go myrmidon"
msgid ""
"This creature resembles the smaller mi-go like a grizzly bear resembles a "
"human.  Its enormous, thick body is covered in an iridescent segmented "
"carapace, like a scarab crossed with an isopod.  It boasts several pairs of "
"deadly looking claws and other appendages, and it moves with a strange, slow "
"grace, like an otherworldly dancer.  It appears to be carrying weaponry."
msgstr ""
"Esta criatura se asemeja al mi-go más pequeño como un oso pardo se asemeja a "
"un humano. Su enorme y grueso cuerpo está cubierto por un caparazón "
"segmentado iridiscente, como un escarabajo cruzado con un isópodo. Presume de "
"tener varios pares de garras de aspecto mortal y otros apéndices, y se mueve "
"con una gracia extraña y lenta, como un bailarín de otro mundo. Parece llevar "
"armas."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "partially harvested mi-go"
msgid_plural "partially harvested mi-gos"
msgstr[0] "mi-go parcialmente recolectado"
msgstr[1] "mi-gos parcialmente recolectados"
msgstr[2] "mi-gos parcialmente recolectados"

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "partially harvested mi-go"
msgid ""
"This creature resembles the smaller mi-go like a grizzly bear resembles a "
"human.  Its enormous, thick body is covered in an iridescent segmented "
"carapace, like a scarab crossed with an isopod.  It has been mostly pulled "
"apart and is stuck to a surgical table that seems to be keeping it alive."
msgstr ""
"Esta criatura se parece al mi-go más pequeño como un oso pardo a un humano. "
"Su enorme y grueso cuerpo está cubierto de un caparazón segmentado "
"iridiscente, como un escarabajo cruzado con un isópodo. Ha sido desgarrado en "
"su mayor parte y está pegado a una mesa quirúrgica que parece mantenerlo con "
"vida."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go scout"
msgid_plural "mi-go scouts"
msgstr[0] "explorador mi-go"
msgstr[1] "exploradores mi-go"
msgstr[2] "exploradores mi-go"

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go scout"
msgid ""
"This slender mi-go is a little smaller than most others of its kind.  It has "
"a weird, oblong thing attached to the center of its body with some sort of a "
"diaphragm or a membrane on the end.  The thing seems like an integral part of "
"the mi-go's body, and all its appendages are supporting it to prevent swaying."
msgstr ""
"Este delgado mi-go es un poco más pequeño que la mayoría de los otros de su "
"clase. Tiene una extraña cosa oblonga unida al centro de su cuerpo con una "
"especie de diafragma o membrana en el extremo. La cosa parece ser una parte "
"integral del cuerpo mi-go, y todos sus apéndices lo sostienen para evitar el "
"balanceo."

#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of special attack of monster "mi-go scout"
msgid "The mi-go scout fires its weapon!"
msgstr "¡El explorador mi-go dispara su arma!"

#: data/json/monsters/misc.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "debug monster"
msgid_plural "debug monsters"
msgstr[0] "depurar monstruo"
msgstr[1] "depurar monstruos"
msgstr[2] "depurar monstruos"

#: data/json/monsters/misc.json
#. ~ Description of monster "debug monster"
msgid "This monster exists only for testing purposes."
msgstr "Este monstruo solo existe para hacer pruebas."

#: data/json/monsters/misc.json data/json/monsters/nether.json
#: data/json/monsters/slimes.json data/json/monsters/zed_amalgamation.json
#: data/json/monsters/zed_lab.json
#: data/mods/CrazyCataclysm/crazy_monsters.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/monsters/nether.json
#: data/mods/Mythos-Creatures/monsters/mythos.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/dream_wound_monsters.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/monster.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "debug monster"
#. ~ Death message of monster "weak debug grabber"
#. ~ Death message of monster "breather"
#. ~ Death message of monster "wraith"
#. ~ Death message of monster "flying polyp"
