#: data/json/npcs/TALK_SURVIVOR_CHEF.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_HEALER_GREY.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_OLD_MAGUS.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_TECHNO_KID.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you go somewhere else?"
msgstr "¿Por qué no te vas a otro lugar?"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CITY_COP.json
#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_HEALER_GREY.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_OLD_MAGUS.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_TECHNO_KID.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Let's trade then."
msgstr "Vamos a negociar entonces."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CITY_COP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of stuff was in the evidence lockup?"
msgstr "¿Qué clase de cosas había en el depósito de pruebas?"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CITY_COP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You've seen other survivors?"
msgstr "¿Has visto a otros supervivientes?"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CITY_COP.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_HEALER_GREY.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_OLD_MAGUS.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_TECHNO_KID.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What can you sell me?"
msgstr "¿Qué me puedes vender?"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CITY_COP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Knives… drugs… um… drugs and shiny things.  Thieves steal all sorts of stuff."
msgstr ""
"Cuchillos... drogas... um... drogas y cosas brillantes. Los ladrones roban "
"todo tipo de cosas."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CITY_COP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, let me check out some of that stuff."
msgstr "Bueno, déjame ver algunas de esas cosas."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CITY_COP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, there are some like me that have holed up around town.  We do some "
"trading… and then sometimes a stranger wanders through thinking they'll find "
"something better here than they left behind."
msgstr ""
"Sí, hay algunos como yo que se han refugiado en la ciudad. Hacemos algo de "
"comercio... y a veces un extraño pasa por aquí pensando que encontrará algo "
"mejor que lo que dejó atrás."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey again.  *kzzz*"
msgstr "Eh, otra vez. *kzzz*"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json data/json/npcs/TALK_TRUE_FOODPERSON.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey.  Let's chat for a second."
msgstr "Oye. Vamos a charlar un segundo."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's because I saved you.  Listen, I could use your help…"
msgstr "Eso es porque te salvé. Escucha, me vendría bien tu ayuda..."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Big fucking deal.  Do what I say or I'll shove that chip back where it "
"belongs."
msgstr ""
"Gran puto asunto. Haz lo que digo o te meteré ese chip de vuelta a donde "
"pertenece."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, I'm nobody.  Enjoy your freedom, I guess."
msgstr "Lo siento, no soy nadie. Disfruta de tu libertad, supongo."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*buzz* Great!  So what happens now?"
msgstr "*zumbido* ¡Genial! ¿Y qué pasa ahora?"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Come with me.  We can help each other out."
msgstr "Ven conmigo. Podemos ayudarnos mutuamente."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We both go our separate ways.  Enjoy your freedom."
msgstr "Los dos vamos por caminos separados. Disfruta de tu libertad."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "…Wait.  *BEEP* Why do I believe you?  *ZZZT* You could be just as bad as them!"
msgstr "...Espera. *BEEP* ¿Por qué te creo? *ZZZT* ¡Podrías ser tan malo como ellos!"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I wouldn't have pulled your chip out if I didn't want you to think for "
"yourself."
msgstr "No te habría sacado el chip si no quisiera que pensaras por ti mismo."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"For all you know, I did.  I'm being nice for now.  You'd better hope that it "
"lasts."
msgstr ""
"Por lo que sabes, lo pude ser. Estoy siendo amable por ahora. Será mejor que "
"esperes que dure."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Forget it.  Enjoy your freedom."
msgstr "Olvídalo. Disfruta de tu libertad."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Okay, okay, *BUZZ* I'm sorry!  Don't hurt me again!  Anything but the chip!"
msgstr ""
"Vale, vale, *ZUMBIDO* ¡Lo siento! ¡No me hagas daño otra vez! ¡Cualquier cosa "
"menos el chip!"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Follow me and do my bidding, then."
msgstr "Sígueme y haz lo que te diga, entonces."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Get out of my sight."
msgstr "Fuera de mi vista."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, *I'm* sorry, I didn't mean that.  Go do what you want."
msgstr "No, lo siento, no quise decir eso. Ve a hacer lo que quieras."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "…kill… *ZTZTZT* …you!"
msgstr "…matar… *ZTZTZT* …te!"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Run while you still can!"
msgstr "¡Corre mientras puedas!"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not if I kill you first!"
msgstr "¡No si te mato primero!"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry!  I shouldn't have said that!"
msgstr "Lo siento. ¡No debería haber dicho eso!"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yeah, *beeeeep* I don't think so.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Sí, *beeeeep* no lo creo. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_CYBORG_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/talk_cyborg_abomination.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyropod_classes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Suit yourself."
msgstr "Como quieras."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What about faction camps?"
msgstr "¿Y los campamentos de bandos?"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me how faction camps work."
msgstr "Hablame como funcionan los campos de bandos."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me how faction camps have changed."
msgstr "Dime cómo han cambiado los campamentos de las facciones."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#: data/json/npcs/common_chat/TALK_COMMON_ALLY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I want you to build a camp here."
msgstr "Quiero que construyas un campamento aquí."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Since we can't build a camp here, where can we build a camp?"
msgstr ""
"Ya que no podemos construir un campamento aquí, ¿dónde podemos construir un "
"campamento?"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#: data/json/npcs/common_chat/TALK_COMMON_ALLY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We need to abandon this camp."
msgstr "Tenemos que abandonar este campamento."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#: data/json/npcs/common_chat/TALK_COMMON_ALLY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Show me what needs to be done at the camp."
msgstr "Muéstrame lo que hay que hacer en el campamento."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nothing.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Nada. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Never mind, let's talk about other things you can do."
msgstr "No importa, hablemos de otras cosas que puedes hacer."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nothing.  Let's get back to work."
msgstr "Nada. Volvamos al trabajo."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Interesting.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Interesante. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, until we go there, let's talk about camps more."
msgstr "Bueno, hasta que vayamos allí, hablemos más de los campamentos."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, then.  Let's get back to work."
msgstr "Bien. Volvamos al trabajo."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The faction camp system allows you to use companions to take over existing "
"buildings or construct new buildings and use them to extend the usefulness of "
"your allies.  When you have a faction camp, you can order your companions to "
"perform missions, such as crafting new items, building up the camp, hunting "
"for food, or recruiting more allies.  Faction camps also simplify some "
"aspects of managing your companions."
msgstr ""
"El sistema de campamento de facción te permite usar PNJs compañeros para "
"tomar edificios existentes o construir nuevos edificios y usarlos para "
"extender la efectividad de tus aliados. Cuando tienes un campamento de "
"facción, puedes ordenar a tus compañeros que lleven a cabo misiones, como la "
"creación de nuevos objetos, la construcción del campamento, la caza de "
"alimentos o el reclutamiento de más aliados. Los campamentos de las facciones "
"también simplifican algunos aspectos de la gestión de tus compañeros."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Give me an overview of how camps work."
msgstr "Dame una visión general de cómo funcionan los campamentos."

#: data/json/npcs/TALK_FACTION_CAMP.json
