#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/burger_flipper_1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Backgrounds/recent_mutation_1.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Backgrounds/recent_mutation_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, did you evacuate?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿evacuaste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/burger_flipper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, did you evacuate then?"
msgstr "Entonces, ¿evacuaste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, please continue."
msgstr "Bien, continua por favor."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That was when I had my old truck, the blue one.  We called 'er ol' yeller.  "
"One time me an' Marty Gumps - or, as he were known to me, Rusty G - were "
"drivin' ol' yeller up Mount Greenwood in the summertime, lookin' fer "
"fireflies to catch."
msgstr ""
"Eso fue cuando tenía mi vieja camioneta, la azul. La llamábamos 'el viejo "
"ruidoso'. Una vez yo y Marty Gumps - o, como era conocido por mí, Rusty G - "
"conducíamos el viejo ruidoso hasta el Monte Greenwood en verano, buscando "
"luciérnagas para atraparlas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fireflies.  Got it."
msgstr "Luciérnagas. Entiendo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How does this relate to what I asked you?"
msgstr "¿Cómo se relaciona esto con lo que te pregunté?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Rusty G - that's my ol' pal Marty Gumps - were in the passenger seat with his "
"trusty 18 gauge lyin' on his lap.  That were his dog's name, only we all just "
"called him 18 gauge for short."
msgstr ""
"Rusty G... ese es mi viejo amigo Marty Gumps... estaba en el asiento del "
"pasajero con su fiel calibre 18 acostado en su regazo. Ese era el nombre de "
"su perro, sólo que todos le llamábamos \"calibre 18\" para abreviar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "18 gauge, the dog.  Got it."
msgstr "Calibre 18, el perro. Comprendo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I see some zombies coming.  We should cut this short."
msgstr "Creo que veo que vienen algunos zombis. Deberíamos acortar esto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Shut up, you old fart."
msgstr "Cállate, viejo pedorro."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Dammit I'm gettin' there, bite yer tongue.  As I was sayin', Rusty G - that's "
"my ol' pal Marty Gumps - were in the passenger seat with his trusty 18 gauge "
"lyin' on his lap.  That were his dog's name, only we all just called him 18 "
"gauge for short."
msgstr ""
"Maldita sea, ya estoy llegando, muérdete la lengua. Como decía, Rusty G., mi "
"viejo amigo Marty Gumps, estaba en el asiento del pasajero con su fiel "
"calibre 18 acostado en su regazo. Ese era el nombre de su perro, sólo que "
"todos le llamábamos \"calibre 18\" para abreviar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Now up the top o' Mount Greenwood there used to be a ranger station, that "
"woulda been before you were born.  It got burnt down that one year, they said "
"it were lightnin' but you an' I both know it were college kids partyin'.  "
"Rusty G an' I left ol' yeller behind and wen' in to check it out.  Burnt out "
"ol' husk looked haunted, we figgered there were some o' them damn kids "
"rummagin' around in it.  Rusty G brought his 18 gauge, and lucky thing cuz o' "
"what we saw."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, en la cima del Monte Greenwood había un puesto de guardabosques, que "
"habia estado allí antes de que nacieras. Se quemó ese año, dijeron que era un "
"relámpago, pero tú y yo sabemos que eran universitarios que estaban de "
"fiesta. Rusty G y yo dejamos al viejo ruidoso atrás y entramos a comprobarlo. "
"La cáscara quemada parecía embrujada, creímos que había algunos de esos "
"malditos niños rebuscando en ella. Rusty G trajo su calibre 18, y por suerte, "
"por lo que vimos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you see?"
msgstr "¿Qué es lo que viste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We really, really have to go."
msgstr "De verdad, realmente tenemos que irnos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "For fuck's sake, shut UP!"
msgstr "Por el amor de Dios, ¡CÁLLATE!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Be patient!  I'm almost done.  Now up the top o' Mount Greenwood there used "
"to be a ranger station, that woulda been before you were born.  It got burnt "
"down that one year, they said it were lightnin' but you an' I both know it "
"were college kids partyin'.  Rusty G an' I left ol' yeller behind and wen' in "
"to check it out.  Burnt out ol' husk looked haunted, we figgered there were "
"some o' them damn kids rummagin' around in it.  Rusty G brought his 18 gauge, "
"and lucky thing cuz o' what we saw."
msgstr ""
"¡Tengan paciencia! Ya casi he terminado. En la cima del Monte Greenwood había "
"un puesto de guardabosques, que habia estado allí antes de que nacieras. Se "
"quemó ese año, dijeron que era un relámpago, pero tú y yo sabemos que eran "
"universitarios que estaban de fiesta. Rusty G y yo dejamos al viejo ruidoso "
"atrás y entramos a comprobarlo. La cáscara quemada parecía embrujada, "
"creíamos que había algunos de esos malditos niños rebuscando en ella. Rusty G "
"trajo su calibre 18, y por suerte, por lo que vimos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A gorram moose!  Livin' in the ol' ranger station!  It near gored Rusty, but "
"he fired up that 18 gauge and blew a big hole in its hide.  Ol' 18 gauge went "
"headin' for the hills but we tracked him down.  Moose went down like a bag o' "
"potatoes, but a real big bag iff'n y'catch m'drift."
msgstr ""
"¡Un maldito alce! ¡Viviendo en la estación de guardabosque! Casi destripa a "
"Rusty, pero pudo disparar su calibre 18 y hacerle un agujero en su pellejo. "
"Calibre 18 se fue corriendo por el monte pero pudimos rastrearlo. El alce "
"cayó como un saco de patatas, pero un saco enorme, pillas lo que te quiero "
"decir."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I catch your drift."
msgstr "Te entiendo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you done yet?  Seriously!"
msgstr "¿Ya terminaste? ¡En serio!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "For the love of all that is holy, PLEASE shut the hell up!"
msgstr "Pero te lo pido por lo que más quieras, ¡POR FAVOR, callate la boca!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the story!"
msgstr "¡Gracias por la historia!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/codger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<name_b>."
msgstr "<name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/confused_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Huh."
msgstr "Huh"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/confused_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"OK, fine.  Can you at least tell me what you remember about the events "
"leading up to now?"
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, bien. ¿Puedes al menos decirme lo que recuerdas de los eventos "
"que te llevaron al ahora?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/confused_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What, don't you remember?  No, sorry, that's not fair, it was a weird time.  "
"OK, well, I guess this all started with the riots, didn't it?  We were just "
"leading our lives, doing our jobs, and then people started rioting.  Not the "
"usual protests that turned violent or anything, either, people just left "
"their houses and started breaking shit.  The news tried to downplay it but "
"they couldn't keep it off the internet.  I don't know what caused it, they "
"said it was some kind of drug or toxin in the water?  Still, I didn't really "
"realize how bad it was getting at first.  Somewhere along the way the "
"\"rioters\" started getting up and walking around with holes in their chests, "
"and that's when the real panic took over.  The next few days - or weeks, not "
"really sure - are a blur to me.  You'd have to ask someone else how we got "
"from there to total collapse."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué, no te acuerdas? No, lo siento, no es justo, fue una época rara. Vale, "
"bueno, supongo que todo empezó con los disturbios, ¿no? Estábamos llevando "
"nuestras vidas, haciendo nuestro trabajo, y entonces la gente empezó a "
"manifestarse. No las típicas protestas que se vuelven violentas o algo así, "
"la gente simplemente salió de sus casas y empezó a romper cosas. Las noticias "
"trataron de restarle importancia, pero no pudieron evitarlo en Internet. No "
"sé qué lo causó, dijeron que era algún tipo de droga o toxina en el agua. Aun "
"así, al principio no me di cuenta de lo mal que se estaba poniendo la cosa. "
"En algún momento, los \" alborotadores \" empezaron a levantarse y a caminar "
"con agujeros en el pecho, y fue entonces cuando el verdadero pánico se "
"apoderó de todo. Los siguientes días -o semanas, no estoy seguro- se me hacen "
"borrosos. Habría que preguntarle a otra persona cómo pasamos de ahí al "
"colapso total."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/confused_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/confused_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for filling me in."
msgstr "Gracias por informarme."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Salvor_Market/salvor_fabricator_talk.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Salvor_Market/salvor_fabricator_talk.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened?"
msgstr "¿Qué ha pasado?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "But you did get out."
msgstr "Pero saliste."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you do when you found out about the Cataclysm?"
msgstr "¿Qué hiciste cuando te enteraste del Cataclismo?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/cop_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was it like, surviving out there with an injury?"
msgstr "¿Cómo fue sobrevivir ahí fuera con una lesión?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Lucky you.  How did you get away?"
msgstr "Qué afortunado. ¿Cómo te escapaste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was just <freaking> chaos on the streets, man.  But I'm used to chaos.  "
"You don't live as long as I've lived and not know how to keep away from a "
"fight you can't win.  Biggest worry wasn't the zombies and the monsters, "
"honestly.  But I swear, some cops got a nightstick so far up their ass…  I "
"didn't have time to ditch my orange when stuff kept swipin' at me, and I "
"swear, cops got a look at me, they decided I was the big problem.  Goddamn "
"walking corpse next to me, who do they pick to shoot at?  Pricks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you keep from getting arrested?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo evitaste que te arrestaran?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were you in for in the first place?"
msgstr "¿Por qué te encerraron en primer lugar?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Woah, lucky for you.  How did you find out about <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "Guau, tuviste suerte. ¿Cómo te enteraste de <the_cataclysm>?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Something must have driven you out of there."
msgstr "Algo te debe haber obligado a salir de ahí."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/criminal_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got any tips about the boss zombie?"
msgstr "¿Tienes algún consejo sobre el jefe zombi?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/cyborg_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh God… *Zzzzt* I… I don't know what ha-happened.  *BEEEEEEP* They told me I "
"was going to become the very b-best!  And then I c-can only remember pain and "
"screams.  P-Please don't *Zzzt* leave me here!"
msgstr ""
"Oh Dios... *Zzzzt* Yo... no sé qué ha pasado. *BEEEEEEP* ¡Me dijeron que me "
"iba a convertir en el mejor! Y entonces solo p-puedo recordar dolor y gritos. "
"¡Por favor, *Zzzt* no me dejes aquí!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/cyborg_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're okay, it's over now."
msgstr "Estás bien, ya ha pasado."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were your dreams?"
msgstr "¿Qué soñaste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"OK, so, the first dream I had every night for three weeks.  I dreamed that I "
"was running through the woods with a stick, fighting giant spiders.  For "
"reals!  Every night."
msgstr ""
"Bien, entonces, el primer sueño que tuve cada noche durante tres semanas. "
"Soñé que corría por el bosque con un palo, luchando contra arañas gigantes. "
"¡De verdad! Todas las noches."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, that doesn't seem that unusual though."
msgstr "OK, eso no parece tan inusual."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wow, crazy, I can't believe you really dreamed <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr "Guau, qué loco, no puedo creer que soñaste sobre el <the_cataclysm>."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"OK, that's just, like, the beginning though.  So, a week before it happened, "
"after the spider dream, I would get up and go pee and then go back to bed "
"'cause I was kinda freaked out, right?  And then I'd have this other dream, "
"like, where my boss died and came back from the dead!  And then, at work a "
"few days later, my boss' husband was visiting and he had a heart attack and I "
"heard the next day that he'd come back from the dead!  Just like in my dream, "
"only it was a different person!"
msgstr ""
"Vale, eso es sólo, como, al principio. Una semana antes de que ocurriera, "
"después del sueño de la araña, me levante e iba a mear y luego volvía a la "
"cama porque estaba un poco asustado, ¿verdad? Y luego tenía este otro sueño, "
"como, ¡donde mi jefe moría y volvía de la muerte! Y luego, en el trabajo unos "
"días después, el marido de mi jefe estaba de visita y tuvo un ataque al "
"corazón y me enteré al día siguiente que había vuelto de la muerte! ¡Igual "
"que en mi sueño, sólo que era una persona diferente!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That is kinda strange."
msgstr "Eso es un poco extraño."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"RIGHT?!  And there's more!  So, a week before it happened, after the spider "
"dream, I would get up and go pee and then go back to bed 'cause I was kinda "
"freaked out, right?  And then I'd have this other dream, like, where my boss "
"died and came back from the dead!  And then, at work a few days later, my "
"boss' husband was visiting and he had a heart attack and I heard the next day "
"that he'd come back from the dead!  Just like in my dream, only it was a "
"different person!"
msgstr ""
"¡¿VERDAD?! ¡Y hay más! Así que, una semana antes de que ocurriera, después "
"del sueño de la araña, me levantaba e iba a mear y luego volvía a la cama "
"porque estaba un poco asustado, ¿verdad? Y luego tenía este otro sueño, como, "
"¡donde mi jefe moría y volvía de la muerte! Y luego, en el trabajo unos días "
"después, el marido de mi jefe estaba de visita y tuvo un ataque al corazón y "
"me enteré al día siguiente que había vuelto de la muerte! ¡Igual que en mi "
"sueño, sólo que era una persona diferente!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"RIGHT?!  Anyway, I still get weird dreams, but not of the future anymore.  "
"Like, I get a lot of creepy dreams since the world ended.  Like, every couple "
"nights, I dream about a field of black stars all around the Earth, and for "
"just a second they all stare at the Earth all at once like a billion tiny "
"black eyeballs.  And then they blink and look away, and then in my dream the "
"Earth is a black star like all the other ones, and I'm stuck on it still, all "
"alone and freakin' out.  That's the worst one.  There are a few others."
msgstr ""
"¡¿VERDAD?! De todos modos, todavía tengo sueños raros, pero ya no del futuro. "
"Tengo muchos sueños espeluznantes desde que el mundo se acabó. Cada dos "
"noches sueño con un campo de estrellas negras alrededor de la Tierra, y por "
"un segundo todas miran fijamente a la Tierra como si fueran mil millones de "
"pequeños ojos negros. Y luego parpadean y miran hacia otro lado, y luego en "
"mi sueño la Tierra es una estrella negra como todas las demás, y estoy "
"todavía atrapado en ella, solo y asustado. Ese es el peor. Hay algunos otros."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me some more of your weird dreams."
msgstr "Cuéntame más de tus sueños raros."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think we all have dreams like that now."
msgstr "Me parece que ahora todos tenemos sueños así."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, probably.  Sometimes I also dream that I am just like, a mote of dust, "
"floating in a vast, uncaring galaxy.  That one makes me wish that my pot "
"dealer, Filthy Dan, hadn't been eaten by a giant crab monster."
msgstr ""
"Sí, probablemente. A veces también sueño que soy como una mota de polvo, "
"flotando en una vasta e indiferente galaxia. Eso me hace desear que mi "
"traficante de marihuana, Dan el Sucio, no hubiera sido comido por un monstruo "
"cangrejo gigante."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Poor Filthy Dan.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Pobre Dan el Sucio. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for telling me that stuff.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Gracias por contarme esas cosas. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem to know a lot, what do you think caused it all?"
msgstr "Parece que sabes mucho, ¿qué crees que ha provocado todo esto?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/dreamer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a tough one, but I keep thinking back to this dream I had like, a year "
"before it all started.  I dreamed there was this big ball of evil energy that "
"was just waiting to suck up all the good thoughts on the earth and turn us "
"into monsters and things?  So I guess that's what I think happened.  "
"Everything else just seems too far-fetched, you know?"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una pregunta difícil, pero sigo pensando en un sueño que tuve como un "
"año antes de que todo comenzara. Soñé que había una gran bola de energía "
"maligna que estaba esperando para absorber todos los buenos pensamientos de "
"la tierra y convertirnos en monstruos y cosas... Así que supongo que eso es "
"lo que creo que pasó. Todo lo demás parece demasiado inverosímil, ¿sabes?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you survive on the run?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sobreviviste dando vueltas por ahí?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "And that's it?  You spent months just living off the land?"
msgstr "¿Y eso es todo? ¿Pasaste meses viviendo sólo de la tierra?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Complacent?"
msgstr "¿Complaciente?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to your original crew?"
msgstr "¿Y qué le pasó a tu grupo original?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What do you think happened?  You see them around anywhere?"
msgstr "¿Qué crees que pasó? ¿Los ves en algún lugar?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you survive after that?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sobreviviste después de eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What got you out of the subway?"
msgstr "¿Qué te sacó del metro?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I didn't meet you in the subway though.  You left."
msgstr "No te conocí en el metro. Te fuiste."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any idea what the actual cause was?"
msgstr "¿Tienes idea de cuál fue la causa real?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not really.  Government fed us all kinds of conflicting stories, and there "
"was some absolutely heinous stuff going on.  I mean, you can't have missed "
"that video of the woman killing her own baby, right?  God, that still gives "
"me nightmares.  I don't know what it was about it, something about the look "
"on her face.  Worse stuff came out of course, and now we've both seen worse "
"things with our own eyes, but that one still comes back to haunt me.  Anyway, "
"they never could control the riots, and by the time the rioters started "
"turning into undead it was way too late.  I don't know if morale just broke "
"or what but I heard rumors the military and police started turning on each "
"other as much as the crowds.  What actually made the dead come back to life "
"though?  I haven't got a clue."
msgstr ""
"La verdad es que no. El gobierno nos alimentó con todo tipo de historias "
"contradictorias, y hubo algunas cosas absolutamente atroces. Quiero decir, no "
"puedes haberte perdido ese video de la mujer matando a su propio bebé, "
"¿verdad? Dios, eso todavía me da pesadillas. No sé lo que era, algo sobre la "
"mirada en su cara. Salieron cosas peores, por supuesto, y ahora ambos hemos "
"visto cosas peores con nuestros propios ojos, pero esa todavía me persigue. "
"De todos modos, nunca pudieron controlar los disturbios, y cuando los "
"alborotadores empezaron a convertirse en muertos vivientes ya era demasiado "
"tarde. No sé si la moral se rompió o qué, pero oí rumores de que los "
"militares y la policía empezaron a atacarse entre sí y a la multitud. ¿Pero "
"qué hizo que los muertos volvieran a la vida? No tengo ni idea."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_4.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_4.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't leave me hanging, what happened next?"
msgstr "No me dejes colgado, ¿qué pasó después?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_4.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_4.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where did you go from there?"
msgstr "¿A dónde fuisteis desde allí?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_4.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What's this, some kinda Back to the Future thing?  How could you not know "
"what happened?  The world damn well ended, that's what.  And it didn't start "
"with an earthquake, birds, snakes, or airplanes.  It started with riots, and "
"they had to dispatch cops and then the military to take care of the "
"<freaking> criminals.  The government tried to pad it claiming it was some "
"kind of mind control, but I didn't see too much different from the usual "
"bullshit: entitled babies looking for an excuse to break the law.  It just "
"got way worse, this time, until it was time to get out of dodge.  I heard "
"rumors they were even bombing some of the urban centers to try to control it "
"- which, I have to admit, is maybe a bit too hard-core."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Giant bees?  Tell me more."
msgstr "¿Abejas gigantes? Dime mas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "But bees aren't usually aggressive…"
msgstr "Pero las abejas no suelen ser agresivas..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "But bees aren't usually aggressive… do you mean wasps?"
msgstr "Pero las abejas no suelen ser agresivas... ¿te refieres a las avispas?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry.  Could you tell me more about them?"
msgstr "Perdón. ¿Me puedes contar algo más de ellos?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  Sorry."
msgstr "Está bien. Perdón."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay listen.  Don't believe that government stuff.  There's a common thread "
"to all of it: the riots, the military failing to contain it, even the giant "
"monsters they said were appearing in the last few days and had to be wiped "
"out with nukes."
msgstr ""
"Vale, escucha. No te creas esas cosas del gobierno. Hay un hilo conductor en "
"todo ello: los disturbios, los militares que no pudieron contenerlo, incluso "
"los monstruos gigantes que decían que estaban apareciendo en los últimos días "
"y que había que aniquilar con armas nucleares."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You've got my attention."
msgstr "Tienes mi atención."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/ex_pilot_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You were a pilot?  Can you fly a helicopter?"
msgstr "¿Eras piloto? ¿Sabes pilotar helicópteros?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/ex_pilot_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ 'pot' and 'mary jane' are both slang terms for marijuana, a recreational
#. drug that's federally illegal in the US.  In several states, possessing
#. more than a certain quantity of marijuana is considered 'possession with
#. intent to distribute' and can incur a felony conviction. Some states also
#. allow conviction records of non-violent drug offenses to be 'sealed'
#. (restricted from being publicly published or considered by the court) if
#. the convicted person does not commit further crimes.
msgid ""
"Uh, well probably?  I flew fixed-wing for work, but my interest in flying was "
"for helitack - uh, that's helicopter transport for firefighting teams.  "
"Anyway, I got a stupid pot conviction and that disqualified me.  Took a job "
"with the airline to keep fresh until I could finish probation and get the "
"records sealed.  Funny, you smoke some mary jane and they say you can't save "
"lives with firefighting.  But they'll let you fly a plane with hundreds of "
"people in it, not like anyone's ever crashed one of those on purpose before.  "
"So yeah, get me a helicopter and I'd be happy to fly."
msgstr ""
"Eh, bueno, ¿probablemente? Volaba en aviones para trabajar, pero lo que me "
"interesaba era el helitack, es decir, el transporte en helicóptero para "
"equipos de bomberos. De todos modos, me condenaron por una tontería "
"relacionada con la marihuana y eso me descalificó. Acepté un trabajo en la "
"aerolínea para mantenerme al día hasta que terminara la libertad condicional "
"y se sellaran mis antecedentes. Es curioso, fumas un poco de marihuana y te "
"dicen que no puedes salvar vidas combatiendo incendios. Pero te dejan pilotar "
"un avión con cientos de personas a bordo, como si nadie hubiera estrellado "
"uno de esos a propósito antes. Así que sí, dame un helicóptero y estaré "
"encantado de pilotarlo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a tall order.  I guess the short version is that I got evacuated to a "
"FEMA camp for my so-called safety, but luckily I made it out."
msgstr ""
"Es una tarea difícil. Supongo que la versión corta es que fui evacuado a un "
"campamento de FEMA por mi supuesta seguridad, pero por suerte logré salir."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me more about that FEMA camp."
msgstr "Cuéntame más sobre ese campamento del FEMA."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you get out?"
msgstr "¿Cómo saliste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was terrifying.  We were shipped there on a repurposed school bus, about "
"thirty of us.  You can probably see the issues right away.  A few of the "
"folks on board the bus had injuries, and some schmuck who had seen too many "
"B-movies tried to insist that anyone who 'had been bitten' was going to "
"'turn'.  Fucking idiot, right?  I've been bitten a dozen times now and the "
"worst I got was a gross infection."
msgstr ""
"Fue aterrador. Nos enviaron allí en un autobús escolar modificado, unos "
"treinta de nosotros. Probablemente puedas ver los problemas de inmediato. "
"Algunos de los que iban a bordo del autobús tenían heridas, y algún imbécil "
"que había visto demasiadas películas de serie B trató de insistir en que "
"cualquiera que \"hubiera sido mordido\" iba a \"convertirse'\". Maldito "
"idiota, ¿verdad? Me han mordido una docena de veces y lo peor que he tenido "
"ha sido una grave infección."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened after that?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasó después de eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That guy started a frenzy.  People were already panicked.  There was an armed "
"guy overseeing the transport, acting like a cop but really he was just some "
"dumb-ass kid they'd handed a rifle to.  He tried to calm things down, and I "
"guess it actually worked for a bit, although the 'kill the infected' bunch "
"were freaked out and were clearly ready to jump the moment the granny with "
"the cut on her arm started frothing at the mouth.  They started acting up "
"again when we got to the camp.  That didn't go well for them.  A few heavily "
"armed soldiers dragged them away, and I never saw them again."
msgstr ""
"Ese tipo desató el caos. La gente ya estaba en pánico. Había un tipo armado "
"supervisando el transporte, actuando como un policía, pero en realidad solo "
"era un chico tonto al que le habían dado un rifle. Intentó calmar los ánimos "
"y supongo que funcionó durante un rato, aunque el grupo de «matar a los "
"infectados» estaba asustado y claramente dispuesto a saltar en cuanto la "
"abuela con el corte en el brazo empezó a echar espuma por la boca. Volvieron "
"a armar jaleo cuando llegamos al campamento. No les salió bien. Unos soldados "
"fuertemente armados se los llevaron a rastras y no volví a verlos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Maybe another time.  I don't really like thinking about it."
msgstr "Tal vez en otro momento. No me gusta mucho pensar en ello."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry.  Tell me more about that FEMA camp."
msgstr "Lo siento. Cuéntame más sobre el campamento de la FEMA."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry for asking.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Perdón por preguntar. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry for asking.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Perdón por preguntar ¡.  <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh?"
msgstr "¿Oh?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Damn right.  They lied to us for god knows how long about what was going on "
"because they didn't want us to figure it out.  It probably started as a way "
"to keep the people in line, but it backfired somehow.  My guess is they tried "
"to de-educate us, tried to mislead us, and when that wasn't working they "
"tried actual drugs in the water to make us stupid or something.  Instead of "
"just stupid, some people got violent.  Then they tried to leverage that to "
"put in martial law, but that didn't work and they wound up fighting hordes of "
"people.  Only they didn't realize their <freaking> brain drugs were some kind "
"of mutagen that turn people into zombies."
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto que sí. Nos mintieron durante Dios sabe cuánto tiempo sobre lo "
"que estaba pasando porque no querían que nos diéramos cuenta. Probablemente "
"empezó como una forma de mantener a la gente a raya, pero de alguna manera "
"les salió el tiro por la culata. Mi hipótesis es que intentaron deseducarnos, "
"intentaron engañarnos y, cuando eso no funcionó, intentaron echar drogas en "
"el agua para volvernos estúpidos o algo así. En lugar de volverse estúpidos, "
"algunos se volvieron violentos. Entonces intentaron aprovechar eso para "
"imponer la ley marcial, pero no funcionó y acabaron luchando contra hordas de "
"gente. Solo que no se dieron cuenta de que las <freaking> drogas cerebrales "
"eran una especie de mutágeno que convertía a las personas en zombis."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about all the other stuff?"
msgstr "¿Y todo lo demás?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/fema_evacuee_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I think it's mostly mutation.  I don't know what they used, but it's some "
"real mad science shit, I didn't think most of this was even possible.  I also "
"wonder if whatever they put in the water has made us a bit crazy.  Maybe some "
"of this is just a hallucination?  That one blows my mind a bit, I'm not sure "
"I believe it but I got nothin' else."
msgstr ""
"Creo que es mayormente una mutación. No sé lo que usaron, pero es una "
"verdadera mierda de ciencia loca, no pensé que la mayoría de esto fuera "
"posible. También me pregunto si lo que pusieron en el agua nos ha vuelto un "
"poco locos. ¿Tal vez algo de esto es sólo una alucinación? Eso me vuelve "
"loco, no estoy seguro de creerlo pero no tengo ninguna otra idea."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/grad_student_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/grad_student_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you do next?"
msgstr "¿Qué hiciste después?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/grad_student_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/grad_student_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were you studying?"
msgstr "¿Qué estabas estudiando?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/grad_student_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Something must have driven you out of the motel."
msgstr "Algo debe haberte sacado del motel."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did that go?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo estuvo eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cool.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Genial. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cool.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Genial. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Figured what out?"
msgstr "¿Descubrir qué?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Never mind.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "No importa. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Never mind.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "No importa. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's good you found your calling.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Qué bueno que encontraste tu vocación. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's good you found your calling.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Qué bueno que encontraste tu vocación. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay, y'know, I'm honestly gonna stop ya there.  Who gives a rat's ass?  I "
"won't waste a second of time on thinkin' about that."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ya sabes, honestamente voy a detenerte ahí. ¿A quién le importa una "
"mierda? No voy a perder un segundo de tiempo en pensar en eso."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Seriously?  You must have some idea."
msgstr "¿En serio? Debes tener alguna idea."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What difference does it make?  Why waste brain cells on that?  I'm a finely "
"tuned killing machine.  Point me at the zombies and I'll do my thing.  I "
"don't want to get up in it, and find something that takes the magic out of it."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué diferencia hay? ¿Por qué desperdiciar células cerebrales en eso? Soy una "
"máquina de matar bien afinada. Apúntame a los zombis y haré lo mío. No quiero "
"ponerme a ello y encontrar algo que le quite la magia."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Kindred/NPC_Brigitte_LaCroix.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I see.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Ya veo. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I see.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Ya veo. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We-e-e-ell now, that's a fun one.  I haven't got a single solid idea, you "
"know?  But whatever made it start, I think the goop is behind it all."
msgstr ""
"Bu-e-e-eno ahora, eso sí que es divertido. No tengo una sola idea sólida, "
"¿sabes? Pero lo que sea que lo hizo comenzar, creo que el pringue está detrás "
"de todo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The goop?  What do you mean?"
msgstr "¿El pringue? ¿A qué te refieres?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are your other ideas?"
msgstr "¿Cuáles son tus otras ideas?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Those zombies are just spitting it.  Goop, black tarry stuff coming out their "
"eyes and nose and mouth.  Whatever it is, it's what's making them walk again. "
" Somehow doesn't seem to be too contagious, I got tons of it on me… still not "
"a zombie.  And then there are those goopy monsters around, whatever they are, "
"I think they're connected.  Maybe they're behind it, or maybe they're "
"something else caused by the same stuff.  Dunno, but mark my words: it's the "
"goop."
msgstr ""
"Esos zombis lo están escupiendo. Una sustancia negra y alquitranada que sale "
"de sus ojos, nariz y boca. Sea lo que sea, es lo que los hace caminar de "
"nuevo. De alguna manera no parece ser muy contagioso, tengo toneladas de él "
"en mí... y todavía no soy un zombi. Y luego están esos monstruos pegajosos "
"cercanos, sean lo que sean, creo que están conectados. Tal vez están detrás "
"de esto, o tal vez hay algo más que ha causado la misma cosa. No lo sé, pero "
"recuerda mis palabras: es el pringue."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Is all this just based on the goop from zombies being black and slimy, like "
"the black slimes?"
msgstr ""
"¿Todo esto se basa en que el pringue de los zombis es negro y viscoso, como "
"los légamos negros?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You got any better ideas?  Besides, not like there's any teacher checkin' our "
"work.  Maybe I'm wrong, don't really give a shit.  But the zombies and those "
"slime things showed up about the same time, and they both have this "
"connection to black goo, so I'm stickin' to my guns."
msgstr ""
"¿Tienes alguna idea mejor? Además, no es que haya ningún profesor revisando "
"nuestro trabajo. Tal vez me equivoque, no me importa una mierda. Pero los "
"zombis y esas cosas de légamo aparecieron casi al mismo tiempo, y ambos "
"tienen esta conexión con la sustancia viscosa negra, así que me mantengo en "
"mis trece."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, probably the same stuff everyone's thinking.  No special ideas.  Like, "
"maybe this is some kind of military superweapon gone wrong.  Or maybe the "
"world just is like this every so often, and that's what killed the dinosaurs. "
" Who knows."
msgstr ""
"Oh, probablemente lo mismo que todo el mundo está pensando. Ninguna idea "
"especial. Como, que tal vez esto es una especie de superarma militar que "
"salió mal. O tal vez el mundo es así de vez en cuando, y eso es lo que mató a "
"los dinosaurios. Quién sabe."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were you saying about goop?"
msgstr "¿Qué decías sobre el pringue?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your son."
msgstr "Cuéntame sobre tu hijo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, you went to one of the FEMA camps?"
msgstr "¿Así que te fuiste a uno de los campamentos FEMA?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was it you said before?"
msgstr "¿Qué fue lo que dijiste antes?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where did you go then?"
msgstr "¿Adónde fuiste entonces?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's quite a story.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Esa es una historia interesante. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's quite a story.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Esa es una historia interesante. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How could that have caused everything that went down?"
msgstr "¿Cómo puede eso haber causado todo lo que fue mal?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Huh.  Interesting stuff.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Huh. Interesante. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/gung_ho_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Huh.  Interesting stuff.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Huh, Interesante. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/high_school_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/high_school_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where did things go from there?"
msgstr "¿Adónde fueron las cosas desde allí?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/high_school_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/high_school_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did you get home?"
msgstr "¿Llegaste a casa?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened on your sick day?"
msgstr "¿Y qué pasó ese día que no fuiste a trabajar?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did you get evacuated?"
msgstr "¿Y te evacuaron?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Something must have happened to drive you out?"
msgstr "¿Algo debe haber pasado para que te fueras?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I just can't talk about that right now.  I can't."
msgstr "No quiero hablar de eso ahora. No puedo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It might help to get it off your chest."
msgstr "Podría ayudarte a desahogarte hablar de ell."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Suck it up.  If we're going to work together I need to know you."
msgstr "Aguántate. Si vamos a trabajar juntos, necesito conocerte."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was it that 'broke' you?"
msgstr "¿Qué fue lo que te \"quebró\"?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No.  I can't.  Just, no."
msgstr "No. No puedo. Simplemente, no."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry… I'll let you be."
msgstr "Lo siento... te dejaré en paz."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you get out of there?"
msgstr "¿Cómo saliste de allí?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What finally brought you down?"
msgstr "¿Qué fue lo que finalmente te hizo bajar?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you see, up there on the roof?"
msgstr "¿Y qué viste desde el tejado?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any chance you could point the way to that cabin for me?"
msgstr "¿Me podrías indicar la dirección hacia esa cabaña?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "<npc_name> marks the location of the cabin on your map."
msgstr "<npc_name> marca la ubicación de la cabaña en tu mapa."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/soldier_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/soldier_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for telling me all that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Gracias por decirme todo eso. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you get down?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo bajaste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I suppose it couldn't hurt now.  I doubt anyone's still there anyway."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que ahora ya no pasa nada. De todos modos, dudo que haya alguien allí "
"todavía."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/Brigitte_LaCroix_Background.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/Lapin_01.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/NC_Farmer_background.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/NC_SURVIVOR_CHEF_background.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the directions.  I'll check it out."
msgstr "Gracias por las indicaciones. Lo comprobaré."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, fat chance I'm giving up that kind of personal information to someone I "
"barely know.  What are you trying to pull?"
msgstr ""
"Sí, no voy a dar esa información personal a alguien que apenas conozco. ¿Qué "
"estás tratando de hacer?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that cabin"
msgstr "Revisa esa cabaña"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that cabin"
msgid "Maybe there's something left in that cabin you heard about."
msgstr "Tal vez quede algo en esa cabaña de la que oíste hablar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
msgid "Any luck finding the cabin?"
msgstr "¿Y? ¿Pudiste encontrar la cabaña?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
msgid ""
"Thanks so much for coming back here with me!  I'm not sure I would have ever "
"gotten here alive."
msgstr "¡Muchas gracias por acompañarme! No se si hubiera llegado vivo hasta aquí."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
msgid "Great!"
msgstr "¡Genial!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/Brigitte_LaCroix_Background.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/Lapin_01.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/NC_Farmer_background.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/NC_SURVIVOR_CHEF_background.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that LMOE shelter"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that graveyard"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin in the woods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that restaurant"
msgid "Not that surprising."
msgstr "No es tan sorprendente."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_3.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where was that?"
msgstr "¿Dónde fue eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Clearly you escaped at some point."
msgstr "Claramente escapaste en algún momento."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_3.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hospital_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for telling me that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Gracias por avisarme.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "A demon?"
msgstr "¿Un demonio?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My brother and I were out on a hunting trip.  We saw helicopters overhead… "
"big, military ones, loaded up with crazy high-end military stuff like you "
"only see on TV.  Laser cannons even.  They were heading in the direction of "
"our parent's ranch.  Something about it really shook us up, and we started "
"heading back that way… we weren't that far off when we saw this huge, "
"floating eyeball appear out of fucking nowhere.  Ha.  Hard to believe we're "
"in a time where I don't feel like I need to convince you I'm telling the "
"truth."
msgstr ""
"Mi hermano y yo estábamos de excursión de caza. Vimos helicópteros "
"sobrevolándonos... grandes helicópteros militares, cargados con material "
"militar de alta tecnología como el que solo se ve en la televisión. Incluso "
"cañones láser. Se dirigían hacia el rancho de nuestros padres. Algo en ello "
"nos inquietó mucho, y empezamos a regresar por allí... No estábamos muy lejos "
"cuando vimos aparecer de la nada un enorme ojo flotante. Ja. Es difícil creer "
"que estemos en una época en la que no siento la necesidad de convencerte de "
"que estoy diciendo la verdad."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We watched the eyeball just blast one of the Apache choppers with some kind "
"of ray.  The chopper fired back, but it went down.  It was coming right for "
"us… I veered, got out of the way, but a chunk of the chopper smacked into the "
"bed and our truck did a crazy backflip right off the road.  The impact "
"knocked me out cold.  My brother… he wasn't so lucky."
msgstr ""
"Vimos como el globo ocular disparaba a uno de los helicópteros Apache con "
"algún tipo de rayo. El helicóptero devolvió el fuego, pero se estrelló. Venía "
"directo hacia nosotros... giré y me aparté del camino, pero un trozo del "
"helicóptero se estrelló contra la camioneta y nuestro vehículo dio una vuelta "
"de campana fuera de la carretera. El impacto me dejó inconsciente. Mi "
"hermano... no fue tan afortunado."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, no."
msgstr "Oh, no."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did you keep running?"
msgstr "¿Seguiste corriendo?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/hunter_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for telling me your story.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Gracias por contarme tu historia. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lab_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/lab_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't see where this is going."
msgstr "No veo a dónde va esto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lab_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/lab_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay…"
msgstr "Vale…"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lab_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Was there anything else of use in that email?"
msgstr "¿Había algo más de utilidad en ese correo electrónico?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay, so, hear me out.  This might sound crazy, but we're dealing with the "
"<freaking> walking dead, so I think I get a pass on that.  You know your "
"Greek mythology at all?"
msgstr ""
"Vale, escúchame. Puede que esto suene descabellado, pero estamos lidiando con "
"los <freaking> caminantes, así que creo que me lo perdonas. ¿Sabes algo de "
"mitología griega?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not really.  How is that relevant?"
msgstr "En realidad no. ¿Qué importancia tiene eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, why?"
msgstr "Claro, ¿por qué?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay, well, I know this sounds like an Indiana Jones B-plot, but I think "
"someone found Pandora's Box, the actual thing or close to it.  I think they "
"tried to somehow harness it, to use the power in it for something.  Maybe "
"even something good, who knows, the power of the gods seems like it would be "
"a green energy source to me.  Whatever it was, they screwed it up, and "
"released it for real.  Not just a metaphorical thing like in the stories, but "
"actually set the forces of Hades loose on Earth.  Yeah, I know it's "
"farfetched, but like I said: I think I get a pass on that."
msgstr ""
"Vale, sé que esto suena como una trama B de Indiana Jones, pero creo que "
"alguien encontró la Caja de Pandora, la cosa real o cerca de ella. Creo que "
"trataron de aprovecharla de alguna manera, para usar el poder en ella para "
"algo. Tal vez incluso algo bueno, quién sabe, el poder de los dioses me "
"parece que sería una fuente de energía verde. Sea lo que sea, lo arruinaron, "
"y lo liberaron de verdad. No sólo una cosa metafórica como en las historias, "
"sino que realmente soltaron las fuerzas de Hades en la Tierra. Sí, sé que es "
"inverosímil, pero como dije: Creo que tengo un pase en eso."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What?  Pandora's box?"
msgstr "¿Qué? ¿La caja de Pandora?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"According to legend, Pandora was in the house of the gods and found an "
"unopened box.  She decided to investigate, and when she opened it and "
"unthinkable horrors and diseases spilled out.  Sound familiar?"
msgstr ""
"Según la leyenda, Pandora estaba en la casa de los dioses y encontró una caja "
"sin abrir. Decidió investigar y, al abrirla, salieron horrores y enfermedades "
"impensables. ¿Te resulta familiar?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, what's that go to do with anything?"
msgstr "Claro, ¿qué tiene que ver eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Come on, don't leave me hanging."
msgstr "Vamos, no me dejes colgado."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened when you went out?"
msgstr "¿Y qué pasó cuando saliste?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for telling me all that.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Gracias por decirme todo eso. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You think this is an invasion?"
msgstr "¿Crees que esto es una invasión?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Those rioters had a reputation for being absolutely psycho."
msgstr "Esos manifestantes tenían fama de ser absolutamente psicópatas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not many people made it out of the riots alive."
msgstr "No fueron muchos los que salieron vivos de los disturbios."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you survive?"
msgstr "¿Cómo has sobrevivido?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What made you come back?"
msgstr "¿Qué te hizo volver?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You joined the riots?"
msgstr "¿Te uniste a los disturbios?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/left_for_dead_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You must have some insights into what caused all this, then."
msgstr "Debes tener alguna idea de lo que causó todo esto, entonces."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My husband made it out with me, but got eaten by one of those <freaking> "
"plant monsters a few days before I met you.  This hasn't been a great year "
"for me."
msgstr ""
"Mi marido salió conmigo, pero se lo comió uno de esos <freaking> monstruos "
"vegetales unos días antes de conocerte. Este no ha sido un buen año para mí."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My wife made it out with me, but got eaten by one of those <freaking> plant "
"monsters a few days before I met you.  This hasn't been a great year for me."
msgstr ""
"Mi esposa salió conmigo, pero fue devorada por uno de esos <freaking> "
"monstruos vegetales unos días antes de conocerte. Este no ha sido un buen año "
"para mí."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry to hear it."
msgstr "Lamento escucharlo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about those plant monsters."
msgstr "Háblame de esos monstruos de las plantas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, that's messed up."
msgstr "No, eso es un desastre."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yeah, I get that.  Sometimes I feel like my existence began shortly after the "
"Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"Sí, lo entiendo. A veces siento que mi existencia comenzó poco después del "
"Cataclismo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess those of us who made it this far have to have made it for a reason, "
"or something.  I don't mean like a religious reason, just… we're survivors."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que los que llegamos hasta aquí tenemos que haberlo hecho por una "
"razón, o algo así. No me refiero a una razón religiosa, sólo... somos "
"supervivientes."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Haha, yeah, I can see why you'd think that.  I don't mean it's a good "
"apocalypse.  I just mean that at least now I know what I'm doing every day.  "
"I'd still kill a hundred zombies for an internet connection and a night "
"watching crappy movies with… sorry.  Let's change the subject."
msgstr ""
"Jaja, sí, puedo ver por qué pensarías eso. No quiero decir que sea un buen "
"apocalipsis. Sólo quiero decir que al menos ahora sé lo que hago todos los "
"días. Todavía mataría a cien zombis por una conexión a internet y una noche "
"viendo películas de mierda con... lo siento. Cambiemos de tema."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry you lost someone."
msgstr "Siento que hayas perdido a alguien."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just another fucked-up tale of love and loss.  Not one I like to tell."
msgstr "Solo otra historia jodida de amor y pérdida. No es una que me guste contar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You said you lost someone."
msgstr "Dijiste que habías perdido a alguien."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Never mind.  Sorry I brought it up."
msgstr "No importa. Siento haber sacado el tema."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I appreciate the sentiment, but I don't think it would.  Drop it."
msgstr "Aprecio el sentimiento, pero no creo que lo haga. Déjalo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK."
msgstr "OK."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, just shut the fuck up already.  This doesn't have anything to do with "
"you, or with us."
msgstr "Oh, cállate de una vez. Esto no tiene nada que ver contigo ni con nosotros."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "All right, fine.  I had someone.  I lost him."
msgstr "De acuerdo, bien. Había alguien. Lo perdí."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "All right, fine.  I had someone.  I lost her."
msgstr "De acuerdo, bien. Tenía a alguien. La perdí."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He was at home when the bombs started dropping and the world went to hell.  I "
"was at work.  I tried to make it to our house, but the city was a war zone.  "
"Things I can't describe lurching through the streets, crushing people and "
"cars.  Soldiers trying to stop them, but hitting people in the crossfire as "
"much as anything.  And then the collateral damage would get right back up and "
"join the enemy.  If it hadn't been for my husband, I would have just left, "
"but I did what I could and I slipped through.  I actually made it alive."
msgstr ""
"Él estaba en casa cuando empezaron a caer las bombas y el mundo se convirtió "
"en un infierno. Yo estaba en el trabajo. Intenté llegar a nuestra casa, pero "
"la ciudad era una zona de guerra. Cosas que no puedo describir se tambaleaban "
"por las calles, aplastando a personas y coches. Los soldados intentaban "
"detenerlos, pero acababan disparando a la gente en el fuego cruzado. Y luego "
"los daños colaterales se levantaban y se unían al enemigo. Si no hubiera sido "
"por mi marido, me habría marchado, pero hice lo que pude y logré escapar. De "
"hecho, salí con vida."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She was at home when the bombs started dropping and the world went to hell.  "
"I was at work.  I tried to make it to our house, but the city was a war zone. "
" Things I can't describe lurching through the streets, crushing people and "
"cars.  Soldiers trying to stop them, but hitting people in the crossfire as "
"much as anything.  And then the collateral damage would get right back up and "
"join the enemy.  If it hadn't been for my wife, I would have just left, but I "
"did what I could and I slipped through.  I actually made it alive."
msgstr ""
"Ella estaba en casa cuando empezaron a caer las bombas y el mundo se "
"convirtió en un infierno. Yo estaba en el trabajo. Intenté llegar a nuestra "
"casa, pero la ciudad era una zona de guerra. Cosas que no puedo describir se "
"tambaleaban por las calles, aplastando a personas y coches. Los soldados "
"intentaban detenerlos, pero acababan disparando a la gente en el fuego "
"cruzado. Y luego los daños colaterales se levantaban y se unían al enemigo. "
"Si no hubiera sido por mi mujer, me habría marchado, pero hice lo que pude y "
"logré escapar. De hecho, salí con vida."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You must have seen some shit."
msgstr "Debes haber visto alguna mierda."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I take it home was bad."
msgstr "Supongo que en la casa estaba complicado el tema."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You must have seen some shit on the way there."
msgstr "Debes haber visto cosas terribles en tu camino."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did you make it into the house?"
msgstr "¿Entraste en la casa?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I did.  Took a few hours to get an opening.  And you wanna know the fucked up "
"part?  Like, out of all this?  My husband was still alive.  He'd been in the "
"basement the whole time, pinned under a collapsed piece of floor.  And he'd "
"lost a ton of blood, he was delirious by the time I found him.  I couldn't "
"get him out, so I gave him food and water and just stayed with him and held "
"his hand until he passed.  And then… well, then I did what you have to do to "
"the dead now.  And then I packed up the last few fragments of my life, and I "
"try to never look back."
msgstr ""
"Lo conseguí. Tardé unas horas en encontrar un hueco. ¿Y quieres saber la "
"parte más jodida de todo esto? Mi marido todavía estaba con vida. Había "
"estado en el sótano todo el tiempo, inmovilizado bajo un trozo de suelo "
"derrumbado. Había perdido un montón de sangre y estaba desvariando en el "
"momento en que lo encontré. No lo pude sacar, le di comida y agua y me quedé "
"sujetándole la mano hasta que murió. Al final... hice lo que hay que se debe "
"hacer ahora con los muertos. Recogí los restos de mi vida e intento no mirar "
"atrás."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/lost_partner_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I did.  Took a few hours to get an opening.  And you wanna know the fucked up "
"part?  Like, out of all this?  My wife was still alive.  She'd been in the "
"basement the whole time, pinned under a collapsed piece of floor.  And she'd "
"lost a ton of blood, she was delirious by the time I found her.  I couldn't "
"get her out, so I gave her food and water and just stayed with her and held "
"her hand until she passed.  And then… well, then I did what you have to do to "
"the dead now.  And then I packed up the last few fragments of my life, and I "
"try to never look back."
msgstr ""
"Yo lo hice. Me llevó unas horas abrir un espacio. ¿Y quieres saber la parte "
"jodida? Como, ¿fuera de todo esto? Mi esposa todavía estaba viva. Estuvo en "
"el sótano todo el tiempo, atrapado bajo el piso colapsado. Y había perdido "
"una tonelada de sangre, estaba delirando cuando la encontré. No pude sacarla, "
"así que le di comida y agua y me quedé con ella, sosteniéndolela mano hasta "
"que murió. Y entonces... bueno, entonces hice lo que tienes que hacer con los "
"muertos ahora. Y luego empaqueté los últimos fragmentos de mi vida, e intento "
"no mirar atrás."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/nerd_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/nerd_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you survive school?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sobreviviste en la escuela?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/nerd_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/nerd_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about your parents?"
msgstr "¿Qué hay de tus padres?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/nerd_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/nerd_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What got you out of there?"
msgstr "¿Qué te sacó de ahí?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/nerd_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What got you out of the house?"
msgstr "¿Qué te hizo salir de la casa?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Before <the_cataclysm>?  Who cares about that?  This is a new world, and "
"yeah, it's pretty miserable.  It's the one we've got though, so let's not "
"dwell in the past when we should be making the best of what little we have "
"left."
msgstr ""
"¿Antes de <the_cataclysm>? ¿A quién le importa eso? Este es un mundo nuevo y, "
"sí, es bastante miserable. Pero es el que tenemos, así que no nos quedemos "
"anclados en el pasado cuando deberíamos aprovechar al máximo lo poco que nos "
"queda."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can respect that."
msgstr "Puedo respetar eso."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I don't really want to talk about the time before, you know?"
msgstr "Realmente no quiero hablar de tiempos pasados, ¿sabes?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Keep it vague if you want, but please, can you fill me in a little?"
msgstr "No lo compliques si quieres, pero por favor, ¿puedes informarme un poco?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I - fine.  Drugs in the water, some kind of bioweapon I guess.  You know how "
"things were with China, they blamed it on them mostly.  Made people violent "
"and ugly.  There were riots.  People I cared about joined them, and I guess "
"I'll never know why.  Riots led to military and police action, which made the "
"riots worse.  People acted like animals, not just the rioters but everyone.  "
"Then came the monsters and nightmares walking the world like real Armageddon, "
"and everyone died, and started coming back as monsters themselves.  There's "
"your story.  If you want more, talk to someone else."
msgstr ""
"Yo - bien. Drogas en el agua, algún tipo de arma biológica, supongo. Ya sabes "
"cómo fueron las cosas con China, les echaron la culpa sobre todo a ellos. "
"Hizo que la gente fuera violenta y desagradable. Hubo disturbios. La gente "
"que me importaba se unió a ellos, y supongo que nunca sabré por qué. Los "
"disturbios llevaron a la acción militar y policial, lo que empeoró los "
"disturbios. La gente se comportó como animales, no sólo los alborotadores, "
"sino todo el mundo. Luego vinieron los monstruos y las pesadillas caminando "
"por el mundo como un verdadero Armageddon, y todo el mundo murió, y empezaron "
"a volver como monstruos ellos mismos. Ahí tienes tu historia. Si quieres más, "
"habla con otra persona."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for that."
msgstr "Gracias por eso."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To be honest… I don't really remember.  I remember vague details of my life "
"before the world was like this, but <the_cataclysm> itself?  It's all a blur. "
" I think something pretty bad must have happened to me.  I remember a few "
"things: snatches of violence, something about a woman killing her baby.  I "
"feel like I'd rather not remember."
msgstr ""
"Para ser honesto... no lo recuerdo realmente. Recuerdo vagos detalles de mi "
"vida antes de que el mundo fuera así, ¿pero <the_cataclysm>en sí? Todo está "
"borroso. Creo que algo bastante malo me debe haber pasado. Recuerdo algunas "
"cosas: fragmentos de violencia, algo sobre una mujer matando a su bebé. "
"Siento que prefiero no recordar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To be honest… I don't really remember.  I remember vague details of my life "
"before the world was like this, but <the_cataclysm> itself?  It's all a blur. "
" I don't know how I got where I am now, or how any of this happened.  I think "
"something pretty bad must have happened to me.  Or maybe I was just hit in "
"the head really hard.  Or both.  Both seems likely.  First thing I remember "
"is seeing an already-read text on my phone from the emergency government "
"broadcast system, saying the United States had fallen."
msgstr ""
"Para ser honesto... no lo recuerdo realmente. Recuerdo vagos detalles de mi "
"vida antes de que el mundo fuera así, ¿pero<the_cataclysm> en sí? Todo está "
"borroso. No sé cómo llegué a donde estoy ahora, o cómo sucedió todo esto. "
"Creo que algo muy malo debe haberme ocurrido. O tal vez me golpearon muy "
"fuerte en la cabeza. O ambas. Ambas cosas parecen probables. Lo primero que "
"recuerdo es ver un mensaje de texto ya leído en mi teléfono del sistema de "
"transmisión gubernamental de emergencia, diciendo que los Estados Unidos "
"habían caído."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think happened?"
msgstr "¿Qué crees que sucedió?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_3.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That does sound a little crazy…"
msgstr "Eso suena un poco loco..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There were some clues.  Like, I had a nasty headache that lasted a few days, "
"but no cuts or bruises.  And there were scorch marks on the trees in weird "
"slashing patterns around me.  Whatever happened to me, I think it was some "
"weird shit."
msgstr ""
"Había algunas pistas. Por ejemplo, yo tenía un dolor de cabeza bastante feo "
"que me duró unos días, pero no tenía ni cortes ni golpes. Y había marcas de "
"fuego en los árboles en extrañas formas de corte alrededor mío. Lo que me "
"haya pasado, seguro que fue alguna cosa extraña."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you trying to get your memory back then?"
msgstr "¿Estás tratando de recuperar tu memoria entonces?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to you after that?"
msgstr "¿Y qué te pasó después de eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It can't be healthy to abandon your past like that…"
msgstr "No puede ser saludable abandonar tu pasado de esa manera..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You're asking me what I think caused all this?  It was all over the news.  "
"Some kind of Chinese bio-weapon.  It's no different from the pandemic a few "
"years back, but this time they got the formula right.  Maybe too right.  "
"Doesn't matter anyway, I hear it got out on them and wiped them out too.  "
"Serves em right."
msgstr ""
"¿Me estás preguntando qué creo que causó todo esto? Salió en todas las "
"noticias. Algún tipo de arma biológica china. No es diferente de la pandemia "
"de hace unos años, pero esta vez tienen la fórmula correcta. Tal vez "
"demasiado bien. No importa de todos modos, escuché que se les escapó y los "
"aniquiló también. Se lo tienen merecido."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me more about what actually went down, though?"
msgstr ""
"Sin embargo, ¿podrias decirme más sobre lo que realmente ocurrió?Sin embargo, "
"¿podrias decirme más sobre lo que realmente ocurrió?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How does that explain all the other crazy stuff?"
msgstr "¿Cómo explica eso todas las demás locuras?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, you know.  First there were the riots from the mind-control drugs in "
"the water.  Except I think we can all see now it was actually a virus again.  "
"The military and the cops did their damndest to put it down but it got out of "
"hand.  Then the virus mutated and started bringing the dead back to life like "
"in some kinda B-movie, and shit got really real.  They let the big things "
"loose, or they set them on us, I dunno.  Huge unspeakable monsters… still "
"makes me shudder to think of them.  They obviously weren't built for combat "
"though, and the military took 'em down fast."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ya sabes. Primero fueron los disturbios por las drogas de control "
"mental en el agua. Excepto que creo que todos podemos ver ahora que en "
"realidad era un virus de nuevo. Los militares y los policías hicieron todo lo "
"posible para acabar con él, pero se les fue de las manos. Entonces el virus "
"mutó y empezó a resucitar a los muertos como en una película de serie B, y la "
"mierda se volvió realmente real. Soltaron a las cosas grandes, o las pusieron "
"sobre nosotros, no sé. Enormes monstruos indescriptibles... todavía me da "
"escalofríos pensar en ellos. Obviamente no fueron construidos para el "
"combate, y los militares los eliminaron rápidamente."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_4.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What?  Of course it does.  They started with a bioweapon and then it went "
"full nuclear.  Only the weapons we had now were a lot worse than H-bombs.  "
"Uncle Sam managed to beat back the really nasty stuff, but I guess it was "
"with his dying breath."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué? Por supuesto que sí. Empezaron con un arma biológica y luego se volvió "
"totalmente nuclear. Sólo que las armas que teníamos ahora eran mucho peores "
"que las bombas H. El Tío Sam se las arregló para rechazar las cosas realmente "
"desagradables, pero supongo que fue con su último aliento."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can respect that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Respeto esa decisión. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/no_past_5.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fair enough.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Me parece justo.  <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you survive outside?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sobreviviste afuera?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you see in those first few days?"
msgstr "¿Qué viste en esos primeros días?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened after the acid mist?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasó después de la neblina ácida?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"By morning, the area around the lake was covered in a pinkish mold, and there "
"were walking mushrooms around shooting clouds of the dust in the air.  We "
"didn't know what was going on, but neither of us wanted to stay and find out. "
" We packed up our shit, scraped off the boat, and took off upriver."
msgstr ""
"Por la mañana, el área alrededor del lago estaba cubierta de un moho rosado, "
"y había hongos caminantes alrededor disparando nubes de polvo en el aire. No "
"sabíamos lo que estaba pasando, pero ninguno de nosotros quería quedarse y "
"averiguarlo. Empacamos nuestras cosas, sacamos el bote y nos fuimos río "
"arriba."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to your friend?"
msgstr "¿Qué le pasó a tu amigo?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess they didn't know."
msgstr "Supongo que no pudieron decirte nada."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "She was dead?"
msgstr "¿Ella murió?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's awful.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Eso es horrible. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/out_of_town_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's awful.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Eso es horrible.  <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to you?"
msgstr "¿Qué te ha pasado?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about your shelter?"
msgstr "¿Y qué pasó con tu refugio?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You said you could tell me more about the shelter if I wanted.  How did these "
"things get built?"
msgstr ""
"Dijiste que podrías contarme más cosas sobre el refugio si quería. ¿Cómo se "
"construyeron estos edificios?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What do you think happened?  You must have some interesting theories on why "
"everything went to shit."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué crees que ocurrió? Debes tener algunas teorías interesantes sobre por "
"qué todo se fue a la mierda."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Hey, uh…  I noticed you left a computer down in your shelter.  I didn't "
"intend to pry, but you said I could go through everything.  So, I read a "
"little of what you wrote.  You wanna talk about it?"
msgstr ""
"Eh... me he dado cuenta de que te has dejado el ordenador en tu refugio. No "
"tenía intención de curiosear, pero dijiste que podía revisarlo todo. Así que "
"leí un poco de lo que escribiste. ¿Quieres hablar de ello?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did you get there?"
msgstr "¿Y pudiste llegar?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The shelter's in your hands, at this point."
msgstr "El refugio depende de ti, a partir de ahora."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me that story again?"
msgstr "¿Podría contarme esa historia otra vez?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I could go check out that shelter for you if you like.  Bring back any "
"supplies you left behind?"
msgstr ""
"Puedo ir a ver ese refugio por ti si quieres. ¿Traigo algún suministro que te "
"hayas dejado?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "<npc_name> marks the location of the LMOE shelter on your map."
msgstr "<npc_name> marca la localización del refugio LMOE en tu mapa."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I know this might seem weird but… your shelter wasn't on the way out of town, "
"was it?  A hole in the ground, surrounded by trees?  Full of supplies with a "
"sign out front that says 'I'm gonna shoot you'?"
msgstr ""
"Sé que esto puede parecer raro pero... tu refugio no estaba a la salida de la "
"ciudad, ¿verdad? ¿Un agujero en el suelo, rodeado de árboles? ¿Lleno de "
"provisiones con un letrero en el frente que dice \"Te voy a disparar\"?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "A contractor?  How much does something like a survivalist shelter cost?"
msgstr "¿Un contratista? ¿Cuánto cuesta un refugio de supervivencia?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"But we're good to go, right?  I mean… the door is the only trick you had?  No "
"clever traps hidden in the walls or anything?"
msgstr ""
"Pero podemos irnos, ¿no? Quiero decir... ¿la puerta es el único truco que "
"tenías? ¿No hay trampas inteligentes escondidas en las paredes o algo así?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You wouldn't keep ALL your tricks and secrets from me, though, would you?  "
"After everything we've been through?"
msgstr ""
"Pero no me ocultarías TODOS tus trucos y secretos, ¿verdad? ¿Después de todo "
"lo que hemos pasado?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's all I wanted to know."
msgstr "Eso es todo lo que quería saber."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/bunker_shop/TALK_BUNKER_MERCHANT.json
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/dialog_statue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Interesting…"
msgstr "Interesante..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How many of these places did the company build?"
msgstr "¿Cuántos de estos lugares construyó la empresa?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Dozens, they told me.  Probably more by the end of it.  But they obviously "
"didn't say where or who for.  It was kind of a hot business and I think they "
"were some of the best doing it."
msgstr ""
"Docenas, me dijeron. Probablemente más al final. Pero obviamente no dijeron "
"dónde ni para quién. Era un negocio candente y creo que eran de los mejores "
"haciéndolo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right…"
msgstr "Claro…"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay, listen… across the hall from the bedroom… by the pillars… it's a fake "
"wall.  Directly across the hall.  If you push in a little bit, the whole "
"thing kinda slides aside.  I hid some guns back there and a handful of "
"rounds, too.  I meant to bring a lot more - I had boxes on back order - but "
"it started getting hard to buy past a certain point.  Might as well share now "
"that we're here.  A spare bullet could save your life."
msgstr ""
"Vale, escucha... al otro lado del pasillo del dormitorio... por los "
"pilares... hay una pared falsa. Directamente al otro lado del pasillo. Si "
"empujas un poco, todo se desliza hacia un lado. Escondí algunas armas allí y "
"un montón de balas, también. Tenía la intención de conseguir mucho más - "
"tenía pedidos de cajas - pero empezó a ser difícil comprar a partir de cierto "
"punto. Ahora que estamos aquí, podríamos compartirlas. Una bala de sobra "
"puede salvarte la vida."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The wall thing is pretty nifty, I have to admit."
msgstr "Lo de la pared es bastante ingenioso, tengo que admitirlo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, but they put the secret room in their advertising.  Not really a secret "
"then, is it?"
msgstr ""
"Sí, pero en su publicidad incluyen la habitación secreta. No es un verdadero "
"secreto en realidad, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hmm, good point."
msgstr "Hmm, tienes razón."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, you're right!  I'm sorry for intruding!"
msgstr "¡No, si tienes razón! ¡Perdona por entrometerme!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"For all I know, you COULD have something to do with this.  Who really knows "
"what happened?"
msgstr ""
"Por lo que sé, PODRIAS tener algo que ver con esto. ¿Quién sabe realmente lo "
"que pasó?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I certainly wouldn't tell you.  The way you talk… the questions you "
"ask… they're extremely suspicious.  Why did you ask about the shelter anyway? "
" What do you want from me?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, ciertamente no te lo diría. La forma en que hablas... las preguntas "
"que haces... son extremadamente sospechosas. ¿Por qué me preguntaste por el "
"refugio? ¿Qué quieres de mí?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I just wanted the loot, I'll be honest."
msgstr "Sinceramente, sólo quería el botín."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Well… I'm actually a government agent sent to assassinate you.  I just had to "
"find out the location of your secret stash before I took you out!"
msgstr ""
"Pues, en realidad soy un agente del gobierno enviado a asesinarte. ¡Sólo "
"tenía que averiguar la localización de tu escondite secreto antes de "
"eliminarte!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I thought we could team up.  It sounded like a good place to stay safe."
msgstr ""
"Pensé que podríamos formar un equipo. Me pareció un buen lugar para "
"permanecer a salvo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*tenses up and stares in disbelief.  \"You're playing with me.  The "
"government doesn't exist anymore…  You better be messing around or I-\""
msgstr ""
"*se tensa y se queda mirándote con incredulidad. \"Estás de broma. El "
"gobierno ya no existe... Más vale que estés jugando o yo...\""

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why else would I ask about your shelter?  I don't need your gear.  I don't "
"need your help.  Look around you!  I'm tracking down the last free thinkers "
"who have been putting the puzzle pieces together.  It's YOU I'm after!"
msgstr ""
"¿Por qué si no iba a preguntar por tu refugio? No necesito su equipo. No "
"necesito tu ayuda. ¡Mira a tu alrededor! Estoy rastreando a los últimos "
"librepensadores que han estado juntando las piezas del rompecabezas. ¡Es a TI "
"a quien busco!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I'm just messing with you, don't worry.  What, can't take a joke?"
msgstr ""
"Sí, me estoy quedando contigo, no te preocupes. ¿Qué, no puedes soportar una "
"broma?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Prepare to meet your end, <npc_name>.  *Attack <npc_name>.*"
msgstr "Prepárate para tu final, <npc_name>. *Ataca <npc_name>.*"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, listen, just keep your questions to yourself.  I don't trust you and "
"you shouldn't trust me, either."
msgstr ""
"Sí, oye, guárdate tus preguntas para ti. No confío en ti y tú tampoco "
"deberías confiar en mí."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, I won't ask again."
msgstr "Lo siento, no lo volveré a preguntar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It IS a good place to stay safe.  Just don't go prying, okay?"
msgstr "Es un buen lugar para estar seguro. Pero no vayas a husmear, ¿vale?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.
msgid "You got it."
msgstr "Ya lo tienes."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You think that's funny?!  Some of us watched the warning signs for years.  "
"All the news, all the violence and the secret plots…  Now the dead are "
"walking, reality itself is tearing apart, and you're making jokes like that?!"
msgstr ""
"¡¿Crees que es gracioso?! Algunos de nosotros vimos las señales de "
"advertencia durante años. Todas las noticias, toda la violencia y los "
"complots secretos... Ahora los muertos están caminando, la realidad misma se "
"está desgarrando, ¡¿y tú bromeas así?!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah…?  I didn't realize it bothered you so much."
msgstr "¿Sí...? No sabía que te molestase tanto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I marked the spot for you.  When you get there, pry off the metal above the "
"door and you'll see the special latch I made to keep thieves out.  I trust "
"you to make the right decisions."
msgstr ""
"Te he marcado el lugar. Cuando llegues allí, haz palanca en el metal que hay "
"sobre la puerta y verás el pestillo especial que hice para impedir el paso a "
"los ladrones. Confío en que tomes las decisiones correctas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, calm down…"
msgstr "Vale, cálmate…"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "My… what do you mean?  How would YOU know what the sign says?"
msgstr "Mi... ¿qué quieres decir? ¿Cómo sabrías TÚ lo que dice el cartel?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I uh… found my way inside it a while ago.  The door was already open.  I "
"kinda went through it already assuming whoever owned it was dead."
msgstr ""
"Yo... encontré la forma de entrar hace un rato. La puerta ya estaba abierta. "
"La atravesé asumiendo que el dueño estaba muerto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"So it WAS yours?  I broke in and stole a bunch of stuff from it.  Sorry, I "
"guess."
msgstr ""
"¿Así que ERA tuyo? Entre por la fuerza y robe algunas cosas. Los siento, "
"supongo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Well, I got inside one and found a computer with a bunch of… conspiracy "
"theory documents?  I'm not sure how to put it.  It seemed like whoever wrote "
"it wasn't doing well."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, entré en uno y encontré un ordenador con un montón de... ¿documentos "
"sobre teorías de la conspiración? No estoy seguro de cómo decirlo. Parecía "
"que quien lo escribió no andaba bien."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "There was a dead guy inside.  It didn't take much to make that connection."
msgstr "Había un muerto dentro. No me costó mucho hacer esa conexión."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The whole front door had been blown off and everything had been looted.  "
"Nothing left.  It seemed like something major had happened, that's all."
msgstr ""
"Habían volado la puerta principal y habían saqueado todo. No quedaba nada. "
"Parece que había pasado algo importante, eso es todo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I had no idea.  It's <the_cataclysm>.  I was just trying to survive."
msgstr "No tenía ni idea.  Es <the_cataclysm>.  Solo intentaba sobrevivir."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Finders, keepers."
msgstr "El que lo encuentra, se lo queda."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "C'mon, you would do the same!  It's life or death out here!"
msgstr "¡Vamos, tú harías lo mismo! ¡Es a vida o muerte aquí fuera!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I guess I know exactly how much to trust you now."
msgstr "Supongo que ahora sé exactamente hasta qué punto confiar en ti."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You sure do."
msgstr "Seguro que si."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "This is the world now.  If I didn't take it, someone else would have."
msgstr "Así es el mundo ahora. Si no lo hubiera cogido, otro lo hubiera hecho."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're right, sorry."
msgstr "Tienes razón, lo siento."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm just doing what I have to do.  Stick with me and we'll find plenty of "
"stuff to replace it."
msgstr ""
"Sólo hago lo que tengo que hacer. Quédate conmigo y encontraremos un sinfín "
"de cosas para sustituirlas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh…  Yeah, that would definitely do it.  It's a shame someone already got in. "
" I had a lot of stuff saved up there.  But I suppose it wouldn't matter much "
"now."
msgstr ""
"Oh... Sí, eso serviría definitivamente. Es una pena que ya haya entrado "
"alguien. Tenía un montón de cosas guardadas allí. Pero supongo que ya no "
"importa mucho."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Stick with me and we'll find plenty of stuff to replace it."
msgstr "Quédate conmigo y encontraremos un sinfín de cosas para sustituirlo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry.  I'm sure we can find lots of stuff to replace whatever I took."
msgstr ""
"Lo siento. Estoy seguro de que podemos encontrar un montón de cosas para "
"reemplazar las que me llevé."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well…  I did.  And that's just how it goes.  It wasn't even that difficult."
msgstr "Bueno... lo hice. Y así es como funciona. Ni siquiera fue tan difícil."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm sorry.  I guess I just didn't know how to tell you I needed what was in "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Lo siento. Supongo que no sabía cómo decirte que necesitaba lo que había "
"dentro."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<npc_name> inhales sharply and breaks eye contact.\n"
"\n"
"\"I…  I mean, I can sympathize with someone who thinks that way…  The "
"government lies all the time and they're probably out there somewhere STILL "
"lying.  But nah, I wouldn't leave my computer laying around, unprotected.\""
msgstr ""
"&<npc_name> toma una bocanada de aire y desvia la mirada..\n"
"\n"
"\"Yo... es decir, puedo simpatizar con alguien que piense de esa manera... El "
"gobierno miente todo el tiempo y probablemente estén por ahí en algún lugar "
"TODAVÍA a la espera. Pero nah, yo no dejaría mi ordenador tirado por ahí, "
"desprotegido\"."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Are you sure?  It kind of feels like it might be yours by the way you're "
"acting…"
msgstr "¿Estás seguro? Parece que podría ser tuyo por la forma en que actúas..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"There was a bunch of notes about Chinese bio-weapons and this guy who worked "
"at an airport…  If you want to talk about it, we can."
msgstr ""
"Había un puñado de notas sobre armas biológicas chinas y un tipo que "
"trabajaba en un aeropuerto... Si quieres hablar de ello, podemos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"But you DID leave your computer unprotected.  AND full of evidence.  It's "
"exactly what a government agent would need to track you down…  Someone like "
"me…"
msgstr ""
"Pero sí DEJASTES tu ordenador desprotegido. Y lleno de pruebas. Es "
"exactamente lo que un agente del gobierno necesitaría para rastrearte... "
"Alguien como yo..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nope.  Not mine.  Listen, maybe we shouldn't talk about this right now."
msgstr "No. No es mio. Escucha, sería mejor no hablar de esto ahora mismo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why not?  Now that it's all finally come to a head, maybe some of your "
"theories are right."
msgstr ""
"¿Por qué no? Ahora que todo se ha aclarado, quizá algunas de tus teorías sean "
"ciertas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, I understand.  Sorry for being nosy."
msgstr "Vale, lo entiendo. Perdón por ser entrometido."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<npc_name> sighs and pauses for a moment.\n"
"\n"
"\"Listen…  I know what you think I am, but the threats are real.  The dead "
"are walking, strange hellspawn crawling out of…  well, I can't even talk "
"about it.  Whatever demonic, technological abomination, bio-weapon the "
"communists unleashed on the world is definitely out of their control.  Look "
"around you!  Isn't it obvious something bigger is going on?\""
msgstr ""
"& <npc_name> suspira y se detiene por un momento.\n"
"\n"
"\"Escucha... Sé lo que crees que soy, pero las amenazas son reales. Los "
"muertos están caminando, extraños engendros del infierno saliendo de... "
"bueno, ni siquiera puedo hablar de ello. Cualquiera que sea el demonio, "
"abominación tecnológica, arma biológica que los comunistas desataron en el "
"mundo está definitivamente fuera de su control. ¡Mira a tu alrededor! ¿No es "
"obvio que algo más grande está pasando?\""

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Something bigger?  You mean you think someone did this intentionally?"
msgstr ""
"¿Algo más grande? ¿Quieres decir que crees que alguien hizo esto "
"intencionalmente?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's an invasion.  Or, at least, I think that's what they were trying to do "
"at first.  Sudden bouts of violence, sending agitators to riots, doing false "
"flags with covert and overt agents alike…  When they couldn't get what they "
"wanted, they went full 'scorched earth'.  They decided to destroy everything "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"Es una invasión. O, al menos, creo que eso es lo que intentaban hacer al "
"principio. Ataques repentinos de violencia, enviando agitadores a los "
"disturbios, creando situaciones de falsa alarma con agentes tanto encubiertos "
"como públicos... Cuando no consiguieron lo que querían, se volcaron de lleno "
"en lo de la \"tierra quemada\". Decidieron destruirlo todo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you mean?  Who is 'they'?"
msgstr "¿A qué te refieres? ¿Quiénes son 'ellos'?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The government.  Whoever was left, really.  I don't know…  I'm starting to "
"think that maybe some of those folks were right…  Maybe this is some kind of "
"punishment for humanity.  Maybe some god decided they'd had enough of us.  Or "
"maybe there's no answer.  I can't explain some of the things I've seen."
msgstr ""
"El gobierno. Quienquiera que quedara, en realidad. No lo sé... Estoy "
"empezando a pensar que tal vez algunas de esas personas tenían razón... Tal "
"vez esto es una especie de castigo a la humanidad. Tal vez algún dios decidió "
"que habían tenido suficiente de nosotros. O tal vez no hay ninguna respuesta. "
"No puedo explicar algunas de las cosas que he visto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think you might be right.  The government probably does have something to "
"do with it."
msgstr "Creo que puede que tengas razón. Probablemente el gobierno tenga algo que ver."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Spiritual] I feel like this could definitely be some kind of divine "
"punishment."
msgstr ""
"[Espiritual] Siento que esto podría ser definitivamente algún tipo de castigo "
"divino."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Maybe the explanation is more scientific.  Zombies and flesh-eating monsters "
"only come from supervillains and gods in fiction."
msgstr ""
"Quizás la explicación sea más científica. Los zombis y los monstruos "
"carnívoros sólo aparecen en la ficción como supervillanos y dioses."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[US Marshal] I actually used to be a US Marshal, and there were crazy rumors "
"coming from all over back in the day.  A buddy of mine heard that China built "
"a portal to another dimension.  Or a time machine.  Someone else claimed it "
"was America who made it, and it was actually some kind of doomsday device.  "
"There was a lot of money getting sunk into the Department of Energy, DARPA, "
"military contractors…  We all knew something was up, but it was impossible to "
"say what."
msgstr ""
"[Alguacil EEUU]  Yo fui alguacil de los EE.UU., y había rumores disparatados "
"que llegaban de todas partes. Un amigo mío oyó que China construyó un portal "
"a otra dimensión. O una máquina del tiempo. Alguien más afirmó que fue "
"Estados Unidos quien lo hizo, y que en realidad era una especie de "
"dispositivo del día del juicio final. Se invertía mucho dinero en el "
"Departamento de Energía, APIAD, contratistas militares... Todos sabíamos que "
"pasaba algo, pero era imposible saber qué."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Hub 01 Ancillary] I have an idea what happened.  This might sound strange, "
"but I've been doing jobs for these people in a hidden bunker who gave me some "
"high-tech armor and told me our reality… 'broke' somehow.  That's why those "
"crazy portal storms keep happening.  They also told me it's probably going to "
"get worse."
msgstr ""
"[Auxiliar Hub 01] Tengo una idea de lo que pasó. Esto puede sonar extraño, "
"pero he estado haciendo trabajos para esta gente en un búnker oculto que me "
"dio una armadura de alta tecnología y me dijo que nuestra realidad... 'se "
"rompió' de alguna forma. Es por eso que esas locas tormentas de portales "
"siguen sucediendo. También me dijeron que probablemente va a empeorar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I met this woman who was… uh… obsessed with bones?  She said that since "
"<the_cataclysm>, the bones of living things 'hum' with some kind of special "
"power and that she wants to collect lots of them to either end the world or "
"save the world.  I'm honestly still not entirely clear how or what's supposed "
"to happen…  How about that idea?  Did THAT ever cross your mind?"
msgstr ""
"Conocí a una mujer que estaba... ¿obsesionada con los huesos? Decía que, "
"desde <the_cataclysm>, los huesos de los seres vivos \"zumban\" con algún "
"tipo de poder especial y que ella quiere reunir un montón de ellos para "
"acabar con el mundo o salvarlo. Sinceramente, aún no tengo del todo claro "
"cómo o qué se supone que va a pasar... ¿Qué te parece la idea? ¿Se te ha "
"pasado eso por la cabeza?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Honestly, it's probably aliens.  I can't really think of another reasonable "
"explanation for all of this."
msgstr ""
"Honestamente, probablemente sean alienígenas. Realmente no puedo pensar en "
"otra explicación razonable para todo esto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't think there's any explanation.  Sometimes bad things just happen."
msgstr ""
"No creo que haya ninguna explicación. A veces las cosas malas simplemente "
"suceden."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<lets_go>  I'm trying to stick it to 'The Man' while we've still got a chance."
msgstr ""
"<lets_go> Estoy intentando plantarle cara al «El hombre» mientras aún "
"tengamos oportunidad."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"We should keep moving…  No sense dwelling on fate.  If those people are "
"right, then this is all we've got: survival."
msgstr ""
"Debemos seguir adelante... No tiene sentido obsesionarse con el destino. Si "
"esa gente tiene razón, entonces solo nos queda esto: sobrevivir."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Maybe.  I guess multiple things could be possible.  You really don't think "
"that there's someone or something behind this?  Someone who flew a little too "
"close to the sun?  Poked the beast?"
msgstr ""
"Quizás. Supongo que varias cosas podrían ser posibles. ¿De verdad no crees "
"que hay alguien o algo detrás de esto? ¿Alguien que voló demasiado cerca del "
"sol? ¿Incitó a la bestia?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think it's possible, but ultimately unknowable.  What matters now is "
"survival and actually fighting the monsters that are trying to kill us.  We "
"shouldn't dwell on crazy theories."
msgstr ""
"Creo que es posible, pero en última instancia incognoscible. Lo que importa "
"ahora es sobrevivir y luchar contra los monstruos que intentan matarnos. No "
"deberíamos obsesionarnos con teorías descabelladas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A Marshal, huh?  I could tell there was something a bit square about you.  "
"Or… round, I suppose, ha!  In my experience, when people at that level start "
"talking stuff like that, there's at least some truth to it."
msgstr ""
"Un Alguacil, ¿eh? Me di cuenta de que había algo un poco cuadriculado en ti. "
"O... redondo, supongo, ¡ja! En mi experiencia, cuando la gente de ese nivel "
"empieza a decir cosas así, hay algo de verdad en ellas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I might not have 'real' authority anymore, and we might not have a real "
"'society', but it's still not nice to make fat jokes…"
msgstr ""
"Puede que ya no tenga autoridad 'real', y puede que no tengamos una "
"'sociedad' real, pero sigue sin estar bien hacer chistes de gordos..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "They were talking a LOT in that time, that's for sure."
msgstr "Hablaron MUCHO en ese tiempo, eso seguro."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"High-tech armor?  And there's a whole group of them down in a bunker?  "
"Probably best to keep people like that on our good side.  What they're saying "
"seems to check out.  Reality does seem pretty fucked.  Kinda makes me wonder "
"how involved THEY were if they know all that, though."
msgstr ""
"¿Una armadura de alta tecnología? ¿Y hay un grupo entero de ellos en un "
"búnker? Probablemente sea mejor mantener a gente como esa en nuestro buen "
"bando. Lo que dicen parece ser cierto. La realidad está bastante jodida. "
"Aunque me hace preguntarme qué tan involucrados ELLOS estaban si saben todo "
"eso."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm not sure yet.  It's suspicious, yes, but they seem to be nearly as "
"confused as we are about some things.  Almost like they're scared by what's "
"happened."
msgstr ""
"Aún no estoy seguro. Es sospechoso, sí, pero al parecer están tan confundidos "
"como nosotros sobre algunas cosas. Casi como si estuvieran asustados por lo "
"que ha pasado."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I didn't say it was a SOLID theory, but maybe she's onto something.  This is "
"evil on a cosmic scale; I don't know how else to explain it.  Maybe she's "
"right.  Maybe the bones really are 'singing'."
msgstr ""
"No he dicho que sea una teoría SÓLIDA, pero quizás ella este en lo cierto. "
"Esto es el mal a escala cósmica; no sé de qué otra forma explicarlo. Quizá "
"tenga razón. Tal vez los huesos realmente estén 'cantando'."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So… are you down to kick some alien ass with me?"
msgstr "Así que... ¿te apuntas a partirle la cara a los alienígenas conmigo?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's not dwell on it.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "No nos detengamos en eso.  <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can't accept that.  Everything was just fine for a while, but the bad "
"started some years ago, with bad people doing bad things.  I think we all "
"knew it was gonna end one way or another.  But there's got to be some sort of "
"deeper explanation for… this!  Someone is responsible!"
msgstr ""
"No puedo aceptar eso. Todo fue bien durante un tiempo, pero lo malo empezó "
"hace unos años, con gente mala haciendo cosas malas. Creo que todos sabíamos "
"que iba a terminar de una forma u otra. ¡Pero tiene que haber algún tipo de "
"explicación más profunda para... esto! ¡Alguien es responsable!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Possibly, but we can never know for sure.  Sometimes bad things gather into "
"uncontrollable avalanches."
msgstr ""
"Posiblemente, pero nunca podremos saberlo con certeza. A veces las cosas "
"malas se acumulan incontrolablemente."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Those bad people are probably all dead now.  If bad things continue to "
"happen, it's just the nature of the universe.  Entropy and chaos are the "
"natural order of things."
msgstr ""
"Esa gente mala probablemente ya esté muerta. Si siguen ocurriendo cosas "
"malas, es simplemente la naturaleza del universo. La entropía y el caos son "
"el orden natural de las cosas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, it does seem a little grim…  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Sí, parece un poco sombrío...  <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<lets_go>  We don't have time for this nonsense…"
msgstr "<lets_go>  No tenemos tiempo para estas tonterías..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's always how it goes: someone knows someone else, they get drunk at some "
"Virginia wine party for rich elites, and suddenly state secrets are leaking "
"out.  'Oh, my Russian contacts got this covert intelligence'…  'My secret "
"Chinese spies think this crazy thing is happening'…  Sometimes they know and "
"sometimes they don't.  It's up to us to put the truth together."
msgstr ""
"Siempre es así: alguien conoce a otra persona, se emborrachan en alguna "
"fiesta de vinos de Virginia para élites ricas y, de repente, se filtran "
"secretos de Estado. Oh, mis contactos Rusos consiguieron esta información "
"encubierta'... 'Mis espías Chinos secretos piensan que esta cosa loca está "
"sucediendo'... A veces lo saben y a veces no. Depende de nosotros averiguar "
"la verdad."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm tired of talking.  Let's get moving and put that truth together for "
"ourselves…"
msgstr ""
"Estoy cansado de hablar. Pongámonos en marcha y construyamos esa verdad por "
"nosotros mismos..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"<lets_go>  I feel like it's useless worrying who they are when they're some "
"of the only friends we've got…"
msgstr ""
"<lets_go>  Siento que es inútil preocuparse por quiénes son cuando son "
"algunos de los únicos amigos que tenemos..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Once again, I'm staying out of the bone bullshit.  I hope the best for you "
"and the bone woman.  You definitely seem like you have things under control."
msgstr ""
"Una vez más, me mantengo al margen de la mierda del hueso. Te deseo lo mejor "
"a ti y a la mujer de los huesos. Definitivamente parece que tienes las cosas "
"controladas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe I shouldn't have mentioned it…  Let's just get moving."
msgstr "Tal vez no debería haberlo mencionado... Pongámonos en marcha."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Honestly, it doesn't matter who opened up what portal to wherever.  "
"Extraterrestrial monster?  Engineered bio-weapon?  Three children standing on "
"each others' shoulders in an alien Halloween costume?  I'll blast 'em either "
"way."
msgstr ""
"Sinceramente, no importa quién abrió qué portal a donde sea. ¿Monstruo "
"extraterrestre? ¿Arma biológica de ingeniería? ¿Tres niños parados uno sobre "
"el hombro del otro con un disfraz alienígena de Halloween? Los reventaré de "
"cualquier manera."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "'War of the Worlds', baby!  That's what I like to hear!  <lets_go>"
msgstr "¡La Guerra de los Mundos, nena! ¡Eso es lo que me gusta oír!  <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I refuse to believe things are just random.  Especially this!  The dead don't "
"start rising all over the world for no reason!"
msgstr ""
"Me niego a creer que las cosas sean simplemente aleatorias. ¡Especialmente "
"esto! ¡Los muertos no empiezan a levantarse por todo el mundo sin motivo "
"alguno!"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Let's keep moving.  This is a topic for another day, when we've actually "
"found some answers…"
msgstr ""
"Sigamos avanzando. Este es un tema para otro día, cuando hayamos encontrado "
"algunas respuestas..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that LMOE shelter"
msgstr "Echa un vistazo a ese refugio LMOE"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that LMOE shelter"
msgid "Maybe there's something left in that LMOE shelter you heard about."
msgstr "Tal vez quede algo en ese refugio LMOE del que oíste hablar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that LMOE shelter"
msgid "Any luck finding the LMOE shelter?"
msgstr "¿Has tenido suerte buscando el refugio LMOE?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that LMOE shelter"
msgid ""
"Damn, can't believe we finally made it.  I was smart enough not to store "
"anything that might rot, so as long as nobody else already broke in, I bet "
"there's at least two weeks of good food just sitting there.  Pristine "
"workshop down there, too.  It cost me a pretty penny to get built.  I could "
"tell you all about it sometime if you ever wanted.  Anyway, thanks for "
"helping me get back here.  It sure ain't safe to travel on your own anymore."
msgstr ""
"Joder, no me puedo creer que por fin lo hayamos conseguido. Fui lo "
"suficientemente inteligente como para no almacenar nada que pudiera pudrirse, "
"así que mientras nadie más haya entrado, seguro que hay al menos dos semanas "
"de buena comida allí. El taller está impecable. Me costó un dineral "
"construirlo. Podría hablarte de eso alguna vez si quieres. De todos modos, "
"gracias por ayudarme a volver. Ya no es nada seguro viajar solo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_1.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid ""
"You approach the LMOE and do as you were told, prying back a thin piece of "
"metal atop the doorframe, revealing an opening.  You reach inside and grab a "
"handle attached to a wire, pull hard on it, and hear a heavy metal *clunk*.  "
"The door is open."
msgstr ""
"Te acercas al LMOE y haces lo que te han dicho: retiras una fina pieza de "
"metal del marco de la puerta, dejando al descubierto una abertura. Introduces "
"la mano en el interior y agarras un asa sujeta a un cable, tiras con fuerza "
"de ella y oyes un pesado *clunk* metálico. La puerta se abre."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like it didn't work out."
msgstr "Suena como si no hubiera funcionado."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, I'd really be interested in seeing those maps."
msgstr "Oye, me gustaría ver esos mapas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why did you leave your bunker?"
msgstr "¿Por qué dejaste el búnker?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for telling me that.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Gracias por avisarme. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I do.  I'd be willing to part with them for, say, $1000.  Straight from "
"your ATM account, no cash cards."
msgstr ""
"Sí, lo sé. Estaría dispuesto a separarme de ellos por, digamos, 1000 dólares. "
"Directamente de tu cuenta de cajero automático, sin tarjetas de crédito."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$1000] You have a deal."
msgstr "[$1000] Trato hecho."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Whatever's in that map benefits both of us."
msgstr "Lo que sea que esté en ese mapa nos beneficia a ambos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How 'bout you fucking hand it over and I don't get pissed off?"
msgstr "¿Qué tal si me lo entregas y así no me cabreo?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry for changing the subject.  What was it you were saying?"
msgstr "Perdón por cambiar el tema. ¿Qué me estabas diciendo?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "All right.  Here they are."
msgstr "Está bien. Aquí tienes."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks!  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "¡Gracias!  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks!  <end_talking>"
msgstr "¡Gracias! <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice try.  You want the maps, you pay up."
msgstr "Buen intento. Si queréis los mapas, paga."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prepper_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Bien.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So tell me this 'hell of a story'"
msgstr "Así que cuéntame esta \"gran historia\"..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were you in for?"
msgstr "¿Y por qué estabas preso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a story in itself, my friend.  I had one of the largest grow-ops on "
"the Eastern seaboard.  Hah, the stories I could tell you… but I won't.  "
"That's all way behind me."
msgstr ""
"Esa es una historia en sí misma, amigo mío. Tuve uno de los mayores cultivos "
"de la costa este. Hah, las historias que podría contarte... pero no lo haré. "
"Eso ya quedó atrás."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This sounds a lot cooler than it is: possession of an unlicensed nuclear "
"accelerator."
msgstr ""
"Esto suena mucho más genial de lo que es: la posesión de un acelerador "
"nuclear sin licencia."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I got a little bit into black market organ trading.  It sounds worse than it "
"was… but it was pretty bad."
msgstr ""
"Me metí un poco en el mercado negro de órganos. Suena peor de lo que era... "
"pero era bastante malo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Assault charges.  I really don't want to get into it, let's just say that you "
"don't want to talk during a movie around me okay?"
msgstr ""
"Cargos por asalto. No quiero entrar en eso, digamos que no querrás hablar "
"durante una película a mi alrededor, ¿vale?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know, I don't really want to say anymore.  It's all behind me, and I'd "
"like to keep it that way."
msgstr ""
"Sabes, realmente no quiero decir nada más. Todo ha quedado atrás, y me "
"gustaría que siguiera siendo así."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you get out of lockup?"
msgstr "¿Cómo saliste del aislamiento?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you do from there?"
msgstr "¿Qué hiciste desde allí?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We let out the others in solitary.  We were stuck in, the guard bots had gone "
"haywire and wouldn't let anyone out, and the rest of the people except this "
"one guard had turned.  We spent a few days pulping <zombies> and trying to "
"figure a safe way past the bots.  Food was running short.  Finally we picked "
"the worst, only plan we could think of: we dragged some storage lockers to "
"the entry hall, used them as shields, and pushed them until we were close "
"enough to take out the bots' sensors with our weapons."
msgstr ""
"Dejamos salir a los demás en solitario. Estábamos atrapados, los robots "
"guardianes se habían vuelto locos y no dejaban salir a nadie, y el resto de "
"la gente excepto este guardia se había convertido. Pasamos unos días "
"machacando <zombies> e intentando encontrar una forma segura de pasar los "
"robots. La comida se estaba acabando. Finalmente elegimos el peor y único "
"plan que se nos ocurrió: arrastramos algunos armarios de almacenamiento al "
"vestíbulo de entrada, los usamos como escudos y los empujamos hasta que "
"estuvimos lo suficientemente cerca como para eliminar los sensores de los "
"robots con nuestras armas."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did that actually work?"
msgstr "¿Funcionó realmente?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It worked better than I'd imagined, honestly.  We thought the bots would "
"shoot the lockers but I guess they mistook us for family.  There were six of "
"us and four of them, and four of us made it out."
msgstr ""
"Funcionó mejor de lo que imaginé, honestamente. Pensamos que los robots "
"dispararían a las taquillas pero supongo que nos confundieron con la familia. "
"Éramos seis de nosotros y cuatro de ellos, y cuatro de nosotros logramos "
"salir."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/prisoner_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to the others that made it?"
msgstr "¿Y qué pasó con los otros que escaparon?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/professor_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/professor_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Do you think there's some way your knowledge could help us understand all "
"this?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cree que hay alguna manera de que su conocimiento pueda ayudarnos a entender "
"todo esto?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/professor_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/professor_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hard to say.  I'm not really an organic chemist, I did geological chemistry.  "
"I'm at a loss to how that relates, but if you come across something where my "
"knowledge would help I'll gladly offer it."
msgstr ""
"Es difícil de decir. No soy realmente un químico orgánico, hice química "
"geológica. No sé cómo se Es difícil de decir. No soy realmente un químico "
"orgánico, hice química geológica. No sé cómo se relaciona eso, pero si "
"encuentras algo en lo que mis conocimientos puedan ayudar, se lo ofreceré con "
"gusto.relaciona eso, pero si encuentras algo en lo que mis conocimientos "
"puedan ayudar, se lo ofreceré con gusto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/professor_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/professor_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cool.  What did you say before that?"
msgstr "Genial. ¿Qué dijiste antes de eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My story.  Huh.  It's nothing special.  I had people, but they've risen to be "
"with the Lord.  I don't understand why He didn't take me too, but I suppose "
"it'll all be clear in time."
msgstr ""
"Mi historia. Huh. No es nada especial. Tenía gente, pero se han levantado "
"para estar con el Señor. No entiendo por qué no me llevó a mí también, pero "
"supongo que todo se aclarará con el tiempo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you mean in a religious sense, or…?"
msgstr "¿Quieres decir en un sentido religioso, o...?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Of course.  It's clear enough, isn't it?  That… that end, was the Rapture.  "
"I'm still here, and I still don't understand why, but I will keep Jesus in my "
"heart through the Tribulations to come.  When they're past, I'm sure He will "
"welcome me into the Kingdom of Heaven.  Or… or something along those lines.  "
"It's not going exactly like I thought it would, but that's prophecy for you."
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto. Está bastante claro, ¿no? Ese... ese final, fue el Rapto. "
"Todavía estoy aquí, y todavía no entiendo por qué, pero mantendré a Jesús en "
"mi corazón a través de las Tribulaciones venideras. Cuando haya pasado, estoy "
"seguro de que Él me dará la bienvenida al Reino de los Cielos. O... o algo "
"parecido. No va exactamente como pensé que iría, pero eso es una profecía "
"para ti."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What if you're wrong?"
msgstr "¿Y si estás equivocado?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What will you do then?"
msgstr "¿Y qué vas a hacer entonces?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What?  How could you say something like that?  I can't believe you'd look at "
"all this and think it could be anything but the end-times.  The dead are "
"walking, the gates of Hell itself have opened, the Beasts of the Devil walk "
"the Earth, and the Righteous have all be drawn up into the Lord's Kingdom.  "
"What more proof could you possibly ask for?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué? ¿Cómo puedes decir algo así? No puedo creer que mires todo esto y "
"pienses que podría ser cualquier cosa menos el fin de los tiempos. Los "
"muertos están caminando, las puertas del mismo infierno se han abierto, las "
"bestias del diablo caminan por la tierra, y los justos han sido todos "
"llevados al Reino del Señor. ¿Qué más pruebas podrías pedir?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What will you do, then?"
msgstr "¿Qué harás entonces?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I will keep the faith, and keep praying, and strike down the agents of Hell "
"where I see them.  That's all we few can do, isn't it?  I suppose perhaps "
"we're the meek that shall inherit the Earth.  Although I don't love our odds."
msgstr ""
"Voy a mantener la fe, y voy a seguir rezando, y voy a derrotar a los agentes "
"del Infierno cada vez que pueda. Eso es lo que tenemos que hacer, ¿no? "
"Supongo que seremos los humildes quienes poblaremos la Tierra. Aunque no me "
"gustan nuestras posibilidades."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's clear enough, isn't it?  That… that end, was the Rapture.  I'm still "
"here, and I still don't understand why, but I will keep Jesus in my heart "
"through the Tribulations to come.  When they're past, I'm sure He will "
"welcome me into the Kingdom of Heaven.  Or… or something along those lines."
msgstr ""
"Está bastante claro, ¿no? Ese... ese final, fue el Rapto. Todavía estoy aquí, "
"y todavía no entiendo por qué, pero mantendré a Jesús en mi corazón a través "
"de las Tribulaciones a venir. Cuando hayan pasado, estoy seguro de que Él me "
"dará la bienvenida al Reino de los Cielos. O... o algo parecido."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I meant more the actual events.  What happened?"
msgstr "Me refería más a los hechos reales. ¿Qué pasó?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/religious_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh.  Well, I think it follows the good word in Revelations, if I remember "
"right.  I haven't talked to a preacher in a bit, you know.  There were the "
"plagues… the first one was the one a couple years ago, that big pandemic, "
"that was when people started talking about the end being near.  Then there "
"was a plague of blood, or was it violence?  That was the riots.  Then the "
"seas turned red with blood, that was from all the people being shot.  Then a "
"plague of fire, I remember that one for sure, that was when there were bombs "
"and things going off everywhere to try to contain the riots.  And then demons "
"and monsters walked the Earth, and the dead rose from their graves, and "
"finally the meek inherited.  Clear as day."
msgstr ""
"Oh. Bueno, creo que sigue la buena palabra en las Revelaciones, si recuerdo "
"bien. No he hablado con un predicador en un tiempo, ya sabes. Hubo las "
"plagas... la primera fue la de hace un par de años, esa gran pandemia, que "
"fue cuando la gente empezó a hablar de que el fin estaba cerca. Luego hubo "
"una plaga de sangre, ¿o fue de violencia? Fueron los disturbios. Luego los "
"mares se volvieron rojos de sangre, eso fue por toda la gente que fue "
"disparada. Luego una plaga de fuego, la recuerdo con seguridad, fue cuando "
"hubo bombas y cosas que estallaron por todas partes para tratar de contener "
"los disturbios. Y entonces los demonios y los monstruos caminaron por la "
"Tierra, y los muertos se levantaron de sus tumbas, y finalmente los mansos "
"heredaron. Claro como el día."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I lived alone, on the old family property way out of town.  My husband passed "
"away a bit over a month before this started… cancer.  If anything good has "
"come out of all this, it's that I finally see a positive to losing him so "
"young.  I'd been shut in for a while anyway.  When the news started talking "
"about Chinese bio weapons and sleeper agents, and showing the rioting in "
"Boston and such, I curled up with my canned soup and changed the channel."
msgstr ""
"Vivía sola, en la vieja propiedad familiar, lejos de la ciudad. Mi marido "
"falleció un mes antes de que esto empezara... de cáncer. Si algo bueno ha "
"salido de todo esto, es que por fin veo algo positivo en perderle tan joven. "
"De todas formas llevaba un tiempo encerrada en mí misma. Cuando las noticias "
"empezaron a hablar de armas biológicas chinas y agentes durmientes, y a "
"mostrar los disturbios en Boston y demás, me acurruqué con mi sopa enlatada y "
"cambié de canal."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I lived alone, on the old family property way out of town.  My wife passed "
"away a bit over a month before this started… cancer.  If anything good has "
"come out of all this, it's that I finally see a positive to losing her so "
"young.  I'd been shut in for a while anyway.  When the news started talking "
"about Chinese bio weapons and sleeper agents, and showing the rioting in "
"Boston and such, I curled up with my canned soup and changed the channel."
msgstr ""
"Vivía sola, en la casa de mi familia en las afueras del pueblo. Mi mujer se "
"murió casi un mes antes de que empezara esto... cáncer. Si algo bueno salió "
"de todo esto, es que finalmente puedo ver lo bueno de haberla perdido tan "
"joven. Estuve encerrado por un tiempo, igualmente. Cuando las noticias "
"empezaron a hablar de las bioarmas chinas y agentes durmientes, y a mostrar "
"los disturbios en Boston y esas cosas, me acurruqué con mi sopa enlatada y "
"cambié de canal."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I could help you clear out your farm if you wanted.  You just have to show me "
"the way…"
msgstr ""
"Podría ayudarte a limpiar tu granja si quieres. Sólo tienes que mostrarme el "
"camino..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "<npc_name> marks the location of the farm on your map."
msgstr "<npc_name> marca la granja en tu mapa."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I guess you look sturdy enough to take them on.  I marked the spot for you."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que pareces lo suficientemente fuerte como para enfrentarte a ellos. "
"Te he marcado el lugar."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know if I trust you quite like that, just giving away so many "
"personal details all at once.  Maybe later…"
msgstr ""
"No sé si me fío de ti totalmente, dando tantos detalles personales de "
"repente. Tal vez más tarde..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, didn't mean to intrude."
msgstr "Lo siento, no quería entrometerme."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/NC_Farmer_background.json
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that farm"
msgstr "Revisa esa granja"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that farm"
msgid "You were told to check out a farm that might be infested with zombies."
msgstr "Te dijeron que revisaras una granja que podría estar infestada de zombis."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
msgid "Any luck finding the farm?"
msgstr "¿has tenido suerte encontrando la granja?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
msgid ""
"I don't know how I can ever make it up to you!  I barely made it out of this "
"place alive.  I wasn't sure I'd ever see it again, to be honest."
msgstr ""
"¡No sé cómo podré recompensarte! Apenas salí con vida de este lugar. No "
"estaba seguro de si volvería a verlo, para ser honesto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
msgid "I guess I don't blame you.  I knew it wouldn't be easy."
msgstr "Supongo que no te culpo. Sabía que no sería fácil."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where's Buck now?"
msgstr "¿Dónde está Buck ahora?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I see where this is headed.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Ya veo a dónde se dirige esto. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I see where this is headed.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Ya veo a dónde se dirige esto.  <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry about Buck.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Siento lo de Buck. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/rural_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry about Buck.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Siento lo de Buck. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Listen.  I'm gonna cut this off short.  I work for you, okay?  I'm not "
"interested in getting attached.  You didn't pay me to be your friend."
msgstr ""
"Escuchen. Voy a acortar esto. Trabajo para ti, ¿vale? No me interesa "
"encariñarme. No me pagaste para ser tu amigo."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm not looking for a friend, but I've paid my dues and earned my way.  You "
"gotta pony up too.  We're stuck with each other for a bit."
msgstr ""
"No estoy buscando una amistad, pero ya pagué mis deudas y me hice mi camino. "
"Vas a tener que ponerte con algo. Estamos atrapados el uno con el otro por un "
"rato."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Don't mouth off to me.  I know where everyone else working for me comes from. "
" If I'm going to let you stand behind me with a loaded gun, you're going to "
"toe the <freaking> line too."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is this enough whisky for you?"
msgstr "¿Es suficiente whisky para ti?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine.  Let's talk business, then."
msgstr "Bien. Hablemos de negocios, entonces."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine, have it your way."
msgstr "Bien, haz lo que quieras."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine, then.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Está bien, entonces.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have it your way."
msgstr "Como quieras."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I respect where you're coming from, but no.  Not interested.  If you don't "
"like it, I can find another boss easy enough."
msgstr ""
"Respeto el lugar de donde vienes, pero no. No me interesa. Si no te gusta, "
"puedo encontrar otro jefe fácilmente."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"<swear!>  You're just gonna keep badgering me about this forever, aintcha.  "
"Fine.  Bring me a bottle of single malt, we share a drink, I tell you the "
"story."
msgstr ""
"¡Maldita sea! Vas a seguir insistiendo con esto para siempre, ¿verdad? Está "
"bien. Tráeme una botella de whisky de malta, compartimos una copa y te cuento "
"la historia."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll get looking for that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Lo buscaré.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_avatar.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<end_talking_later>"
#. ~ Avatar response indicated that the conversation is over via TALK_DONE.
msgid "I'll get back to you on that."
msgstr "Hablaremos más tarde."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, okay.  I can respect that.  How about this: bring me a bottle of single "
"malt, we share a drink, I tell you the story."
msgstr ""
"Sí, está bien. Puedo respetar eso. Qué te parece esto: tráeme una botella de "
"malta simple, compartimos un trago y te cuento la historia."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, yeah, this is a good choice.  Hold on to it for me, let's have a drink "
"later.  Right now we're practically swimming in good whisky, but some day the "
"last bottle will get drunk.  It's gonna be a long time before any of us is "
"brewing nice scotch, and we ain't never gettin' peat from Islay ever again.  "
"Makes me shed a tear just thinking about it."
msgstr ""
"Oh, sí, es una buena elección. Guárdalo por mí, tomemos un trago más tarde. "
"Ahora mismo estamos prácticamente nadando en buen whisky, pero algún día la "
"última botella se emborrachará. Va a pasar mucho tiempo antes de que alguno "
"de nosotros prepare un buen escocés, y no volveremos a recibir turba de Islay "
"nunca más. Me hace derramar una lágrima sólo de pensar en ello."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You owe me a story."
msgstr "Me debes una historia."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why was a guy with your skillset guarding a warehouse?  Must've been some "
"warehouse."
msgstr ""
"¿Y qué hacía un tipo con tus habilidades cuidando un depósito? Debe haber "
"sido un depósito importante."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was working for the Free Merchants like?"
msgstr "¿Cómo era trabajar para los Mercaderes Libres?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was working for the Old Guard like?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo era trabajar para la Vieja Guardia?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for that.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Gracias por eso.  <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fucking dull.  Caravan patrols were a bit more fun, for a while, but a guy "
"can only eat so much road dust.  Guarding that pile of bricks full of "
"sad-sack pussies who can't even justify surviving <the_cataclysm>?  Well, I "
"dunno.  They're not a bad bunch but I'm fine not working for them now."
msgstr ""
"Jodidamente aburrido. Las patrullas de caravanas eran un poco más divertidas, "
"por un tiempo, pero un tipo no puede comer mucho polvo de la carretera. "
"¿Vigilar ese montón de ladrillos llenos de coños tristes que no pueden ni "
"siquiera justificar su supervivencia en el <the_cataclysm>?. Bueno, no lo sé. "
"No son un mal grupo pero estoy bien no trabajando para ellos ahora."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scavenger_merc_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why was someone with your skillset guarding a warehouse?  Must've been some "
"warehouse."
msgstr ""
"¿Por qué alguien con tus habilidades estaba vigilando un almacén? Debe haber "
"sido algún almacén."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What came of it?"
msgstr "¿Qué salió de eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"If I got you the right stuff, do you think you'd be able to like… do science "
"to it?"
msgstr ""
"Si te consigo el material adecuado, ¿crees que te serias capaz de ... hacer "
"ciencia?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened with your leadership run?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasó con tu carrera de liderazgo?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Lamento oír eso.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I mean, if you find anything related to all this that boils down to "
"analytical biochemistry, I could probably help you decipher it and maybe "
"explain it a bit.  To do more, like analyze samples and such, I'd need a safe "
"lab of my own, with quite a lot of fancy gear, and a reliable power grid.  I "
"think that's a long way down the road."
msgstr ""
"Si encuentras algo relacionado con todo esto que se reduce a la bioquímica "
"analítica, probablemente podría ayudarte a descifrarlo y tal vez explicarlo "
"un poco. Para hacer más, como analizar muestras y demás, necesitaría un "
"laboratorio seguro propio, con bastante equipos de lujo, y una red eléctrica "
"fiable. Creo que es un largo camino por recorrer."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/scientist_2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I mean, if you find anything related to all this that falls under the "
"theoretical physics banner, I could probably help you decipher it and maybe "
"explain it a bit.  To do more, like construct functioning models and such, "
"I'd need a safe lab of my own, with quite a lot of fancy gear, and a reliable "
"power grid.  I think that's a long way down the road."
msgstr ""
"Quiero decir, si encuentras algo relacionado con todo esto que caiga bajo el "
"estandarte de la física teórica, probablemente podría ayudarte a descifrarlo "
"y tal vez explicarlo un poco. Para hacer más, como construir modelos de "
"funcionamiento y cosas así, necesitaría un laboratorio propio seguro, con "
"bastante equipo de lujo, y una red eléctrica fiable. Creo que es un largo "
"camino por recorrer."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/soldier_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/soldier_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fair enough, thanks.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Me parece justo, gracias. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/soldier_2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened in Newport?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasó en Newport?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, that's quite the story.  <the_cataclysm> happened on my wedding day."
msgstr "Oh, esa es toda la historia. El <the_cataclysm> sucedió el día de mi boda."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, I'm sorry…"
msgstr "Oh, lo siento..."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem surprisingly calm about all this."
msgstr "Pareces sorprendentemente tranquilo con todo esto."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I have this weird hope.  It's probably stupid, but I saw my fiancé peel "
"out of there with his sister - my maid of honor - in her pickup truck as "
"things went bad.  So, until I run into them again one way or another, I'm "
"just gonna keep on believing they're out there, doing well.  That's more than "
"most of us have."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, tengo una extraña esperanza. Probablemente sea estúpido, pero vi a mi "
"prometido salir de allí con su hermana -mi dama de honor- en su camioneta "
"mientras las cosas se ponían feas. Así que, hasta que me los vuelva a "
"encontrar de una forma u otra, voy a seguir creyendo que están ahí fuera, y "
"que les va bien. Eso es más de lo que la mayoría de nosotros tenemos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I have this weird hope.  It's probably stupid, but I saw my fiancée "
"peel out of there with her brother - my best man - in his pickup truck as "
"things went bad.  So, until I run into them again one way or another, I'm "
"just gonna keep on believing they're out there, doing well.  That's more than "
"most of us have."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, tengo esta extraña esperanza. Probablemente sea una estupidez, pero vi "
"a mi prometida salir de allí con su hermano, mi padrino, en su camioneta "
"cuando las cosas se pusieron feas. Así que, hasta que me encuentre con ellos "
"de nuevo de una forma u otra, voy a seguir creyendo que están ahí fuera, "
"haciéndolo bien. Eso es más de lo que la mayoría de nosotros tenemos."

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/Backgrounds/wedding_1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were you saying before that?"
msgstr "¿Qué decías antes de eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/OtherSurvivorStories/Brigitte_LaCroix_Background.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know those goth kids that used to hang out in malls?  I got out of a bad "
"situation with one.  I did okay but they got bit and we did a viking funeral, "
"very nice.  Before the end, they told me about this other goth kid that was "
"hanging out in graveyards and rocking out to metal or something.  That's the "
"last place I would go, but some people are just broken in the head, you know?"
msgstr ""
"¿Conoces a esos chicos góticos que solían pasar el rato en los centros "
"comerciales? Salí de una mala situación con uno. A mí me fue bien pero a "
"ellos los mordieron y les hicimos un funeral vikingo, muy bonito. Antes de "
"terminar, me hablaron de otro chico gótico que andaba por cementerios y "
"tocaba metal o algo así. Ese es el último lugar al que iría, pero hay gente "
"que tiene la cabeza rota, ¿sabes?"

