#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Provides hair cuts
msgid "Barber"
msgstr "Barbero"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Can I interest you in a trim?  It'll cost you 6 merch for a haircut or 3 for "
"a beard trim.  I can do color and styling too."
msgstr ""
"¿Te interesa un recorte? Te costará 6 mercas por un corte de pelo o 3 por un "
"recorte de barba. Puedo cambiar el color y el estilo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter2.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer2.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The doctor needs some help building an anesthetic machine.  Do you have "
"anything that could help?"
msgstr ""
"El médico necesita ayuda para construir una máquina de anestesia. ¿Tienes "
"algo que pueda servir de ayuda?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What is your job here?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es tu trabajo aquí?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[3 merch] I'll have a shave."
msgstr "[3 mercas] Quiero un afeitado."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[6 merch] I'll get a haircut."
msgstr "[6 mercas] Quiero cortarme el pelo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What?  I'm a barber… I cut hair.  There's demand for cheap cuts and a shave "
"out here."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué?, Soy un barbero y corto el pelo. Hay demanda de cortes y afeitados "
"baratos por aquí."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't imagine what I'd need your assistance with."
msgstr "No puedo ni imaginar para qué necesitaría tu ayuda."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stand still while I get my clippers…"
msgstr "Quedate quieto mientras busco mis tijeras..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks…"
msgstr "Gracias..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Want a drink?"
msgstr "¿Quieres beber algo?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm looking for information."
msgstr "Estoy buscando información."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's this token you gave me?"
msgstr "¿Qué es esta ficha que me diste?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to exchange ten tokens"
msgstr "Me gustaría cambiar diez fichas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "Thanks for bringing the glasses back."
msgstr "Gracias por devolver los vasos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to exchange five tokens"
msgstr "Me gustaría cambiar cinco fichas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to exchange four tokens"
msgstr "Me gustaría cambiar cuatro fichas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to exchange three tokens"
msgstr "Me gustaría cambiar tres fichas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to exchange two tokens"
msgstr "Me gustaría cambiar dos fichas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to exchange a token."
msgstr "Me gustaría cambiar una ficha."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "Thanks for bringing the glass back."
msgstr "Gracias por devolver el vaso."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If it isn't obvious, I oversee the bar here.  The scavengers bring in old "
"world alcohol that we sell for special occasions.  For most that come through "
"here though, the drinks we brew ourselves are the only thing they can afford."
msgstr ""
"Si no es evidente, yo superviso el bar. Los rebuscadores traen alcohol del "
"viejo mundo que vendemos en ocasiones especiales. Aunque casi todos los que "
"pasan por aquí solo pueden pagar las bebidas que elaboramos nosotros mismos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We have a policy of keeping information to ourselves.  Ask the patrons if you "
"want to hear rumors or news."
msgstr ""
"Tenemos una política de mantener la información para nosotros mismos. "
"Preguntale a los patrones si quieres escuchar rumores o noticias."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for nothing."
msgstr "Gracias por nada."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Take a look at our selection and let me know what you're interested in."
msgstr "Revisá nuestra selección y avisame si te interesa algo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We have a decent variety of drinks.  What interests you?"
msgstr "Tenemos una decente variedad de bebidas. ¿Qué te gustaría?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What are you in the mood for?"
msgstr "¿De qué tienes ganas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Our selection is a bit limited at the moment.  If you're willing to help out, "
"I can get some more variety in here."
msgstr ""
"Nuestra selección es un poco limitada en este momento. Si estás dispuesto a "
"ayudar, podría tener más variedad aquí."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just a glass of water, please."
msgstr "Solo un vaso de agua, por favor."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "<npc_name> sets a glass of water on the counter."
msgstr "<npc_name> pone un vaso de agua en el mostrador."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$8] I'll take a beer."
msgstr "[$8] Me gustaría una cerveza."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$12] I'll take a shot of brandy."
msgstr "[$12] Me gustaría un trago de brandy."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "<npc_name> sets a shot and a token on the counter…"
msgstr "<npc_name> pone un vaso y una ficha en el mostrador…"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$12] I'll take a shot of rum."
msgstr "[$12] Quiero un trago de ron."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$15] I'll take a shot of whiskey."
msgstr "[$15] Quiero un trago de whisky."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Bring the token back with your glass and I'll exchange it for a merch."
msgstr "Devuelve la ficha con el vaso y te lo cambio por un merca."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Some people like to hang on to them thinking they'll have value someday, but "
"I'd prefer it if you brought it back with your glass and I'll give you a "
"merch back from your purchase."
msgstr ""
"A algunas personas nos gusta conservarlos pensando que algún día tendrán "
"valor, pero preferiría que me lo devolvieras con tu vaso y te devolveré el "
"merca de tu compra."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Make 2 Stills"
msgstr "Hacer 2 Destiladores"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 2 Stills"
msgid ""
"The wine and beer we can brew are sufficient to attract most patrons, but we "
"need something a bit stronger to get them to forget their misery.  Could you "
"build me a pair of stills?"
msgstr ""
"El vino y la cerveza que podemos elaborar son suficientes para atraer a la "
"mayoría de los clientes, pero necesitamos algo un poco más fuerte para que "
"olviden su miseria. ¿Podrías construirme un par de alambiques?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 2 Stills"
msgid ""
"This should let us start producing whiskey, rum, and brandy when we get "
"access to the ingredients."
msgstr ""
"Eso nos va a permitir empezar a producir whisky, ron y brandy cuando tengamos "
"acceso a los ingredientes."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 2 Stills"
msgid "I'm sure you could find the design for the stills in home brewing books."
msgstr ""
"Estoy seguro de que puedes encontrar el diseño para los destiladores en los "
"libros de destilación casera."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 2 Stills"
msgid "Do you have the stills?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los alambiques?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 2 Stills"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 Yeast"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Sugar Beet Seeds"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Simple Knife Spears"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 5 Headlamps"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 3 Leather Body Armor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Molotov Cocktails"
msgid "Thank you for the delivery."
msgstr "Gracias por la entrega."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 20 Yeast"
msgstr "Encontrar 20 de Levadura"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 Yeast"
msgid ""
"The last batch that I brewed was terrible, I'm fairly sure something "
"contaminated the yeast we have been using.  Could you locate a source of "
"fresh yeast for us to use?  I'd need about 20 teaspoons of dry yeast to get "
"started."
msgstr ""
"La última remesa que destilé salió horrible, estoy bastante seguro de que "
"algo contaminó la levadura que hemos usado. ¿Podrías localizar una fuente de "
"levadura fresca para que usemos? Necesito cerca de 20 cucharadas de levadura "
"seca para empezar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 Yeast"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Sugar Beet Seeds"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "A Crutch to Lean on"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 3 Hotplates"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 200 Multivitamin Pills"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 4 Charcoal Purifiers"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a Chemistry Set"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Filter Masks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 4 Pairs of Rubber Gloves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Scalpels"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Advanced Emergency Care"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Syringes"
msgid "Thank you for your assistance."
msgstr "Gracias por tu asistencia."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 Yeast"
msgid "Yeast should be common in homes or bakeries."
msgstr "La levadura debería ser común en las casas o en las panaderías."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 Yeast"
msgid "Do you have the yeast?"
msgstr "¿Tienes la levadura?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 10 Sugar Beet Seeds"
msgstr "Encontrar 10 Sem. de Remolacha Az."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Sugar Beet Seeds"
msgid ""
"Sugar and molasses remains in short supply.  I've put in a request for more, "
"but it is unlikely that I'm going to see a reliable source for some time.  If "
"you are interested, we are going to need sugar beet seeds to meet future "
"demand regardless of what the scavengers can find.  Could you bring me at "
"least enough seeds to plant a small 10 meter long patch?"
msgstr ""
"El azúcar y la melaza siguen escaseando. He pedido más, pero es poco probable "
"que encuentre una fuente fiable en algún tiempo. Si te interesa, vamos a "
"necesitar semillas de remolacha azucarera para satisfacer la demanda futura, "
"independientemente de lo que puedan encontrar los carroñeros. ¿Podrías "
"traerme al menos suficientes semillas para plantar una pequeña parcela de 10 "
"metros de largo? (10 semillas)"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Sugar Beet Seeds"
msgid "Farms or supply stores might have a few seeds…"
msgstr "Las granjas o tiendas de suministros podrían tener algunas semillas..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Sugar Beet Seeds"
msgid "Do you have the sugar beet seeds?"
msgstr "¿Ya conseguiste las semillas de remolacha azucarera?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
msgstr "Consigue 12 Depósitos de Metal de 60 Litros"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
msgid ""
"The drinks we brew here have become a major draw for visitors and the "
"occasional trader.  Our batches have become larger, but we are still running "
"out of storage space between trading runs.  I've been able to get a few "
"volunteers to help me build a set of standing tanks, but I still need 12 "
"60-liter metal tanks to build them.  I've talked with the scrappers, but we "
"are a low priority at the moment."
msgstr ""
"Las bebidas que elaboramos aquí se han convertido en un gran atractivo para "
"los visitantes y los comerciantes ocasionales. Nuestras remesas son cada vez "
"más grandes, pero seguimos quedándonos sin espacio de almacenamiento entre "
"los intercambios comerciales. He conseguido que algunos voluntarios me ayuden "
"a construir un conjunto de depósitos de pie, pero aún necesito 12 depósitos "
"metálicos de 60 litros para construirlos. He hablado con los chatarreros, "
"pero de momento tenemos poca prioridad."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
msgid "Scrapping vehicles might be your best bet."
msgstr "Desguazar vehículos puede ser la mejor posibilidad."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 60-Liter Metal Tanks"
msgid "Do you have the 60-liter metal tanks?"
msgstr "¿Ya conseguiste los depósitos de metal de 60 litros?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
msgstr "Consigue 2 Bidones de 200 litros"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
msgid ""
"The other survivor outposts that we have contact with have been more than "
"eager to trade for beer or other drinks.  Transporting the drinks to them has "
"presented a number of challenges though.  If you could locate a pair of "
"200-liter drums, we should be able to keep them supplied while turning a "
"significant profit."
msgstr ""
"Los otros puestos avanzados de supervivientes con los que hemos contactado se "
"han mostrado más que dispuestos a comerciar por cerveza u otras bebidas. Sin "
"embargo, el transporte de las bebidas hasta ellos ha presentado una serie de "
"desafíos. Si pudieras encontrar un par de bidones de 200 litros, podríamos "
"abastecerles y obtener un beneficio considerable."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
msgid "Factories or junk yards are the only places I know where to look."
msgstr ""
"Las fábricas o los depósitos de chatarra son los únicos lugares que conozco "
"donde buscar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 200-Liter Drums"
msgid "Do you have the 200-liter drums?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los bidones de 200 litros?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My partner is in charge of fortifying this place, you should ask him about "
"what needs to be done."
msgstr ""
"Mi compañero está a cargo de fortificar el lugar, deberías preguntarle a él "
"acerca de lo que se necesita hacer."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll talk to him then…"
msgstr "Hablaré con él entonces..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Howdy."
msgstr "Buenas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
msgid "Crop Overseer"
msgstr "Supervisor de cultivos"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I hope you are here to do business."
msgstr "Espero que hayas venido para hacer negocios."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I figured you might be looking for some help…"
msgstr "Me imaginé que podrías estar buscando algo de ayuda..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm interested in investing in agriculture…"
msgstr "Estoy interesado en invertir en la agricultura..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to discuss my field…"
msgstr "Me gustaría hablar sobre mi campo..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/No_Hope/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_Captain.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you need done?"
msgstr "¿Qué necesitas que se haga?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My job is to manage our outpost's agricultural production.  I'm constantly "
"searching for trade partners and investors to increase our capacity.  If you "
"are interested, I typically have tasks that I need assistance with."
msgstr ""
"Mi trabajo consiste en gestionar la producción agrícola de nuestro puesto "
"avanzado. Busco constantemente socios comerciales e inversores para aumentar "
"nuestra capacidad. Si estás interesado, normalmente tengo tareas en las que "
"necesito ayuda."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Back to check on your field?  What can I help you with?"
msgstr "¿De vuelta a revisar tu campo? ¿En qué te puedo ayudar?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There's a field on the other side of the house that isn't being used for "
"anything right now.  We're willing to let you purchase it for your own "
"agricultural enterprises if you're interested."
msgstr ""
"Hay un campo al otro lado de la casa que ahora mismo no se utiliza para nada. "
"Estamos dispuestos a dejar que lo compres para tus propias actividades "
"agrícolas si estás interesado."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me more about this field."
msgstr "Cuéntame un poco más sobre ese campo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you build a fence around my field?"
msgstr "¿Puedes construir una valla alrededor de mi campo?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm looking to expand my field…"
msgstr "Quiero expandir mi campo…"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to plant some seeds…"
msgstr "Me gustaría plantar algunas semillas…"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to harvest some plants…"
msgstr "Me gustaría cosechar algunas plantas…"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We'll help plow the land and put up a sign to let everybody know it's yours.  "
"Once it's plowed, you can hire some workers to plant or harvest the crops for "
"a small fee of course.  Oh, and if you're growing anything we have a demand "
"for, we'll gladly take it off your hands after the harvest."
msgstr ""
"Te ayudaremos a arar la tierra y pondremos un cartel para que todo el mundo "
"sepa que es tuya. Una vez arada, puedes contratar a algunos trabajadores para "
"que planten o cosechen los cultivos, por un pequeño precio, claro. Ah, y si "
"cultivas algo que tengamos demanda, te lo quitaremos de las manos con mucho "
"gusto después de la cosecha."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm interested.  How much is it going to cost?"
msgstr "Estoy interesado. ¿Cuánto va a costar?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "350 merch should be enough to cover the purchase and the labor to plow it."
msgstr ""
"350 mercas deberían ser suficientes para cubrir la compra y la mano de obra "
"para arar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[350 merch] Seems like a fair price.  I'll take it."
msgstr "[350 mercas] Parece un precio justo. Lo tomaré."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid ""
"<npc_name> jots your name down on a ledger and yells out to nearby laborers "
"to begin plowing your new field."
msgstr ""
"<npc_name> anota tu nombre en un libro de contabilidad y grita a los obreros "
"cercanos que comiencen a arar su nuevo campo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm a bit short right now.  <end_talking_later>"
msgstr "Ahora mismo estoy un poco corto de dinero. <end_talking_later>"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, we could build a sturdy picket fence around it that will keep most "
"wildlife from nibbling at your crops.  Your crop yields will increase "
"slightly as well."
msgstr ""
"Por supuesto, podemos construir una valla resistente que impida que la mayor "
"parte de la fauna silvestre mordisquee tus cultivos. El rendimiento de tus "
"cultivos también aumentará un poco."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We'll have to divert a decent amount of lumber from our other projects for "
"the fence, but we can get it done for 200 merch."
msgstr ""
"Tendremos que desviar una cantidad decente de madera de nuestros otros "
"proyectos para la valla, pero podemos hacerlo por 200 mercas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[200 merch] Alright, build me a fence."
msgstr "[200 mercas] Muy bien, constrúyeme una valla."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid ""
"After counting your money, <npc_name> directs a nearby laborer to begin "
"constructing a fence around your plot…"
msgstr ""
"Después de contar tu dinero, <npc_name> indica a un obrero de cerca que "
"empiece a construir una valla alrededor de tu parcela..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have that much right now.  <end_talking_later>"
msgstr "No tengo mucho ahora mismo. <end_talking_later>"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We'll have to divert a decent amount of lumber from our other projects for "
"the fence, but we can get it done for 300 merch."
msgstr ""
"Tendremos que desviar una cantidad considerable de madera de nuestros otros "
"proyectos para la valla, pero podemos conseguirlo por 300 mercas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[300 merch] Alright, build me a fence."
msgstr "[300 mercas] Muy bien, constrúyeme una valla."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We can plow some more land around your field to give you room for more "
"plants.  Any existing plants or items in the way will be destroyed.  The "
"fence will also get moved and expanded.  Everything can be done for 200 "
"merch.  Still interested?"
msgstr ""
"Podemos arar un poco más de tierra alrededor de tu campo para darte espacio "
"para más plantas. Se destruirán todas las plantas u objetos que se encuentren "
"en el camino. La valla también se moverá y ampliará. Todo se puede hacer por "
"200 mercas. ¿Sigues interesado?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We can plow some more land around your field to give you room for more "
"plants.  Any existing plants or items in the way will be destroyed.  It'll "
"only cost 100 merch to expand.  Still interested?"
msgstr ""
"Podemos arar un poco más de tierra alrededor de tu campo para darle espacio a "
"más plantas. Cualquier planta u objeto existente en el camino será destruido. "
"Sólo te costará 100 mercas la ampliación. ¿Sigues interesado?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[200 merch] Yeah, let's do it."
msgstr "[200 mercas] Sí, hagámoslo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[100 merch] Yeah, let's do it."
msgstr "[100 mercas] Sí, hagámoslo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We'll plant the field with your choice of crop if you are willing to finance "
"it.  When the crop is ready to harvest, you can have us liquidate it or "
"harvest it for you.  Planting will cost 1 merch per plot."
msgstr ""
"Plantaremos el campo con el cultivo que elijas si estás dispuesto a "
"financiarlo. Cuando el cultivo esté listo para ser cosechado, puedes hacer "
"que lo liquidemos o que lo cosechemos por ti. La plantación tendrá un coste "
"de 1 merca por parcela."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[1 merch / plot] I'd like to plant some seeds."
msgstr "[1 merca / parcela] Me gustaría plantar algunas semillas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You can either have us liquidate the crop and give you the cash or pay us to "
"harvest it for you.  Harvesting will cost 1 merch per plot."
msgstr ""
"Puedes hacer que liquidemos la cosecha y te demos el dinero en efectivo o "
"pagarnos para que la cosechemos por ti. La cosecha costará 1 merc por parcela."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_crop_overseer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[1 merch / plot] I'd like to harvest the field."
msgstr "[1 merca / parcela] Me gustaría cosechar el campo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How can I help you today?"
msgstr "¿Cómo puedo ayudarte?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm sorry, I don't have time to help you at the moment."
msgstr "Lo siento, no tengo tiempo para ayudarle en este momento."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything else I can help with?"
msgstr "¿Hay algo más en lo que le pueda ayudar?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe I could help you with something?"
msgstr "¿Tal vez pueda ayudarte con algo?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I couldn't find any crutches, but I made these.  Will they work?"
msgstr "No pude encontrar muletas, pero hice estas. ¿Funcionarán?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "These will have to do…"
msgstr "Estos tendrán que hacer..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I have other patients to attend to.  Come back later."
msgstr "Tengo otros pacientes que atender. Vuelve más tarde."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't right now, I have other matters to attend to."
msgstr "Ahora mismo no puedo, tengo otros asuntos que atender."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[80 merch, 30m] I need you to patch me up."
msgstr "[80 mercas, 30min] Necesito que me cures."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[200 merch, 1h] I need you to patch my friends up."
msgstr "[200 mercas, 1h] Necesito curar a mis amigos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you mean something like pacemaker, then maybe.  What's the trouble?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you mean something like pacemaker, we can't really do much without "
"anesthesia."
msgstr ""
"Si te refieres a algo como un marcapasos, realmente no podemos hacer gran "
"cosa sin anestesia."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"No, i mean something, eeh, more sci-fi.  There are robo-guys in a stone "
"castle, they say they have such technology.  They even installed something "
"into me, look!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"No, i mean something, eeh, more sci-fi.  There are robo-guys in a stone "
"castle, they say they have such technology."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Curious.  Sorry, i have no idea how it works, and i'd be afraid to even touch "
"this parts."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Are you all right?  Sci-fi bionic by robots in a stone castle?  I have some "
"antipsychotics, if it helps."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm running out of office supplies.  I know… of all the things to need at a "
"time like this!  I just need to be able to keep track of and organize medical "
"records so that I can focus on helping people.  Ten binders and a ream of "
"paper should tide me over until some shipments come in."
msgstr ""
"Me estoy quedando sin material de oficina. Lo sé... ¡de todas las cosas que "
"se necesitan en un momento como éste! Sólo necesito poder llevar un control y "
"organizar los historiales médicos para poder centrarme en ayudar a la gente. "
"Diez carpetas y una resma de papel deberían servirme hasta que lleguen "
"algunos envíos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see what I can find."
msgstr "Veré lo que puedo encontrar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thanks, this will help a lot."
msgstr "Gracias, esto ayudará mucho."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Collect Office Supplies"
msgstr "Reunir Suministros de Oficina"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Collect Office Supplies"
msgid ""
"The doctor needs office supplies to keep track of medical records.  Bring "
"them 10 Book binders and 500 paper."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect Office Supplies"
msgid "Have you found the supplies yet?"
msgstr "¿Ya conseguiste los suministros?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect Office Supplies"
msgid "Thanks!  This should help keep things organized for a while."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Esto debería ayudar a mantener las cosas organizadas durante un "
"tiempo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "A Crutch to Lean on"
msgstr "Una muleta en la que apoyarse"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Description of mission "A Crutch to Lean on"
msgid "Bring the doctor some crutches."
msgstr "Llévale al doctor unas muletas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "A Crutch to Lean on"
msgid ""
"One of the laborers injured their foot pretty badly and I don't want them "
"walking on it for a few days at least.  Do you think you could find a pair of "
"crutches?"
msgstr ""
"Uno de los obreros se ha lesionado bastante el pie y no quiero que ande con "
"él al menos durante unos días. ¿Crees que podrías encontrar un par de muletas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "A Crutch to Lean on"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 Car Batteries"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 5 Backpacks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 80lb (10000 units) of Sugar"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 30 Glass Sheets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 100 Aspirin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 3 Hotplates"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 200 Multivitamin Pills"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 4 Charcoal Purifiers"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a Chemistry Set"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Filter Masks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 4 Pairs of Rubber Gloves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Scalpels"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Advanced Emergency Care"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Syringes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Simple Knife Spears"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 5 Headlamps"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 3 Leather Body Armor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Molotov Cocktails"
msgid "I'm counting on you."
msgstr "Cuento contigo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "A Crutch to Lean on"
msgid ""
"You might be able to find some in hospitals, but some makeshift crutches "
"would be better than nothing."
msgstr ""
"Quizá puedas encontrar algunas en los hospitales, pero unas muletas "
"improvisadas serían mejor que nada."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "A Crutch to Lean on"
msgid "Do you have the crutches?"
msgstr "¿Tienes las muletas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
msgstr "Consigue 5 pares de guantes médicos"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
msgid "Bring the doctor 5 pairs of medical gloves."
msgstr "Encuentra 5 pares de guantes médicos"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
msgid ""
"We're getting a lot of scrapes and bruises coming in right now, but it's only "
"a matter of time before we see a serious injury.  I'm not prepared for when "
"that happens and I'm hoping you can help.  To start off, I'm going to need "
"some more medical gloves to help prevent infections.  Can you bring me 5 "
"pairs?"
msgstr ""
"Ahora mismo nos llegan muchos raspones y moratones, pero es sólo cuestión de "
"tiempo que veamos una lesión grave. No estoy preparado para cuando eso ocurra "
"y espero que puedas ayudar. Para empezar, voy a necesitar más guantes médicos "
"para evitar infecciones. ¿Puedes traerme 5 pares?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Syringes"
msgid "Hospitals or clinics might have a few sitting around."
msgstr "Los hospitales y las clínicas pueden tener algunas por ahí."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 5 Pairs of Medical Gloves"
msgid "Do you have the medical gloves?"
msgstr "¿Conseguiste los guantes?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
msgstr "Anestesia para el Doctor."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
msgid ""
"Bring the doctor 3000 units of anesthetic.  Ask around the commune for "
"assistance in building an anesthetic machine."
msgstr ""
"Lleva al doctor 3000 unidades de anestesia. Pide ayuda en la comuna para "
"construir una máquina de anestesia."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
msgid ""
"I want to make sure we are setup to handle any major surgeries that come our "
"way, but pain management is going to be an issue.  For longer surgeries, "
"we're going to need some anesthetic.  Can you bring me 3000 units to start?  "
"We're also going to need an anesthetic machine to deliver it.  Maybe some "
"people around the commune can help with that?"
msgstr ""
"Quiero asegurarme de que estamos preparados para hacer frente a cualquier "
"cirugía importante que se nos presente, pero el control del dolor va a ser un "
"problema. Para las cirugías más largas, vamos a necesitar algo de anestesia. "
"¿Puedes traerme 3000 unidades para empezar? También vamos a necesitar una "
"máquina de anestesia para administrarla. ¿Tal vez algunas personas de la "
"comuna puedan ayudar con eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
msgid "Hospitals or clinics might have some.  Labs could have some as well."
msgstr ""
"Los hospitales o las clínicas podrían tener algunas. Los laboratorios también "
"podrían tener."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
msgid "Any progress on getting some anesthetic or parts?"
msgstr "¿Algún progreso en la obtención de anestesia o piezas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Anesthetic for the Doctor"
msgid ""
"The scavengers found more medical equipment than I expected and with the help "
"from the scrappers, I've been able to get most of it up and running.  I "
"should be able to perform more operations now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer2.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to hire your services."
msgstr "Me gustaría contratar tus servicios."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was sent here to assist in setting up the farm.  Most of us have no real "
"skills that transfer from before the Cataclysm, so things are a bit of trial "
"and error."
msgstr ""
"Me enviaron aquí para ayudar a construir la granja. La mayoría de nosotros no "
"tenemos habilidades reales usables desde antes del Cataclismo, así que las "
"cosas son un poco de prueba y error."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, I don't have anything to trade.  The work program here splits what "
"we produce between the refugee center, the farm, and ourselves.  If you are a "
"skilled laborer, then you can trade your time for a bit of extra income on "
"the side.  Not much I can do to assist you as a farmer though."
msgstr ""
"Lo siento, no tengo nada que intercambiar. El programa de trabajo aquí "
"reparte lo que producimos entre el centro de refugiados, la granja y nosotros "
"mismos. Si eres un trabajador cualificado, entonces puedes intercambiar tu "
"tiempo por un poco de ingreso extra. Sin embargo, no puedo hacer mucho para "
"ayudarte como agricultor."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh."
msgstr "Oh."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You mind?"
msgstr "¿Te importaría?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm just a lucky guy that went from being chased by the undead to the noble "
"life of a dirt farmer.  We get room and board, but won't see a share of our "
"labor unless the crop is a success."
msgstr ""
"Sólo soy un tipo afortunado que pasó de ser perseguido por los muertos "
"vivientes a la noble vida de un agricultor de tierra. Tenemos alojamiento y "
"comida, pero no veremos una parte de nuestro trabajo a menos que la cosecha "
"sea un éxito."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It could be worse…"
msgstr "Podría ser peor..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've got no time for you.  If you want to make a trade or need a job, look "
"for the foreman or crop overseer."
msgstr ""
"No tengo tiempo. Si quieres hacer un oficio o necesitas un trabajo, busca al "
"capataz o al capataz agricultor."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_farmer2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll talk with them then…"
msgstr "Hablaré con ellos entonces..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Appears at the ranch after you progress in the refugee center quests.
#. Faction critical.
msgid "Foreman"
msgstr "Capataz"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hello again.  If you have no other business with me, I'd like to talk to you "
"about something."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Can I help you, marshal?"
msgstr "¿Puedo ayudarte, alguacil?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Morning sir, how can I help you?"
msgstr "Buenos días, señor, ¿le puedo ayudar en algo?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Morning ma'am, how can I help you?"
msgstr "Buenos días, señora, ¿la puedo ayudar en algo?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The merchant at the Refugee Center sent me to get a prospectus from you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I heard you were setting up an outpost out here."
msgstr "Escuché que estabas estableciendo un puesto de avanzada aquí."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's your job here?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es tu ocupación aquí?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Hey, are you looking for workers here?  I know a couple people back at the "
"refugee center that might be willing to come."
msgstr ""
"Oye, ¿estás buscando trabajadores aquí? Conozco a un par de personas en el "
"centro de refugiados que podrían estar dispuestos a venir."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, are you looking for workers here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm afraid I don't have anything to offer."
msgstr "Creo que no tengo nada que ofrecer."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have anything to offer, but maybe the scrappers could help find some "
"materials."
msgstr ""
"No tengo nada que ofrecer, pero tal vez los desguazadores podrían ayudarte a "
"encontrar algunos materiales."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have anything to offer, but maybe the scavenger boss could help find "
"some materials."
msgstr ""
"No tengo nada que ofrecer, pero tal vez el jefe carroñero podría ayudarte a "
"encontrar algunos materiales."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have anything to offer, but you could talk to the scavenger boss and "
"the scrappers; They might be able to help."
msgstr ""
"No tengo nada que ofrecer, pero podrías hablar con el jefe de los "
"rebuscadores y los desguaces; quizá puedan ayudarte."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks anyway."
msgstr "Gracias de todas formas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ya, that representative from the Old Guard asked the two of us to come out "
"here and begin fortifying this place as a refugee camp.  I'm not sure how "
"fast he expects the two of us to get setup, but we were assured additional "
"men were coming out here to assist us. "
msgstr ""
"Ya, ese representante de la Vieja Guardia nos pidió a los dos que viniéramos "
"aquí y empezáramos a fortificar este lugar como campo de refugiados. No se "
"con qué velocidad espera que nosotros dos nos instalemos, pero nos aseguraron "
"que vendrían más hombres para ayudarnos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How many refugees are you expecting?"
msgstr "¿Cuántos refugiados están esperando?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hopefully moving out here was worth it…"
msgstr "Esperemos que mudarse aquí haya valido la pena..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm the engineer in charge of turning this place into a working camp.  This "
"is going to be an uphill battle, we used most of our initial supplies getting "
"here and boarding up the windows.  I've got a huge list of tasks that need to "
"get done, so if you could help us keep supplied I'd appreciate it.  If you "
"have material to drop off you can just back your vehicle into here and dump "
"it on the ground, we'll sort it."
msgstr ""
"Soy el ingeniero encargado de convertir este lugar en un campamento de "
"trabajo. Esto va a ser una batalla difícil, hemos utilizado la mayoría de "
"nuestros suministros iniciales para llegar aquí y tapiar las ventanas. Tengo "
"una lista enorme de tareas que hay que hacer, así que si puedes ayudarnos a "
"mantenernos abastecidos te lo agradecería. Si tienes material para dejar, "
"puedes traer tu vehículo aquí y dejarlo, nosotros lo ordenaremos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're still in early stages of getting set up, but we're not overly flush for "
"hands, that's for sure.  If they're willing to put in a hard day's work, we "
"can get them busy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll tell them that, but they seemed good for a bit of hard labor."
msgstr "Les diré eso, pero parecían buenos para un poco de trabajo duro."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"we're still in early stages of getting set up, but we're not overly flush for "
"hands, that's for sure.  I don't think we'd turn many people away, of course, "
"but besides strong hands and willing labor, we could really use someone who "
"could cook.  I can't tell you what it'd do for morale.  You could try asking "
"some of the people staying on the surface in the refugee center maybe, I "
"don't think they were part of most of the original discussions about the "
"ranch."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll keep an eye out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You've done a lot for the ranch, by generally helping the community with both "
"wellness and trade.  As the project lead, I want to make sure these efforts "
"don't go unnoticed."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mean setting up the doctor's office?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is this about bootstrapping the trade relating to the bar?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Understood.  Back to business."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ever since you got the bartender set up, our liquor business has been running "
"so much better!  As thanks for your efforts, I wanted to reward you with a "
"portion of recent profits."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I heard you helped jumpstart our local medical services.  With that basic "
"need covered, everyone has been able to focus on their work a lot more, so to "
"thank you for your efforts, I wanted to reward you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Cut 200 planks"
msgstr "Cortar 200 tablones"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Cut 200 planks"
msgid ""
"Our first project is to enclose the barn so that new refugees have a safe "
"place to sleep.  Before we can begin serious improvements, we need lumber to "
"work with.  Enclosing the four barn entrances will take nearly 400 planks… if "
"you could provide half of that, we should be able to take care of the other "
"half and construction.  If you don't have a truck, I'd make finding one your "
"first priority."
msgstr ""
"Nuestro primer proyecto es cerrar el granero para que los nuevos refugiados "
"tengan un lugar seguro donde dormir. Antes de empezar a hacer mejoras serias, "
"necesitamos madera para trabajar. Para encerrar las cuatro entradas del "
"granero se necesitarán casi 400 tablones... si pudieras proporcionar la mitad "
"de eso, deberíamos poder encargarnos de la otra mitad y de la construcción. "
"Si no tienes un camión, yo haría que encontrar uno fuera tu primera prioridad."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Cut 200 planks"
msgid "The more men we can bring to the camp, the quicker improvements can be made."
msgstr ""
"Cuantos más hombres podamos traer al campo, más rápido se podrán hacer las "
"mejoras."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Cut 200 planks"
msgid "Avoid destroying the furniture, we'll be needing it."
msgstr "Evitá destruir los muebles, los vamos a necesitar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Cut 200 planks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Blankets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2500 Nails"
msgid "Do you have them?"
msgstr "¿Los tienes?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Cut 200 planks"
msgid ""
"Great, I'll send word that we could use another set of hands or two to help "
"out here."
msgstr ""
"Genial, enviaré un mensaje diciendo que nos vendría bien otro par de manos o "
"dos para ayudar aquí."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 25 Blankets"
msgstr "Consigue 25 Mantas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Blankets"
msgid ""
"With the barn entrances enclosed, the refugees moving in there should feel "
"safer, but the weather can be bitter here.  We're going to need to build "
"makeshift beds in the stalls to ward off disease and frostbite.  We can take "
"care of the frames, but will need your help looting blankets.  We'd need 25 "
"blankets to provide the most basic sleeping accommodations."
msgstr ""
"Con los graneros con las puertas cerradas, los refugiados que se mueven hacia "
"allí deberían sentirse más seguros, pero el tiempo puede ser difícil aquí. "
"Vamos a tener que construir camas improvisadas en los establos para evitar "
"congelarnos y  enfermedades. Podemos encargarnos de las estructuras, pero "
"necesitaremos su ayuda para saquear las mantas. Necesitaríamos 25 mantas para "
"tener las comodidades más básicas para dormir."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Blankets"
msgid ""
"I'd start with looting hotels or you could sew them together… but that would "
"be a last resort."
msgstr ""
"Empezaría con el saqueo de hoteles o podría combinarlos... pero eso sería el "
"último recurso."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Blankets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2500 Nails"
msgid "Avoid destroying the furniture here, we'll be needing it."
msgstr "Evita destruir los muebles de aquí, los necesitaremos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Blankets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2500 Nails"
msgid "Your assistance is always appreciated."
msgstr "Tu asistencia siempre es apreciada."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 2500 Nails"
msgstr "Conseguir 2500 Clavos"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2500 Nails"
msgid ""
"Our supply of nails has been depleted.  I'm going to have to ask you to get "
"us a few more boxes.  Hardware stores should have a few if they haven't been "
"looted.  I suppose you may be able to find handfuls of them in building "
"rubble.  We'd need 2500 to have enough that we won't be sending you back out "
"too soon."
msgstr ""
"Nuestro suministro de clavos se ha agotado. Voy a tener que pedirte que nos "
"consiga unas cuantas cajas más. Las ferreterías deberían tener unas cuantas "
"si no han sido saqueadas. Supongo que podrá encontrar puñados de ellas en los "
"escombros de los edificios. Necesitaríamos 2500 para tener suficiente para no "
"enviarte de vuelta demasiado pronto."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2500 Nails"
msgid ""
"Deconstructing furniture isn't going to be efficient, try looking for boxes "
"or grabbing any sitting on top of rubble piles."
msgstr ""
"La deconstrucción de muebles no va a ser eficiente, trata de buscar cajas o "
"agarrar cualquier cosa sentada sobre montones de escombros."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 30lb (3888 units) of Salt"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30lb (3888 units) of Salt"
msgid ""
"I'm sure you've noticed the new workers that have started trickling in.  The "
"Free Merchant counsel is demanding that we immediately begin projects to "
"become self-sufficient due to limited supplies.  We are going to need to "
"rapidly setup an agricultural industry before winter and starvation catches "
"us unprepared and unsupported.  In order to get a half dozen shovels and a "
"couple of bags of seeds, we are going to have to trade for it.  I've already "
"got the deal lined up, but the only thing they are willing to trade it for is "
"salt.  I negotiated them down from 50 lbs to 30… we were hoping you might "
"have access to a source."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30lb (3888 units) of Salt"
msgid ""
"Salt is key to preserving meat and other perishables… without any excess food "
"it wouldn't do us much good now, but I imagine we'll need to send you out to "
"get more in the future."
msgstr ""
"La sal es clave para preservar la carne y otros productos perecederos... sin "
"ningún exceso de comida no nos servirá de mucho ahora, pero imagino que "
"tendremos que enviarte a buscar más en el futuro. "

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30lb (3888 units) of Salt"
msgid ""
"If you can find a source of salt water you should be able to boil it down.  "
"Alternatively, you can go into the cities and search restaurants."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30lb (3888 units) of Salt"
msgid "Do you have the salt?"
msgstr "¿Tienes sal?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30lb (3888 units) of Salt"
msgid "We are going to begin preparing our fields immediately."
msgstr "Vamos a empezar a preparar nuestros campos inmediatamente."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 30 Bottles (120 units) of Liquid Fertilizer"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30 Bottles (120 units) of Liquid
#. Fertilizer"
msgid ""
"Well, our first crop will be planted shortly, but I'm starting to suspect "
"that our profit margin is going to be much smaller than we expect.  With "
"limited seed for our original crop, our next course of action is to increase "
"the soil's fertility.  Is there any way you could find or produce a basic "
"liquid fertilizer for us?  We'd need at least 120 units or 30 full bottles to "
"make a significant improvement in our output."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30 Bottles (120 units) of Liquid
#. Fertilizer"
msgid ""
"I don't know the exact recipe, but I'm sure you could make it from a "
"commercial fertilizer or produce it from bonemeal."
msgstr ""
"No sé la receta exacta pero estoy seguro de que podrías hacerla con un "
"fertilizante comercial o producirla con harina de huesos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30 Bottles (120 units) of Liquid
#. Fertilizer"
msgid "I'd look through a few basic chemistry books to find a simple recipe."
msgstr "Revisaría algunos libros de química básica para encontrar una simple receta."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30 Bottles (120 units) of Liquid
#. Fertilizer"
msgid "Do you have the liquid fertilizer?"
msgstr "¿Tienes fertilizante liquido?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 30 Bottles (120 units) of Liquid
#. Fertilizer"
msgid "This really should make the first winter easier to survive."
msgstr "Esto va a hacer el primer invierno más fácil de sobrevivir."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 75 Rocks"
msgstr "Recoger 75 piedras"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 75 Rocks"
msgid ""
"Our current assessment for survivability has increased significantly thanks "
"to your efforts.  The next priority issue is securing a cleaner water source. "
" Drinking from the pond on the back end of the ranch has led to an outbreak "
"of dysentery.  We need to improve the sanitary conditions in the camp as "
"quickly as possible.  To do so, the first step is to dig a well and construct "
"stone fireplaces in the barn for the migrants to boil water.  We are going to "
"need at least 75 rocks from you if we hope to accomplish the task before we "
"all get sick.  After we have them installed, you will have free access to "
"them, guaranteed."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 75 Rocks"
msgid ""
"If you take a shovel to a pile of rubble, you should be able to pull out "
"structural grade rocks."
msgstr ""
"Si llevas una pala a un montón de escombros deberías ser capaz de sacar "
"piedra de grado estructural."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 75 Rocks"
msgid "Do you have the rocks?"
msgstr "¿Tienes las piedras?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 75 Rocks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 Pipes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2 Electric Motors"
msgid "I appreciate the work you do."
msgstr "Aprecio el trabajo que hacés. "

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 50 Pipes"
msgstr "Consigue 50 Tubos"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 Pipes"
msgid ""
"To fabricate the well's hand pump and construct components for several other "
"projects, we are going to need to find or fabricate a number of steel pipes.  "
"Plumbing is a distant possibility for now, but some form of irrigation will "
"eventually become desirable.  You could assist us with procuring 50 steel "
"pipes, if you so have the chance."
msgstr ""
"Para fabricar la bomba manual del pozo y construir componentes para varios "
"otros proyectos vamos a necesitar encontrar o fabricar una serie de tubos de "
"acero. La fontanería es una posibilidad lejana por ahora, pero alguna forma "
"de irrigación se convertirá eventualmente en deseable. Podrías ayudarnos a "
"conseguir 50 tubos de acero, si tiene la oportunidad."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 Pipes"
msgid ""
"Hopefully we will be able to assign new migrants to help fulfill our needs in "
"the future."
msgstr ""
"Con suerte, podremos asignar nuevos migrantes para ayudar a cumplir nuestras "
"necesidades futuras."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 Pipes"
msgid ""
"Pipes are used in numerous metal constructions.  Smashing abandoned furniture "
"may provide the material we need."
msgstr ""
"Las tuberías se utilizan en numerosas construcciones metálicas. Destrozar los "
"muebles abandonados puede proporcionar el material que necesitamos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 Pipes"
msgid "Do you have the pipes?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los tubos?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 2 Electric Motors"
msgstr "Reunir 2 motores eléctricos"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2 Electric Motors"
msgid ""
"With the well's completion, we are rapidly closing the sustainability gap.  "
"In order to expand from here, we will need massive quantities of lumber to "
"construct fortifications and new buildings.  We have already begun work on a "
"manually operated sawmill, but we will need two electric motors to control "
"the actual blades.  We were hoping you might be able to secure the motors for "
"us."
msgstr ""
"Con la finalización del pozo estamos cerrando rápidamente la brecha de la "
"sostenibilidad. Para expandirnos desde aquí necesitaremos cantidades masivas "
"de madera para construir fortificaciones y nuevos edificios. Ya hemos "
"comenzado a trabajar en un aserradero manual pero necesitaremos dos motores "
"electricos para controlar las cuchillas. Esperábamos que pudieras asegurarnos "
"los motores."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2 Electric Motors"
msgid ""
"Power for the motors will be provided by a salvaged truck battery, you need "
"not bring additional mechanical components."
msgstr ""
"La energía para los motores será proporcionada por una batería de camión "
"recuperada, no necesitas traer ningún componente mecánico adicional."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2 Electric Motors"
msgid ""
"A car dealership or a golf course might have some electric vehicles to get "
"one from.  Otherwise there's probably something broken down along the road."
msgstr ""
"Un concesionario de coches o un campo de golf podrían tener algunos vehículos "
"eléctricos de donde sacar uno. Si no, probablemente haya algo averiado en la "
"carretera."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2 Electric Motors"
msgid "Do you have the motors?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los motores?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 150 Units of Bleach"
msgstr "Reúne 100 unidades de Lejilla"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 150 Units of Bleach"
msgid ""
"Disease and infection remains a persistent problem among the refugees.  "
"Without dedicated medical personnel and facilities, I doubt everyone will be "
"willing to stick around when the next outbreak happens.  Until we can get a "
"former medic or nurse, I'm just going to have to improvise.  Sterilization "
"would be the first step I imagine.  Bring me 150 units of bleach so we can "
"get started."
msgstr ""
"Las enfermedades y las infecciones siguen siendo un problema persistente "
"entre los refugiados. Sin personal e instalaciones médicas dedicadas dudo que "
"todos estén dispuestos a quedarse cuando ocurra el próximo brote. Hasta que "
"podamos conseguir un ex-médico o enfermera, tendré que improvisar. La "
"esterilización sería el primer paso que imagino. Tráeme 150 unidades de lejía "
"para que podamos empezar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 150 Units of Bleach"
msgid "I'm sure you can find bleach in most homes…"
msgstr "Estoy seguro de que puedes encontrar lejia en la mayoría de los hogares..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 150 Units of Bleach"
msgid ""
"If you can't find a large supply I'd recommend checking hospitals or research "
"labs."
msgstr ""
"Si no puedes encontrar un suministro grande, te recomiendo buscar en "
"hospitales o laboratorios de investigación."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 150 Units of Bleach"
msgid "Do you have the bleach?"
msgstr "¿Tienes lejía?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 36 bandages"
msgstr "Reune 36 vendajes"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 36 bandages"
msgid ""
"We've started planning a medical clinic, but we are going to need a lot more "
"supplies if we hope to warrant sending one of the few people with medical "
"experience from the refugee center to our outpost.  I know first aid "
"equipment is rare, but they have all the basic supplies that I'm uncertain "
"of.  If you could bring in thirty-six bandages I'm sure we could supplement "
"them to make theirs last a bit longer."
msgstr ""
"Hemos empezado a planear una clínica médica pero vamos a necesitar muchos más "
"suministros si esperamos el envío de una de las pocas personas con "
"experiencia médica del centro de refugiados a nuestro puesto de avanzada. Sé "
"que los botiquines de primeros auxilios son raros, pero tienen todos los "
"suministros básicos que yo sepa. Si pudieras traer 36 vendajes estoy seguro "
"que podríamos complementarlos para que duren un poco más."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 36 bandages"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 6 bottles (60 units) of antiseptic"
msgid "We'll do our best to make them last…"
msgstr "Haremos todo lo posible para que duren..."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 36 bandages"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 6 bottles (60 units) of antiseptic"
msgid "Homes, hospitals, labs, and doctor offices would be where I'd check."
msgstr ""
"Casas, hospitales, laboratorios y oficinas de médicos son lugares en donde yo "
"buscaría."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 36 bandages"
msgid "Do you have the bandages?"
msgstr "¿Tienes vendajes?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 6 bottles (60 units) of antiseptic"
msgstr "Reune 6 botellas (60 unidades) de antiséptico"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 6 bottles (60 units) of antiseptic"
msgid ""
"We've started planning a medical clinic, but we are going to need a lot more "
"supplies if we hope to warrant sending one of the few people with medical "
"experience from the refugee center to our outpost.  I know first aid "
"equipment is rare, but they have all the basic supplies that I'm uncertain "
"of.  If you could bring in 6 bottles of antiseptic, I'm sure we could "
"supplement them to make theirs last a bit longer."
msgstr ""
"Hemos empezado a planear una clínica médica, pero vamos a necesitar muchos "
"más suministros si queremos justificar el envío de una de las pocas personas "
"con experiencia médica del centro de refugiados a nuestro puesto de avanzada. "
"Sé que el equipo de primeros auxilios es escaso, pero tienen todos los "
"suministros básicos necesarios. Si pudieras traer 6 tarros de antiséptico "
"estoy seguro de que podríamos complementarlos para que duren un poco más."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 6 bottles (60 units) of antiseptic"
msgid "Do you have the antiseptic?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los antisépticos?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 2 Arc Welders"
msgstr "Consigue 2 Soldadores de arco"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Arc Welders"
msgid ""
"The work you have done has swayed the leaders at the refugee center to send "
"someone out to assist with our medical needs.  The next step is for us to get "
"a sort of chop-shop setup so that we can begin using scrap metal to build "
"fortifications and equipment.  We are going to need a pair of arc welders for "
"our mechanics to use."
msgstr ""
"El trabajo que has realizado ha convencido a los dirigentes del centro de "
"refugiados para que envíen a alguien a ayudarnos con nuestras necesidades "
"médicas. El siguiente paso es montar una especie de desguace para poder "
"empezar a utilizar los restos de metal para construir fortificaciones y "
"equipamientos. Vamos a necesitar un par de soldadores de arco para que "
"nuestros mecánicos puedan utilizarlos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Arc Welders"
msgid "With two, we should be able to repair one if it breaks."
msgstr "Con dos, vamos a poder reparar una si se rompe."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Arc Welders"
msgid ""
"The only place I've seen them is garages, but I imagine you could find them "
"in some stores."
msgstr ""
"El único lugar donde los he visto es en los garajes, pero me imagino que "
"podrías encontrarlos en algunas tiendas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Arc Welders"
msgid "Do you have the welders?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los soldadores?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 12 Car Batteries"
msgstr "Consigue 12 Baterías de Coche"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 Car Batteries"
msgid ""
"We have the basic equipment that we need, but without a functioning power "
"grid, we are forced to rely on the readily available vehicle batteries.  This "
"is going to be a chore, but I'll need twelve car batteries to swap between "
"charging and powering our equipment.  The good news is that they don't need "
"to be charged; we can take care of that."
msgstr ""
"Tenemos el equipo básico que necesitamos, pero sin una red de energía en "
"funcionamiento nos vemos obligados a depender de las baterías de los "
"vehículos que ya están disponibles. Esto va a ser una faena, pero necesitaré "
"doce baterías de auto para cambiar entre la carga y la alimentación de "
"nuestro equipo. La buena noticia es que no necesitan estar cargadas, podemos "
"encargarnos de eso."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 Car Batteries"
msgid ""
"Cars can be found in traffic jams along roads or in parking lots… I'm sure "
"you can find a few."
msgstr ""
"Los coches se pueden encontrar en los atascos de las carreteras o en los "
"aparcamientos... Estoy seguro de que puedes encontrar unos pocos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 Car Batteries"
msgid "Do you have the car batteries?"
msgstr "¿Tienes baterías de coche?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 12 Car Batteries"
msgid "I'm impressed with your abilities."
msgstr "Me impresionan tus habilidades"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 2 Two-Way Radios"
msgstr "Consigue 2 Radios Bidireccionales"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Two-Way Radios"
msgid ""
"Check with the nurse when you get a chance; I know she will need help setting "
"up our clinic.  On the construction front, we are going to need to get "
"dedicated scavenger teams setup to bring in the miscellaneous supplies that "
"we use in small quantities.  We are going to start setting up a junk shop for "
"them behind the sawmill, so we could use your help with that.  Communication "
"is the biggest obstacle for the teams… could you bring in a pair of two-way "
"radios?"
msgstr ""
"Pregúntale a la enfermera cuando tengas la oportunidad; sé que necesitará "
"ayuda para montar nuestra clínica. En cuanto a la construcción, vamos a tener "
"que organizar equipos de búsqueda para que traigan los suministros que "
"utilizamos en pequeñas cantidades. Vamos a empezar a montar una tienda de "
"chatarra para ellos detrás del aserradero, así que nos vendría bien vuestra "
"ayuda. La comunicación es el mayor obstáculo para los equipos... ¿podrías "
"traer un par de radios bidireccionales?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Two-Way Radios"
msgid "Organizing the scavenging missions is difficult enough without communication."
msgstr "Organizar las misiones de búsqueda ya es bastante difícil sin la comunicación."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Two-Way Radios"
msgid "You should be able to find them in electronics stores or at a police station."
msgstr ""
"Deberías poder encontrarlos en tiendas de electrónica o en una comisaría de "
"policía."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Two-Way Radios"
msgid "Do you have the two-way radios?"
msgstr "¿Tienes radios bidireccionales?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Two-Way Radios"
msgid "I'm sure the scavengers will find these useful."
msgstr "Estoy seguro de que los rebuscadores encontrarán esto útil."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 5 Backpacks"
msgstr "Conseguir 5 Mochilas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 5 Backpacks"
msgid ""
"The volunteers for the scavenging teams will need to be issued some basic "
"equipment.  When the boss sets up shop in the junk shed, you should ask him "
"what else he needs for his teams.  In the meantime, we can provide a few "
"backpacks to get them started.  Could you find five backpacks to give to the "
"initial team?"
msgstr ""
"A los voluntarios de los equipos de búsqueda se les deberá entregar un equipo "
"básico. Cuando el jefe se instale en el cobertizo de basura, deberías "
"preguntarle qué más necesita para sus equipos. Mientras tanto, podemos "
"proporcionartes algunas mochilas para que empiecen. ¿Podrías encontrar cinco "
"mochilas para dar al equipo inicial?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 5 Backpacks"
msgid "It may be easier to make them if you can't find a school or something."
msgstr "Puede ser más fácil hacerlas si no puedes encontrar una escuela o algo así."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 5 Backpacks"
msgid "Do you have the backpacks?"
msgstr "¿Tienes mochilas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 5 Backpacks"
msgid "Having at least basic equipment greatly increases survivability.  Thanks."
msgstr ""
"Por lo menos, tener el equipamiento básico, aumenta mucho la posibilidad de "
"supervivencia. Gracias. "

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
msgstr "Consigue una copia de La Biblia del Cervecero"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
msgid ""
"Growth has lately begun to stall.  We have individuals passing through the "
"outpost, but the prospect of hard labor just to eke out an existence is "
"driving them away.  We've asked around and decided that, despite our pressing "
"needs, building a bar ought to draw some of the less committed individuals to "
"the outpost.  Unlike other settlements, the more hands we have, the more food "
"we can produce… at least in the long term.  Unfortunately, no one here has "
"brewed alcoholic drinks before, so we are going to need you to find a book "
"called the 'Homebrewer's Bible' or something along those lines."
msgstr ""
"El crecimiento se ha estancado últimamente, tenemos individuos que pasan por "
"el puesto de avanzada, pero la perspectiva de trabajo duro sólo para ganarse "
"la vida los está alejando. Hemos preguntado por ahí y hemos decidido que, a "
"pesar de nuestras necesidades urgentes, la construcción de un bar debería "
"atraer a algunos de los individuos menos comprometidos con el puesto. A "
"diferencia de otros asentamientos, cuantas más manos tengamos, más comida "
"podremos producir... al menos a largo plazo. Desafortunadamente, nadie aquí "
"ha elaborado bebidas alcohólicas antes, así que necesitaremos que encuentres "
"un libro llamado \"La Biblia del Cervecero\" o algo por el estilo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
msgid "I guess you should search homes or libraries?"
msgstr "¿Supongo que debería buscar en bibliotecas u hogares?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
msgid "I guarantee we will toast to your name when the bar is finished."
msgstr "Te garantizo que vamos a brindar en tu nombre cuando el bar esté terminado."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 80lb (10000 units) of Sugar"
msgstr "Reúne 36kg (10000 unidades) de Azucar"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 80lb (10000 units) of Sugar"
msgid ""
"Just flipping through the book, I can tell that one ingredient in most of the "
"alcoholic drinks that we don't have a large supply of is sugar.  What alcohol "
"we have been able to loot isn't going to last us long, so starting our first "
"large batch is a priority.  Could you bring in 80 lbs of sugar?  That should "
"last us until we can start producing our own supply."
msgstr ""
"Solamente hojeando el libro puedo darme cuenta que uno de los ingredientes en "
"la mayoría de las bebidas alcohólicas y del cual no tenemos un gran "
"suministro, es el azúcar. El alcohol que podamos encontrar no nos va a durar "
"mucho, así que es una prioridad comenzar nuestra primer gran remesa. ¿Podrías "
"traernos 36kg de azúcar? Eso nos va a durar hasta que podamos empezar a "
"producir nuestro propio suministro."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 80lb (10000 units) of Sugar"
msgid ""
"You might get lucky finding it, but you could always boil it out of fruit if "
"you are familiar with the process.  Or go into the cities and look in "
"restaurants and bakeries."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 80lb (10000 units) of Sugar"
msgid "Do you have the sugar?"
msgstr "¿Tienes azúcar?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 80lb (10000 units) of Sugar"
msgid ""
"There is a large group of thirsty individuals in our outpost that are truly "
"thankful for your work."
msgstr ""
"Hay un gran grupo de individuos sedientos en nuestro puesto de avanzada que "
"están verdaderamente agradecidos por tu trabajo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Collect 30 Glass Sheets"
msgstr "Reunir 30 Láminas de Cristal"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 30 Glass Sheets"
msgid ""
"Although we are an agricultural outpost, we are restricted to growing plants "
"that are compatible with the New England climate during the warmer months.  "
"The easiest way to work around that is to build greenhouses to supplement our "
"external fields.  There isn't going to be an easy way to build these.  We are "
"going to need a massive number of glass sheets to enclose the frames.  The "
"first house will need 30 sheets of glass if you are still interested."
msgstr ""
"Aunque somos un puesto de avanzada agrícola, estamos limitados a cultivar "
"plantas compatibles con el clima de Nueva Inglaterra durante los meses más "
"cálidos. La forma más fácil de trabajar en esto es construir invernaderos "
"para complementar nuestros campos externos. No va a haber una forma fácil de "
"construirlos, vamos a necesitar un gran número de láminas de cristal para "
"encerrar los marcos. La primera casa necesitará 30 láminas de cristal si aún "
"están interesado."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 30 Glass Sheets"
msgid ""
"Deconstructing existing windows is the only way I know of to keep the sheets "
"intact."
msgstr ""
"La deconstrucción de las ventanas existentes es la única manera que conozco "
"de mantener las hojas intactas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 30 Glass Sheets"
msgid "Do you have the glass sheets?"
msgstr "¿Ya conseguiste las láminas de cristal?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 30 Glass Sheets"
msgid "We'll begin planting our first seeds as soon as we can get these installed."
msgstr ""
"Empezaremos a plantar nuestras primeras semillas tan pronto como podamos "
"instalarlas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Unfortunately, I don't have anything that can help."
msgstr "Por desgracia, no tengo nada que pueda ayudar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I don't know what I could offer."
msgstr "No sé qué podría ofrecer."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Afraid not.  Maybe somebody else could help."
msgstr "Me temo que no. Tal vez alguien más podría ayudar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Maybe the scrapper would have some spare parts?"
msgstr "¿Tal vez el desguace tenga algunas piezas de repuesto?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Mission source for clinic.  Provides medical attention.
msgid "Nurse"
msgstr "Enfermera"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was a practicing nurse, so I've taken over the medical responsibilities of "
"the outpost till we can locate a physician."
msgstr ""
"Yo era auxiliar de enfermería practicante por lo que me he hecho cargo de las "
"responsabilidades médicas del puesto hasta que podamos conseguir un médico."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm willing to pay a premium for medical supplies that you might be able to "
"scavenge up.  I also have a few miscellaneous jobs from time to time."
msgstr ""
"Estoy dispuesto a pagar un extra por los suministros médicos que puedas ser "
"capaz de rebuscar. También tengo algunos trabajos variados de vez en cuando."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of jobs do you have for me?"
msgstr "¿Qué tipo de trabajo tienen para mí?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not now."
msgstr "No ahora."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can take a look at you or your companions if you have any small injuries.  "
"Anything more than some bleeding and you'll need to get a doctor to take a "
"look."
msgstr ""
"Puedo revisarte a ti o a tus compañeros si tienes alguna pequeña herida. Si "
"hay algo más que una hemorragia, tendrás que pedirle a un médico que te "
"revise."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[40 merch, 15m] I need you to patch me up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[100 merch, 30m] I need you to patch my friends up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That's the best I can do on short notice."
msgstr "Eso es lo mejor que puedo hacer con poco tiempo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Collect 100 Aspirin"
msgstr "Reunir 100 Aspirinas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 100 Aspirin"
msgid ""
"I've got a handful of bandages and a few first aid kits to work with at the "
"moment… in other words I'm completely unable to treat most serious medical "
"emergencies.  I'm supposed to have priority on any medical supplies that the "
"scavengers bring in, but I imagine the black market for the stuff will "
"prevent me from ever seeing it.  I could use your help getting me 100 aspirin "
"pills to start with."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 100 Aspirin"
msgid "Aspirin is pretty common in homes and convenience stores."
msgstr "La aspirina es bastante común en los hogares y en las tiendas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 100 Aspirin"
msgid "Do you have the aspirin?"
msgstr "¿Tienes aspirina?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 100 Aspirin"
msgid "We'll go through this pretty quickly, but it does help."
msgstr "Pasaremos por esto bastante rápido, pero ayuda."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Collect 3 Hotplates"
msgstr "Reunir 3 Placa térmica eléctrica Eléctricas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 3 Hotplates"
msgid ""
"I was given a few bottles of bleach when I arrived, but I need a number of "
"hotplates to actually sterilize equipment.  I'm sure you can find them in any "
"old house or appliance store.  Three should be enough for now."
msgstr ""
"Me dieron unas cuantas botellas de lejía cuando llegué, pero necesito varios "
"hornillos para esterilizar realmente el equipo. Estoy seguro de que puedes "
"encontrarlos en cualquier casa vieja o tienda de electrodomésticos. Tres "
"deberían ser suficientes por ahora."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 3 Hotplates"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 200 Multivitamin Pills"
msgid "It should be a fairly common item.  Don't know what else to say."
msgstr "Debería ser un objeto bastante común. No sé qué otra cosa decirte."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 3 Hotplates"
msgid "Do you have the hotplates?"
msgstr "¿Tienes placa térmica eléctricas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Collect 200 Multivitamin Pills"
msgstr "Reunir 200 Pastillas de Multivitaminas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 200 Multivitamin Pills"
msgid ""
"Disease is spreading rapidly due to poor nutrition and there is little that I "
"can do about it.  With food being scarce, people are willing to survive on "
"whatever they can.  I need to start supplementing the outpost's diet with "
"vitamins to prevent potential deaths indirectly attributable to nutrition.  I "
"know it is a lot, but if you could bring me 200 multivitamin pills, I'd be "
"able to treat the most vulnerable before they spread anything to the rest of "
"us."
msgstr ""
"La enfermedad se está extendiendo rápidamente debido a la mala nutrición y "
"hay poco que pueda hacer al respecto. Con la escasez de alimentos, la gente "
"está dispuesta a sobrevivir con lo que pueda. Necesito empezar a complementar "
"la dieta del puesto de avanzada con vitaminas para prevenir posibles muertes "
"indirectamente atribuibles a la nutrición. Sé que es mucho, pero si me "
"trajeran 200 píldoras multivitamínicas podría tratar a los más vulnerables "
"antes de que contagien al resto de nosotros."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Collect 200 Multivitamin Pills"
msgid "Do you have the vitamins?"
msgstr "¿Tienes vitaminas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Make 4 Charcoal Purifiers"
msgstr "Fabricar 4 Potabilizadores de Carbón"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 4 Charcoal Purifiers"
msgid ""
"Despite my recommendations, we continue to have travelers come in with "
"illnesses that I've been able to trace back to contaminated drinking water.  "
"When boiling water isn't an option, they need some form of charcoal water "
"filter that they can use.  If you could build me four charcoal water filters, "
"I'll distribute them to groups as they pass through."
msgstr ""
"A pesar de mis recomendaciones, seguimos teniendo viajeros que llegan con "
"enfermedades que he podido rastrear hasta el agua potable contaminada. Cuando "
"hervir el agua no es una opción, necesitan algún tipo de filtro de agua a "
"carbón que puedan usar. Si me construyes cuatro filtros de agua de carbón, "
"los distribuiré a los grupos a medida que pasen."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 4 Charcoal Purifiers"
msgid ""
"With some basic survival and crafting skills, you should be able to make them "
"with little effort."
msgstr ""
"Con alguna habilidad básica en supervivencia y fabricación, deberías poder "
"construirlos sin mucho esfuerzo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 4 Charcoal Purifiers"
msgid "Do you have the charcoal water filters?"
msgstr "¿Tienes filtros de carbón para el agua?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find a Chemistry Set"
msgstr "Consigue un Equipo de Química"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a Chemistry Set"
msgid ""
"I've been working on producing some of our own medical supplies, but I'm "
"going to need a chemistry set to get everything that I need in order.  Is "
"there any way you could go through one of the school chemistry labs and steal "
"me a chemistry set?"
msgstr ""
"Estuve trabajando en la producción de algunos suministros médicos propios, "
"pero voy a necesitar un equipo de química para poner todo lo que necesito en "
"orden. ¿Hay alguna forma de que puedas ir a los laboratorios de las escuelas "
"y me robes un equipo de química?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a Chemistry Set"
msgid "You might be able to find one in a pharmacy if you can't find a school."
msgstr "Podrías encontrar una en una farmacia si no puedes encontrar una escuela."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a Chemistry Set"
msgid "Do you have the chemistry set?"
msgstr "¿Tienes el equipo de química?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 10 Filter Masks"
msgstr "Consigue 10 Filtros de Máscara"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Filter Masks"
msgid ""
"The number of airway infections that I've encountered in the past week has "
"depleted my supply of masks.  Could you find me 10 filter masks?  I tend to "
"only distribute them in severe cases, so I'll be sure to make them last."
msgstr ""
"El número de infecciones de las vías respiratorias que he encontrado en la "
"última semana ha agotado mi suministro de máscaras. ¿Podría encontrarme 10 "
"máscaras con filtro? Tiendo a distribuirlas sólo en casos severos, así que me "
"aseguraré de que duren."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Filter Masks"
msgid "You may be able to make one if you had the right guide."
msgstr "Podrías hacer uno si tuvieras la guía adecuada."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Filter Masks"
msgid "Do you have the filter masks?"
msgstr "¿Tienes las mascarillas de filtro?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 4 Pairs of Rubber Gloves"
msgstr "Consigue 4 Pares de Guantes de Goma"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 4 Pairs of Rubber Gloves"
msgid ""
"The bodily fluids that I often have to clean up and the caustic chemicals I "
"deal with have done a number on my current pair of gloves.  Could you find me "
"four pairs of heavy rubber gloves?  That should be enough that I can task a "
"few laborers with cleanup details in the event of an outbreak."
msgstr ""
"Los fluidos corporales que a menudo tengo que limpiar y los químicos "
"cáusticos que uso han mermado mi cantidad de guantes. ¿Podrías conseguirme "
"cuatro pares de guantes de goma resistente? Eso debería ser suficiente para "
"asignarle tareas de higiene a algunos trabajadores en el caso de un brote."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 4 Pairs of Rubber Gloves"
msgid "You should be able to find them in cleaning closets."
msgstr "Deberías poder encontrarlos en los armarios de limpieza."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 4 Pairs of Rubber Gloves"
msgid "Do you have the rubber gloves?"
msgstr "¿Tienes un par de guantes de goma?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 2 Scalpels"
msgstr "Consigue 2 Escalpelos"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Scalpels"
msgid ""
"I heard that we may have a physician on his way here.  The workers have "
"already begun expanding the clinic, but I need you to locate a pair of "
"scalpels to use in surgery when he arrives.  I'm sure you should be able to "
"find them in a hospital or craft shop."
msgstr ""
"Oí que puede que tengamos un médico de camino aquí. Los trabajadores ya han "
"empezado a ampliar la clínica pero necesito que localices un par de bisturís "
"para usar en la cirugía cuando llegue. Estoy seguro de que podrá encontrarlos "
"en un hospital o en una tienda de artesanías."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Scalpels"
msgid "Hospitals and crafting stores should have a few."
msgstr "Los hospitales y las tiendas de fabricación deberían tener algunos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 2 Scalpels"
msgid "Do you have the scalpels?"
msgstr "¿Tienes los bisturís?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Advanced Emergency Care"
msgstr "Consigue Guía de Cuidados Avanzados de Emergencia"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Advanced Emergency Care"
msgid ""
"Have you heard of a book called the 'Guide to Advanced Emergency Care?'  I "
"really need a copy.  The doctor is requesting a lot of supplies that I'm not "
"familiar with, but I believe I could make if I could get a copy of the book."
msgstr ""
"¿Ha oído hablar de un libro llamado \"Guía de Cuidados Avanzados de "
"Emergencia\"? Realmente necesito una copia. El doctor está solicitando un "
"montón de suministros que no conozco pero creo que podría hacer si pudiera "
"conseguir una copia del libro."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Advanced Emergency Care"
msgid "Libraries are the only place I'd think to look."
msgstr "Las bibliotecas son los únicos lugares donde los buscaria."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Advanced Emergency Care"
msgid "Do you have the Guide to Advanced Emergency Care?"
msgstr "¿Tienes la Guía de Cuidados de Emergencia Avanzados?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 10 Syringes"
msgstr "Consigue 10 Jeringas"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Syringes"
msgid ""
"We are starting to isolate a few natural antibiotic serums, but we don't have "
"the supplies to administer the cocktails.  I need you to bring me 10 empty "
"syringes to use.  I'll take care of cleaning them to prevent transferring "
"infections."
msgstr ""
"Estamos empezando a aislar algunos sueros antibióticos naturales pero no "
"tenemos los suministros para administrar los cócteles. Necesito que me "
"traigas 10 jeringas vacías para usar. Me encargaré de limpiarlas para "
"prevenir la transferencia de infecciones."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 Syringes"
msgid "Do you have the empty syringes?"
msgstr "¿Ya conseguiste las jeringas vacías?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Mission source, shopkeep
msgid "Scavenger Boss"
msgstr "Jefe Rebuscador"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome to the junk shop."
msgstr "Bienvenido al negocio de objetos usados."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's see what you've managed to find."
msgstr "Vamos a ver qué conseguiste."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any lucky find?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nope, current run hasn't returned yet.  Come back in <interval>.  You might "
"find something you like."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, thanks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Are you interested in the scavenging runs or one of the other tasks that I "
"might have for you?"
msgstr ""
"¿Estás interesado en las salidas a buscar basura o alguna de las otras tareas "
"que puedo tener para ti?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me more about the scavenging runs."
msgstr "Cuéntame más sobre las campañas de recolección."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of tasks do you have for me?"
msgstr "¿Qué tipo de tareas tienen para mí?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, thanks."
msgstr "No, gracias."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We don't have any of the parts needed right now, but we could send out a "
"scavenging party to a hospital if you have anyone willing to go."
msgstr ""
"No tenemos ninguna de las piezas necesarias en este momento, pero podríamos "
"enviar un grupo de búsqueda a un hospital si tienes a alguien dispuesto a ir."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Make 12 Simple Knife Spears"
msgstr "Hacer 12 lanzas simples de cuchillo"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Simple Knife Spears"
msgid ""
"I can usually use additional survival gear to kit out the new recruits.  The "
"most basic weapon that everyone gets is the simple knife spear… it provides a "
"good mix of range, power, and ease of use when engaging the more common "
"monsters.  Could you make me a dozen of them?  I may need more later, but "
"that should help the first few teams."
msgstr ""
"Normalmente puedo usar equipo de supervivencia adicional para equipar a los "
"nuevos reclutas. El arma más básica que todos tienen es la lanza simple con "
"cuchillo... proporciona una buena mezcla de alcance, potencia y facilidad de "
"uso cuando se enfrentan a los monstruos más comunes. ¿Podrías hacerme una "
"docena de ellas? Puede que necesite más después, pero eso debería ayudar a "
"los primeros equipos."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Simple Knife Spears"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 5 Headlamps"
msgid "You should be able to make them with the most basic of skills."
msgstr "Deberías poder hacerlas solo con tus habilidades más básicas."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Simple Knife Spears"
msgid "Do you have the simple knife spears?"
msgstr "¿Ya tienes las lanzas cuchillo simples?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Make 5 Headlamps"
msgstr "Hacer 5 Linternas Frontales"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 5 Headlamps"
msgid ""
"Night is the ideal time for my team to go on raids, but they are going to "
"need better light sources to speed up their missions.  Could you craft a set "
"of five headlamps for them?  Keeping both hands free greatly helps during "
"combat."
msgstr ""
"La noche es el momento ideal para que mi equipo salga de incursión pero van a "
"necesitar mejores fuentes de luz para acelerar las misiones. ¿Podrías "
"fabricar un equipo de cinco faros delanteros para ellos? Tener las dos manos "
"libres ayuda mucho durante el combate."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 5 Headlamps"
msgid "Do you have the headlamps?"
msgstr "¿Ya conseguiste las linternas frontales?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Make 3 Leather Body Armor"
msgstr "Hacer 3 Armaduras de Cuero"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 3 Leather Body Armor"
msgid ""
"Clothing that can withstand the wear and tear of climbing through windows and "
"fighting back wild animals is in high demand.  The best that we have been "
"able to find is leather body armor, but it is difficult to make with our "
"limited resources.  Could you craft us three pairs of leather body armor?  "
"The life expectancy of my scavengers would drastically increase if you did."
msgstr ""
"La ropa que puede soportar el desgaste de subir a través de las ventanas y "
"luchar contra los animales salvajes esta muy solicitada. Lo mejor que hemos "
"podido conseguir es una armadura corporal de cuero, pero es difícil de hacer "
"con nuestros recursos limitados. ¿Podrías fabricar  tres pares de chalecos de "
"cuero? La esperanza de vida de mis rebuscadores aumentaría drásticamente si "
"lo hicieras."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 3 Leather Body Armor"
msgid "Finding the leather might be easier in town rather than making it yourself."
msgstr "Encontrar el cuero puede ser más fácil en la ciudad que hacerlo uno mismo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 3 Leather Body Armor"
msgid "Do you have the leather body armors?"
msgstr "¿Ya tienes las armaduras de cuero?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Make 12 Molotov Cocktails"
msgstr "Hacer 12 Cócteles Molotov"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Molotov Cocktails"
msgid ""
"When outnumbered or forced to pull back, my scavengers have been taught to "
"throw Molotov cocktails to keep monsters from chasing them.  We go through "
"one or two on every mission, so we can always use a few more.  Would you be "
"willing to make us a dozen?  I'm willing to pay you what I can for your "
"assistance."
msgstr ""
"Cuando les superan en número o les obligan a retirarse, mis rebuscadores han "
"sido enseñados a lanzar cócteles molotov para evitar que los monstruos los "
"persigan. Gastamos uno o dos por cada misión, así que siempre podemos usar "
"más. ¿Estarías dispuesto a hacernos una docena? Estoy dispuesto a pagarte lo "
"que pueda por tu ayuda. "

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Molotov Cocktails"
msgid ""
"Alcohol or kerosene is probably easier to refine rather than find in large "
"quantities."
msgstr ""
"El alcohol o queroseno es probablemente más fácil de refinar que de encontrar "
"en grandes cantidades."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make 12 Molotov Cocktails"
msgid "Do you have the Molotov cocktails?"
msgstr "¿Tienes Cocteles Molotov?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_special/specials.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
#. ~ Name of NPC faction camp
msgid "Scrapper"
msgstr "Peleón"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't mind me."
msgstr "No me prestes atención."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I chop up useless vehicles for spare parts and raw materials.  If we can't "
"use a vehicle immediately, we haul it into the ring we are building to "
"surround the outpost.  It provides a measure of defense in the event that we "
"get attacked."
msgstr ""
"Descuartizo vehículos inútiles para obtener piezas de repuesto y materias "
"primas. Si no podemos usar un vehículo inmediatamente lo arrastramos al "
"anillo que estamos construyendo para rodear el puesto de avanzada. "
"Proporciona una medida de defensa en caso de que seamos atacados."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't personally, the teams we send out to recover the vehicles usually "
"need a hand, but can be hard to catch since they spend most of their time "
"outside the outpost."
msgstr ""
"Yo personalmente no, pero los equipos que mandamos a recuperar vehículos "
"generalmente necesitan una mano pero son difíciles de encontrar porque pasan "
"la mayor parte del tiempo afuera del puesto."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "An angle grinder and a hacksaw?  I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "¿Una amoladora angular y una sierra para metales? Veré lo que puedo hacer."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Tools for Scrap"
msgstr "Herramientas por Chatarra"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Tools for Scrap"
msgid ""
"The scrapper is willing to part with some scrap to help build an anesthetic "
"machine in exchange for an angle grinder and a hacksaw."
msgstr ""
"El chatarrero está dispuesto a desprenderse de chatarra para ayudar a "
"construir una máquina de anestesia a cambio de una amoladora angular y una "
"sierra para metales."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Tools for Scrap"
msgid "Have you found the tools yet?"
msgstr "¿Ya conseguiste las herramientas?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Tools for Scrap"
msgid ""
"These will be very useful, thanks!  I found the parts that you needed and can "
"work with the doctor to build the equipment whenever they are ready."
msgstr ""
"Esto será muy útil, ¡gracias! He encontrado las piezas que necesitaba y puedo "
"trabajar con el médico para construir el equipamiento cuando esté listo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
msgid "Laborer"
msgstr "Obrero"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please leave me alone…"
msgstr "Por favor, déjame solo…"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's sad."
msgstr "Qué triste."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Uhm."
msgstr "Uhm."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What could I possibly have that could help?"
msgstr "¿Qué podría hacer para ayudar?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You need something?"
msgstr "¿Necesitas algo?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The rate is a bit steep, but I still have my quotas that I need to fulfill.  "
"The logs will be dropped off in the garage at the entrance to the camp.  I'll "
"need a bit of time before I can deliver another load."
msgstr ""
"El precio es un poco alto pero todavía tengo que cumplir con mi cuota. Los "
"leños serán dejados en en el garage a la entrada del campamento. Necesito un "
"poco de tiempo antes de que pueda entregar otra carga."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[800 merch, 1d] 10 logs"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "<npc_name> drops the logs off in the garage…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4800 merch, 7d] 100 logs"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_later> <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
msgid "Woodworker"
msgstr "Carpintero"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't have much time to talk."
msgstr "No tengo mucho tiempo para hablar."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I turn the logs that laborers bring in into lumber to expand the outpost.  "
"Maintaining the saw is a chore, but breaks the monotony."
msgstr ""
"Convierto en madera los leños que traen los trabajadores para expandir el "
"puesto. El mantenimiento de la sierra es un embole pero rompe la monotonía."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Bringing in logs is one of the few tasks we can give to the unskilled, so I'd "
"be hurting them if I outsourced it.  Ask around though, I'm sure most people "
"could use a hand."
msgstr ""
"Traer leños es una de las pocas tareas que podemos darles a los que no tienen "
"habilidades, así que estaría perjudicándolos si subcontrato la tarea. Igual, "
"preguntá por ahí, seguro que la mayoría de la gente necesita una mano."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/overmap_terrain.json
#. ~ Signage placed on map
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "Clinic"
msgstr "Clinica"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
#. ~ Signage placed on map
msgid "Extra Supplies.  Take what you need."
msgstr "Suministros adicionales. Coge lo que necesites."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
#. ~ Signage placed on map
msgid "Scavenger Storage.  Stay out!"
msgstr "Almacenamiento Rebuscadores. ¡No entrar!"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/mission_mapgen_tacoma_commune.json
#. ~ Signage placed on map
msgid ""
"Your name is crudely scribbled on the sign with 'Not for commune use' below "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Tu nombre está burdamente garabateado en el cartel con \"Para no uso de la "
"comuna\" debajo."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Dana is a young woman who survived with her husband, but she was pregnant
#. and lost the baby.  This class def is for after she moves to Tacoma.
msgid "baker"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Dana, how are things here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got any bread for sale?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello, Dana!  What's with the trailer?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, Pablo!  Dana said you had some plans to build a bakery?"
msgstr "¡Eh, Pablo! ¿Dana dijo que tienes planeado construir una panadería?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to see you Dana, I'm just checking in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not bad.  Much better than before.  Pablo and I have privacy, and the folks "
"here actually appreciate my bread instead of paying me a pittance for it and "
"then taking it to the basement without so much as a 'thanks'."
msgstr ""
"No está mal. Mucho mejor que antes. Pablo y yo tenemos intimidad, y la gente "
"de aquí realmente aprecia mi pan en lugar de pagarme una miseria por él y "
"luego llevárselo al sótano sin ni siquiera decir \"gracias\"."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with the trailer?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any luck with the pregnancy?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ha, this thing!\"  She dusts the flour off her hands and tucks a loose lock "
"of hair back behind her ear.  \"You remember, we signed on as caravan hands "
"to get us out here.  Well, we had a bunch of stops along the way first.  We "
"were headed to a little group of survivors that snagged themselves a huge "
"stock of dry food somehow, and passed this trailer sales yard smack dab in "
"the middle of nowhere, nobody to be seen for miles.  Pablo managed to sweet "
"talk the group into taking a rest stop there.  We searched the yard, and a "
"lot of the stuff wasn't suitable, but this baby was ready to go.  Long story "
"short, we got the keys to that vintage truck outside, hitched this thing up, "
"and upgraded our caravan.\""
msgstr ""
"Ja, esta cosa!\". Se quita la harina de las manos y se coloca un mechón de "
"pelo suelto detrás de la oreja. \"Recuerdas que nos alistamos como ayudantes "
"de caravana para llegar hasta aquí. Bueno, primero hicimos un montón de "
"paradas por el camino. Nos dirigíamos a un pequeño grupo de supervivientes "
"que se había hecho con una gran cantidad de comida curada, y pasamos por "
"delante de una caravana en medio de la nada, sin que se viera a nadie en "
"kilómetros a la redonda. Pablo se las arregló para convencer al grupo de "
"hacer una parada para descansar allí. Buscamos en el patio, y muchas de las "
"cosas no eran aptas, pero este pequeño estaba listo para irse. Resumiendo, "
"conseguimos las llaves del camión antiguo, lo enganchamos y ampliamos nuestra "
"caravana\"."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you get the keys to the truck?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What made this trailer so good?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*turns serious.  \"We went inside the dealership to see if they were there.  "
"Owner was still in there.  I… I think he took his own life, maybe figured "
"destroying the brain would keep him from reviving.  It… it didn't.  The "
"shotgun took out enough though, he couldn't, uh, he couldn't really see.  "
"Just this miserable, half-faced… we put him down.  I think we did him a "
"favor, if there was any of him left in there.  Didn't feel wrong going "
"through his pockets.  Gross, but not wrong.\"  She blows out a stream of air, "
"sending a small cloud of flour rising in the air, then shrugs."
msgstr ""
"*se pone seria. \"Entramos en el concesionario para ver si estaban allí. El "
"dueño seguía dentro. Yo... creo que se quitó la vida, tal vez pensó que "
"destruir el cerebro le impediría revivir. No... no lo hizo. La escopeta le "
"quitó lo suficiente, no podía, uh, no podía ver realmente. Sólo este "
"miserable, con media cara... tuvimos que finalizarlo. Creo que le hicimos un "
"favor, si es que quedaba algo de él ahí dentro. No me sentí mal revisando sus "
"bolsillos. Asquerosa, pero sin culpa\". Suelta una bocanada de aire que "
"levanta una pequeña nube de harina y se encoge de hombros."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's all propane!\"  She grins.  \"The oven, especially.  We don't need "
"electric, which means we don't need to run the gennie and attract attention.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Seems like a tiny kitchen for a bakery."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Won't you run out of propane?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*sighs and nods.  \"Making do with what I've got, but yeah.  I can only crank "
"out a couple loaves a day, and can't do anything fun.  Pablo has been talking "
"about setting me up a separate kitchen to really get going, but we've got so "
"much critical work to do, and fresh bread is a luxury, even if it's great for "
"morale.\""
msgstr ""
"*suspira y asiente. \"Me las arreglo con lo que tengo, pero sí. Sólo puedo "
"hacer un par de panes al día, y no puedo hacer nada divertido. Pablo ha "
"estado hablando de montarme una cocina aparte para arrancar de verdad, pero "
"tenemos mucho trabajo esencial que hacer, y el pan fresco es un lujo, aunque "
"sea estupendo para la moral.\""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You bet we will.  We've been collecting tanks and have enough for a while, "
"but I'm burning through it faster than the scavengers can bring in more.  "
"Pablo is working out some plans with the others to get me a real wood fired "
"kitchen soon, and that'll also boost my capacity.  Maybe he could give you "
"some scavenging work if you ask."
msgstr ""
"Claro que sí. Hemos estado recolectando depósitos y tenemos suficiente para "
"un tiempo, pero los estoy consumiendo más rápido de lo que los carroñeros "
"pueden traer más. Pablo está trabajando en algunos planes con los demás para "
"conseguirme pronto una cocina de leña de verdad, y eso también aumentará mi "
"capacidad. Quizá pueda darte algún trabajo de carroñero si se lo pides."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shrugs.  \"We got our hands on a few boxes of test strips so that's good.  "
"Being stressed isn't good for conception and I've been pretty fuckin' "
"stressed for a while.  I like our chances a lot better now, that's for sure.  "
"And, well, we've got our own private space at least.\"  She smirks and then "
"blushes slightly, hiding it by fiddling with her baking project."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "bookkeeper"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Pablo is a young professional who survived with his wife, but she was
#. pregnant and lost the baby.
msgid "Bookkeeper"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks up at you from a ledger, takes a moment to place you, then smiles "
"broadly.  \"Great to see you, my friend.  To what do I owe the pleasure?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Pablo!  How are things going here?"
msgstr "¡Hola, Pablo! ¿Cómo van las cosas por aquí?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello, Pablo!  What's with the trailer?"
msgstr "¡Hola, Pablo! ¿Qué pasa con el trailer?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, Pablo!  I heard you might be willing to trade for propane?"
msgstr "¡Eh, Pablo! ¿He oído que podrías estar dispuesto a comerciar con propano?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just popping in to say hi.  Talk to you later!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Can't complain,\" he stretches his neck and pops his shoulder.  \"No, really, "
"I can't.  The work is hard, but people here really want to *do* something, "
"not just hide inside and hope someone saves us.  I've been helping doing "
"general labor a bit, but also working out an inventory system for our "
"supplies.  It's already helped us get a few important bits in earlier than "
"we'd have noticed otherwise.  Post-apocalyptic accounting, ha!  Who'd have "
"thought?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Keeping inventory is similar to accounting?  Really?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you want the honest truth, only a bit.  It's not much like filing income "
"tax.  Still, I know my way around a spreadsheet and I don't mind staring at "
"numbers all day.  I think people were dubious at first, but now that it's "
"starting to show real value they're coming around.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, Dana tells that story better than me.  Basically we found it at an old "
"trailer park and she liked the bakery, so we figured out a way to get it back "
"here.  We definitely earned some cred for coming with our own shelter."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, she would say that.\"  He makes intense eye contact.  \"Not just a "
"bakery, my friend.  A real, post apocalyptic, honest-to-god culinary "
"experience!  We're planning to grow food and crops here.  Central's plan is "
"to import our crops directly, and pay us for our work.  I don't think they've "
"even thought much about transport, outside just shipping them back home.  If "
"we do local site processing we can prevent storage losses, and make higher "
"value material to sell out!  And Central still benefits from having a "
"dedicated bread basket!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know anything about building a 'culinary experience'?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm being a bit tongue-in-cheek there.  Really I want some big wood fired "
"ovens, tools for milling grain, tinning and canning equipment, stuff like "
"that.  We'll make flour, jam, pickles, bread, maybe some sauerkraut and "
"things.  All the old school ways of preserving food, from before fridges were "
"commonplace."
msgstr ""
"Estoy hablando en broma. En realidad, quiero grandes hornos de leña, "
"herramientas para moler el grano, equipo para enlatar y hacer conservas, "
"cosas así. Haremos harina, mermelada, encurtidos, pan, quizá chucrut y cosas "
"así. Todas las formas de conservación de la vieja escuela, de antes de que "
"las neveras fueran comunes."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, but do you know anything about that?"
msgstr "Vale, ¿pero sabes algo de eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well…\" he tugs jokingly at his collar as though letting off steam.  \"I know "
"a bit.  I used to make pickles and jams as a hobby.  With my mom.  When I was "
"a teenager.  But I know the principles!  And Dana knows more than you'd think "
"about grain and flour because she's a huge nerd for her craft.  We do have "
"some knowledge gaps between design and implementation though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of gaps?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not where you might think.\"  He sets aside his ledger and pulls out a page "
"of bullet-point notes written in neat block letters.  \"Everyone is on board "
"with the idea and the amount of actual building to get it online is small "
"enough that the carpenters are willing to help out, so I don't need any "
"assistance with design.  For the really short term I basically just need "
"materials.  I've been collecting spare wood, but to get a good wood-fired "
"oven I need to secure a source of firebrick.  In the longer run, Dana knows "
"the principles of milling, but I need a resource book if I want to set up a "
"functioning mill, first a muscle-powered one and then a windmill for long "
"term.  I wish I'd thought of asking Jenny.  She's a mechanical engineer, but "
"she would probably know how to get me started at least.  I'm also still "
"looking into how to make a good vermin-proof cellar.  Longer term, I will "
"need to work my way around our reliance on sugar, salt, and vinegar from "
"before the Cataclysm, but our stocks of those will hold out for months while "
"I sort things out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No problem.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "No hay problema.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, I'd better go look into that."
msgstr "Bueno, será mejor que vaya a ver qué pasa."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I… I honestly don't know why I didn't think of that.  I could even have asked "
"the supply caravans to do it.  If it comes down to it though, I trust you "
"more than them.  Would you mind?"
msgstr ""
"Yo... Sinceramente, no sé por qué no se me ocurrió. Incluso podría haber "
"pedido a las caravanas de suministros que lo hicieran. Pero, si llega el "
"caso, confío más en ti que en ellos. ¿Te importaría?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Seguro.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "Claro, veré qué puedo hacer."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh… oh, ok!  It's a good thing you showed me this, my basic guesses missed "
"some important points.  Thanks, this will be helpful for a lot more than just "
"the bakery."
msgstr ""
"Oh... oh, ¡vale! Menos mal que me lo has enseñado, mis suposiciones básicas "
"pasaban por alto algunos puntos importantes. Gracias, esto me será útil para "
"mucho más que para la panadería."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any time!  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "¡Cuando quieras!  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I heard you might be willing to trade for propane?"
msgstr "¿He oído que podría estar dispuesto a comerciar con propano?"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Dana said you had some plans to build a bakery?"
msgstr "Dana dijo que tenías planes de construir una panadería"

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't mind keeping my eye out for some firebricks for you."
msgstr "No me importaría echarle un ojo a algunos ladrillos refractarios."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can pass a note to Jenny about helping with the mill designs, if you want."
msgstr ""
"Puedo pasarle una nota a Jenny sobre ayudar con los diseños del molino, si "
"quieres."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Survival 4, Fabrication 4] I know how to build a good root cellar.  Here, "
"let me show you."
msgstr ""
"[Supervivencia 4, Fabricación 4] Sé cómo construir una buena bodega de "
"raíces. Déjame enseñarte."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Get Pablo some fire bricks."
msgstr "Tráele a Pablo unos ladrillos refractarios."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get Pablo some fire bricks."
msgid "Find some fire bricks to help Pablo build an oven."
msgstr "Consigue ladrillos refractarios para ayudar a Pablo a construir un horno."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Pass a message to Jenny Forcette."
msgstr "Pásale un mensaje a Jenny Forcette."

#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pass a message to Jenny Forcette."
msgid "Ask Jenny Forcette if she can help Pablo Nunez with his mill designs."
msgstr ""
"Pregunta a Jenny Forcette si puede ayudar a Pablo Núñez con los diseños de su "
"molino."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Any time, what's on your mind?"
msgstr "Cuando quieras, ¿qué te preocupa?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like your opinion on a job we're doing."
msgstr "Me gustaría conocer tu opinión sobre un trabajo que estamos realizando."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Raise your hand for a high-five.]"
msgstr "[Levanta la mano para chocar los cinco]."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I ask you a bit about yourself?"
msgstr "¿Puedo preguntarte un poco sobre ti?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You picked up a lot of useful skills over the years, hey."
msgstr "Has adquirido muchas habilidades útiles a lo largo de los años, ¿eh?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I just wanted to chat, you know.  To relax."
msgstr "Solo quería charlar, ya sabes. Para relajarme."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The way you said something earlier made me realize… you have a crush on Jenny "
"Forcette, don't you."
msgstr ""
"Por cómo dijiste algo antes, me di cuenta de que... estás enamorado de Jenny "
"Forcette, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*high fives you back enthusiastically."
msgstr "*Te devuelve el saludo con entusiasmo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*returns the high five with a flourish"
msgstr "*devuelve el choque de manos con una floritura"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*leaps into the air and gives you a spinning high five."
msgstr "*salta en el aire y te da un choque de manos giratorio."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*smacks your hand with a resounding clap."
msgstr "*te da una palmada sonora en la mano."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*pretends to fake you out for a moment, then grins and returns the high five"
msgstr ""
"*finge engañarte por un momento, luego sonríe y te devuelve el choque de "
"manos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Nod and continue talking.]"
msgstr "[Asiente con la cabeza y sigue hablando]."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Nod and head on out.]"
msgstr "[Asiente con la cabeza y salga]."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure.  Can I tell you about this idea I had for a comic I'm never gonna make?"
msgstr ""
"Claro. ¿Puedo contarte una idea que se me ocurrió para un cómic que nunca voy "
"a hacer?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Lately I've been thinking about my Steam library and all those games I was "
"putting off for a bad time.  Now it's a bad time and I can't play 'em.  "
"Tragedy of our era, right?"
msgstr ""
"Últimamente he estado pensando en mi biblioteca de Steam y en todos esos "
"juegos que estaba dejando para un mal momento. Ahora es un mal momento y no "
"puedo jugarlos. La tragedia de nuestra era, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You remember that girl from high school I had that huge crush on?  Emily?  I "
"wonder if she's still alive.  I shoulda asked her out."
msgstr ""
"¿Te acuerdas de aquella chica del instituto por la que estaba tan enamorado? "
"¿Emily? Me pregunto si seguirá viva. Debería haberle pedido salir."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aw dude.  I was just remembering about this crowdfunded board game I backed "
"right before things went to hell.  It'd be fulfilling right about now, I bet."
msgstr ""
"Ay, tío. Justo ahora me acordaba de ese juego de mesa financiado mediante "
"crowdfunding al que apoyé justo antes de que todo se fuera al garete. Seguro "
"que ahora mismo estaría muy bien."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Does it ever seem to you like the stars are in different places from where "
"they used to be?  I can find all the old constellations, but they look "
"different now."
msgstr ""
"¿Alguna vez te parece que las estrellas están en lugares diferentes a donde "
"solían estar? Puedo encontrar todas las constelaciones antiguas, pero ahora "
"se ven diferentes."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Since everything went down, I keep having this recurring dream where I'm at "
"Foodplace again, and Luke Skywalker is there, demanding an EB2 combo with "
"extra Beverage, and he's being a real Karen about it.  Do you think it means "
"something?"
msgstr ""
"Desde que todo se vino abajo, sigo teniendo un sueño recurrente en el que "
"estoy de nuevo en Foodplace y Luke Skywalker está allí, exigiendo un combo "
"EB2 con bebida extra, y se está comportando como una auténtica Karen. ¿Crees "
"que significa algo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Maybe it's weird but this whole thing sorta feels like an extended camping "
"trip.  With zombies."
msgstr ""
"Quizás sea raro, pero todo esto me parece como un viaje de campamento "
"prolongado. Con zombis."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I slept weird last night.  Got this awful crick in my neck."
msgstr "Anoche dormí raro. Tengo un dolor horrible en el cuello."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Do you think the internet is still out there somewhere, floating around in "
"some still-functional servers somehow?  It's weird to think about what "
"happened to all that data."
msgstr ""
"¿Crees que Internet sigue ahí fuera, flotando en algún lugar en servidores "
"que aún funcionan de alguna manera? Es extraño pensar en lo que habrá sido de "
"todos esos datos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Remember that guy Daren in elementary who used to tell all those weird-ass "
"creepy stories?  Chris hated him but I thought he was interesting.  I wonder "
"if he's alive, he'd have loved this."
msgstr ""
"¿Te acuerdas de ese chico, Daren, que en primaria contaba todas esas "
"historias raras y espeluznantes? Chris lo odiaba, pero a mí me parecía "
"interesante. Me pregunto si estará vivo, le habría encantado esto."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You know what I could really use right now?  A hot bath."
msgstr "¿Sabes lo que me vendría muy bien ahora mismo? Un baño caliente."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Next time we hit a library, I'm gonna see if they've got a copy of Gideon the "
"Ninth.  I read that book a while ago, but I was super high and I don't "
"remember much of it."
msgstr ""
"La próxima vez que vayamos a la biblioteca, voy a ver si tienen una copia de "
"Gideon the Ninth. Leí ese libro hace un tiempo, pero estaba muy drogado y no "
"recuerdo mucho."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Do you remember what day of the week it is?"
msgstr "¿Recuerdas qué día de la semana es hoy?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Next time I get a chance, I'm gonna make a nice big bowl of mac and cheese."
msgstr ""
"La próxima vez que tenga oportunidad, voy a preparar un buen plato grande de "
"macarrones con queso."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Y'know, these shoes are surprisingly comfy.  You wouldn't think it to look at "
"'em."
msgstr "Sabes, estos zapatos son sorprendentemente cómodos. No lo dirías al verlos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Do you think zombies know what's going on?  Like, are the original people "
"still in there watching all this happen?  I sure hope not."
msgstr ""
"¿Crees que los zombis saben lo que está pasando? ¿Siguen ahí dentro las "
"personas originales viendo cómo ocurre todo esto? Espero que no."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's funny how fast all this weird shit starts to feel normal, don't you "
"think?"
msgstr ""
"Es curioso lo rápido que todas estas cosas raras empiezan a parecer normales, "
"¿no crees?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're always gonna be friends, right?  Even with the apocalypse… changing us?"
msgstr "Siempre seremos amigos, ¿verdad? ¿Incluso con el apocalipsis... cambiándonos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you miss most about the internet?"
msgstr "¿Qué es lo que más echas de menos de Internet?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Now that we've got no responsibilities, is there anything you'd like to see "
"or do?"
msgstr "Ahora que no tenemos responsabilidades, ¿hay algo que te gustaría ver o hacer?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think the rest of the world is like these days?"
msgstr "¿Cómo crees que es el resto del mundo hoy en día?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you miss any food from the old days?"
msgstr "¿Echas de menos alguna comida de los viejos tiempos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "<talk_snippet_modded_liam_Friends4ever>"
msgstr "<talk_snippet_modded_liam_Friends4ever>"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aww, of course.  No matter what happens, you're always you and I'm always me, "
"right?  We've been through worse than this.\"  He pauses, his brow furrowed.  "
"\"Well, okay, maybe we haven't.  But we've stuck through it all for so many "
"years, what's a little apocalypse gonna change?  Or a little mutation, or "
"grievous bodily harm, or zombies, or interdimensional monster attacks and "
"serious life-altering PTSD, or whatever.  Who cares.  You're my family, more "
"than my birth family ever was."
msgstr ""
"Claro, por supuesto. Pase lo que pase, tú siempre serás tú y yo siempre seré "
"yo, ¿verdad? Hemos pasado por cosas peores que esto. Hace una pausa y frunce "
"el ceño. «Bueno, vale, quizá no. Pero hemos aguantado todo esto durante "
"tantos años, ¿qué va a cambiar un pequeño apocalipsis? O una pequeña "
"mutación, o lesiones corporales graves, o zombis, o ataques de monstruos "
"interdimensionales y un trastorno de estrés postraumático grave que te cambia "
"la vida, o lo que sea. A quién le importa. Tú eres mi familia, más de lo que "
"mi familia biológica jamás lo fue."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Continue chatting.]"
msgstr "[Sigue hablando.]"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"OK, I know you're leading me up to say something dirty, and yeah I miss that, "
"but you know what?  Really the thing I miss most is social media.  No "
"seriously!  Stop looking at me like that!  I liked being able to just talk to "
"people no matter where they were, any time.  I had friends in Sweden, and "
"Brazil, and the West Coast.  I'm never gonna know what happened to them, and "
"that busts me up bad.  They mattered to me, you know?\"  His voice catches a "
"bit, and he coughs.  \"You're here though, and that helps a lot.  Can't "
"imagine trying to do this lone-wolf.  How about you, what were you thinking "
"of when you asked?"
msgstr ""
"Vale, sé que me estás llevando a decir algo obsceno, y sí, lo echo de menos, "
"pero ¿sabes qué? Lo que más echo de menos son las redes sociales. ¡En serio! "
"¡Deja de mirarme así! Me gustaba poder hablar con la gente sin importar dónde "
"estuvieran, en cualquier momento. Tenía amigos en Suecia, Brasil y la costa "
"oeste. Nunca sabré qué les pasó, y eso me destroza. Significaban mucho para "
"mí, ¿sabes? —Se le quiebra un poco la voz y tose—. Pero tú estás aquí, y eso "
"ayuda mucho. No me imagino intentando hacer esto en solitario. ¿Y tú, en qué "
"pensabas cuando me lo preguntaste?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I mean, there's the obvious stuff like, uh, video streaming,\" he winks "
"at you, \"but I think lately I'm missing Wikipedia.  I have all these random "
"questions about things, and I can't answer them.  I feel like I'm living in a "
"box.  How did we survive for thousands of years like this?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, hay cosas obvias como, eh, el streaming de vídeo —te guiña un ojo—, "
"pero creo que últimamente echo de menos Wikipedia. Tengo un montón de "
"preguntas aleatorias sobre cosas y no sé responderlas. Siento como si viviera "
"en una caja. ¿Cómo hemos sobrevivido así durante miles de años?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Online restaurant reviews.\"  He stares at you without a shred of irony.  "
"\"I'm serious, I used to love browsing looking for the funniest or weirdest "
"reviews.  I guess I could broaden it, I miss pointless doom scrolling.  It's "
"harder to find things to keep my mind off things now, and I've got more I "
"wish I could keep my mind off.  What about you?"
msgstr ""
"Reseñas de restaurantes en línea. Te mira fijamente sin una pizca de ironía. "
"«En serio, me encantaba buscar las reseñas más divertidas o extrañas. Supongo "
"que podría ampliarlo, echo de menos el scroll sin sentido. Ahora me cuesta "
"más encontrar cosas que me distraigan, y tengo más cosas de las que me "
"gustaría distraerme. ¿Y tú?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs.  \"You know me, I was never high on the ambition front.  Honestly, "
"if you weren't around I'd probably clean up my dad's old cabin, try to learn "
"how to set up a power supply, and scavenge for parts until I'd built the best "
"damn gaming rig the world will ever see.  Then I'd load up whatever games I "
"could find.\"  He pauses.  \"Or maybe it'd be easier to set up a console, I "
"dunno.  Most consoles aren't gonna like the no-internet thing right?  There's "
"probably a way to crack 'em but without the internet where would we even "
"check?\"  He rubs his chin.  \"Still.  I'd have maybe found a way.  How about "
"you, what's the big overarching plan for all this?\""
msgstr ""
"*Risas. «Ya me conoces, nunca he sido muy ambicioso. Sinceramente, si no "
"estuvieras aquí, probablemente limpiaría la vieja cabaña de mi padre, "
"intentaría aprender a instalar una fuente de alimentación y buscaría piezas "
"hasta construir el mejor equipo para videojuegos que el mundo haya visto "
"jamás. Luego cargaría todos los juegos que pudiera encontrar». Hace una "
"pausa. «O quizá sería más fácil instalar una consola, no lo sé. A la mayoría "
"de las consolas no les va a gustar eso de no tener Internet, ¿verdad? "
"Probablemente haya alguna forma de piratearlas, pero sin Internet, ¿dónde "
"podríamos buscarlo?». Se frota la barbilla. «Aun así, quizá habría encontrado "
"la manera. ¿Y tú, cuál es tu gran plan para todo esto?»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, well.  I don't really think of life that way, you know?  I guess I'm "
"pretty happy to just hang out with you, doing the shit we're doing, seeing "
"what life brings.  Still, I guess I could see settling down somewhere nice, "
"somewhere quiet, somewhere zombie-free.  I bet it wouldn't take long to get "
"enough food and supplies to live on forever, and then I'd just let myself "
"turn into some kinda wild bush man, with a big crazy long beard.  I'd smell "
"like weed and B.O. and I'd have this giant stack of books to read.  Other "
"survivors would come find me, like a guru on a mountaintop, to ask me "
"questions about Batman.  In time, as the old world was forgotten, I'd "
"convince them that he was a real person.\"  He grins.  \"How 'bout you?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, yo no veo la vida así, ¿sabes? Supongo que soy bastante feliz "
"simplemente pasando el rato contigo, haciendo lo que hacemos, viendo lo que "
"nos depara la vida. Aun así, supongo que podría imaginarme estableciéndome en "
"algún lugar bonito, tranquilo y sin zombis. Apuesto a que no tardaría mucho "
"en conseguir comida y provisiones suficientes para vivir para siempre, y "
"entonces me dejaría convertir en una especie de hombre salvaje, con una barba "
"larga y loca. Olería a hierba y a sudor y tendría una pila gigante de libros "
"para leer. Otros supervivientes vendrían a buscarme, como a un gurú en la "
"cima de una montaña, para hacerme preguntas sobre Batman. Con el tiempo, "
"cuando el viejo mundo cayera en el olvido, los convencería de que era una "
"persona real». Sonríe. «¿Y tú?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh dude, good question.  The news reports made it sound like this is "
"everywhere, you know?  Still, somewhere out there's gotta be better than "
"this, right?  Maybe like, up in the Yukon or Siberia or something it's all "
"kinda normal?  I think most places are like this though, just one big fucked "
"up mess.  Maybe they've got different monsters though, like, carnivorous "
"rocks or some shit.  How 'bout you, what do you think is out there?"
msgstr ""
"Oh, tío, buena pregunta. Las noticias dan a entender que esto ocurre en todas "
"partes, ¿sabes? Aun así, en algún sitio tiene que haber algo mejor que esto, "
"¿no? Quizás en el Yukón o Siberia o algo así, ¿todo es más o menos normal? "
"Aunque creo que la mayoría de los sitios son así, un gran desastre. Quizás "
"tengan monstruos diferentes, como rocas carnívoras o alguna mierda así. ¿Y "
"tú, qué crees que hay ahí fuera?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"See, I like that about you.  Here we are just trying to keep alive and you're "
"thinking all these big thoughts about the rest of the world.  I got no clue "
"how they're doing out there, so I'm just gonna imagine that things are kinda "
"like here, but maybe a bit better.  There's a few places where folks have "
"settled in and they're figuring stuff out.  Those folks are gonna last a long "
"time, maybe they're how we start rebuilding."
msgstr ""
"Mira, eso es lo que me gusta de ti. Aquí estamos, intentando sobrevivir, y tú "
"pensando en todas esas grandes cosas sobre el resto del mundo. No tengo ni "
"idea de cómo les va ahí fuera, así que voy a imaginar que las cosas son más o "
"menos como aquí, pero quizá un poco mejor. Hay algunos lugares donde la gente "
"se ha establecido y está resolviendo las cosas. Esa gente va a durar mucho "
"tiempo, quizá sean ellos quienes nos ayuden a empezar a reconstruir."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I never thought I'd hear myself say this, but I kinda miss the Ediburger3 "
"from Foodplace.  I worked there so long, I hated everything, but as soon as "
"you tell me I'm *never* gonna have a fresh, greasy EB3 again, suddenly it's "
"all my stomach wants.  Don't try to track one down or anything though.  I'm "
"pretty sure I miss the *idea* more than the actual *thing*.  And I don't "
"think we could cook up a copy, it'd be pretty hard to get the right blend of "
"animal product and sawdust for the Meatcylinder.\"  He stares wistfully into "
"space for a moment.  \"How about you, what were you thinking of when you "
"asked?"
msgstr ""
"Nunca pensé que diría esto, pero echo de menos la Ediburger3 de Foodplace. "
"Trabajé allí tanto tiempo que lo odiaba todo, pero en cuanto me dices que "
"nunca volveré a comer una EB3 fresca y grasienta, de repente es lo único que "
"me apetece. Pero no intentes buscarla ni nada por el estilo. Estoy bastante "
"seguro de que echo de menos más la idea que el producto en sí. Y no creo que "
"pudiéramos hacer una réplica, sería muy difícil conseguir la mezcla adecuada "
"de productos animales y serrín para el Meatcylinder. Se queda mirando al "
"vacío con nostalgia durante un momento. ¿Y tú, en qué pensabas cuando me lo "
"preguntaste?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Delivery pizza.  It's not the quality of the pizza I miss, it's the delivery. "
" Having someone just show up at the door with a god damn pizza, ready for you "
"to eat.  We lived in paradise and we knew it not.  How about you?"
msgstr ""
"Pizza a domicilio. No es la calidad de la pizza lo que echo de menos, sino el "
"servicio de entrega. Que alguien se presente en tu puerta con una maldita "
"pizza, lista para comer. Vivíamos en el paraíso y no lo sabíamos. ¿Y tú?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know, my friend, I could really go for an egg salad sandwich right now.  "
"Nice, fresh eggs, some cheap-ass white bread, bit of pickle on there, hint of "
"mustard.  Egg salad gets a bad rap because it sucks if you get it from the "
"store, but you make a good homemade one?  That's something else, I tell you.  "
"What's your poison?"
msgstr ""
"Sabes, amigo mío, ahora mismo me apetecería un sandwich de ensalada de huevo. "
"Huevos frescos, pan blanco barato, un poco de pepinillo, un toque de mostaza. "
"La ensalada de huevo tiene mala fama porque apesta si la compras en la "
"tienda, ¿pero si haces una buena casera? Eso es otra cosa, te lo aseguro. "
"¿Cuál es tu veneno?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know, I'm kinda in the mood for some pub nachos right now.  The whole pub "
"ambience would be good too, but I like how they'd put 'em on wax paper that'd "
"be so soaked with cheese grease you could see right through it.  Those little "
"black olive wheels that tasted like rubber, they were only ever good with pub "
"nachos, you know?  Any other time, garbage.  I'd love to have a big tray of "
"pub nachos, go to a karaoke night, and just sing fuckin' Abba songs until my "
"throat hurt.  You in?"
msgstr ""
"Sabes, ahora mismo me apetece comer nachos de pub. El ambiente del pub "
"también estaría bien, pero me gusta cómo los sirven en papel encerado tan "
"empapado de grasa de queso que se puede ver a través de él. Esas rodajas de "
"aceitunas negras que sabían a goma solo estaban buenas con los nachos de pub, "
"¿sabes? En cualquier otro momento, eran basura. Me encantaría tener una gran "
"bandeja de nachos de pub, ir a una noche de karaoke y cantar jodidas "
"canciones de Abba hasta que me doliera la garganta. ¿Te apuntas?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, sure.  I dunno what more there is to tell, we've known each other for "
"ages."
msgstr "Bueno, claro. No sé qué más hay que contar, nos conocemos desde hace años."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"We hadn't caught up in a while before <the_cataclysm>.  What've you been "
"doing?"
msgstr ""
"No nos habíamos puesto al día en mucho tiempo. <the_cataclysm>. ¿Qué has "
"estado haciendo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shrugs.  \"Same as I was when we used to hang out more, mostly.  I quit my "
"job at Foodplace a while back, got tired of the stupid outfits.  Worked doing "
"labor in construction for a bit, but I didn't like my boss so I ditched it.  "
"Got a job doing deliveries for Amazon, which was absolutely shitty, but I "
"managed to jump from that to a bit of a better delivery job for a smaller "
"company.  It was actually going pretty good before everything happened.\""
msgstr ""
"*Se encoge de hombros. «Más o menos igual que cuando solíamos salir juntos, "
"sobre todo. Hace un tiempo dejé mi trabajo en Foodplace, me cansé de esos "
"estúpidos uniformes. Trabajé un tiempo en la construcción, pero no me gustaba "
"mi jefe, así que lo dejé. Conseguí un trabajo haciendo entregas para Amazon, "
"que era una mierda, pero logré pasar de ahí a un trabajo de reparto un poco "
"mejor en una empresa más pequeña. De hecho, me iba bastante bien antes de que "
"pasara todo esto»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you make it through the Cataclysm?"
msgstr "¿Cómo lograste sobrevivir al Cataclismo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I wanna say it was a hell of a story, but really, I was on the way back to "
"Boston from a delivery and a thing about the riots came on the radio.  I was "
"close to the cabin so I just thought, 'this is starting to sound really "
"fuckin bad.'  I called in sick and took a few days to hunker down out of "
"civilization.  By the time I had to think about going back to work, we were "
"into that wild time when half the people were trying to keep things running "
"and the other half were trying to burn everything down.  I shut the blinds "
"and stayed in, until Chris showed up acting like a freak."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It doesn't feel that way, but I guess so.  I don't know if I ever told you, "
"but my dad was quite the weirdo prepper.  He built the cabin and when I was a "
"kid we'd head out and do drills for the end of the world.  It's part of why I "
"was kinda wacked out on apocalypse stuff when you and I first met, back when "
"we made the plan for where to meet up and all.  He taught me archery and some "
"survival skills but I never really took to it, partly because my ol' man was "
"a real piece of work.\"  He stares off for a minute.  \"To be honest, though, "
"now that we're in the middle of a real-ass apocalypse, I can see a lot of "
"what he taught me was just crap anyway.\""
msgstr ""
"No lo parece, pero supongo que sí. No sé si te lo he contado alguna vez, pero "
"mi padre era un preparador bastante raro. Construyó la cabaña y cuando yo era "
"niño salíamos y hacíamos simulacros para el fin del mundo. Es parte de la "
"razón por la que estaba un poco loco por el apocalipsis cuando tú y yo nos "
"conocimos, cuando hicimos el plan de dónde encontrarnos y todo eso. Me enseñó "
"tiro con arco y algunas técnicas de supervivencia, pero nunca me aficioné, en "
"parte porque mi viejo era un auténtico desastre\". Se queda mirando un "
"momento. \"Para ser honesto, ahora que estamos en medio de un verdadero "
"apocalipsis, puedo ver que mucho de lo que me enseñó era una mierda de todos "
"modos\"."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to your father?  You never talked about him much."
msgstr "¿Qué le pasó a tu padre? Nunca hablaste mucho de él."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*snorts.  \"I was pretty low-contact with him the last couple years.  He got "
"me that job in construction and when I left it, he tried to hit me, found out "
"I'm not so much of a pushover as when I was fifteen.  Asshole.  I was still "
"texting my mom a bit, apparently when things went to shit, he tried to join "
"the riots.  I hope he got gunned down.\""
msgstr ""
"*Resopla. «En los últimos años apenas había tenido contacto con él. Me "
"consiguió ese trabajo en la construcción y, cuando lo dejé, intentó pegarme, "
"pero descubrió que ya no soy tan fácil de manipular como cuando tenía quince "
"años. Gilipollas. Seguía enviando mensajes a mi madre de vez en cuando y, al "
"parecer, cuando todo se fue al garete, intentó unirse a los disturbios. "
"Espero que le hayan pegado un tiro»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I remember your mom as kind of a quiet lady, she seemed all right.  Should we "
"be trying to find her?"
msgstr ""
"Recuerdo a tu madre como una mujer tranquila, parecía buena persona. "
"¿Deberíamos intentar encontrarla?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Harsh, but I hear you.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Es duro, pero te entiendo.  <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, things with her weren't as bad as with my dad, but I don't know if I'd "
"go trying to hunt for her in a zombified city or anything.  Like, sure she "
"didn't beat me up, but she didn't ever lift a finger to help me either.  She "
"was still with him right up until the end, even when it was obvious that she "
"was choosing him over me.  I don't wanna judge her for the life she led, but "
"- \" he trails off for a moment, then twitches his shoulders and resumes.  "
"\"Well, it's like I said.  I hope she's okay but I'm not gonna go risk my "
"neck trying to find her.  You and Chris were my real family, you got me "
"through those years."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, las cosas con ella no eran tan malas como con mi padre, pero no sé si "
"iría a buscarla a una ciudad llena de zombis o algo así. Es decir, claro que "
"no me pegaba, pero tampoco movió un dedo para ayudarme. Siguió con él hasta "
"el final, incluso cuando era obvio que lo prefería a él antes que a mí. No "
"quiero juzgarla por la vida que llevó, pero... —se detiene un momento, luego "
"encoge los hombros y continúa—. Bueno, es como dije. Espero que esté bien, "
"pero no voy a arriesgar mi vida para encontrarla. Tú y Chris eran mi "
"verdadera familia, ustedes me ayudaron a superar esos años."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*stares at you wide-eyed for a beat, then breaks into a shy grin.  \"Aw man, "
"busted.  You *know* I dig those distracted nerdy chicks who don't react to my "
"presence in any way.  It's all good though, you know?  Don't tell her.  I "
"barely know her and it's not like she's in a place to be dating some "
"stranger.\""
msgstr ""
"*Te mira fijamente con los ojos muy abiertos durante un instante y luego "
"esboza una tímida sonrisa. «Ay, tío, me has pillado. Ya sabes que me gustan "
"esas chicas nerds distraídas que no reaccionan ante mi presencia de ninguna "
"manera. Pero no pasa nada, ¿sabes? No se lo digas. Apenas la conozco y no es "
"que esté en condiciones de salir con un desconocido»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your secret's safe with me.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Tus secretos están a salvo conmigo. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your secret's safe with me.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Tus secretos están a salvo conmigo. <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "My opinion?  Sure, my friend, hit me up, what's eating you?"
msgstr "¿Mi opinión? Claro, amigo, dime, ¿qué te preocupa?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Check this out, I found an address of some kind of central refugee management "
"facility.  Should we check it out?  Maybe they'll have answers?"
msgstr ""
"Mira esto, he encontrado la dirección de una especie de centro de gestión de "
"refugiados. ¿Deberíamos ir a verlo? ¿Quizás allí tengan respuestas?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/xe_liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You thinking what I'm thinking about this mystery dropoff for Smokes?"
msgstr "¿Estás pensando lo mismo que yo sobre esta misteriosa entrega de Humos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any ideas about this job to clear out the back bay for Smokes?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea sobre este trabajo para despejar la bahía trasera para Humos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about taking down this bandit camp?"
msgstr "¿Qué te parece si acabamos con este campamento de bandidos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts about bringing this prospectus out to the ranch?"
msgstr "¿Qué opinas de llevar este prospecto al rancho?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the fastest way to find these guys some solar panels?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cuál es la forma más rápida de conseguirles unos paneles solares a estos "
"chicos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Liam, I need a lot of jars.  A shocking amount of jars."
msgstr "Liam, necesito muchos tarros. Una cantidad impresionante de tarros."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Liam, we need bigger jars."
msgstr "Liam, necesitamos tarros más grandes."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How about finding this guy some cigarettes?"
msgstr "¿Qué tal si le buscamos unos cigarrillos a este tipo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Should we go check out those farmers the teamster mentioned?"
msgstr "¿Deberíamos ir a ver a esos granjeros que mencionó el camionero?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"A secret lab in the wilds, with survivors in it, Liam.  You heard the "
"teamster."
msgstr ""
"Un laboratorio secreto en medio de la naturaleza, con supervivientes en su "
"interior, Liam. Ya has oído al camionero."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "This 'scrap metal castle' sounds far fetched to me."
msgstr "Este «castillo de chatarra» me parece una idea descabellada."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What sounds better to you, a 'bullet bank' or a woman who feeds visitors?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué te parece mejor, un «banco de balas» o una mujer que da de comer a los "
"visitantes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about helping out this Dave guy?"
msgstr "¿Qué te parece ayudar a este tal Dave?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"At least Dave has some practicality, and isn't just asking for more trash, "
"right?"
msgstr ""
"Al menos Dave tiene algo de sentido práctico y no se limita a pedir más "
"basura, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts on Dave's cardboard needs?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea sobre las necesidades de cartón de Dave?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Looks like we might be done with cardboard for Dave, it's plastic now."
msgstr "Parece que ya no vamos a usar cartón para Dave, ahora es plástico."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have a feeling this is the last of the cardboard for Dave."
msgstr "Tengo la sensación de que este es el último cartón para Dave."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, this is a different direction for Dave, don't you think?"
msgstr "Oye, esto es algo diferente para Dave, ¿no crees?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you think it's dangerous to get zombie blood, besides the obvious?"
msgstr ""
"¿Crees que es peligroso contagiarse de la sangre de un zombi, aparte de lo "
"obvio?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sneaking into a lab to run some data analysis can't be bad, right?"
msgstr ""
"Colarse en un laboratorio para analizar algunos datos no puede estar mal, "
"¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Who could have guessed there'd be some further complications to our stolen "
"data analysis?"
msgstr ""
"¿Quién podría haber imaginado que habría más complicaciones en nuestro "
"análisis de datos robados?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about checking out this freezing portal lab?"
msgstr "¿Qué te parece echar un vistazo a este laboratorio de portales congelados?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"If you were tired of underground labs, now we're gonna check out secret "
"underground lab tunnels!"
msgstr ""
"Si estabas cansado de los laboratorios subterráneos, ¡ahora vamos a ver "
"túneles secretos de laboratorios subterráneos!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know how to build a still?"
msgstr "¿Sabes cómo construir un alambique?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"How long does brewer's yeast last in the package?  Can we just find it at a "
"supermarket?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cuánto tiempo dura la levadura de cerveza en el envase? ¿Se puede encontrar "
"en cualquier supermercado?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any idea where we could find sugar beet seeds for the bartender?"
msgstr ""
"¿Sabes dónde podríamos encontrar semillas de remolacha azucarera para el "
"camarero?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you like big jugs, Liam?"
msgstr "¿Te gustan las tetas grandes, Liam?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are we gonna transport two giant drums?"
msgstr "¿Cómo vamos a transportar dos tambores gigantes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Bringing a professional arsonist some commercial fertilizer seems like a "
"normal thing to do."
msgstr "Llevarle fertilizante comercial a un pirómano profesional parece algo normal."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, uh.  Alonso's pants, hey."
msgstr "Bueno, eh... Los pantalones de Alonso, oye."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about helping these guys clean up all that dead zombie mess?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué te parece ayudar a estos chicos a limpiar todo ese desastre de zombis "
"muertos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts on finding Boris a power saw?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea sobre dónde encontrar una sierra eléctrica para Boris?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're looking for Boris' kid's old laptop.  Thoughts?"
msgstr "Estamos buscando el viejo portátil del hijo de Boris. ¿Alguna idea?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You ever used a sourdough starter?"
msgstr "¿Alguna vez has usado masa madre?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Draco seems like a kindred spirit for you."
msgstr "Draco parece ser un alma gemela para ti."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you okay with tracking down a copy of the Quran?"
msgstr "¿Te parece bien buscar una copia del Corán?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any idea where to find a really specific reference book about pneumatic guns?"
msgstr ""
"¿Sabes dónde puedo encontrar un libro de referencia muy específico sobre "
"pistolas neumáticas?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think, where should we look for a motor for Jenny?"
msgstr "¿Qué opinas, dónde deberíamos buscar un motor para Jenny?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It shouldn't be too hard to find Jenny a big metal tank, right?"
msgstr ""
"No debería ser muy difícil encontrar un gran tanque metálico para Jenny, "
"¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You ever seen gunsmithing books just lying around?"
msgstr "¿Alguna vez has visto libros sobre armería tirados por ahí?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, we're finding a book about guns for your sweet nerd-girl."
msgstr "Así que estamos buscando un libro sobre armas para tu dulce chica nerd."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Do you think it's the right thing, trying to help the Nunez family move to "
"Tacoma?"
msgstr ""
"¿Crees que es lo correcto intentar ayudar a la familia Núñez a mudarse a "
"Tacoma?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts on helping Uyen out with her antiseptic?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea para ayudar a Uyen con su antiséptico?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts on helping Uyen out with her bandages?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea para ayudar a Uyen con sus vendajes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts on helping Uyen out with her antidepressants?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea para ayudar a Uyen con sus antidepresivos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You and me: hairdressing supply vendors now."
msgstr "Tú y yo: ahora proveedores de productos para peluquería."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What're your thoughts on this mission to kill bandits for the old guard?"
msgstr "¿Qué opinas de esta misión de matar bandidos para la vieja guardia?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do you think we should track down this enemy informant?"
msgstr "¿Cómo crees que deberíamos localizar a este informante enemigo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about these robots?  Crazy stuff, hey?"
msgstr "¿Qué opinas de estos robots? Una locura, ¿eh?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Do you think it's really a monster hitting those trade caravans?  Any ideas "
"how we should deal with it?"
msgstr ""
"¿Crees que realmente es un monstruo el que ataca a esas caravanas "
"comerciales? ¿Alguna idea de cómo deberíamos lidiar con eso?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, we're officially assassins for hire now.  How do you feel about that?"
msgstr "Así que ahora somos oficialmente asesinos a sueldo. ¿Qué te parece?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, now we're radio technicians.  Sounds fun, don't you think?"
msgstr "Bueno, ahora somos técnicos de radio. Suena divertido, ¿no crees?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What do you make of these weird pictographs?  I think they're directions "
"somewhere."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué opinas de estos extraños pictogramas? Creo que son indicaciones para "
"llegar a algún sitio."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where do you think we can get some anesthetic for that robot guy?"
msgstr "¿Dónde crees que podemos conseguir anestesia para ese robot?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts on this scouting mission, checking out this bunker thing?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea sobre esta misión de exploración, echar un vistazo a este búnker?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"How do you think we should start looking for this lost interdimensional "
"building?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo crees que deberíamos empezar a buscar este edificio interdimensional "
"perdido?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You ready to go burn some shit down?"
msgstr "¿Estás listo para ir a quemar algunas cosas?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's not gonna be a problem that we're hunting down Foodperson, is it?"
msgstr "No va a ser un problema que estemos persiguiendo a Comidapersona, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about clearing out these pizzeria squatters?"
msgstr "¿Qué opinas sobre desalojar a estos ocupantes ilegales de la pizzería?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, cake and a party.  Think it was all worth it?"
msgstr "Entonces, pastel y fiesta. ¿Crees que valió la pena?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think, you in the mood to hunt some slimes?"
msgstr "¿Qué te parece, te apetece cazar unos slimes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Liam!  Liam!  Bughunt!"
msgstr "¡Hola, Liam! ¡Liam! ¡Bughunt!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Looks like I've got you doing deliveries again.  Where should we look for all "
"this lumber?"
msgstr ""
"Parece que te voy a tener haciendo entregas otra vez. ¿Dónde deberíamos "
"buscar toda esta madera?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I dunno if you heard, but guess what we're gonna deliver now?  More lumber!"
msgstr "No sé si lo has oído, pero ¿adivinas qué vamos a entregar ahora? ¡Más madera!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any idea where we can find some ropes?"
msgstr "¿Sabes dónde podemos encontrar unas sogas?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "These guys need a wood saw.  You carrying one?"
msgstr "Estos chicos necesitan una sierra para madera. ¿Llevas una?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where could we find a shovel?"
msgstr "¿Dónde podríamos encontrar una pala?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're looking for a charcoal smoker now.  You seen one?"
msgstr "Ahora estamos buscando un ahumador de carbón. ¿Has visto alguno?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"This guy wants us to find a Remington 870 Express for a client.  You know a "
"bit about that stuff, don't you?"
msgstr ""
"Este tipo quiere que encontremos una Remington 870 Express para un cliente. "
"Sabes un poco sobre esas cosas, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Nothing ever went wrong tracking down a nice old guy in a cabin in the woods, "
"right?"
msgstr ""
"Nunca ha pasado nada malo por ir a buscar a un simpático anciano en una "
"cabaña en el bosque, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You fine with helping this guy and his rabbits?"
msgstr "¿Te parece bien ayudar a este tipo y a sus conejos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Does blackberry hunting sound nice?"
msgstr "¿Te apetece ir a recoger moras?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Mind helping Mr. Lapin get in touch with his friends?"
msgstr "¿Le importaría ayudar al Sr. Lapin a ponerse en contacto con sus amigos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Seen an anvil around recently?"
msgstr "¿Has visto un yunque por ahí últimamente?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything we should consider before trying to find Chris Isherwood?"
msgstr ""
"¿Hay algo que debamos tener en cuenta antes de intentar encontrar a Chris "
"Isherwood?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Looks like Barry Isherwood's got himself into some trouble."
msgstr "Parece que Barry Isherwood se ha metido en problemas."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Want to help me collect some dandelions?"
msgstr "¿Quieres ayudarme a recoger dientes de león?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Liam.  Bee balm?"
msgstr "Eh Liam. ¿Bálsamo de abejas?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tonight, on 'to catch a predator'…"
msgstr "Esta noche, en “Atrapar a un depredador”..."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Eddie wants a *lot* of rocks."
msgstr "Eddie quiere *muchas* piedras."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, Liam, you ready to gather sand?"
msgstr "Entonces, Liam, ¿estás preparado para traer arena?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I told Eddie we'd help him gather some clay."
msgstr "Le dije a Eddie que le ayudaríamos a recoger arcilla."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where should we look for jars for the Isherwoods?"
msgstr "¿Dónde deberíamos buscar botes para los Isherwood?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any thoughts about looking for wheat seeds?"
msgstr "¿Alguna idea sobre la búsqueda de semillas de trigo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Liam, you're not afraid of the big bad wolf, are you?"
msgstr "Liam, no tienes miedo del lobo feroz, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about hunting some mystery monsters for Jesse?"
msgstr "¿Qué opinas de cazar algunos monstruos misteriosos para Jesse?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, you ever seen a book about glassblowing?"
msgstr "Eh, ¿alguna vez has visto un libro sobre soplado de vidrio?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Luke Isherwood wants a copy of the DIY Compendium."
msgstr "Luke Isherwood  quiere una copia de Compendio de Bricolaje."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You think Barry's gonna be okay?"
msgstr "¿Crees que Barry estará bien?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Liam!  There's a chef, trapped in a restaurant!  Want to help save them?"
msgstr "¡Liam! ¡Hay un chef atrapado en un restaurante! ¿Quieres ayudar a rescatarlo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about tracking down these survivors camping out on a farm?"
msgstr "¿Qué opinas de localizar a estos supervivientes que acampan en una granja?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Should we go track down this mystery cabin?"
msgstr "¿Deberíamos ir a buscar esta misteriosa cabaña?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Liam, I've got the location of a prepper bunker.  Should we check this out?"
msgstr ""
"Liam, tengo la ubicación de un búnker de supervivencia. ¿Deberíamos ir a "
"echar un vistazo?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do you feel about checking out a zombie-infested farm?"
msgstr "¿Qué te parece visitar una granja infestada de zombis?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sweet, road trip!  That sounds like as good a plan as any, my friend.  Gives "
"me some first season Walking Dead vibes, you know?  Maybe the place will be "
"run by sinister G-men, or a lone crazy scientist who thinks he can cure "
"zombies if he can just get his hands on one super-rare ingredient.  Road trip!"
msgstr ""
"¡Genial, un viaje por carretera! Me parece un plan estupendo, amigo mío. Me "
"recuerda a la primera temporada de Walking Dead, ¿sabes? Quizás el lugar esté "
"dirigido por siniestros agentes federales o por un científico loco y "
"solitario que cree que puede curar a los zombis si consigue un ingrediente "
"muy raro. ¡Viaje por carretera!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Road trip!  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"¡Viaje por carretera! En realidad, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm thinking this kinda sounds like that intercom and their "
"vague-yet-menacing government agency.\"  He pauses.  \"That might be a deep "
"cut, if you never listened to Night Vale.  Anyway, I bet that's where we're "
"going."
msgstr ""
"Creo que esto se parece un poco a ese intercomunicador y a esa agencia "
"gubernamental tan vaga como amenazante. Hace una pausa. «Puede que sea una "
"referencia muy oscura, si nunca has escuchado Night Vale. En cualquier caso, "
"apuesto a que ahí es donde vamos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm thinking this sounds *awesome*, and also possibly we're gonna die.  At "
"least we'll die investigating a vague-yet-menacing government agency.\"  He "
"pauses.  \"That might be a deep cut, if you never listened to Night Vale."
msgstr ""
"Creo que esto suena *genial*, y también que posiblemente vamos a morir. Al "
"menos moriremos investigando una agencia gubernamental vaga pero amenazante. "
"Hace una pausa. «Eso puede ser un golpe duro, si nunca has escuchado Night "
"Vale."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yep, same page.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Sí, la misma página. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*rubs his chin thoughtfully.  \"Maybe we can set up a bottleneck in the "
"hallway?  First we drag a few lockers or something to funnel them, then one "
"of us hangs close to the barricade and the other stands back and fires arrows "
"or something?\"  He shrugs.  \"I'm not great at tactics, and I'm a bit "
"nervous about what's back there.\""
msgstr ""
"*Se frota la barbilla pensativo. «¿Quizás podamos crear un cuello de botella "
"en el pasillo? Primero arrastramos unas cuantas taquillas o algo así para "
"canalizarlos, luego uno de nosotros se queda cerca de la barricada y el otro "
"se queda atrás y dispara flechas o algo así». Se encoge de hombros. «No se me "
"dan bien las tácticas y estoy un poco nervioso por lo que hay ahí atrás»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks man.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Gracias, tío. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You sure we haven't bit off more than we can chew here?\"  He stares at you "
"for a moment.  \"This isn't DOTA2, this is real life.  These guys are gonna "
"have guns and shit.  I know we've been through a lot together but if they're "
"ready for us they could take us out before we're even close enough to see "
"them.  I mean, I'm with you if you think we can do it, but be careful, okay?"
msgstr ""
"¿Estás seguro de que no nos hemos metido en un lío demasiado grande? Te mira "
"fijamente durante un momento. «Esto no es DOTA2, es la vida real. Esos tipos "
"tendrán armas y todo eso. Sé que hemos pasado por muchas cosas juntos, pero "
"si están preparados para nosotros, podrían acabar con nosotros antes de que "
"nos acerquemos lo suficiente como para verlos. Quiero decir, estoy contigo si "
"crees que podemos hacerlo, pero ten cuidado, ¿vale?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Thanks man, I'll keep that in mind.  We gotta do this though.  Any "
"suggestions for how to do it safely?"
msgstr ""
"Gracias, tío, lo tendré en cuenta. Pero tenemos que hacerlo. ¿Alguna "
"sugerencia sobre cómo hacerlo de forma segura?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Thanks man, I'll keep that in mind.  We'll do this carefully.  I'd like your "
"opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, tío, lo tendré en cuenta. Lo haremos con cuidado. De hecho, me "
"gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you're gonna insist on it then I say we drive up quick in the dark, take "
"cover behind the car, and make a ton of noise.  Then we take cover and when "
"they come to check things out, we pick them off.  Or maybe we come in silent, "
"from a distance, and take out their sentries.  A bow is great for that, if we "
"can make the shots.  This whole thing still seems ridiculous though."
msgstr ""
"Si vas a insistir en ello, entonces yo digo que conduzcamos rápido en la "
"oscuridad, nos cubramos detrás del coche y hagamos mucho ruido. Luego nos "
"ponemos a cubierto y, cuando vengan a ver qué pasa, los eliminamos. O tal vez "
"entremos en silencio, desde la distancia, y eliminemos a sus centinelas. Un "
"arco es ideal para eso, si podemos acertar los tiros. Sin embargo, todo esto "
"sigue pareciéndome ridículo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm kinda looking forward to it.  It's good to see people already building up "
"something to last, after everything that's gone down.  Wonder what we'll find "
"out there."
msgstr ""
"Tengo muchas ganas de verlo. Es bueno ver que la gente ya está construyendo "
"algo duradero, después de todo lo que ha pasado. Me pregunto qué "
"encontraremos allí."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That's optimistic, thanks man.  I'd like your opinion on something else, "
"actually."
msgstr ""
"Eso es optimista, gracias, tío. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre "
"otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know, I read an article about how those stupid FEMA evac shelters all had "
"solar power for emergencies.  I bet nobody's looting those, let's track some "
"down and unbolt 'em."
msgstr ""
"Sabes, leí un artículo sobre cómo todos esos estúpidos refugios de evacuación "
"de la FEMA tenían energía solar para emergencias. Apuesto a que nadie los "
"está saqueando, vamos a localizar algunos y desatornillarlos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not a bad thought.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "No es mala idea. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Look, you're the one that agreed to this.  I don't know why you keep agreeing "
"to this stuff.  Maybe we can check hardware stores?  Or just eat a lot of "
"jarred food, and keep the empties?  A hundred jars.  That's a lot, my "
"friend.\"  He shakes his head.  \"You don't have to agree to do *everything* "
"people ask you to do, you know?"
msgstr ""
"Mira, tú eres el que aceptó esto. No sé por qué sigues aceptando estas cosas. "
"¿Quizás podamos buscar en ferreterías? ¿O simplemente comer mucha comida "
"envasada y guardar los envases vacíos? Cien envases. Eso es mucho, amigo mío. "
"Él niega con la cabeza. No tienes que aceptar hacer todo lo que la gente te "
"pide, ¿sabes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your objection is noted.  I'd like your opinion on something else, though."
msgstr ""
"Tomo nota de su objeción. Sin embargo, me gustaría conocer su opinión sobre "
"otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shakes his head at you.  \"Look, you asked last time, and I told you you "
"didn't have to keep taking jobs like this.  Now you're asking again?  *I "
"dunno, stop offering to bring a billion jars to people if you don't know "
"where to find them.*\"  He laughs.  \"I'm just messing with you.\"  His eyes "
"narrow.  \"Or am I?\""
msgstr ""
"*Niega con la cabeza. «Mira, ya me lo preguntaste la última vez y te dije que "
"no tenías por qué seguir aceptando trabajos como este. ¿Y ahora me lo vuelves "
"a preguntar? No sé, deja de ofrecerte a llevar mil millones de tarros a la "
"gente si no sabes dónde encontrarlos». Se ríe. «Solo te estoy tomando el "
"pelo». Entrecierra los ojos. «¿O no?»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"How about it?  Seems like a nice enough thing to do I guess.  I bet plenty of "
"zombies are carrying smokes, and there's probably tons in people's abandoned "
"cars."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué te parece? Supongo que es una buena idea. Apuesto a que muchos zombis "
"llevan cigarrillos, y probablemente hay toneladas en los coches abandonados "
"de la gente."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Sí. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Isn't he just directing us out to that Isherwood farm?"
msgstr "¿No nos está llevando a la granja de Isherwood?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sounds good.  I'm a bit nervous about what we might find, though.  Who knows "
"what the apocalypse would do to a bunch of gun-toting back country folks?  On "
"the other hand, maybe they're sweet, salt-of-the-earth types.  Only one way "
"to find out!"
msgstr ""
"Suena bien. Aunque estoy un poco nervioso por lo que podamos encontrar. "
"¿Quién sabe qué les haría el apocalipsis a un grupo de paletos armados? Por "
"otro lado, quizá sean gente encantadora y sencilla. ¡Solo hay una forma de "
"averiguarlo!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Bien. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Is that just that Hub place, with the intercom?  Not that it's not cool, but "
"it's nothing new to us.  Woah… we've really seen some shit, haven't we."
msgstr ""
"¿Es ese lugar llamado Hub, con el intercomunicador? No es que no sea genial, "
"pero no es nada nuevo para nosotros. Vaya... realmente hemos visto cosas "
"raras, ¿no?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It sounds to me like this might be that intercom we found out in that weird "
"building?  I'm just guessing.  We should go confirm."
msgstr ""
"Me parece que podría tratarse del intercomunicador que encontramos en ese "
"edificio tan extraño. Es solo una suposición. Deberíamos ir a confirmarlo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hell yeah, this sounds so badass!  Let's be careful though, 'secret lab' "
"sounds like a place that's gonna have some defenses."
msgstr ""
"¡Claro que sí, suena genial! Pero tengamos cuidado, «laboratorio secreto» "
"suena como un lugar que tendrá algunas defensas."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You bet.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Por supuesto. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We've been there, remember?  It's got those cyborg guys, the cockney ones."
msgstr "Hemos estado allí, ¿recuerdas? Salen esos tipos cyborg, los cockney."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Far-fetched and awesome!  Let's go see.  Maybe it's an abandoned theme park "
"or something."
msgstr ""
"¡Increíble y alucinante! Vamos a verlo. Quizás sea un parque temático "
"abandonado o algo así."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We've been there, remember"
msgstr "Hemos estado allí, recuerda."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "?  Cody, the blacksmith, she's the food lady"
msgstr "Cody, el herrero, ella es la señora de la comida."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"?  I'm guessing the blacksmith we didn't talk to is the one who would have "
"fed us"
msgstr ""
"Supongo que el herrero con el que no hablamos es el que nos habría dado de "
"comer."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", and Jay is the one with the weird bullet bank."
msgstr ", y Jay es el que tiene el extraño banco de balas."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", and the other guy there must be the one with the bullet bank."
msgstr ", y el otro tipo que está allí debe ser el que tiene el banco de balas."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm open to anything if it means getting fed.  Ugh, unless it's unidentified "
"meat.  I guess we have to be more careful of strangers than we used to.  "
"Still, let's find out."
msgstr ""
"Estoy dispuesto a todo si eso significa comer. Uf, a menos que sea carne no "
"identificada. Supongo que tenemos que tener más cuidado con los desconocidos "
"que antes. Aun así, averigüémoslo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I like his fashion choices, but he, um.  Well, you know.  You met him.  "
"I don't mind helping him out, in theory, but I don't know if bringing him "
"piles of trash is really going to do anyone any good.  The Merchants might "
"think it's a fire hazard."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, me gusta su estilo, pero él, eh... Bueno, ya sabes. Tú lo conociste. "
"No me importa ayudarlo, en teoría, pero no sé si llevarle montones de basura "
"realmente le hará bien a alguien. Los comerciantes podrían pensar que es un "
"peligro de incendio."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's try it out anyway.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Probémoslo de todos modos. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Right, I guess.  I don't quite get why you're doing this stuff for him, he's "
"probably just going to keep piling up the stuff and not doing anything with "
"it.\"  He shrugs.  \"On the other hand, maybe he'll make a kick-ass box fort, "
"I'd be all about that."
msgstr ""
"Sí, supongo. No entiendo muy bien por qué haces estas cosas por él, "
"probablemente solo va a seguir acumulando cosas y no va a hacer nada con "
"ellas. Se encoge de hombros. Por otro lado, tal vez construya un fuerte "
"increíble con cajas, eso me encantaría."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's my hope.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Esa es mi esperanza. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm telling you, this is just going to go on and on forever.\"  He looks sad. "
" \"I'd really love to see him get a cool box fort and feel better, but I "
"think we're just enabling his delusions, my friend."
msgstr ""
"Te lo digo, esto va a seguir así para siempre. Parece triste. Me encantaría "
"que consiguiera un fuerte de cajas molón y se sintiera mejor, pero creo que "
"solo estamos alimentando sus delirios, amigo mío."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's see this through a bit longer.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr ""
"Veamos cómo evoluciona esto un poco más. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre "
"otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I gotta admit, this one surprised me.  I take back some of what I said "
"earlier, I'm just confused now.  Let's see where it goes."
msgstr ""
"Tengo que admitir que esto me ha sorprendido. Retiro parte de lo que he dicho "
"antes, ahora estoy confundido. Veamos cómo evoluciona."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right?  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "¿Verdad? Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It had better be!  I'm not sure why you're doing this, but I do think it's "
"good you're trying to help him.  Maybe we should stop eventually though?\"  "
"He sighs.  \"I don't know what to make of Dave.  I worked with a guy with "
"schizophrenia back at Foodplace, and Dave is nothing like that.  I don't know "
"if he's actually got some kind of mental illness or if it's a stress reaction "
"or something.  He doesn't act like any real person I've ever met, and we got "
"all kinds of strung-out types there."
msgstr ""
"¡Más vale que así sea! No sé muy bien por qué lo haces, pero creo que está "
"bien que intentes ayudarle. Aunque quizá deberíamos dejarlo en algún momento. "
"Suspira. No sé qué pensar de Dave. Trabajé con un chico con esquizofrenia en "
"Lugarcomida, y Dave no se parece en nada a él. No sé si realmente tiene algún "
"tipo de enfermedad mental o si es una reacción al estrés o algo así. No se "
"comporta como ninguna persona real que haya conocido, y allí tenemos todo "
"tipo de tipos estresados."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's good insight.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Es una buena observación. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I'm definitely interested to see where it goes.  I hope it helps Dave "
"somehow.  I don't know what's going on with him except that it's nothing like "
"any schizophrenia or anything like that I've ever seen, and I've seen "
"practically anything you can imagine, working service."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, definitivamente tengo interés en ver cómo evoluciona. Espero que le "
"sirva de ayuda a Dave de alguna manera. No sé qué le está pasando, pero no se "
"parece en nada a la esquizofrenia ni a nada que haya visto antes, y he visto "
"prácticamente todo lo que se pueda imaginar en mi trabajo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have a good feeling.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Tengo un buen presentimiento. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, it probably isn't going to come back alive.  They ooze blood "
"everywhere, when we fight 'em.  It's kinda thicker and goopier than human "
"blood, but I guess not so bad it'd be hard to draw?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, probablemente no vaya a volver con vida. Cuando luchamos contra ellos, "
"rezuman sangre por todas partes. Es un poco más espesa y viscosa que la "
"sangre humana, pero supongo que no es tan difícil de extraer, ¿no?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Gracias. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This sounds *nuts* man.  How are we going to get in and out alive?  A place "
"like that is going to be crawling with zombies and who knows what else.\"  He "
"shudders.  \"Let's be careful, right?"
msgstr ""
"Esto suena *de locos*, tío. ¿Cómo vamos a entrar y salir vivos? Un lugar así "
"estará plagado de zombis y quién sabe qué más. Se estremece. «Tengamos "
"cuidado, ¿vale?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Vale. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This was a total surprise to everyone,\" he grumbles.  \"Still, this can't be "
"any worse than getting the first analysis done, right?"
msgstr ""
"Esto fue una sorpresa total para todos», se queja. «Aun así, esto no puede "
"ser peor que hacer el primer análisis, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's hope not.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Esperemos que no. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&He grins.  \"I'm gonna level with you, this sounds incredibly *cool*.\"  He "
"laughs at his own joke.  \"Seriously though, it's probably going to be a "
"really tricky one"
msgstr ""
"Él sonríe. «Voy a ser sincero contigo, esto suena increíblemente *genial*». "
"Se ríe de su propio chiste. «En serio, probablemente va a ser muy complicado»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  It'd be good to maybe try cybernetics to help us with the cold, they won't "
"be as bulky and confining to fight in as winter gear."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  We'll need to bundle up extra toasty, that'll make fighting tough."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good thoughts.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Buenas ideas. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Compared to what we've done, this doesn't sound so bad.  Creepy as heck "
"though.  We should tell ghost stories on the way."
msgstr ""
"En comparación con lo que hemos hecho, esto no suena tan mal. Aunque da mucho "
"miedo. Deberíamos contar historias de fantasmas por el camino."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I mean, I have a basic understanding of the principles.  We could also see if "
"we could just find a couple stills though, we're not far from the mountains.  "
"I bet every second farm's gonna have a moonshine still set up in one of the "
"sheds."
msgstr ""
"Quiero decir, tengo un conocimiento básico de los principios. También "
"podríamos ver si podemos encontrar un par de alambiques, no estamos lejos de "
"las montañas. Apuesto a que cada dos granjas hay un alambique ilegal "
"instalado en uno de los cobertizos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Good point, although really, how hard can it be to make one?  I'd like your "
"opinion on something else, too."
msgstr ""
"Buen punto, aunque, en realidad, ¿qué tan difícil puede ser hacer uno? "
"También me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I think a supermarket might be the *yeast* likely place to find it!\"  He "
"watches your expression for a moment, then shrugs.  \"Worth a shot.  Anyway, "
"as far as I know, dry yeast lasts practically forever.  Should be able to "
"find some of it anywhere people did baking or brewing."
msgstr ""
"Creo que un supermercado podría ser el lugar más probable para encontrarla. "
"Observa tu expresión por un momento y luego se encoge de hombros. Vale la "
"pena intentarlo. De todos modos, por lo que sé, la levadura seca dura "
"prácticamente para siempre. Deberías poder encontrarla en cualquier lugar "
"donde la gente hornee o elabore cerveza."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, man.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Those Tacoma folks really think about sustainability, hey?  I like that.  Buy "
"local, you know?  I got no idea where to find sugar beet seeds though.  I "
"don't remember having any stocked at the cabin.  Maybe a farm or farm supply "
"store would have them?"
msgstr ""
"La gente de Tacoma realmente piensa en la sostenibilidad, ¿eh? Me gusta eso. "
"Comprar productos locales, ¿sabes? Aunque no tengo ni idea de dónde encontrar "
"semillas de remolacha azucarera. No recuerdo haber tenido ninguna en la "
"cabaña. ¿Quizás las tengan en una granja o en una tienda de suministros "
"agrícolas?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs.  \"If we track these things down for the bartender, I hope we get a "
"nice, sincere 'tanks' at the end.\""
msgstr ""
"*risas. «Si le conseguimos estas cosas al camarero, espero que al final nos "
"dé las gracias de verdad»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Me too.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Yo también. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There's only one way for two folks like us to transport two huge liquid "
"storage drums.  We bundle ourselves in them and roll them down the hill.  "
"First one to the bar buys the other one a drink."
msgstr ""
"Solo hay una forma de que dos personas como nosotros transportemos dos "
"enormes bidones de almacenamiento de líquidos. Nos metemos dentro de ellos y "
"los hacemos rodar cuesta abajo. El primero en llegar al bar invita a la otra "
"persona a una copa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know it'd be me.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Sabes que sería yo. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Of all the jobs we've agreed to do, this is certainly one of them."
msgstr "De todos los trabajos que hemos acordado hacer, este es sin duda uno de ellos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You can say that again.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Ya lo puedes decir. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess I get why the one Boris guy can't do it but I don't quite see why we "
"have to go around asking everyone for him.  He lives here!  Anyway, you know "
"I'm okay with getting my hands dirty, if you want to go offer to help him out "
"I'll get busy with a scrubby.  I've cleaned worse things out of the Foodplace "
"washroom.  Hell, I've cleaned worse things out of the back of my van when I "
"was running for Amazon.\"  He gets a thousand-yard-stare for a moment.  "
"\"Let's not discuss this any more."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que entiendo por qué Boris no puede hacerlo, pero no veo por qué "
"tenemos que ir preguntando a todo el mundo por él. ¡Vive aquí! De todos "
"modos, ya sabes que no me importa ensuciarme las manos, si quieres ir a "
"ofrecerle tu ayuda, yo me pondré manos a la obra con un cepillo. He limpiado "
"cosas peores en el baño del Foodplace. Joder, he limpiado cosas peores en la "
"parte trasera de mi furgoneta cuando trabajaba para Amazon. Se queda mirando "
"al vacío durante un momento. No hablemos más de esto."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks Liam, I knew I could count on you."
msgstr "Gracias, Liam, sabía que podía contar contigo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's just a fetch job, right?  I'd say our best first bet would be to see if "
"Smokes up at the Free Merchant desk has one, and just shell out to get it "
"covered.  These guys are broke as heck, but we can easily make the cash back "
"by doing some good old fashioned scavenging."
msgstr ""
"Es sólo un trabajo de búsqueda, ¿verdad? Yo diría que nuestra mejor apuesta "
"sería ver si Humos en el mostrador de Mercaderes Libres tiene uno, y "
"simplemente pagar para conseguirlo. Estos tipos están arruinados, pero "
"podemos recuperar fácilmente el dinero rebuscando a la antigua usanza."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Worth checking.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Vale la pena comprobarlo. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&His voice comes out a bit softer and lower than usual.  \"This is just a sad "
"one, my friend.  I don't think we'll have any troubles with the delivery, but "
"it's so goddamn sad.\""
msgstr ""
"Su voz suena un poco más suave y grave de lo habitual. «Es una historia "
"triste, amigo mío. No creo que tengamos ningún problema con la entrega, pero "
"es tan triste...»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nah, not me.  I hear they're hard to keep alive or something, and that makes "
"me nervous.  I was never really that much of a baker to be honest.  I love "
"the bread though, pretty excited to see what she makes.\"  He looks "
"thoughtful for a moment.  \"Depending on where the bakery is though, this "
"could be a heck of a job.  We should make sure we're ready to sneak past a "
"lot of zed to get to it."
msgstr ""
"No, yo no. He oído que son difíciles de mantener vivos o algo así, y eso me "
"pone nervioso. Para ser sincero, nunca se me ha dado muy bien la repostería. "
"Sin embargo, me encanta el pan, así que tengo muchas ganas de ver lo que "
"hace. Se queda pensativo por un momento. «Dependiendo de dónde esté la "
"panadería, esto podría ser un trabajo muy duro. Debemos asegurarnos de estar "
"preparados para esquivar a muchos zombis para llegar hasta allí."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Or we could clear the area some other way.  I'd like your opinion on "
"something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"O podríamos despejar la zona de otra manera. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu "
"opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*grins.  \"Yeah, he sure is.  I never got the hang of the guitar, myself, but "
"I respect the journey.  It shouldn't be too hard to find one, right?  Lots of "
"people have them in their houses, or we could maybe loot a music store if we "
"want to get fancy.\""
msgstr ""
"*Sonríe. «Sí, claro que sí. Yo nunca aprendí a tocar la guitarra, pero "
"respeto el esfuerzo. No debería ser muy difícil encontrar una, ¿no? Mucha "
"gente tiene una en casa, o podríamos saquear una tienda de música si queremos "
"hacer algo más sofisticado»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"With your singing voice, I'm glad you never learned.  I'd like your opinion "
"on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Con tu voz para cantar, me alegro de que nunca lo hayas aprendido. De hecho, "
"me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Of course!  People need what comfort they can get, right?  I've always been "
"kinda spiritual, but I'm not the sort to put a label on it or anything.  I "
"don't have a clue where to find one though, I'm not sure I'd even recognize a "
"mosque if I saw one.  Do they stock books like that in normal stores?\"  He "
"frowns.  \"I feel like I should know this, but… well, no Wikipedia, right?"
msgstr ""
"¡Por supuesto! La gente necesita todo el consuelo que pueda obtener, ¿no? "
"Siempre he sido un poco espiritual, pero no soy de los que le ponen etiquetas "
"ni nada por el estilo. Sin embargo, no tengo ni idea de dónde encontrar una, "
"ni siquiera estoy seguro de que reconocería una mezquita si la viera. ¿Venden "
"libros de ese tipo en las tiendas normales? Frunce el ceño. «Siento que "
"debería saberlo, pero... bueno, no hay Wikipedia, ¿verdad?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Cell phones were something else.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Los teléfonos móviles eran otra cosa. Sin embargo, me gustaría conocer tu "
"opinión sobre otro tema."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&He scratches his head.  \"No.  I guess a library or a bookstore.  I have a "
"feeling this is going to be a tough one though.  Maybe we could try like, "
"hardware stores?  Or school libraries?\"  He thinks a bit more.  \"Those seem "
"like our best bets to me, but I'm just guessing.\""
msgstr ""
"Se rasca la cabeza. «No. Supongo que una biblioteca o una librería. Aunque "
"tengo la sensación de que va a ser difícil. ¿Quizás podríamos probar en "
"ferreterías? ¿O en bibliotecas escolares?». Lo piensa un poco más. «Me "
"parecen las mejores opciones, pero solo es una suposición»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, man.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing though."
msgstr "Gracias, tío. Pero me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This one sounds easy to me.  Let's just take apart some old machinery until "
"we find a good one."
msgstr ""
"Esto me parece fácil. Desmontemos algunas máquinas viejas hasta que "
"encontremos una buena."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Kinda wonder why she didn't just get us to get her a compressor, but she "
"probably has her reasons.\"  You notice a bit of an odd tone to his voice.  "
"\"Maybe we could take apart a big compressor for her, the tank would probably "
"be perfect."
msgstr ""
"Me pregunto por qué no nos pidió que le compráramos un compresor, pero "
"seguramente tendrá sus razones. Notas un tono un poco extraño en su voz. "
"«Quizás podríamos desmontar un compresor grande para ella, el tanque "
"seguramente sería perfecto."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Dude.  You have a crush on Jenny."
msgstr "Tío, estás enamorado de Jenny."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*blushes, for some reason.  \"Uh, yeah.  Gun books, hey?  I guess we should "
"look in um, gun stores or libraries?  Or high school lockers, haha.  Oh, that "
"made me sad.\""
msgstr ""
"*Se sonroja, por alguna razón. «Eh, sí. Libros sobre armas, ¿eh? Supongo que "
"deberíamos buscarlos en... ¿tiendas de armas o bibliotecas? O en las "
"taquillas del instituto, jaja. Oh, eso me ha entristecido»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*blushes.  \"Yeah we are.\"  He smiles dopily, apparently forgetting that "
"you'd asked for his thoughts."
msgstr ""
"*Se sonroja—. Sí, lo somos. —Sonríe tontamente, aparentemente olvidando que "
"le habías preguntado qué pensaba."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any opinions on the job itself?"
msgstr "¿Alguna opinión sobre el trabajo en sí?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Just wanted to point that out.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Solo quería señalar eso. Sin embargo, me gustaría conocer tu opinión sobre "
"otro tema."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Uh, right.  Maybe a gun store?  Or a library?  Or we could check high school "
"lockers, haha.  Oh, that made me sad."
msgstr ""
"Eh, claro. ¿Quizás una armería? ¿O una biblioteca? O podríamos mirar en las "
"taquillas del instituto, jaja. Oh, eso me ha entristecido."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You've got it *bad*, dude.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing though."
msgstr ""
"Lo tienes *mal*, tío. Sin embargo, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&He looks at you, a bit surprised.  \"Yeah, of course.  I mean, that "
"situation they're in now is miserable, no matter how much we've helped folks "
"out there.  Can you imagine trying to be a young couple in that cramped "
"space?\"  He waggles his eyebrows suggestively.  \"They're tryin' to have a "
"*baby*, you know.  Gonna be hard in a bunkhouse.  Let's get them out to a "
"nice farm, some fresh air, and, *you* know.\"  He winks, to drive the point "
"far, far further home than necessary.  \"Let the magic happen, right?\""
msgstr ""
"Él te mira, un poco sorprendido. «Sí, claro. Quiero decir, la situación en la "
"que se encuentran ahora es miserable, por mucho que hayamos ayudado a la "
"gente de allí. ¿Te imaginas intentar ser una pareja joven en ese espacio tan "
"reducido?». Mueve las cejas de forma sugerente. «Están intentando tener un "
"*bebé*, ya sabes. Va a ser difícil en un barracón. Llevémoslos a una bonita "
"granja, donde puedan respirar aire fresco y, ya *sabes*». Te guiña el ojo, "
"para dejar el mensaje mucho más claro de lo necesario. «Dejemos que la magia "
"surta efecto, ¿no?»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That was unnecessarily clear.  Still, I'd like your opinion on a different "
"thing, somehow."
msgstr ""
"Eso ha quedado innecesariamente claro. Aun así, me gustaría conocer tu "
"opinión sobre otro tema, de alguna manera."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Seems pretty cut and dry to me.  Let's raid a few first aid kits.  I'm pretty "
"sure you can find that stuff in the basement of those government evac "
"shelters, for example."
msgstr ""
"A mí me parece bastante sencillo. Vamos a saquear unos cuantos botiquines de "
"primeros auxilios. Estoy bastante seguro de que puedes encontrar esas cosas "
"en el sótano de los refugios de evacuación del gobierno, por ejemplo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing, though."
msgstr "Gracias. Sin embargo, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otro tema."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Kinda don't think she needs our help on this one, but she's in a bind I "
"guess.\"  He pauses.  \"No pun intended this time,\" he chuckles.  \"Anyway, "
"let's just find some spare fabric, choppy-choppy, and Bob's your uncle.\"  He "
"thinks for a moment.  \"Actually she'll probably want them disinfected, and "
"we should find her some tape too just to be on the safe side."
msgstr ""
"No creo que necesite nuestra ayuda en esto, pero supongo que está en un "
"aprieto. Hace una pausa. «Esta vez no es un juego de palabras», dice riendo. "
"«En fin, busquemos un poco de tela sobrante, cortemos y listo». Piensa por un "
"momento. «En realidad, probablemente querrá que los desinfectemos, y "
"deberíamos buscarle también cinta adhesiva, por si acaso."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fair enough.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing, though."
msgstr "Me parece bien. Sin embargo, me gustaría conocer tu opinión sobre otro tema."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I admit, I haven't been paying attention to it, but I'm sure those things "
"must be around in half the medicine cabinets in the area, right?  Seems like "
"an easy looting job to me."
msgstr ""
"Lo admito, no le he prestado atención, pero estoy seguro de que esas cosas "
"deben estar en la mitad de los botiquines de la zona, ¿no? A mí me parece un "
"trabajo fácil de saquear."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good point.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing, though."
msgstr "Buen punto. Sin embargo, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Worse things we could do for people than help them get haircuts,\" he shrugs. "
" \"No job too small, right?  Vanessa seems a bit cranky to me, but I'm not "
"judging.  Those folks are in a tough spot.  Maybe she'll turn suddenly nice "
"if we bring her the hair stuff she wants.\"  He grins.  \"I'm one hundred "
"percent sure that's what'll happen."
msgstr ""
"«Hay cosas peores que podríamos hacer por la gente que ayudarles a cortarse "
"el pelo», dice encogiéndose de hombros. «Ningún trabajo es demasiado pequeño, "
"¿verdad? Vanessa me parece un poco malhumorada, pero no la juzgo. Esa gente "
"está pasando por un momento difícil. Quizás se vuelva amable de repente si le "
"llevamos los productos para el cabello que quiere». Sonríe. «Estoy cien por "
"cien seguro de que eso es lo que pasará»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That's my optimistic Liam.  I'd like your opinion on a different thing, "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Ese es mi Liam optimista. Sin embargo, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre "
"otro tema."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs.  \"Look, Makayla is a trained professional, she knows what she's "
"doing with several kilograms of improvised explosives, doesn't she?\"  He "
"shrugs.  \"If not, let's just stay far away when she tests it.\""
msgstr ""
"*Risas. «Mira, Makayla es una profesional cualificada, sabe lo que hace con "
"varios kilos de explosivos improvisados, ¿no?». Se encoge de hombros. «Si no "
"es así, mantengámonos alejados cuando lo pruebe»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*blows out a long breath.  \"Well, my friend, I do think it's good to help "
"clean out some of the mess that's going on.  I'll be with you for it.  I'm "
"just not sure why you figure I'm the right guy for this job.  Shouldn't you "
"have, like, a cop or a soldier or something?  I'm a delivery driver.\""
msgstr ""
"*Exhala un largo suspiro—. Bueno, amigo mío, creo que está bien ayudar a "
"limpiar parte del desastre que se está produciendo. Estaré contigo para eso. "
"Solo que no estoy seguro de por qué crees que soy la persona adecuada para "
"este trabajo. ¿No deberías tener, por ejemplo, un policía o un soldado o algo "
"así? Yo soy repartidor."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't sell yourself short, Liam.  You've got my back."
msgstr "No te subestimes, Liam. Puedes contar conmigo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll handle the tough parts, Liam.  You're there to cover my back, that's all."
msgstr ""
"Yo me encargaré de las partes difíciles, Liam. Tú solo tienes que cubrirme "
"las espaldas, eso es todo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "In troubled times, we learn what sort of people we really are."
msgstr "En tiempos difíciles, descubrimos qué tipo de personas somos realmente."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Meh.  What's a few bandits?  We'll flatten 'em."
msgstr "Bah. ¿Qué son unos cuantos bandidos? Los aplastaremos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks.  You're right.  Okay, I can do this.\"  He shakes his shoulders and "
"limbers up, like a boxer preparing for a match.  \"Let's go."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Tienes razón. Vale, puedo hacerlo». Se sacude los hombros y se "
"calienta, como un boxeador preparándose para un combate. «Vamos»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hold up Balboa, I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Espera, Balboa, en realidad me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, oh yeah that makes sense.  Okay, well, that's something I can do.  I'll "
"cover your back like it's never been covered before.  You and me like Calvin "
"and Hobbes, baby."
msgstr ""
"Ah, sí, tiene sentido. Vale, bueno, eso es algo que puedo hacer. Te cubriré "
"las espaldas como nunca antes se ha hecho. Tú y yo como Calvin y Hobbes, "
"cariño."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, Hooch.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Gracias, Hooch. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*sniffs the air around your head.  \"You been getting in the ganja?  No "
"judgment if so, but maybe you shouldn't be taking mercenary jobs while you're "
"high, y'know?\""
msgstr ""
"*Huele el aire alrededor de tu cabeza—. ¿Has estado fumando marihuana? No te "
"juzgo si es así, pero quizá no deberías aceptar trabajos mercenarios mientras "
"estás colocado, ¿sabes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Shut up, you're not my dad!  Anyway, I'd like your opinion on something else, "
"actually."
msgstr ""
"Cállate, ¡no eres mi padre! De todos modos, me gustaría saber tu opinión "
"sobre otra cosa, en realidad."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gives you some serious side-eye.  \"You okay?  This is serious shit, you're "
"making me kinda worried getting so gung-ho about it.\""
msgstr ""
"*Te mira con recelo. «¿Estás bien? Esto es algo serio, me estás preocupando "
"al ponerte tan entusiasmado con ello»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Don't worry, man.  Trust me, it'll be great.  Anyway, I'd like your opinion "
"on something else."
msgstr ""
"No te preocupes, tío. Confía en mí, será genial. De todos modos, me gustaría "
"saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know, this sounds like it's gonna be some big exciting mystery whodunnit, "
"but I have this feeling if we just look around for someone who is acting "
"obviously and extremely suspicious it'll all fall apart at once."
msgstr ""
"Sabes, esto suena como si fuera a ser un gran y emocionante misterio "
"policíaco, pero tengo la sensación de que si buscamos a alguien que actúe de "
"forma obvia y extremadamente sospechosa, todo se desmoronará de golpe."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I dunno, but compared to the last two missions for that guy, I gotta admit "
"I'm kinda stoked.  Robots?  This sounds *wicked*.  Do you think we're talking "
"more Terminator, or Wall-E?  Doesn't matter.  Robots!"
msgstr ""
"No sé, pero comparado con las dos últimas misiones para ese tipo, tengo que "
"admitir que estoy bastante emocionado. ¿Robots? Suena genial. ¿Crees que se "
"trata más de Terminator o de Wall-E? No importa. ¡Robots!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Uh, well, we *did* meet that weird cyborg guy in the castle full of giant "
"robot dogs matching this exact description, right?  Tell me you remember "
"that.  Damn, it's worse saying it out loud.  I still can't really believe all "
"this stuff has really happened."
msgstr ""
"Eh, bueno, *sí* que conocimos a ese extraño cyborg en el castillo lleno de "
"perros robot gigantes que encaja exactamente con esa descripción, ¿no? Dime "
"que lo recuerdas. Maldita sea, es peor decirlo en voz alta. Todavía no puedo "
"creer que todo esto haya sucedido realmente."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, right, I remember that.  I'd like your opinion on something else, though."
msgstr ""
"Ah, sí, lo recuerdo. Sin embargo, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know me my friend,\" he shrugs and grins at you.  \"I'd have said it was "
"some kinda cryptid or something *before* the world got flooded with monsters "
"and mutants.  Nowadays, I think I'd be more surprised if it was bandits "
"again.  As for how to deal with it, well, I guess we're getting pretty good "
"at dealing with this kind of thing now.  Let's handle it how we usually do: "
"with style."
msgstr ""
"Ya me conoces, amigo\", se encoge de hombros y te sonríe. \"Yo habría dicho "
"que era algún tipo de críptido o algo así *antes* de que el mundo se inundara "
"de monstruos y mutantes. Hoy en día, creo que me sorprendería más que "
"volviera a tratarse de bandidos. En cuanto a cómo lidiar con ello, bueno, "
"supongo que nos estamos volviendo bastante buenos lidiando con este tipo de "
"cosas ahora. Manejémoslo como solemos hacerlo: con estilo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Damn straight.  I'd like your opinion on something else, though."
msgstr "Por supuesto. Sin embargo, me gustaría conocer tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I dunno,\" he points to your Marshal badge.  \"I guess if they give you a "
"shiny bit of metal you're not really an assassin for hire anymore, you're the "
"law.  Judge, jury, and executioner.\"  He scratches his neck and looks away "
"for a moment.  \"You know how I feel about all these high risk missions, but "
"we've gotten this far.  It's different now than when we started out.  I don't "
"think you need my advice, you know I'll have your back whatever happens."
msgstr ""
"«No lo sé», dice señalando tu placa de mariscal. «Supongo que si te dan un "
"trozo de metal brillante, ya no eres un asesino a sueldo, sino la ley. Juez, "
"jurado y verdugo». Se rasca el cuello y desvía la mirada por un momento. «Ya "
"sabes lo que pienso de todas estas misiones de alto riesgo, pero hemos "
"llegado hasta aquí. Ahora es diferente a cuando empezamos. No creo que "
"necesites mi consejo, sabes que te respaldaré pase lo que pase»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I might not need it, but I still like to hear it.  I'd like your opinion on "
"something else, anyway."
msgstr ""
"Puede que no lo necesite, pero me gusta saberlo. De todos modos, me gustaría "
"saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Honestly my friend, this is the kinda stuff I hoped we'd be doing when we "
"offered to help these guys out.  Fresh air, great views, climbing on things "
"we'd have gotten in trouble for in the old days, maybe pushing a zombie off "
"the edge of a maintenance platform to see how big a splat it leaves at the "
"bottom.  Sounds wicked.  Let's bring a couple cold ones up to the top and "
"crack a brew while we survey the wasteland, hey?"
msgstr ""
"Sinceramente, amigo mío, esto es lo que esperaba que hiciéramos cuando nos "
"ofrecimos a ayudar a estos tipos. Aire fresco, vistas espectaculares, trepar "
"por sitios por los que nos habrían castigado en otros tiempos, quizá empujar "
"a un zombi desde el borde de una plataforma de mantenimiento para ver qué "
"mancha deja al caer. Suena genial. Llevemos un par de cervezas frías a la "
"cima y abramos una mientras observamos el páramo, ¿te parece?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like a great idea.  I'd like your opinion on something else, though."
msgstr ""
"Me parece una idea estupenda. Sin embargo, me gustaría conocer tu opinión "
"sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I'm with you there, it's some kind of weird map.  The smart thing to do "
"is probably avoid it, this is some really weird shit.  I've never been one to "
"do the smart thing though, myself.  Probably gonna have troubles sleeping "
"until I know what that thing is trying to lead us to."
msgstr ""
"Sí, estoy de acuerdo contigo, es un mapa muy raro. Lo más inteligente sería "
"evitarlo, es algo realmente extraño. Aunque yo nunca he sido de los que hacen "
"lo más inteligente. Probablemente no podré dormir hasta que sepa adónde nos "
"quiere llevar esa cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I know what you mean.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Sé lo que quieres decir. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I just like, wanna back up a second.  We're trying to score drugs for a "
"cyborg so it can do surgery on you?  That's really where life's taking us, "
"now?"
msgstr ""
"Solo quiero retroceder un segundo. ¿Estamos tratando de conseguir drogas para "
"un cyborg para que pueda operarte? ¿Es ahí donde nos está llevando la vida "
"ahora?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…Yes."
msgstr "…Sí."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*grins.  \"Okay, just wanted to clear that up.  I thought maybe I was having "
"some kind of psychotic break, glad it's at least mutual.  Anyway, first place "
"that comes to mind for that kinda stuff would be a hospital, but that's "
"suicide.  Maybe a pharmacy?  Would they have the right stuff?  Seems like a "
"stretch.  Maybe like, a vet clinic or a private surgery clinic might be "
"safer?  I'll level with you, I never got into anything harder than Mary Jane, "
"this is past my pay grade.\""
msgstr ""
"*Sonríe. «Vale, solo quería aclarar eso. Pensaba que quizá estaba teniendo "
"algún tipo de crisis psicótica, me alegro de que al menos sea mutuo. De todos "
"modos, el primer lugar que se me ocurre para ese tipo de cosas sería un "
"hospital, pero eso es un suicidio. ¿Quizá una farmacia? ¿Tendrían lo "
"necesario? Me parece poco probable. ¿Quizás una clínica veterinaria o una "
"clínica quirúrgica privada serían más seguras? Te seré sincero, nunca he "
"probado nada más fuerte que la marihuana, esto me supera»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Something about this kinda rubs me the wrong way, my friend.  I don't know "
"what it is.  That Rubik guy seems nice enough but I feel like we're not "
"getting the whole story.  Just tread carefully, okay?"
msgstr ""
"Hay algo en todo esto que me molesta, amigo mío. No sé qué es. Ese tal Rubik "
"parece bastante agradable, pero tengo la sensación de que no nos están "
"contando toda la historia. Solo hay que andar con cuidado, ¿vale?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Seems to me we could be wandering the area forever just looking for this "
"thing, to be honest.  I guess we could go up somewhere high like a radio "
"tower, maybe with some binoculars, and see if we can spot it?  Our best bet "
"might be to ask a few folks that have been around though, pool our resources."
msgstr ""
"Me parece que podríamos estar vagando por la zona eternamente solo para "
"encontrar esto, sinceramente. ¿Podríamos subir a algún lugar elevado, como "
"una torre de radio, quizá con unos prismáticos, y ver si lo vemos? Lo mejor "
"sería preguntar a algunas personas que hayan estado por aquí y poner en común "
"nuestros recursos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*leans in close, speaking softly, clearly trying to avoid notice from the "
"pizzaiolo.  \"Are you sure we should be hanging with this guy?  He's not "
"exactly all there, is he?  He reminds me a bit of Chris before things went "
"all chompy-chompy.\""
msgstr ""
"*Se inclina hacia él y le habla en voz baja, tratando claramente de que el "
"pizzero no se dé cuenta. «¿Estás seguro de que deberíamos seguir con este "
"tipo? No está del todo bien, ¿verdad? Me recuerda un poco a Chris antes de "
"que todo se fuera al traste»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Chill, man.  It's just a little light arson, it'll be fine."
msgstr "Tranquilo, tío. Solo es un pequeño incendio provocado, no pasa nada."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I hear you, but he's following us now and I don't know how else to get rid of "
"him."
msgstr "Te entiendo, pero ahora nos está siguiendo y no sé cómo deshacernos de él."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess everything else is wrecked already anyway, what's one more burning "
"building?  And like, it *does* sound fun.  Let's just keep an eye on this "
"guy, he's a slice short of a full pie, if you catch my drift."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que todo lo demás ya está destrozado, ¿qué más da un edificio más en "
"llamas? Y, bueno, la verdad es que suena divertido. Pero vigilemos a este "
"tipo, porque le falta un tornillo, si sabes a lo que me refiero."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I knew you'd come around.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Sabía que cambiarías de opinión. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre "
"otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"True enough, and I don't wanna like, just *kill* him.  Well, I don't have "
"anything against a bonfire this season I suppose.  Let's just make sure "
"neither of us ends up lying face-down in a wood-fired oven, y'know?"
msgstr ""
"Es cierto, y no quiero simplemente «matarlo». Bueno, supongo que no tengo "
"nada en contra de una hoguera en esta época del año. Solo asegurémonos de que "
"ninguno de los dos termine boca abajo en un horno de leña, ¿vale?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're on the same page.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Estamos de acuerdo. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No.\"  He stares at you, his eyes wild.  For a moment, you barely know the "
"man in front of you.  \"The things I've seen when I wore that mask… it "
"changes you.  It's a burden you can't truly understand unless you've borne "
"it.\"  He shudders, and becomes again the Liam you know.  \"Anyone who "
"chooses to keep wearing it after the end of the world… putting them down "
"would be a kindness, believe me."
msgstr ""
"No. Te mira fijamente, con los ojos desorbitados. Por un momento, apenas "
"reconoces al hombre que tienes delante. «Las cosas que he visto cuando "
"llevaba esa máscara... te cambian. Es una carga que no puedes comprender "
"realmente a menos que la hayas soportado». Tiembla y vuelve a ser el Liam que "
"conoces. «Cualquiera que decida seguir llevándola después del fin del "
"mundo... acabar con él sería un acto de bondad, créeme»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Uh… okay.  I'd like your opinion on something else, anyway."
msgstr "Eh... vale. De todos modos, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shrugs.  \"My thoughts on Murder Mario haven't changed much, but he hasn't "
"killed us yet.  I don't love the idea of just killing some other survivors "
"for him.  Foodperson doesn't count.\"  He shudders and takes a quick breath.  "
"\"I have a funny feeling they won't let us talk them out of there, though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What if the cake is a lie?  Also do you really want to follow this guy back "
"to his house?  We both know that's not tomato sauce on his apron.  Don't eat "
"anything he cooks.\"  He shrugs, giving a nonplussed look.  \"Still, we've "
"committed actual murder for him multiple times now, so I guess I'm being a "
"bit of a hypocrite.  Let's party."
msgstr ""
"¿Y si el pastel es una mentira? ¿De verdad quieres seguir a este tipo hasta "
"su casa? Los dos sabemos que eso que tiene en el delantal no es salsa de "
"tomate. No comas nada de lo que cocine. Él se encoge de hombros, con "
"expresión perpleja. «Aun así, ya hemos cometido varios asesinatos por él, así "
"que supongo que estoy siendo un poco hipócrita. Vamos a divertirnos."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You didn't have fun?  I think this whole adventure has been a…"
msgstr "¿No te lo has pasado bien? Creo que toda esta aventura ha sido una..."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think it's worth it all, for the cake.  I'd like your opinion on something "
"else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Creo que vale la pena por el pastel. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión "
"sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"…SLICE!\"  Liam shouts along with you, then gives you a leaping high five "
"before dissolving into belly laughter.  \"OK fine, that makes all the murder "
"and arson worth it, you mad bastard."
msgstr ""
"... ¡CORTAR! —grita Liam junto contigo, y luego te da un choque de manos en "
"el aire antes de echarse a reír a carcajadas—. Vale, está bien, eso hace que "
"todos los asesinatos y los incendios provocados hayan valido la pena, maldito "
"loco."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That, and the cake.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Eso, y la tarta. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I feel like at some point we must have switched to playing Stardew Valley, "
"and I'm not quite sure when that happened.\"  He scratches his head.  \"Oh "
"well, let's just be sure to wear gumboots."
msgstr ""
"Siento que en algún momento debimos haber cambiado a jugar Stardew Valley, y "
"no estoy muy seguro de cuándo ocurrió eso. Se rasca la cabeza. Bueno, "
"asegurémonos de llevar botas de goma."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "And aprons.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Y delantales. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"BUGHUNT!\"  Liam raises his arms over his head and grins.  \"BUUUG HUUUNT!\"  "
"He mimes stomping on ants.  \"I'm doing my part!"
msgstr ""
"¡BUGHUNT! Liam levanta los brazos por encima de la cabeza y sonríe. «¡BUUUG "
"HUUUNT!». Imita pisotear hormigas. «¡Estoy haciendo mi parte!»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I did actually want your opinion on something though."
msgstr "De hecho, quería saber tu opinión sobre algo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's all good, I never minded doing deliveries, especially with a friend for "
"company.  I guess we could try to find lumber in a lumberyard, right?  "
"Probably not a lot of zombies hanging out in lumber yards.  Or maybe we could "
"find an old barn and knock it down and take all the pieces.\"  He laughs.  "
"\"Or saw it ourselves from scratch, if you're feeling like a mad lad.  Make "
"sure we've got a vehicle that can fit it though, that much lumber ain't gonna "
"fit in a hatchback."
msgstr ""
"No hay problema, nunca me ha importado hacer entregas, sobre todo si me "
"acompaña un amigo. Supongo que podríamos intentar encontrar madera en un "
"almacén, ¿no? Probablemente no haya muchos zombis merodeando por los "
"almacenes de madera. O tal vez podríamos encontrar un granero viejo, "
"derribarlo y llevarnos todos los trozos. Se ríe. «O serrarla nosotros mismos "
"desde cero, si te sientes con ganas. Pero asegúrate de que tenemos un "
"vehículo en el que quepa, porque tanta madera no va a caber en un hatchback."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "En realidad, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Something, something, wood pun, something something.  This is starting to "
"feel like Settlers of Catan, think they'll give us some sheep in return?"
msgstr ""
"Algo, algo, juego de palabras con madera, algo, algo. Esto empieza a "
"parecerse a Los colonos de Catán, ¿crees que nos darán algunas ovejas a "
"cambio?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Six ropes?  I find it hard to believe these guys can't just get 'em "
"themselves, but, uh, OK I guess.  Maybe we could take some old seatbelts and "
"tie them together, or something.  It shouldn't be hard to find a few ropes "
"laying around."
msgstr ""
"¿Seis cuerdas? Me cuesta creer que estos chicos no puedan conseguirlas por sí "
"mismos, pero bueno, supongo que vale. Quizás podríamos coger unos cinturones "
"de seguridad viejos y atarlos juntos, o algo así. No debería ser difícil "
"encontrar unas cuantas cuerdas por ahí tiradas."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay, wait, what?  One wood saw?  Why are you agreeing to this?  I like "
"deliveries as much as the next guy, but it's a *single wood saw*.  It's "
"starting to feel like you'll just agree to do anything anyone asks.\"  He "
"sighs.  \"No worries though I guess.  One time I delivered a single cold soda "
"to a guy living way out in the back woods.  Cost him seventy bucks.  People "
"are weird."
msgstr ""
"Vale, espera, ¿qué? ¿Una sierra para madera? ¿Por qué aceptas esto? Me gustan "
"las entregas tanto como a cualquiera, pero es una sola sierra para madera. "
"Empiezo a tener la sensación de que aceptas cualquier cosa que te pidan. "
"Suspira. «Pero no te preocupes. Una vez le llevé un refresco frío a un tipo "
"que vivía en medio del bosque. Le costó setenta dólares. La gente es rara."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "A shovel?"
msgstr "¿Una pala?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, a shovel."
msgstr "Sí, una pala."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "A shovel."
msgstr "Una pala."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/npcs/dialogue/generic_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's right."
msgstr "Así es."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're not joking."
msgstr "No estás bromeando."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*stares at you for a few seconds.  \"At the shovel store, I guess.\""
msgstr "*Te mira fijamente durante unos segundos. «En la tienda de palas, supongo»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What now, a vegetable peele… oh, a smoker?  That's actually kinda legit I "
"guess.  Maybe we should hunt through peoples' backyards.  We could jump over "
"fences like in Shaun of the Dead!"
msgstr ""
"¿Ahora qué, un pelador de verduras... oh, un fumador? En realidad, eso tiene "
"sentido, supongo. Quizás deberíamos buscar en los patios traseros de la "
"gente. ¡Podríamos saltar las vallas como en Shaun of the Dead!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm not a great expert on guns, to be honest.  I know how to shoot a bit, but "
"my focus was always on archery when I was a kid.  That sounds like a pretty "
"rare gun though, I think maybe we should see if we can find some old "
"collector rather than trying to raid a gun store?  Just a guess."
msgstr ""
"Para ser sincero, no soy un gran experto en armas. Sé disparar un poco, pero "
"cuando era niño siempre me centré en el tiro con arco. Sin embargo, parece "
"que se trata de un arma bastante rara, así que quizá deberíamos intentar "
"encontrar algún coleccionista antiguo en lugar de asaltar una armería. Es "
"solo una idea."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nah, you got it.  This is the sort of job that never, ever went wrong, "
"certainly not in any one of a thousand TV tropes.  Let's go find an unknown "
"old man in a secluded cabin."
msgstr ""
"No, lo has entendido. Este es el tipo de trabajo que nunca, jamás salió mal, "
"y desde luego no en ninguno de los miles de tópicos televisivos. Vamos a "
"buscar a un anciano desconocido en una cabaña aislada."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Glad we're on the same page.  I'd like your opinion on something else, "
"actually."
msgstr ""
"Me alegro de que estemos de acuerdo. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión "
"sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hell yeah I am.  This guy seems nice.  Bunnies are cute.  This is the sort of "
"job I like, let's find him some logs.  We should be able to just hunt around "
"the woods for 'em, right?  Might need a hatchet or a saw."
msgstr ""
"Claro que sí. Este tipo parece simpático. Los conejos son monos. Este es el "
"tipo de trabajo que me gusta, vamos a buscarle unos troncos. Podremos "
"encontrarlos cazando por el bosque, ¿no? Quizás necesitemos un hacha o una "
"sierra."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It sure does!  Is it blackberry season though?  I guess if they're not ripe, "
"we could check around abandoned kitchens and fridges, see if we can find some "
"that are still intact."
msgstr ""
"¡Claro que sí! ¿Pero es temporada de moras? Supongo que si no están maduras, "
"podríamos buscar en cocinas y neveras abandonadas, a ver si encontramos "
"algunas que estén intactas."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nah.  Lapin's sweet.  I wanna smoke a joint with the bunny man.  If you ever "
"turn into a zombie I'm gonna come back here and settle down as an assistant "
"bunny tamer.  Hope you don't mind."
msgstr ""
"No. Lapin es un encanto. Quiero fumarme un porro con el hombre conejo. Si "
"alguna vez te conviertes en zombi, volveré aquí y me instalaré como asistente "
"de domador de conejos. Espero que no te importe."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No hard feelings.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"No hay resentimientos. De hecho, me gustaría conocer tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"An anvil?  Where do you come up with this stuff?  Yeah, I met this guy, "
"Wile-E Coyote, he had a bunch of 'em."
msgstr ""
"¿Un yunque? ¿De dónde sacas estas cosas? Sí, conocí a un tipo, el Coyote, que "
"tenía un montón."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll track him down.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Lo localizaré. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm worried for these guys.  My gut tells me they're dealing with something "
"really dangerous.  Let's make sure we're packing heat, you know?"
msgstr ""
"Estoy preocupado por estos chicos. Mi instinto me dice que están lidiando con "
"algo realmente peligroso. Asegurémonos de llevar armas, ¿vale?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Roger that.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Entendido. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You can say that again.  This is some serious shit, my friend.  I know we've "
"been through a lot, but this might be the big one.  We need to make sure "
"we're ready for anything before we even consider going in there."
msgstr ""
"Ya lo puedes decir. Esto es algo muy serio, amigo mío. Sé que hemos pasado "
"por muchas cosas, pero esto podría ser lo más importante. Tenemos que "
"asegurarnos de que estamos preparados para cualquier cosa antes de siquiera "
"plantearnos entrar ahí."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Roger that.  I'd like your opinion on something else, first."
msgstr "Entendido. Primero me gustaría conocer tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"After the shit these poor bastards have gone through, picking some dandelions "
"for them seems kind of anticlimactic.  Still, I am a big fan of dandelion "
"wine."
msgstr ""
"Después de todo lo que han pasado estos pobres desgraciados, recogerles unos "
"dientes de león me parece un poco decepcionante. Aun así, soy un gran fan del "
"vino de diente de león."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Picking flowers in a field seems okay to me.  I don't mind helping Claire "
"out, she's a nice enough person.  Gotta say though, I get a bit of a weird "
"vibe off these guys.  They're so… I don't know.  It's like we walked into a "
"Norman Rockwell painting in the middle of the end of the world."
msgstr ""
"Recoger flores en un campo me parece bien. No me importa ayudar a Claire, es "
"una persona muy agradable. Aunque tengo que decir que estos chicos me dan un "
"poco de mala espina. Son tan... No sé. Es como si hubiéramos entrado en un "
"cuadro de Norman Rockwell en medio del fin del mundo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Bee bombs!  Kaboom!\"  He mimes an explosion with his hands.  \"Seriously "
"though it's a very versatile plant, we should get some seeds for ourselves."
msgstr ""
"¡Bombas de abejas! ¡Kaboom!». Imita una explosión con las manos. «En serio, "
"es una planta muy versátil, deberíamos conseguir algunas semillas para "
"nosotros."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see what I can do.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Veré qué puedo hacer. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs.  \"I was going to make a joke about herding cats, but yours is "
"better.  I was always more of a dog man myself, I don't know anything about "
"catching a feral cat.  Maybe we open a can of tuna?  Or is that a cliché?\""
msgstr ""
"*risas. «Iba a hacer una broma sobre pastorear gatos, pero la tuya es mejor. "
"Yo siempre he sido más de perros, no sé nada sobre cómo atrapar a un gato "
"salvaje. ¿Quizás abrimos una lata de atún? ¿O eso es un cliché?»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm still… 'feline' it out myself.  I'd like your opinion on something else, "
"actually."
msgstr ""
"Todavía estoy... «felino» por mí mismo. Me gustaría tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa, en realidad."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Even if we work together it's gonna take a while to just find enough good "
"rocks lying around.  We'll probably want to get a shovel and dig around a bit "
"maybe?  Or break up bigger ones with a sledge.  I'm impressed at these guys, "
"keeping going after everything that's happened."
msgstr ""
"Aunque trabajemos juntos, nos llevará un tiempo encontrar suficientes piedras "
"buenas por ahí. ¿Quizás deberíamos conseguir una pala y cavar un poco? O "
"romper las más grandes con un mazo. Me impresiona que estos chicos sigan "
"adelante después de todo lo que ha pasado."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Even if we work together it's gonna take a while to just find enough good "
"rocks lying around.  We'll probably want to get a shovel and dig around a bit "
"maybe?  Or break up bigger ones with a sledge.  Something about this stuff "
"feels weird to me though.  Too pastoral for the apocalypse."
msgstr ""
"Aunque trabajemos juntos, nos llevará un tiempo encontrar suficientes piedras "
"buenas por ahí. ¿Quizás deberíamos conseguir una pala y cavar un poco? O "
"romper las más grandes con un mazo. Sin embargo, hay algo en todo esto que me "
"parece extraño. Demasiado bucólico para el apocalipsis."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I hear you.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Sí, te entiendo. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Gathering sand sounds, honestly, sort of pleasant.  Like, meditative, you "
"know?  Maybe we find some batteries and get a bit of music going, smoke a "
"joint if you're so inclined, then fill some buckets of sand for Eddie to do "
"whatever the hell he's doing with it.  No zombies, no gunfire, just sand."
msgstr ""
"Recoger arena suena, sinceramente, bastante agradable. Como meditativo, "
"¿sabes? Quizás encontremos unas pilas y pongamos un poco de música, fumemos "
"un porro si te apetece, y luego llenemos unos cubos de arena para que Eddie "
"haga lo que sea que esté haciendo con ella. Sin zombis, sin disparos, solo "
"arena."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I believe he's making bricks.  I'd like your opinion on something else, "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Creo que está haciendo ladrillos. Sin embargo, me gustaría saber tu opinión "
"sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I like a good, well defined physical job.  Let's go to the riverside!  I feel "
"like the odds of getting badly injured while gathering clay are sort of low.  "
"Make sure to get some music going though, right?  Maybe bring some "
"refreshments?  And shovels."
msgstr ""
"Me gusta el trabajo físico, bien definido. ¡Vamos a la orilla del río! Creo "
"que las probabilidades de sufrir lesiones graves mientras recogemos arcilla "
"son bastante bajas. Pero hay que llevar música, ¿no? ¿Y quizá algo para "
"picar? Y palas."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You do make it sound good.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Lo haces sonar muy bien. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Big jars aren't really that uncommon.  Lots of people got super into canning "
"in the last few months before shit really hit the fan, like they did with "
"toilet paper a few years back.  Maybe a bit more reasonable, I guess, though "
"learning how to pickle meat probably didn't save anyone from zombies.  I bet "
"we can track down a few just by raiding houses, and if they're not empty "
"we'll just have to eat what's inside or something."
msgstr ""
"Los tarros grandes no son tan raros. Mucha gente se aficionó a hacer "
"conservas en los últimos meses antes de que todo se fuera al garete, igual "
"que hicieron con el papel higiénico hace unos años. Quizás sea algo más "
"razonable, supongo, aunque aprender a encurtir carne probablemente no salvó a "
"nadie de los zombis. Apuesto a que podemos encontrar algunos simplemente "
"registrando casas, y si no están vacías, tendremos que comer lo que haya "
"dentro o algo así."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Do you need a snack, man?  Never mind.  I'd like your opinion on something "
"else, actually."
msgstr ""
"¿Quieres algo para picar, tío? No importa. En realidad, me gustaría saber tu "
"opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm sort of surprised they don't have plenty of wheat seeds of their own,\" "
"Liam shrugs.  \"What the hell do I know about farming though?  Nothing, "
"that's what.  Including having no idea about where to find wheat seeds, sorry "
"man.  I would have said 'on a farm' but we're on one and they're asking us, "
"so I just don't know what to think anymore.  My life is a shambles."
msgstr ""
"Me sorprende un poco que no tengan muchas semillas de trigo propias —Liam se "
"encoge de hombros—. Pero, ¿qué demonios sé yo de agricultura? Nada, eso es lo "
"que sé. Ni siquiera tengo ni idea de dónde encontrar semillas de trigo, lo "
"siento, tío. Habría dicho «en una granja», pero estamos en una y nos lo están "
"preguntando a nosotros, así que ya no sé qué pensar. Mi vida es un desastre."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fair enough.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Me parece justo. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know, it's a harmful stereotype that wolves are dangerous to humans.  Of "
"course I'm not afraid.\"  He smirks at you, then grins.  \"Except let's be "
"honest, this is probably going to be a giant monster zombie wolf or "
"something, right?  Let's go take the bastard down."
msgstr ""
"Sabes, es un estereotipo dañino que los lobos sean peligrosos para los "
"humanos. Por supuesto que no tengo miedo». Te sonríe con aire burlón y luego "
"sonríe abiertamente. «Pero seamos sinceros, probablemente se trate de un lobo "
"zombi gigante o algo así, ¿no? Vamos a acabar con ese cabrón."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's the spirit.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Así se habla. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fast, unidentified monsters are killing the local wildlife, and we're going "
"to get 'em.\"  He looks thoughtful.  \"I'm pretty sure this was an episode of "
"the X-Files.  Or like, several episodes?  As long as we're Scully and Mulder "
"we'll be fine, but if we're the local cops coming in to investigate, we're "
"*toast*.  Just in case, let's make sure we've got our good gear."
msgstr ""
"Monstruos rápidos y no identificados están matando a la fauna local, y vamos "
"a atraparlos». Parece pensativo. «Estoy bastante seguro de que esto era un "
"episodio de Expediente X. ¿O eran varios episodios? Mientras seamos Scully y "
"Mulder, no habrá problema, pero si somos los policías locales que vienen a "
"investigar, estamos perdidos. Por si acaso, asegurémonos de llevar nuestro "
"mejor equipo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Will do, Scully.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Lo haré, Scully. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Funny you should ask, yeah I have.  My dad borrowed it from the library once "
"and I leafed through it.  So I guess we could try looking at a library?  I "
"got no better ideas, I was like thirteen, I don't remember what was in the "
"thing, and he got all pissy at me for checking it out anyway."
msgstr ""
"Es curioso que lo preguntes, sí, lo he leído. Mi padre lo sacó una vez de la "
"biblioteca y yo lo hojeé. Así que supongo que podríamos intentar buscarlo en "
"una biblioteca. No se me ocurre nada mejor, tenía como trece años, no "
"recuerdo qué ponía en él y él se enfadó mucho conmigo por echarle un vistazo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, yeah he does, because he's a man of discerning tastes.\"  Liam nods "
"approvingly.  \"Or because he wants something to prop his car up while he "
"changes the tire.  It's a big book, is what I'm saying.  We should make sure "
"we've got a copy for ourselves though, it's one of the prepper bibles."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, sí, lo hace, porque es un hombre de gustos exigentes». Liam asiente "
"con la cabeza en señal de aprobación. «O porque quiere algo con lo que "
"sostener su coche mientras cambia la rueda. Es un libro grande, eso es lo que "
"digo. Deberíamos asegurarnos de tener una copia para nosotros, es una de las "
"biblias de los preppers."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great info, thanks.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Muy buena información, gracias. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre "
"otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*leans in close, speaking softly.  \"I do not say this lightly: this "
"motherfucker has *seen some shit*.  Look at that thousand-yard-stare.  We did "
"a good thing getting him out, but I don't know if he's ever really gonna be "
"*out*, you know?\""
msgstr ""
"*Se inclina hacia él y le habla en voz baja—. No lo digo a la ligera: este "
"hijo de puta ha *visto cosas muy duras*. Fíjate en esa mirada perdida. "
"Hicimos bien en sacarlo de allí, pero no sé si alguna vez estará realmente "
"*fuera*, ¿sabes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you think we can do anything for him?"
msgstr "¿Crees que podemos hacer algo por él?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "He'll suck it up.  We've all been through shit."
msgstr "Lo aguantará. Todos hemos pasado por momentos difíciles."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Scary stuff.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Da miedo. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We can get him home in one piece.  Get him back to his people.  I'd offer him "
"a drink or a toke, but I think they're like, Amish or something.  After that, "
"our best bet is to make ourselves scarce, to him we're always gonna be the "
"people he met in the tower.  He won't wanna be reminded of that."
msgstr ""
"Podemos llevarlo a casa sano y salvo. Devolverlo a su gente. Le ofrecería una "
"copa o un porro, pero creo que son como los amish o algo así. Después de eso, "
"lo mejor que podemos hacer es desaparecer, para él siempre seremos las "
"personas que conoció en la torre. No querrá que se lo recuerden."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do you know so much about this?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sabes tanto sobre esto?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks abruptly uncomfortable.  \"You know a bit about me and my dad, right?  "
"I went to counseling for a few years after I got out.  Since what went down "
"with Chris, I've been thinking about it more too.\"  He shakes his head.  "
"\"We could all use a decent counsellor, honestly.  Even before the world "
"ended.\""
msgstr ""
"*Parece repentinamente incómodo. «Sabes algo sobre mí y mi padre, ¿verdad? "
"Fui a terapia durante unos años después de salir. Desde lo que pasó con "
"Chris, también he estado pensando más en ello». Niega con la cabeza. «A todos "
"nos vendría bien un buen terapeuta, sinceramente. Incluso antes de que se "
"acabara el mundo»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, man.  You have layers.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, tío. Tienes muchas facetas. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra "
"cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I guess we have.\"  Liam looks off into the distance for a moment.  "
"\"We sure fuckin' have."
msgstr "Sí, supongo que sí. Liam mira a lo lejos por un momento. Claro que sí, joder."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Damn straight.  I'd like your opinion on something else."
msgstr "Por supuesto. Me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*rubs his chin.  \"Mmmaaaybe?  What kind of chef?  I worked as a dishwasher "
"in a fancy place for a couple months.  If they're a line chef, then yes.  "
"Sous-chef or above?  Leave 'em for the zombies.  I hated that job.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Duly noted.  I'd like your opinion on something else, though."
msgstr "Tomamos nota. Sin embargo, me gustaría conocer su opinión sobre otro asunto."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Seems like a good idea to me.  If they're alive, then we meet some new "
"people, that's always fun.\"  He hesitates.  \"Well, it used to always be "
"fun.  New people are a bit scarier these days.  But still, as a general rule, "
"I'm a fan.  Anyway, if they're not alive, then we clear 'em out and we have a "
"farm of our very own.  It's win-win, as long as none of us gets devoured by "
"an undead menace."
msgstr ""
"Me parece una buena idea. Si están vivos, conoceremos gente nueva, y eso "
"siempre es divertido. Duda. Bueno, antes siempre era divertido. Hoy en día, "
"la gente nueva da un poco más de miedo. Pero, en general, me gusta. De todos "
"modos, si no están vivos, los eliminamos y tendremos nuestra propia granja. "
"Todos salimos ganando, siempre y cuando ninguno de nosotros sea devorado por "
"una amenaza no muerta."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well summarized.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Bien resumido. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We could if you want.  I got complex feelings about prepper cabins in the "
"woods, obviously.  As far as loot goes though, they're pretty top tier, and "
"low-risk.  Maybe we'll find a nice bow.  Or like, guns or whatever.  Or a bow!"
msgstr ""
"Podríamos hacerlo si quieres. Obviamente, tengo sentimientos encontrados "
"sobre las cabañas de supervivencia en el bosque. Sin embargo, en lo que "
"respecta al botín, son de primera categoría y de bajo riesgo. Quizás "
"encontremos un buen arco. O armas de fuego o algo así. ¡O un arco!"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You and your death springs.  I'd like your opinion on something else, "
"actually."
msgstr ""
"Tú y tus muelles de muerte. En realidad, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre "
"otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fuck yeah we should.  Usually I'd be all, 'be careful my friend, preppers "
"leave traps 'n shit', but in this case we have said prepper's word on the "
"matter.  We could be running our operation from a cozy, well protected "
"bunker!  What are we waiting for?"
msgstr ""
"Claro que sí, deberíamos hacerlo. Normalmente diría: «Ten cuidado, amigo, los "
"preppers dejan trampas y cosas así», pero en este caso tenemos la palabra del "
"prepper en cuestión. ¡Podríamos llevar a cabo nuestra operación desde un "
"búnker acogedor y bien protegido! ¿A qué esperamos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the enthusiasm.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr ""
"Gracias por el entusiasmo. En realidad, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre "
"otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Normally I'd say something about needing to be careful, blah blah, and that's "
"all true, but we're doing this for a friend, so I'm way more keen.  Let's "
"help out our new pal.  The three of us can handle this, right?"
msgstr ""
"Normalmente diría algo sobre la necesidad de tener cuidado, bla, bla, bla, y "
"todo eso es cierto, pero lo hacemos por un amigo, así que estoy mucho más "
"motivado. Ayudemos a nuestro nuevo amigo. Entre los tres podemos con esto, "
"¿no?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right on.  I'd like your opinion on something else, actually."
msgstr "Muy bien. De hecho, me gustaría saber tu opinión sobre otra cosa."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I want to talk about something a bit more fundamental now."
msgstr "Ahora quiero hablar de algo un poco más fundamental."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can we chat about something else?"
msgstr "¿Podemos hablar de otra cosa?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid " *pshhhttt* This is big turtle, I read you loud and clear, red burrito."
msgstr "*pshhhttt* Aquí la tortuga grande, te recibo alto y claro, burrito rojo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, here we are.  What's up?"
msgstr "Bueno, aquí estamos. ¿Qué tal?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Big turtle?  Red burrito?  Seriously?"
msgstr "¿Una tortuga grande? ¿Un burrito rojo? ¿En serio?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*shrugs.  \"Not my favorite job, but sure.  I'll keep an eye out.\""
msgstr "*Se encoge de hombros—. No es mi trabajo favorito, pero vale. Estaré atento."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As you know, I am experienced in practically every low-wage job on the "
"Eastern seaboard, and I'm probably a regional leading expert on video games.  "
"My dad made me learn archery and I kinda kept it up.  What else is there?"
msgstr ""
"Como sabes, tengo experiencia en prácticamente todos los trabajos mal pagados "
"de la costa este, y probablemente soy el mayor experto regional en "
"videojuegos. Mi padre me hizo aprender tiro con arco y más o menos lo seguí "
"practicando. ¿Qué más hay?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sounds weird calling it \"orders\", I'm your friend, not your minion.  No "
"worries though, what up?"
msgstr ""
"Suena raro llamarlo «órdenes», soy tu amigo, no tu subordinado. Pero no te "
"preocupes, ¿qué pasa?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, what do you want?"
msgstr "Claro, ¿qué quieres?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I mean, I'm not sure what I can teach you about, but okay."
msgstr "Es decir, no estoy seguro de qué puedo enseñarte, pero está bien."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't sell yourself short, Liam.  I just wanted to know about…"
msgstr "No te subestimes, Liam. Solo quería saber sobre..."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "A… seminar?  About what, how not to burn yourself on the frier at Foodplace?"
msgstr "¿Un seminario? ¿Sobre qué, cómo no quemarse con la freidora en Foodplace?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Y'know, you have more useful skills than you think."
msgstr "Sabes, tienes más habilidades útiles de las que crees."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Roger that red burrito, that's a ten-forward on the callsigns.  Glad you like "
"'em."
msgstr ""
"Entendido, burrito rojo, eso es un diez adelante en los indicativos. Me "
"alegro de que te gusten."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're weird, my friend.  Red burrito, out."
msgstr "Eres raro, amigo mío. Red Burrito, fuera."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Years ago, you and your old group of friends made a pact.  It seemed like a "
"joke at the time: if the world ended, you'd all meet up at Liam's cabin, if "
"you could, and work together to help each other out.  Now, the unthinkable "
"has happened, and somehow you've made it out in one piece.  It's been years "
"since you saw those friends, though you've kept a little bit in touch on "
"social media, and you can only hope that the others perhaps took the idea "
"seriously.  Even if they did, it would be a hard trip.  The roads were "
"blocked off by military forces trying to prevent the riots from spreading, "
"and you had to make the last part of the journey on foot.\n"
"\n"
"As the morning light breaks into day, you've reached Liam's cabin, a "
"ramshackle building in the woods outside <city>.  You can see Liam's car in "
"front, looking a bit more run down since you last saw him a few years ago.  "
"You feel a swell of relief: at least Liam seems to have made it!  As you "
"approach the door, you hear a shout of terror from inside, and then the "
"unmistakable sound of a gunshot.  Were you a moment too late?"
msgstr ""
"Hace años, tú y tu antiguo grupo de amigos hicisteis un pacto. En aquel "
"momento parecía una broma: si el mundo se acababa, os reuniríais todos en la "
"cabaña de Liam, si podías, y colaboraríais para ayudarse mutuamente. Ahora, "
"lo impensable ha sucedido y, de alguna manera, has salido ileso. Han pasado "
"años desde que viste a esos amigos, aunque has mantenido un poco el contacto "
"a través de las redes sociales, y solo puedes esperar que los demás se "
"tomaran en serio la idea. Incluso si lo hicieron, sería un viaje difícil. Las "
"carreteras estaban bloqueadas por las fuerzas militares que intentaban evitar "
"que se extendieran los disturbios, y tuviste que hacer la última parte del "
"viaje a pie.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando la luz de la mañana da paso al día, llegas a la cabaña de Liam, un "
"edificio destartalado en el bosque a las afueras de <city>. Puedes ver el "
"coche de Liam delante, con un aspecto un poco más deteriorado desde la última "
"vez que lo viste hace unos años. Sientes una oleada de alivio: ¡al menos Liam "
"parece haberlo conseguido! Al acercarte a la puerta, oyes un grito de terror "
"desde el interior y, a continuación, el inconfundible sonido de un disparo. "
"¿Has llegado un momento demasiado tarde?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd better get in there and check it out."
msgstr "Será mejor que vaya allí y lo compruebe."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Special NPC you can only meet through the 'start with a friend' scenario.
#. Will need his own class and items before completing this.
msgid "Liam"
msgstr "Liam"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "expert in entry level jobs"
msgstr "Experto en puestos de trabajo de nivel inicial."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Job description of "expert in entry level jobs" NPC class
msgid "It's you and me in this together, buddy."
msgstr "Estamos juntos en esto, amigo."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*, your old friend, stares at you with blank, confused eyes.  He is standing "
"over a freshly mangled corpse, a smoking shotgun at his feet.  \"Holy shit "
"dude.\"  He blinks.  \"Is this about Chris?  If you're here to kill me, just "
"get it over with man.  I don't know what the fuck is happening but I can't "
"take you out too.\""
msgstr ""
"*, tu viejo amigo, te mira con ojos vacíos y confundidos. Está parado sobre "
"un cadáver recién destrozado, una escopeta humeante a sus pies. \"Joder "
"tío.\" Parpadea. \"¿Esto es por Chris? Si estás aquí para matarme, hazlo de "
"una vez. No sé qué cojones está pasando, pero no puedo acabar contigo "
"también.\""

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Get ahold of yourself, man.  What's happening?  Chris?"
msgstr "Contrólate, tío. ¿Qué pasa? ¿Chris?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gestures at the body.  \"Chris.  You know Chris, you've known Chris for "
"years.  We all agreed to meet up here if shit got bad, remember?  We got here "
"around the same time, set up a little camp.  Something seemed really off "
"since we arrived though, Chris kept going on and on about how the food wasn't "
"good enough.\"  He shifts his gaze back to you, eyes red.  \"We got plenty of "
"food!  I tried to calm him down but just now the fucker came running in with "
"an axe, tried to take my head off!  I… I…\" Liam gestures again to the "
"corpse.  \"Then you came in.  Do you got anything to do with this?\""
msgstr ""
"*Señala el cadáver. «Chris. Conoces a Chris, lo conoces desde hace años. "
"Todos acordamos reunirnos aquí si las cosas se ponían feas, ¿recuerdas? "
"Llegamos más o menos a la misma hora y montamos un pequeño campamento. Sin "
"embargo, desde que llegamos, algo parecía estar muy mal. Chris no paraba de "
"quejarse de que la comida no era lo suficientemente buena». Vuelve a mirarte, "
"con los ojos enrojecidos. «¡Tenemos comida de sobra! Intenté calmarlo, pero "
"hace un momento el cabrón entró corriendo con un hacha e intentó cortarme la "
"cabeza. Yo... yo...». Liam vuelve a señalar el cadáver. «Entonces entraste "
"tú. ¿Tienes algo que ver con esto?»."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I heard gunshots, so I came in to see what's up.  I was just on my way here "
"to see if you'd made it."
msgstr ""
"Oí disparos, así que vine a ver qué pasaba. Iba de camino aquí para ver si lo "
"habías conseguido."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, shit.  I'm guessing my story sounds like a lot of bullshit then.\"  "
"Liam sags into the sofa behind him, wiping his eyes with his sleeve.  \"What "
"the hell are we gonna do?  Holy shit."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, mierda. Supongo que mi historia suena a mentira entonces. Liam se "
"desploma en el sofá detrás de él, secándose los ojos con la manga. ¿Qué "
"diablos vamos a hacer? Mierda."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I believe you.  People have been acting crazy for weeks, it must have got "
"Chris too.  Come on.  We're in this together."
msgstr ""
"Te creo. La gente lleva semanas comportándose como locos, seguro que Chris "
"también se ha contagiado. Vamos. Estamos juntos en esto."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Pull yourself together.  You did what you had to.  The shit has hit the fan, "
"no time for moping around."
msgstr ""
"Recompónete. Hiciste lo que tenías que hacer. La mierda ha salido a la luz, "
"no hay tiempo para lamentarse."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks.  It's good to hear that.  Look, I'm sure I should be questioning you "
"and making sure you're not gonna attack me with an axe or something, but I "
"just can't anymore.  Come on, let's get Chris out of here and then figure out "
"what to do next."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Me alegro de oírlo. Mira, estoy seguro de que debería interrogarte y "
"asegurarme de que no vas a atacarme con un hacha o algo así, pero ya no puedo "
"más. Vamos, saquemos a Chris de aquí y luego decidamos qué hacer."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure thing.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Por supuesto.  <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All right, yeah.  Fair call.  I'm just a bit shell shocked, but it's good to "
"see you.  Let's get Chris out of here and figure out what to do next"
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, sí. Es justo. Estoy un poco conmocionado, pero me alegro de "
"verte. Saquemos a Chris de aquí y pensemos qué hacemos ahora."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_starting_follower.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check to see if Liam is OK"
msgstr "Comprueba si Liam está bien"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid " *pshhhttt* Hey stinkyface.  It's your favorite mushroom girl.  Over."
msgstr "*pshhhttt* Hola, cara de apestoso. Soy tu chica seta favorita. Cambio."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I love just standing around, it's what I was made for."
msgstr "Me encanta estar quieto, es para lo que me hicieron. "

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My 'abilities'?  I can shapeshift, and teleport, but I can't do it on "
"command.  Also, I have unique powers of thyroid failure."
msgstr ""
"¿Mis \"habilidades\"? Puedo cambiar de forma y teletransportarme, pero no "
"puedo hacerlo a voluntad. Además, tengo un poder único de insuficiencia "
"tiroidea."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure.  Here we are, talking."
msgstr "Claro. Aquí estamos, hablando."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's your story, anyway?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es tu historia, de todos modos?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Seriously?  You figure you're the boss of me now?  Fine, whatever, what do "
"you want me to do."
msgstr ""
"¿En serio? ¿Crees que ahora eres mi jefe? Bien, como quieras, qué quieres que "
"haga."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, sure, why not.  I love hearing myself talk.  What did you want to know "
"about?"
msgstr "Sí, claro, por qué no. Me encanta oírme hablar. ¿Qué quieres saber de mí?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mean you'll talk about more than just mushrooms?  What've you got?"
msgstr "¿Quieres decir que hablarás de algo más que de setas? ¿Qué tienes?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What?  You're not content with me being a personal tutor, now you want to "
"start a post-apocalyptic university?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué? ¿No te conformas con que sea tutor personal, ahora quieres fundar una "
"universidad postapocalíptica?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Come on, you love hearing yourself talk."
msgstr "Vamos, te encanta oírte hablar."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You kind of already know, don't you?  I used to be a post-doc researcher in "
"mycology, then I wound up stuck in the lobby at that stupid refugee center, "
"then you came and yeeted us all out of there.  What more is there?"
msgstr ""
"Como que ya lo sabes, ¿no? Solía ser un investigador post-doctoral en "
"micología, luego terminé atrapado en el vestíbulo de ese estúpido centro de "
"refugiados, luego viniste y nos sacaste a todos de allí. ¿Qué más hay?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't remember, did you tell me how you wound up in that place?"
msgstr "No lo recuerdo, ¿me contaste cómo acabaste en ese lugar?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Pretty sure I did, but I do love hearing the sound of my own voice.  I got "
"evacuated on to the local concentration center, then picked up on a "
"repurposed school bus and dragged out to that shithole.  We heard the place "
"was getting more people than they could fit, and the few who'd got there "
"first had set up some sort of self-appointed processing lineup.  The chick "
"processing me to get in saw my Chinese name and conveniently 'lost' my "
"paperwork.  I was sent out to the lobby to wait for 'further processing', "
"while I watched busloads of people get processed and taken in.  By the time "
"they 'found' my paperwork, wouldn't you know it, the place was too full for "
"me.  They oh-so-kindly let me camp out in the front since I'd been on one of "
"the first buses."
msgstr ""
"Seguro que sí, pero me encanta oír el sonido de mi propia voz. Me evacuaron "
"al centro de contención local, luego me recogieron en un autobús escolar "
"reutilizado y me arrastraron hasta aquel agujero de mierda. Oímos que el "
"lugar estaba recibiendo más gente de la que cabía, y los pocos que habían "
"llegado primero habían establecido una especie de fila de procesamiento "
"autoproclamada. La chica que me procesó vio mi nombre chino y \"perdió\" mi "
"documentación. Me enviaron al vestíbulo para que esperara \"más trámites\", "
"mientras veía cómo procesaban e introducían a autobuses llenos de gente. "
"Cuando \"encontraron\" mis papeles, el lugar estaba demasiado lleno para mí. "
"Muy amablemente, me dejaron acampar en la parte delantera, ya que había "
"estado en uno de los primeros autobuses."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can read the newspapers as well as anyone, I know how people who look like "
"me get smeared.  My grandparents were from China.  That means I'm obviously "
"personally responsible for all this.  I don't know any other reason they let "
"hundreds of other educated people in and left me sitting out there to rot."
msgstr ""
"Puedo leer los periódicos tan bien como cualquiera, sé cómo se difama a la "
"gente que se parece a mí. Mis abuelos eran de China. Eso significa que "
"obviamente soy personalmente responsable de todo esto. No conozco otra razón "
"por la que hayan dejado entrar a cientos de otras personas con educación y a "
"mí me hayan dejado aquí sentado para que me pudra."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, before <the_cataclysm> I was working at a university bookstore, "
"remember?  But that was just an in-between after finishing my PhD, while I "
"looked for a post-doc placement I was interested in.  Which, I suppose, I've "
"got now?  You didn't recruit my for my fragile body, intractable obesity, or "
"sunny disposition."
msgstr ""
"Antes d<the_cataclysm> trabajaba en una librería universitaria, ¿recuerdas? "
"Pero eso fue sólo una etapa intermedia después de terminar el doctorado, "
"mientras buscaba un puesto de posdoctorado que me interesara. ¿Qué, supongo, "
"ahora tengo? No me contrataste por mi cuerpo frágil, mi obesidad intratable o "
"mi carácter alegre."

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do you know I didn't recruit you for your sass, though?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sabes que no te recluté por tu impertinencia?"

#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gives a single rough laugh.  \"Fair call, sass like mine is what will get us "
"through these trying times.\""
msgstr ""
"*pone una risa áspera. \"Claro que sí, la insolencia es lo que nos hará "
"superar estos tiempos difíciles\"."

