msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/laser.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/laser.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Makeshift Scrambler Rifle"
msgid_plural "Makeshift Scrambler Rifles"
msgstr[0] "Rifle De Interferencias Improvisado"
msgstr[1] "Rifles De Interferencias Improvisados"
msgstr[2] "Rifles De Interferencias Improvisados"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/laser.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/laser.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Makeshift Scrambler Rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Makeshift Scrambler Rifle"
msgid ""
"This 'energy weapon' appears to be haphazardly jury-rigged from commercially "
"available electronics.  It has a radar dish placed where a barrel would be, "
"and the frame of a weapon is covered in a mesh of wiring.  Despite its "
"appearance, this weapon can temporarily stun robots if you manage to hit "
"their sensors."
msgstr ""
"Esta \"arma de energía\" parece haber sido improvisada a partir de "
"componentes electrónicos disponibles en el mercado. Tiene una antena "
"parabólica colocada donde estaría un cañón, y el armazón del arma está "
"cubierto por una malla de cables. A pesar de su apariencia, esta arma puede "
"aturdir temporalmente a los robots si consigues alcanzar sus sensores."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/laser.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/laser.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "xm34 EMP projector"
msgid_plural "xm34 EMP projectors"
msgstr[0] "proyector PEM xm34"
msgstr[1] "proyectores PEM xm34"
msgstr[2] "proyectores PEM xm34"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/mining_rod.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/mining_rod.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "mining rod launcher"
msgid_plural "mining rod launchers"
msgstr[0] "lanzador de varas de minería"
msgstr[1] "lanzadores de varas de minería"
msgstr[2] "lanzadores de varas de minería"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/mining_rod.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/mining_rod.json
#. ~ Description of gun "mining rod launcher"
#. ~ Description of "mining rod launcher"
msgid ""
"Based on an old TsKBEM design, this is a rail launcher used in mining "
"exploration.  The rod is fired into a rock face and a seismic mapper on the "
"launcher displays ore veins.  Not being designed for combat, it is difficult "
"to use without the augmented strength of an exosuit and the reloading process "
"is quite slow.  The barrel is covered in warning labels indemnifying the "
"manufacturer of any injuries caused by misuse."
msgstr ""
"Basado en un antiguo diseño de TsKBEM, este es un lanzador de barras "
"utilizado en la exploración minera. La barra se dispara contra una pared "
"rocosa y un mapeador sísmico situado en el lanzador muestra las vetas de "
"mineral. Al no estar diseñado para el combate, es difícil de usar sin la "
"fuerza aumentada de un exotraje y el proceso de recarga es bastante lento. El "
"cañón está cubierto de etiquetas de advertencia que eximen al fabricante de "
"cualquier daño causado por un uso indebido."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/needle.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/needle.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "GG-860 Wasp Rifle"
msgid_plural "GG-860 Wasp Rifles"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/needle.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/needle.json
#. ~ Description of gun "GG-860 Wasp Rifle"
#. ~ Description of "GG-860 Wasp Rifle"
msgid ""
"This light coilgun fires 3x35mm armor-piercing flechette.  Classified as a "
"support crew weapon that can be stashed in hidden lockers throughout the "
"floors of a ship.  Designed to be fired in short bursts, if the flechettes "
"pierce a ship's hull they leave tiny holes that are easily repaired."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/needle.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/needle.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistol"
msgid_plural "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistols"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/needle.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/needle.json
#. ~ Description of gun "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistol"
#. ~ Description of "3x35mm automatic 'Wandering Priest' coilpistol"
msgid ""
"An automatic coilgun made entirely of lightweight ceramics, with no moving "
"pieces and if loaded with splinter rounds almost entirely invisible on most "
"security scanners.  No one is sure who manufactures this assassin's tool, but "
"they randomly come onto the back room markets frequented by the unsavory."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Magnadrive 230K"
msgid_plural "Magnadrive 230K"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Magnadrive 230K"
#. ~ Description of "Magnadrive 230K"
msgid ""
"A heavy plasma railgun that easily defeats most forms of conventional armor "
"and flash-incinerates anything  behind it.  Its large size and liability to "
"overheat make it unsuitable for infantry use, but it is a common sight on "
"military vehicles and in the hands of power-armored troops, especially when "
"heavy armor is expected."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "PAM-41 2g"
msgid_plural "PAM-41 2gs"
msgstr[0] "PAM-41 2g"
msgstr[1] "PAM-41 2gs"
msgstr[2] "PAM-41 2gs"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Description of gun "PAM-41 2g"
#. ~ Description of "PAM-41 2g"
msgid ""
"A short and stubby 2 gram plasma railgun occasionally used by espatiers as a "
"hull breaching tool.  Like larger plasma weapons, it propels toroids of "
"plasma that detonate on contact, but its reduced size heavily hampers its "
"range and damage output.  Fired within an atmosphere, its very low range "
"makes it dangerous to shooter and target alike."
msgstr ""
"Un cañón de riel de plasma de 2 gramos, corto y rechoncho, utilizado "
"ocasionalmente por los espaciadores como herramienta para romper el casco. Al "
"igual que las armas de plasma más grandes, propulsa toroides de plasma que "
"detonan al contacto, pero su reducido tamaño dificulta en gran medida su "
"alcance y su producción de daños. Si se dispara dentro de una atmósfera, su "
"escaso alcance lo hace peligroso tanto para el tirador como para el objetivo."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "377-UASTA (weaponized)"
msgid_plural "377-UASTA (weaponized)"
msgstr[0] "377-UASTA (convertido en arma)"
msgstr[1] "377-UASTA- (convertido en arma)"
msgstr[2] "377-UASTA- (convertido en arma)"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Description of gun "377-UASTA (weaponized)"
#. ~ Description of "377-UASTA (weaponized)"
msgid ""
"A common modification for directed plasma torches that involves the "
"installation of oversize capacitor banks and judiciously bypassed safety "
"mechanisms, allowing them to function as a deadly if decidedly short-ranged "
"weapons.  In most cases, the resulting \"gun\" can still perform its original "
"metalworking functions, albeit at a much lower efficiency.\n"
"\n"
"Unlike purposefully made plasma weapons, the propelled plasma bottle won't "
"cause a considerable explosion upon contact, allowing for relatively safe "
"operation within enclosed spaces."
msgstr ""
"Una modificación común de los sopletes de plasma dirigido que implica la "
"instalación de baterías de condensadores sobredimensionadas y mecanismos de "
"seguridad cuidadosamente anulados, lo que les permite funcionar como armas "
"mortales aunque de corto alcance. En la mayoría de los casos, el \"arma\" "
"resultante puede seguir desempeñando sus funciones originales de metalurgia, "
"aunque con una eficacia mucho menor.\n"
"\n"
"A diferencia de las armas de plasma fabricadas a propósito, la botella de "
"plasma propulsada no provocará una explosión considerable al entrar en "
"contacto, lo que permite un funcionamiento relativamente seguro en espacios "
"cerrados."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "direct fusion gun"
msgid_plural "direct fusion gun"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/gun/plasma.json
#. ~ Description of gun "direct fusion gun"
#. ~ Description of "direct fusion gun"
msgid ""
"Exhaust from a salvaged starship engine is channeled through a series of "
"magnetic coils and focused into a searing fan of plasma, creating a crude but "
"effective short range weapon that can easily melt through most forms of "
"armor.  Its makeshift nature and lack of proper cooling systems make it prone "
"to overheating and catastrophic failure."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/plasma.json
