msgid "caecilian larva"
msgid_plural "caecilian larvas"
msgstr[0] "larva de cecilia"
msgstr[1] "larvas de cecilia"
msgstr[2] "larvas de cecilia"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "caecilian larva"
msgid ""
"Caecilians are a viviparous.  Their larvae are born inside the female and fed "
"with specials cells until they get out of her body."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "caecilian"
msgid_plural "caecilians"
msgstr[0] "cecilia"
msgstr[1] "cecilias"
msgstr[2] "cecilias"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "caecilian"
msgid ""
"One of several species of amphibians with a worm like body.  Caecilians can "
"be found in the tropics burrowed in the ground but are equally capable of "
"swimming."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de anfibios con el cuerpo como un gusano. Las "
"cecilias se pueden encontrare en los trópicos enterradas en el suelo pero son "
"capaces de nadar."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant caecilian"
msgid_plural "giant caecilians"
msgstr[0] "cecilia gigante"
msgstr[1] "cecilias gigantes"
msgstr[2] "cecilias gigantes"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant caecilian"
msgid ""
"A caecilian grown close to a snake in length.  It uses its strong head to dig "
"on the soil looking for mutated worms to devour."
msgstr ""
"Es una cecilia de un tamaño similar a una serpiente. Utiliza su potente "
"cabeza para cavar en la tierra buscando por gusanos mutados para devorar."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "minhocao"
msgid_plural "minhocaos"
msgstr[0] "minhocao"
msgstr[1] "minhocaos"
msgstr[2] "minhocaos"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "minhocao"
msgid ""
"A huge mutated caecilian as large and heavy as the largest constrictors.  It "
"resembles something out of amazonian folklore, but may be passive unless "
"provoked."
msgstr ""
"Es una enorme cecilia mutada, grande y pesada como la constrictora más "
"grande. Parece algo del folklore amazónico pero puede ser pasiva si no se la "
"provoca."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "anaconda"
msgid_plural "anacondas"
msgstr[0] "anaconda"
msgstr[1] "anacondas"
msgstr[2] "anacondas"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "anaconda"
msgid ""
"The anaconda is one of the largest and heaviest snakes in the world.  It "
"kills its prey by constriction and is a very good swimmer."
msgstr ""
"La anaconda es una de las serpientes más grandes y pesadas del mundo. Mata a "
"sus presas por constricción y es muy buena nadadora."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "boa"
msgid_plural "boas"
msgstr[0] "boa"
msgstr[1] "boas"
msgstr[2] "boas"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "boa"
msgid ""
"The boa constrictor is a large but modestly sized snake who shares habitat "
"with the anaconda.  Instead of the water it prefers arboreal and terrestrial "
"environments."
msgstr ""
"La boa constrictora es una serpiente grande pero no tanto que comparte "
"hábitat con la anaconda. En lugar del agua, prefiere ambientes arbóreos y "
"terrestres."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "python"
msgid_plural "pythons"
msgstr[0] "pitón"
msgstr[1] "pitones"
msgstr[2] "pitones"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "python"
msgid ""
"Pythons are a family of constrictor snakes native to the old world.  They are "
"in most regards similar in niche to boas but are dedicate egg layers."
msgstr ""
"Las pitones son una familia de serpientes constrictoras nativas del viejo "
"mundo. En la mayoría de los aspectos, su hábitat es similar al de las boas, "
"pero se caracterizan por ser grandes ponedoras de huevos."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pond turtle"
msgid_plural "pond turtles"
msgstr[0] "tortuga de estanque"
msgstr[1] "tortugas de estanque"
msgstr[2] "tortugas de estanque"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pond turtle"
msgid ""
"Distributed worldwide due to pet trade, pond turtles can be found on most "
"temperate to warm climates living in different aquatic environments."
msgstr ""
"Distribuidas por todo el mundo debido al comercio de mascotas, las tortugas "
"de estanque pueden encontrarse en la mayoría de los climas templados a "
"cálidos, viviendo en diferentes medios acuáticos."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "wood turtle"
msgid_plural "wood turtles"
msgstr[0] "tortuga marina de madera"
msgstr[1] "tortugas marinas de madera"
msgstr[2] "tortugas marinas de madera"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "wood turtle"
msgid ""
"Wood turtles can be found mostly in central and south America along with some "
"relatives in Asia and Oceania.  They are adapted to rainforests and can move "
"around on land and water."
msgstr ""
"Las tortugas de madera se encuentran sobre todo en América Central y del Sur, "
"junto con algunos parientes en Asia y Oceanía. Están adaptadas a las selvas "
"tropicales y pueden desplazarse por tierra y agua."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "snapping turtle"
msgid_plural "snapping turtles"
msgstr[0] "tortuga mordedora"
msgstr[1] "tortugas mordedoras"
msgstr[2] "tortugas mordedoras"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "snapping turtle"
msgid ""
"A genus of turtles known for their strong bite.  They can be found beyond US "
"borders from Mexico to some parts of South America."
msgstr ""
"Es un género de tortugas conocido por su fuerte mordida. Pueden encontrarse "
"fuera de la frontera de Estados Unidos, desde México hasta algunas partes de "
"América del Sur."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "tortoise"
msgid_plural "tortoises"
msgstr[0] "tortuga de tierra"
msgstr[1] "tortugas de tierra"
msgstr[2] "tortugas de tierra"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "tortoise"
msgid ""
"Unlike turtles, tortoises are adapted mostly to dry environments.  Many "
"species worldwide have grown to big sizes if the conditions are just right."
msgstr ""
"A diferencia de las tortugas marinas, las tortugas de tierra están adaptadas "
"sobre todo a entornos secos. Muchas especies de todo el mundo han alcanzado "
"grandes tamaños si las condiciones son las adecuadas."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "giant tortoise"
msgid_plural "giant tortoises"
msgstr[0] "tortuga de tierra gigante"
msgstr[1] "tortugas de tierra gigantes"
msgstr[2] "tortugas de tierra gigantes"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "giant tortoise"
msgid ""
"A large tortoise weighting half a ton.  Probably grown to this size by the "
"Cataclysm instead of ecological isolation."
msgstr ""
"Es un galápago grande que pesa media tonelada. Probablemente, creció a este "
"tamaño debido al Cataclismo en lugar de la aislación ecológica."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "titanochelon"
msgid_plural "titanochelons"
msgstr[0] "titanochelon"
msgstr[1] "titanochelons"
msgstr[2] "titanochelons"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "titanochelon"
msgid ""
"A truly massive tortoise similar in shape to a sauropod dinosaur.  Looks "
"quite docile but will react if threatened."
msgstr ""
"Es un galápago verdaderamente enorme con una forma similar a un dinosaurio "
"saurópodo. Parece bastante dócil pero va a reaccionar si se siente amenazado."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "triffid lifegiver"
msgid_plural "triffid lifegivers"
msgstr[0] "trífido cuidador"
msgstr[1] "trífidos cuidadores"
msgstr[2] "trífidos cuidadores"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "triffid lifegiver"
msgid ""
"An enormous triffid that crawls over the surrounding overgrowth.  It barely "
"moves unlike the others and instead seems to act as a sort of progenitor "
"figure."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme trífido que se repta sobre la maleza circundante. Apenas se mueve, "
"a diferencia de los demás, y parece actuar como una especie de figura "
"progenitora."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "triffid overqueen"
msgid_plural "triffid overqueens"
msgstr[0] "sobrereina trífida"
msgstr[1] "sobrereinas trífidas"
msgstr[2] "sobrereinas trífidas"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "triffid overqueen"
msgid ""
"An enormous triffid rooted to the ground.  It absorbs nutrients and sunlight "
"all day and night to release new podlings into the garden."
msgstr ""
"Es un enorme trífido enraizado al suelo. Absorbe los nutrientes y la luz "
"solar durante el día y la noche para liberar nuevos trífidos capsuleros en el "
"jardín."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "triffid podling"
msgid_plural "triffid podlings"
msgstr[0] "capsulero trífido"
msgstr[1] "capsuleros trífidos"
msgstr[2] "capsuleros trífidos"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "triffid podling"
msgid ""
"A very small triffid born out of a triffid pod.  Like all triffids its a very "
"dangerous plant but for now its just a harmless colorful flower."
msgstr ""
"Es un trífido diminuto recién salido de una cápsula trífida. Al igual que "
"todos los trífidos es una planta muy peligrosa pero por ahora es una flor "
"colorida e inofensiva."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "triffid gardenling"
msgid_plural "triffid gardenlings"
msgstr[0] "jardinero trífido"
msgstr[1] "jardineros trífidos"
msgstr[2] "jardineros trífidos"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "triffid gardenling"
msgid ""
"A young triffid that has grown some time on the garden grounds.  It is still "
"a juvenile but it can already fend for itself to a degree."
msgstr ""
"Es un trífido de poca edad que ha crecido en el jardín. Todavía es joven pero "
"ya puede defenderse en cierto grado."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "dionaea"
msgid_plural "dionaeas"
msgstr[0] "dionaea"
msgstr[1] "dionaeas"
msgstr[2] "dionaeas"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "dionaea"
msgid ""
"A strange triffid bearing something similar to a head.  Its false mouth is "
"covered in razorsharp needles."
msgstr ""
"Un extraño trífido con algo parecido a una cabeza. Su falsa boca está "
"cubierta de agujas afiladas."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "sarracenia"
msgid_plural "sarracenias"
msgstr[0] "sarracenia"
msgstr[1] "sarracenias"
msgstr[2] "sarracenias"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "sarracenia"
msgid ""
"A strange triffid with a wide vase-like body.  It moves carefully while "
"carrying what appears to be a half-digested prey."
msgstr ""
"Un extraño trífido con un cuerpo ancho en forma de jarrón. Se mueve con "
"cuidado mientras lleva lo que parece ser una presa a medio digerir."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "rafflesia"
msgid_plural "rafflesias"
msgstr[0] "rafflesia"
msgstr[1] "rafflesias"
msgstr[2] "rafflesias"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "rafflesia"
msgid ""
"A large walking plant with an enormous flower-like upper body.  Its center "
"has what appears to be a mouth and seems to emit a really bad aroma."
msgstr ""
"Una gran planta trepadora con un enorme cuerpo superior en forma de flor. Su "
"centro tiene lo que parece ser una boca y parece emitir un aroma realmente "
"desagradable."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "rafflesia"
msgid "The rafflesia spews toxic gas!"
msgstr "¡La raflesia expulsa gas tóxico!"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "yateveo"
msgid_plural "yateveos"
msgstr[0] "yateveo"
msgstr[1] "yateveos"
msgstr[2] "yateveos"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_triffid.json
#. ~ Description of monster "yateveo"
msgid ""
"A large walking plant shaped in the likes of a tree.  It has several long "
"vines ending in sharp wooden spikes."
msgstr ""
"Una gran planta andante con forma de árbol. Tiene varias lianas largas que "
"terminan en puntas de madera afiladas."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "garden zombie"
msgid_plural "garden zombies"
msgstr[0] "zombi jardin"
msgstr[1] "zombis jardín"
msgstr[2] "zombis jardín"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "garden zombie"
msgid ""
"A zombie wearing some kind of gardening or botanic attire and is smeared full "
"of vines, thorns, pollen and sap.  The triffids have it controlled somehow "
"but its purpose remains unclear."
msgstr ""
"Un zombi que viste algún tipo de atuendo de jardinería o botánica y está "
"embadurnado de enredaderas, espinas, polen y savia. Los trífidos lo tienen "
"bajo control de algún modo, pero su propósito sigue sin estar claro."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "garden zombie"
msgid "The zombie spews a cloud of pollen!"
msgstr "¡El zombi arroja una nube de polen!"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "garden child"
msgid_plural "garden children"
msgstr[0] "pibe de jardín"
msgstr[1] "pibes de jardín"
msgstr[2] "pibes de jardín"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "garden child"
msgid ""
"This child zombie seems to have been adopted by plants.  It has several "
"thorny vines and sprouts covering its head and body."
msgstr ""
"Este niño zombi parece haber sido adoptado por las plantas. Tiene varias "
"enredaderas espinosas y brotes cubriéndole la cabeza y el cuerpo."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "spriteling"
msgid_plural "spritelings"
msgstr[0] "duendeling"
msgstr[1] "duendelings"
msgstr[2] "duendelings"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "spriteling"
msgid ""
"An undead child mutated by alien flora.  It has several colorful flowers on "
"its scalp and an unsettling serene expression."
msgstr ""
"Es un pibe muerto vivo mutado por flora extraterrestre. Tiene varias flores "
"coloridas en su cuero cabelludo y una expresión serena perturbadora."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mossy boomer"
msgid_plural "mossy boomers"
msgstr[0] "búmer musgoso"
msgstr[1] "búmers musgosos"
msgstr[2] "búmers musgosos"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mossy boomer"
msgid ""
"A fat and slow zombie covered in plant growths of unknown origin.  Some vines "
"seem to extend into its mouth and guts."
msgstr ""
"Un zombi gordo y lento cubierto de crecimientos vegetales de origen "
"desconocido. Algunas enredaderas parecen extenderse hasta su boca y tripas."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "sap belcher"
msgid_plural "sap belchers"
msgstr[0] "vientre de savia"
msgstr[1] "vientres de savia"
msgstr[2] "vientres de savia"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "sap belcher"
msgid ""
"This big and bloated zombie seems full of sap.  Its already overgrown body "
"shows several flowering plants growing over it."
msgstr ""
"Este zombi grande e hinchado parece estar lleno de savia. Su cuerpo, ya muy "
"crecido, muestra varias plantas con flores que crecen sobre él."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pollinated eructor"
msgid_plural "pollinated eructors"
msgstr[0] "eructor polinizador"
msgstr[1] "eructores polinizadores"
msgstr[2] "eructores polinizadores"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pollinated eructor"
msgid ""
"This engorged zombie has smears of strange pollen on its mouth and plants "
"over its body.  It shambles around eructing the stuff all over the place."
msgstr ""
"Este zombi engullido tiene manchas de extraño polen en la boca y plantas por "
"todo el cuerpo. Se pasea eructando la materia por todas partes."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bramble brute"
msgid_plural "bramble brutes"
msgstr[0] "bestia de la zarza"
msgstr[1] "bestias de la zarza"
msgstr[2] "bestias de la zarza"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bramble brute"
msgid "A large and muscular zombie covered in thick alien vegetation."
msgstr "Un zombi grande y musculoso cubierto de espesa vegetación alienígena."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "overgrown terror"
msgid_plural "overgrown terrors"
msgstr[0] "terror de gran tamaño"
msgstr[1] "terrores de gran tamaño"
msgstr[2] "terrores de gran tamaño"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "overgrown terror"
msgid ""
"This massive muscled zombie has the equivalent of a small garden growing all "
"over its body."
msgstr ""
"Este enorme zombi musculoso tiene el equivalente a un pequeño jardín "
"creciéndole por todo el cuerpo."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "forest screamer"
msgid_plural "forest screamers"
msgstr[0] "gritón de bosque"
msgstr[1] "gritones de bosque"
msgstr[2] "gritones de bosque"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "forest screamer"
msgid ""
"The plant growth on this slender zombie makes it look like some kind of "
"forest apparition.  It looks like it could throw a curse at you at any moment."
msgstr ""
"La planta que creció en este zombi flaco lo hace parecer una especie de "
"aparición del bosque. Tiene el aspecto de algo que podría hacerte una "
"maldición en cualquier momento."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "glade banshee"
msgid_plural "glade banshees"
msgstr[0] "banshee de claro"
msgstr[1] "banshees de claro"
msgstr[2] "banshees de claro"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "glade banshee"
msgid ""
"With its ragged looks and overgrown coverage this zombie looks like a hag "
"from some cursed forest."
msgstr ""
"Con su aspecto andrajoso y su cobertura exagerada, este zombi parece una "
"bruja de algún bosque maldito."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mire walker"
msgid_plural "mire walkers"
msgstr[0] "caminante de cienaga"
msgstr[1] "caminantes de cienaga"
msgstr[2] "caminantes de cienaga"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mire walker"
msgid ""
"This zombie seems to have been roaming the surrounding swamps and rivers.  It "
"has several water plants clinging to its body."
msgstr ""
"Este zombi parece haber estado vagando por los pantanos y ríos de los "
"alrededores. Tiene varias plantas acuáticas pegadas al cuerpo."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mangrove lurker"
msgid_plural "mangrove lurkers"
msgstr[0] "merodeador de manglar"
msgstr[1] "merodeadores de manglar"
msgstr[2] "merodeadores de manglar"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/zed_plant.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mangrove lurker"
msgid ""
"This zombie seems to have adapted to hunt in the water.  It uses the aquatic "
"plants on its body to hide before hitting with its teeth."
msgstr ""
"Este zombi parece haberse adaptado a moverse en el agua. Utiliza las plantas "
"acuáticas de su cuerpo para esconderse antes de golpear con sus dientes."

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_nether.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "alien reef"
msgstr "arrecife extraterrestre"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_residential.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "overgrown lot"
msgstr "lote cubierto de vegetación"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_residential.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "overtaken lot"
msgstr "lote sobretomado"

#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_termites.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "termite mound"
msgstr "termitero"

