#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<talk_snippet_modded_liam_meeting1>"
msgid ""
"*, your old friend, looks up at you in shock.  At his feet lies a corpse, its "
"head almost completely blown off by the shotgun that drops limply from Liam's "
"fingers as you approach.  \"I swear, dude, this is not what it looks like.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Not what it looks like?  It looks like you just blew someone's head off, "
"Liam.  Holy shit, is that… Chris?  Did you kill Chris?"
msgstr ""
"¿No es lo que parece? Parece que le volaste la cabeza a alguien, Liam. "
"Mierda, ¿es… Chris? ¿Lo mataste a Chris?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No!  Dammit, no!\"  Liam looks briefly panicked, then his eyes widen.  \"I "
"have something for this, hold on.\"  He reaches to the sofa behind him, "
"slowly, keeping his hands away from the shotgun on the floor.  \"Look.  Chris "
"left a note.\"  Liam holds up the paper, in Chris' clear handwriting.  You "
"can just make it out: it reads somewhat like a suicide note, and realization "
"starts to dawn.  Liam nods, seeing you start to understand.  \"Chris got bit "
"while we were on our way here.  We tried to treat it, I did everything I "
"could think of, but the infection got worse and worse.  Chris told me to just "
"turn my back, but I couldn't do that.  We had a pact.  You know that.\"  "
"Liam's eyes are red rimmed, and he wipes them with a sleeve.  \"I stayed here "
"until… until the transition.  We wrote this letter and a bunch more, stuff "
"for Chris's family, if we can find them, you know?"
msgstr ""
"¡No! Maldita sea, ¡no! Liam parece brevemente asustado, luego sus ojos se "
"ensanchan. \"Tengo algo para esto, espera\". Se acerca al sofá que hay detrás "
"de él, despacio, manteniendo las manos alejadas de la escopeta que hay en el "
"suelo. \"Mira. Chris dejó una nota\". Liam sostiene el papel, con la letra "
"clara de Chris. Puedes distinguirla: parece una nota de suicidio, y empiezas "
"a darte cuenta. Liam asiente al ver que empiezas a comprender. \"Chris fue "
"mordido cuando veníamos hacia aquí. Intentamos tratarlo, hice todo lo que se "
"me ocurrió, pero la infección empeoraba cada vez más. Chris me dijo que le "
"diera la espalda, pero no podía hacerlo. Teníamos un pacto. Tú lo sabes\". "
"Liam tiene los ojos enrojecidos y se los limpia con una manga. \"Me quedé "
"aquí hasta... hasta la transición. Escribimos esta carta y un montón más, "
"cosas para la familia de Chris, si podemos encontrarlos, ¿sabes?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So Chris turned into a zombie right in front of you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Wait.  Zombies?  I knew things were going to shit, but are you telling me "
"it's really zombies?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah.\"  Liam wipes his face again, and flops down on the couch.  \"I thought "
"there'd be more time between passing out and getting back up, I was going to "
"do this outside.  God damn, that was the hardest thing I've ever done.\"  He "
"looks up at you, his face drained, across the body of one of your oldest "
"friends.  \"Fucking hell.  You're alive.  You made it here.  I'm sorry for "
"the rough introduction, I should be hugging you right now.  You're not bit or "
"anything?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I'm fine.  Want to get this cleaned up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Bit?  Like, the whole classic 'one bite and you're done' zombie movie stuff?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah.  You probably heard some wacky shit on the news, hey?  I heard all "
"kinds of garbage, anything from evil mushrooms to interdimensional monsters, "
"but no.  It's zombies, classic fucking zombies.  I'm still struggling with it "
"myself."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You got it.  I know, it feels really contrived, doesn't it?  It's exactly "
"like the old movies in every way, like someone had designed it to be.  I "
"don't know if it's every bite or what, but Chris just had one that barely "
"broke the skin and you see where that ended up.  Took about three days.  My "
"advice is, we don't let these things teeth anywhere near our skin.  They're "
"pretty clumsy bastards, though.  They definitely can't just nibble you as "
"they go by, they've gotta grab you first.  Unfortunately, seems like they're "
"pretty fuckin' good at that.  Once you get grabbed, best bet is to go full "
"ham on the zombie grabbing you with everything you've got, and try to shake "
"loose, but honestly it's better to not get grabbed."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, no bites.  I'm fine.  Want to get this cleaned up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*lets out a long sigh and nods.  \"Let's get poor Chris outside for a proper "
"burial to start.  I can't tell you how glad I am to see you.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm glad to see you too, Liam.  Wish it was a better situation.  Let's do "
"this."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<talk_snippet_modded_liam_Friends4ever>"
msgid ""
"Aww, of course.  No matter what happens, you're always you and I'm always me, "
"right?  We've been through worse than this.\"  He pauses, his brow furrowed.  "
"\"Well, okay, maybe we haven't.  But we've stuck through it all for so many "
"years, what's a little undead apocalypse gonna change?  Hell, I think we're "
"in for one of those classic buddy-buddy zombie movie experiences, like, uh, "
"Dawn of the Dead.\"  He pauses.  \"Maybe not that one.  Night of the Living "
"Dead?\"  He pauses again.  \"Zombieland, maybe.  Who cares.  You're my "
"family, more than my birth family ever was."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda/modinfo.json
#. ~ MOD name
msgid "Dark Days Ahead"
msgstr "Futuros Dias Oscuros"

#: data/mods/dda/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "Dark Days Ahead"
msgid "Core content for Cataclysm-DDA"
msgstr "Contenido básico para Cataclismo-DDA"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "Tutorial"
msgid "Tutorial for Cataclysm-DDA"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "dummy"
msgid_plural "dummies"
msgstr[0] "maniquí"
msgstr[1] "maniquies"
msgstr[2] "maniquies"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "dummy"
msgid "This dummy serves for only one purpose - to teach players how to hit monsters."
msgstr ""
"Este maniquí sólo sirve para un propósito: enseñar a los jugadores a golpear  "
"monstruos."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/monsters.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "dummy"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s is destroyed."
msgstr "%s destruido."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/overmap_terrain.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "tutorial room"
msgstr "sala de tutorial"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Welcome to the Cataclysm tutorial!  As you play, pop-ups like this one will "
"appear to guide you through the basic game actions.\n"
"\n"
"At any time, you can press <keybind:HELP_KEYBINDINGS> to open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Keybindings menu</color> to view or modify the controls for "
"the game or specific menu that you are in.\n"
"\n"
"Pressing <keybind:POPUP_WAIT:QUIT> will close the pop-up."
msgstr ""
"¡Bienvenido al tutorial de Cataclismo! Mientras juegas, aparecerán ventanas "
"emergentes como esta para guiarte a través de las acciones básicas del juego.\n"
"\n"
"En cualquier momento, puedes pulsar <keybind:HELP_KEYBINDINGS> para abrir el "
"<color_light_cyan>Menú de atajos de teclado</color> y ver o modificar los "
"controles o otros menús específicos.\n"
"\n"
"Al pulsar <keybind:POPUP_WAIT:QUIT> se cerrará la ventana emergente."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The character in the center of the screen represents you.  By default, you "
"can move around using the <color_yellow>numpad</color>, "
"<color_yellow>vikeys</color>, or the <color_yellow>arrow keys</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Movement Controls:\n"
"North: <keybind:UP>\n"
"South: <keybind:DOWN>\n"
"West: <keybind:LEFT>\n"
"East: <keybind:RIGHT>\n"
"Northwest: <keybind:LEFTUP>\n"
"Northeast: <keybind:RIGHTUP>\n"
"Southwest: <keybind:LEFTDOWN>\n"
"Southeast: <keybind:RIGHTDOWN>\n"
"Wait in place: <keybind:pause>\n"
"\n"
"You can also use <keybind:SELECT> to select the location you want to move, "
"and then press it again to confirm the movement.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please move to the door to the east."
msgstr ""
"El personaje en el centro de la pantalla te representa. Por defecto, puedes "
"moverte con el <color_yellow>teclado numérico</color>, las "
"<color_yellow>vikeys</color> o las<color_yellow> teclas de dirección</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Controles de movimiento:\n"
"Norte: <keybind:UP>\n"
"Sur: <keybind:DOWN>\n"
"Oeste: <keybind:LEFT>\n"
"Este: <keybind:RIGHT>\n"
"Noroeste: <keybind:LEFTUP>\n"
"Noreste: <keybind:RIGHTUP>\n"
"Sudoeste: <keybind:LEFTDOWN>\n"
"Sureste: <keybind:RIGHTDOWN>\n"
"Esperar quieto: <keybind:pause>\n"
"\n"
"También puedes usar <keybind:SELECT> para seleccionar el lugar al que quieras "
"moverte, y pulsarlo de nuevo para confirmar el movimiento.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, muévete hacia la puerta del este."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You're standing next to a closed door.  To open it, either walk into it, or "
"press <keybind:open> and then a movement key.  Using <keybind:open> will also "
"let you open windows, gates, fences, safes and more."
msgstr ""
"Estás junto a una puerta cerrada. Para abrirla, camina hacia a ella o pulsa "
"<keybind:open> y luego una tecla de movimiento. Pulsar <keybind:open> también "
"te permitirá abrir ventanas, puertas, vallas, cajas fuertes y mucho más."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You can close an opened door by pressing <keybind:close> and then a movement "
"key.  Closing doors behind you can often slow down crowds of monsters greatly."
msgstr ""
"Puedes cerrar una puerta abierta pulsando <keybind:close> y a continuación "
"una tecla de movimiento.  Cerrar puertas detrás de ti puede frenar "
"temporalmente a una multitud de monstruos."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Most monsters will have to smash their way through a closed door.  If a door "
"is locked or partially broken, you can smash it by pressing <keybind:smash> "
"and then a movement key."
msgstr ""
"La mayoría de los monstruos tendrán que abrirse paso a golpes a través de una "
"puerta cerrada. Si una puerta está cerrada o parcialmente rota, puedes "
"romperla pulsando <keybind:smash> y a movimiento hacia ella."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You can smash through windows by pressing <keybind:smash> and then a movement "
"key.  A smashed window takes a long time to climb through, and it's possible "
"to hurt yourself on the broken glass, but it's a good last-ditch escape "
"route.  Smashing a broken window again will clear the glass so you can move "
"through it safely, although it will still be quite slow.  Almost everything "
"can be smashed, given you have enough strength or are doing enough damage."
msgstr ""
"Puedes destrozar las ventanas pulsando <keybind:smash> y a continuación una "
"tecla de movimiento. Se tarda mucho en atravezar una ventana rota, y es "
"posible hacerse daño con los cristales rotos, pero es una buena vía de escape "
"en caso de necesidad. Si vuelves a golpear la ventana, el cristal se caerá y "
"podrás moverte por ella con seguridad de no cortarte, aunque seguirá siendo "
"lento pasar por ella. Casi todo se puede romper, siempre que tengas "
"suficiente fuerza o hagas suficiente daño."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just stepped on a space with one or more items.  If you wish to pick it "
"up, press <keybind:pickup>.  To select the tile directly underneath you, "
"press <keybind:pause>.\n"
"\n"
"In the <color_light_cyan>Pickup</color> menu, press:\n"
"<keybind:RIGHT> to select the items you wish to pick up\n"
"<keybind:LEFT> to deselect\n"
"<keybind:CONFIRM> to confirm\n"
"\n"
"Note that you don't need to stand directly on the space with items to pick "
"them up, you can pick them up when standing near them.\n"
"\n"
"If the item is too big to fit in any of your pockets, or is a weapon that you "
"want to wield, you can press <keybind:wield> to wield it from the ground or "
"from the <color_light_cyan>Pickup</color> menu.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please pick up the <color_light_cyan>baseball "
"bat</color> you're standing on and move to the door to the south."
msgstr ""
"Acabas de pasar por una posición con uno o más objetos. Si deseas recogerlos, "
"pulsa <keybind:pickup>. Para seleccionar la posición que está justo debajo de "
"tí, pulsa <keybind:pause> .\n"
"\n"
"En el menú de <color_light_cyan>Recogida</color>, pulsa\n"
"<keybind:RIGHT> para seleccionar los objetos que quieras recoger\n"
"<keybind:LEFT> para deseleccionarlos\n"
"<keybind:CONFIRM> para confirmar la acción\n"
"\n"
"No es necesario que te encuentres sobre la posición con objetos para "
"recogerlos, puedes recogerlos en una posición adyacente a ellos.\n"
"\n"
"Si un objeto no cabe en alguno de tus bolsillos o mochilas, o es un arma que "
"quieres empuñar, puedes pulsar <keybind:wield> para empuñarlo desde el suelo "
"o desde el menú de <color_light_cyan>Recogida</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, recoge el <color_light_cyan>bate de "
"béisbol</color> sobre el que te encuentras y dirígete a la puerta del sur."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"There is a display rack next to you with a steel spear lying on it.  You can "
"press <keybind:wield> to directly wield an item, without the need of picking "
"it up first.  Pressing <keybind:wield> will open the <color_light_cyan>Wield "
"item</color> menu.  Select the item you want to wield and confirm by pressing "
"<keybind:CONFIRM>.\n"
"\n"
"As you have no free space in your inventory, you will have to drop the "
"<color_light_cyan>baseball bat</color> on the ground before you can wield the "
"spear.\n"
"\n"
"If you wish to free your hands (i.e. wield nothing), press <keybind:wield> "
"and select your currently wielded item.  Alternatively, you could drop the "
"wielded item by pressing <keybind:drop> and selecting your currently wielded "
"item.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please wield the spear and move to the counters "
"west of you."
msgstr ""
"Hay un expositor a tu lado con una lanza de acero. Puedes pulsar "
"<keybind:wield> para empuñar directamente un objeto, sin necesidad de "
"recogerlo en primer lugar. Al pulsar <keybind:wield>, se abrirá el menú de "
"<color_light_cyan>Empuñar objeto</color>. Selecciona el objeto que quieres "
"empuñar  y confírmalo pulsando <keybind:CONFIRM>.\n"
"\n"
"Como no tienes espacio libre en tu inventario, tendrás que dejar caer el "
"<color_light_cyan>bate de béisbol</color> al suelo antes de poder empuñar la "
"lanza.\n"
"\n"
"Si deseas liberar tus manos (es decir, no empuñar nada), pulsa "
"<keybind:wield> y selecciona el objeto que empuñas. Alternativamente, puedes "
"dejar caer el objeto que empuñas pulsando <keybind:drop> y seleccionar el "
"objeto a empuñar en ese momento.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, empuña la lanza y muévete hacia los "
"mostradores que están al oeste de tu posición."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a type of clothing!  To wear clothing, press "
"<keybind:wear> and then select an item.  To take off clothing, press "
"<keybind:take_off>, or simply take it off and drop it in one action by "
"pressing <keybind:drop>."
msgstr ""
"¡El objeto que acabas de recoger es un tipo de ropa!. Para ponerte ropa, "
"pulsa <keybind:wear> y a continuación selecciona un objeto. Para quitarte la "
"ropa, pulsa <keybind:take_off>, o simplemente quítatela y tirala en una sola "
"acción al pulsar <keybind:drop>."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a good weapon!  To wield a weapon, press "
"<keybind:wield>, then pick what to wield.  To wield nothing, either drop your "
"weapon with <keybind:drop>, or press <keybind:wield> to put it away."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a comestible!  To eat a comestible, press "
"<keybind:eat>.  Comestibles are items you can use up, like food, drink, "
"pills, etc.  Most food expires eventually, so be careful.  Some comestibles, "
"especially drugs, can cause subtle, long-term effects."
msgstr ""
"¡El objeto que acabas de recoger es comestible! Para comer un comestible, "
"pulsa <keybind:eat>. Los comestibles son objetos que puedes consumir, como "
"comida, bebidas, pastillas, etc. La mayoría de los alimentos caducan con el "
"tiempo, así que ten cuidado. Algunos comestibles, especialmente las drogas, "
"pueden causar efectos sutiles a largo plazo."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a tool!  To activate a tool, press "
"<keybind:apply>.  Some tools have a set charge, which can be reloaded once "
"depleted.  Others are single-use items, and still others are reusable."
msgstr ""
"¡El objeto que acabas de recoger es una herramienta! Para activar una "
"herramienta, pulsa <keybind:apply>.  Algunas herramientas tienen una carga "
"fija, que puede ser recargada una vez se agota. Otras son de un solo uso y "
"otras son reutilizables."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a firearm!  Guns are very powerful weapons but "
"they require ammunition.  Firearms have many special attributes.  Most modify "
"the damage done by their ammunition.  They also have dispersion, which "
"affects their chance to hit.  Some guns are semi-automatic, while others can "
"fire a burst.  Some firearms (mainly bows and other muscle-powered weapons) "
"have a range, which is added on top of the ammo's range when firing."
msgstr ""
"¡El objeto que acabas de recoger es un arma de fuego!. Las armas de fuego son "
"armas muy poderosas, pero requieren munición. Las armas de fuego tienen "
"muchos atributos especiales. La mayoría modifican el daño causado por su "
"munición. También tienen dispersión, que afecta a su probabilidad de acertar. "
"Algunas armas son semiautomáticas, mientras que otras pueden disparar una "
"ráfaga. Algunas armas de fuego (sobre todo los arcos y otras armas de "
"potencia muscular) tienen un alcance, que se añade al alcance de la munición "
"al disparar."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is ammunition, used with a gun.  It has many "
"special attributes.  The damage value is the maximum done on a standard hit; "
"a critical hit or headshot will do much more damage.  Some monsters or NPCs "
"will wear armor which reduces the damage from gunfire; a high armor-pierce "
"value will reduce this effect.  The range is the maximum range the ammo can "
"achieve, and the dispersion affects its chance to hit."
msgstr ""
"El objeto que acabas de recoger es munición utilizado con una arma de fuego. "
"Tiene muchos atributos especiales. El valor de daño es el máximo hecho en un "
"golpe estándar; un golpe crítico o un disparo a la cabeza harán mucho más "
"daño. Algunos monstruos o PNJs llevarán una armadura que reduce el daño de "
"los disparos; un valor alto de penetración de armadura reducirá este efecto. "
"El alcance es la distancia máxima que puede alcanzar la munición, y la "
"dispersión afecta a su probabilidad de golpear."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just put on an article of clothing that provides physical protection.  "
"There are three types of damage that clothing defends against: "
"<color_light_cyan>bashing</color>, <color_light_cyan>cutting</color>, and "
"<color_light_cyan>ballistic</color>.  Most monsters deal bashing damage, but "
"cutting is often the more deadly of the two.  Not many enemies deal ballistic "
"damage; among them are some robots, turrets, and non-playable characters "
"(NPCs)."
msgstr ""
"Acabas de ponerte una prenda de vestir que te proporciona protección física. "
"Hay tres tipos de daño contra los que la ropa te protege: "
"<color_light_cyan>contundente</color>, <color_light_cyan>cortante</color> y "
"<color_light_cyan>penetrante</color>. La mayoría de los monstruos infligen "
"daño contundente, pero el corte suele ser el más letal de los dos. No hay "
"muchos enemigos que inflijan daño perforante, entre ellos algunos robots, "
"torretas y personajes no jugables (PNJs)."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just put on an article of clothing that provides ample storage space.  "
"This will allow you to carry more stuff, but be aware that there is also a "
"limit on the weight you can carry which depends on your strength.  The item "
"you put on also encumbered your torso.  This will make combat a little more "
"difficult.  To check encumbrance, press <keybind:player_data>.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please move to the corridor to the north and wear "
"all clothing you find on the racks."
msgstr ""
"Te acabas de equipar con un objeto que te proporciona amplio espacio de "
"almacenamiento. Esto te permitirá llevar más cosas, pero ten en cuenta que "
"existe un límite en el peso que puedes llevar que depende de tu fuerza. El "
"objeto que te pusistes te causará también incomododidad en el torso. Esto "
"causará que el combatir sea un poco más difícil. Para comprobar la "
"incomodidad, pulsa <keybind:player_data>.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, dirígete al pasillo del norte y ponte toda la "
"ropa que encuentres en los estantes."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just put on an article of clothing that protects against the environment. "
" The most common and important are respiratory devices, which will protect "
"you against smoke, airborne toxins or organisms, and other common hazards.  "
"However, they also make it a little harder to breathe when running, so you'll "
"move more slowly.  To check your encumbrance, press <keybind:player_data>."
msgstr ""
"Acabas de ponerte una prenda que te protege contra el medio ambiente. Los más "
"comunes e importantes son los dispositivos respiratorios, que te protegerán "
"contra el humo, las toxinas, organismos transportados por el aire y otros "
"peligros habituales. Sin embargo, también dificulta un poco la respiración al "
"correr, por lo que te moverás más despacio. Para comprobar tu incomodidad, "
"pulsa <keybind:player_data>."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"If you press <keybind:inventory> and then the letter of your weapon, you'll "
"see its combat stats.  Bashing damage ignores most armor, but varies greatly "
"and requires strength.  Cutting damage is a fixed amount, but is blocked by "
"armor.  The To-hit bonus affects your chances of hitting.  The amount of time "
"it takes to swing your melee weapon depends on both its size and weight; "
"small, compact weapons are the fastest."
msgstr ""
"Si pulsas <keybind:inventory> y luego la letra de tu arma, verás sus "
"estadísticas de combate. El daño contundente ignora la mayoría de las "
"armaduras, pero varía mucho y requiere fuerza. El daño cortante es una "
"cantidad fija, pero es bloqueado por la armadura. La bonificación por golpe "
"afecta tus probabilidades de golpear. La cantidad de tiempo que te lleva "
"realizar un ataque con tu arma c. a c. depende de su tamaño y peso; las armas "
"pequeñas y compactas son las más rápidas."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Hitting a monster will stun it briefly, allowing you to escape or get in "
"another attack.  Your dexterity and melee skills are used to determine "
"whether an attack hits, while strength affects damage."
msgstr ""
"Cuando golpeás a un monstruo lo vas a aturdir momentáneamente, lo que te "
"permite escapar o volver a atacarlo. Tu destreza y tu habilidad para el "
"cuerpo a cuerpo son los que determinan si acertás tus golpes, mientras que la "
"fuerza determina el daño."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Looks like you suddenly felt pain.  The pain status is indicated on the "
"sidebar and also in the <keybind:player_data> menu.\n"
"\n"
"Small amounts of pain are tolerable, but as it gets worse your stats will "
"drop and you will move much slower.  To reduce pain, take painkillers like "
"<color_light_cyan>codeine</color> on the rack nearby (by activating it with "
"<keybind:apply>), or simply wait it out."
msgstr ""
"Parece que de repente has sentido dolor. El estado del dolor se indica en la "
"barra lateral y también en el menú <keybind:player_data>.\n"
"\n"
"Las pequeñas cantidades de dolor son tolerables, pero a medida que aumenta el "
"dolor, tus estadísticas bajarán y te moverás mucho más lento. Para reducir el "
"dolor, toma analgésicos como la <color_light_cyan>codeína</color> en el "
"estante cercano (activándolo con <keybind:apply>), o simplemente espera a que "
"se pase."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"When you kill a monster it will often leave behind a corpse.  Corpses can be "
"important sources of food, but you must butcher them by standing on the "
"corpse and pressing <keybind:butcher>.  You'll need a bladed weapon in your "
"inventory, preferably a small, very sharp one.  An unskilled butcher may only "
"get a few pieces of meat, or none at all.  Note that many monsters, such as "
"zombies, leave tainted meat, unsuitable for consumption."
msgstr ""
"Cuando matas a un monstruo generalmente queda un cadáver. Los cadáveres "
"pueden ser fuentes de comida pero tienes que descuartizarlos parándote en el "
"mismo espacio y pulsando <keybind:butcher>. Vas a necesitar un arma blanca en "
"el inventario, mejor si es pequeña y muy afilada. Si el descuartizamiento no "
"te sale bien, solo obtendrás algunos trozos de carne, o ninguno. Acuérdate "
"que muchos monstruos, como los zombis, dejan carne contaminada que no se "
"puede consumir."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"That drug you just took is a <color_light_cyan>painkiller</color>.  "
"Painkillers are very important to keep on hand, as pain both penalizes your "
"stats and makes you slower.  Be careful though, as the stronger painkillers "
"can make you woozy, and some are even addictive.\n"
"\n"
"Please also note that painkillers don't work the moment you take them.  They "
"need some time to start working, and you don't need to take another dose "
"right now if you don't see the immediate effect.  Just wait, and sooner or "
"later the pain will start going away."
msgstr ""
"Esa droga que tomaste es un <color_light_cyan>analgésico</color>. Los "
"analgésicos son muy importantes ya que el dolor penaliza tus estadísticas y "
"te hace moverte más lento. Pero ten cuidado, los más fuertes te pueden marear "
"y algunos son adictivos.\n"
"\n"
"Por favor, fíjate que los analgésicos no funcionan instantáneamente. "
"Necesitan tiempo para empezar a hacer efecto así que no necesitas tomarte "
"otro enseguida si no ves un efecto inmediato. Tienes que esperar y tarde o "
"temprano el dolor va a empezar a irse."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"That drug you just took placed an effect on you.  To check your effects, "
"press <keybind:player_data>.  Most only last a short while, while others, "
"like chronic disease, last until cured by some other means."
msgstr ""
"La droga que acabas de tomar tuvo un efecto. Para ver sus efectos, pulsa "
"<keybind:player_data>. La mayoría duran poco pero otros, como las "
"enfermedades crónicas, duran hasta que sean curadas de alguna forma."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just drank a bottle of water, reducing your thirst level and reducing the "
"water level in the bottle.  You'll probably want to drop empty bottles, or "
"you might want to save them to refill from a water source later."
msgstr ""
"Te tomaste una botella de agua, reduciendo tu nivel de sed y reduciendo el "
"nivel de agua en la botella. Probablemente quieras dejar algunas botellas "
"vacías, o tal vez quieras guardarlas para volverlas a llenar."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just activated a grenade!  You probably want to throw it.  To throw an "
"item, press <keybind:throw> and then select the item to throw.  The maximum "
"range depends on your strength and the object's weight and size.  Throwing "
"isn't very good in most combat situations, but if you've got some fire power…"
msgstr ""
"¡Acabas de activar una granada! Probablemente quieras arrojarla. Para arrojar "
"un objeto, pulsa <keybind:throw> y elige a donde quieres arrojarla. El "
"alcance máximo depende de tu fuerza y del peso y tamaño del objeto. Arrojar "
"cosas no es lo mejor para la mayoría de las situaciones de combate, pero si "
"tienes potencia de fuego…"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"This thing here on the floor is a <color_light_cyan>trap</color>.  Traps are "
"permanent until set off, and can be an important defensive tactic, "
"particularly when sleeping in unsafe territory.  Try stepping on the bubble "
"wrap.  Don't worry, it's harmless, but it will make some noise.  There are "
"other types of traps that will cause varying amounts of damage or even "
"teleport you, so watch your step carefully."
msgstr ""
"La cosa que hay aquí en el suelo es una <color_light_cyan>trampa</color>. Las "
"trampas son permanentes hasta que se activan, y pueden ser una táctica "
"defensiva importante, sobre todo cuando se duerme en un territorio inseguro. "
"Intenta pisar el plástico de burbujas. No te preocupes, es inofensivo, pero "
"hará algo de ruido. Hay otros tipos de trampas que causan distintos daños o "
"incluso te teletransportan, así que ten cuidado al pisar."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Finally, to fire a gun, press <keybind:fire>. You'll automatically target the "
"last monster you shot at, or the closest monster to you.  You can change your "
"target with the <color_yellow>movement keys</color>, or cycle through "
"monsters with <keybind:TARGET:PREV_TARGET> and <keybind:TARGET:NEXT_TARGET>.  "
"Select the <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> as a target and press "
"<keybind:fire> to fire a single shot.  With many guns, you can change the "
"fire mode to burst or full auto by pressing <keybind:select_fire_mode>.\n"
"\n"
"There are detailed instructions on how to aim and fire in the "
"<color_light_cyan>Aiming and firing</color> menu, so make sure to check it "
"carefully.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please fire a couple of times at the dummy and move "
"to the corridor to the west."
msgstr ""
"Por último, para disparar un arma de fuego, pulsa <keybind:fire>. Apuntarás "
"automáticamente al último monstruo al que hayas disparado, o al que tengas "
"más cerca. Puedes cambiar de objetivo con las <color_yellow>teclas de "
"movimiento</color>, o recorrer los monstruos con "
"<keybind:TARGET:PREV_TARGET>y <keybind:TARGET:NEXT_TARGET>. Selecciona el "
"<color_light_cyan>maniquí</color> como objetivo y pulsa <keybind:fire> para "
"hacer un disparo. Con muchas armas, puedes cambiar el modo de disparo a "
"ráfaga o automático pulsando <keybind:select_fire_mode>.\n"
"\n"
"Hay instrucciones detalladas sobre cómo apuntar y disparar en el menú "
"<color_light_cyan>Apuntar y disparar</color>, así que asegúrate de "
"consultarlo detenidamente.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, dispara un par de veces al maniquí y dirígete "
"al pasillo del oeste."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Firing your gun will increase your recoil level.  You can see its level in "
"the <color_light_cyan>Aiming and firing</color> menu (by pressing "
"<keybind:fire>).  Generally speaking, the more damaging the ammo, the worse "
"the recoil.  Recoil severely reduces your chance to hit, but you can "
"eliminate recoil by pausing (<keybind:pause>) for a turn.  High strength "
"reduces recoil, so weak characters might want to stick to .22 or 9x19mm guns."
msgstr ""
"Disparar tu arma aumentará tu nivel de retroceso. Puedes ver tu nivel en el "
"menú de <color_light_cyan>Apuntar y disparar</color> (pulsando "
"<color_yellow>'f'</color>). En general, cuanto más potente sea la munición, "
"peor será el retroceso. El retroceso reduce severamente tus probabilidades de "
"golpear, pero puedes eliminar el retroceso haciendo una pausa "
"(<color_yellow>'.' (punto)</color>) por un turno. Una fuerza elevada reduce "
"el retroceso, por lo que los personajes débiles deberían limitarse a armas "
"del .22 o 9x19mm."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"This is a staircase leading down.  To go downstairs, step onto the staircase "
"and press the <keybind:LEVEL_DOWN> key.  Similarly, to go upstairs, stand on "
"the staircase leading up and press the <keybind:LEVEL_UP> key."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una escalera que lleva hacia abajo. Para bajar, ponte en la escalera "
"y pulsa la tecla <keybind:LEVEL_DOWN> . Del mismo modo, para subir, sitúate "
"en la escalera que lleva hacia arriba y pulsa la tecla <keybind:LEVEL_UP>."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"It's dark down here!  Without a source of light, you'll be limited to seeing "
"only one space in any direction.  You'll encounter darkness while underground "
"or at night.  Press <keybind:LEVEL_UP> to go back upstairs, and look around "
"for a flashlight."
msgstr ""
"¡Está oscuro aquí abajo! Sin una fuente de luz, estás limitado a ver "
"solamente un espacio en todas las direcciones. Va a estar oscuro siempre que "
"estés bajo tierra o sea de noche. Pulsa <keybind:LEVEL_UP> para subir otra "
"vez, y busca una linterna."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"It's dark down here!  Fortunately, you have a "
"<color_light_cyan>flashlight</color>.  Press <keybind:apply> and then select "
"your flashlight to turn it on."
msgstr ""
"¡Está oscuro aquí abajo! Afortunadamente, tienes una "
"<color_light_cyan>linterna</color>. Pulsa <keybind:apply> y selecciona la "
"linterna para encenderla."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"From a water source like this, you can fill any containers you might have.  "
"Examine the dispenser by pressing <keybind:examine>.  Next, press "
"<color_yellow>'c'</color> to fill a container, then select the "
"<color_light_cyan>plastic bottle</color> to put the water into.\n"
"\n"
"The Examine command (<keybind:examine>) can be used for interacting with many "
"types of terrain and furniture.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please fill the plastic bottle with water, drink a "
"little of it (by pressing <keybind:eat> and selecting <color_light_cyan>clean "
"water</color>), and then move to the corridor to the north."
msgstr ""
"Desde una fuente de agua como ésta, puedes llenar cualquier contenedor que "
"tengas. Examina el dispensador pulsando <keybind:examine>. Después  pulsa "
"<color_yellow>'c' </color>para llenar contenedor y, por último seleciona la "
"<color_light_cyan>botella de plástico</color> como contenedor a llenar de "
"agua.\n"
"El comando Examinar (<keybind:examine>) se puede usar para interactuar con "
"muchos tipos de terreno y muebles.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, llena la botella con agua, bebe un poco de "
"ella (pulsando <keybind:eat> y seleccionando <color_light_cyan>agua "
"potable</color>), y trás ello dirígete al corredor del norte."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"This door is locked.  There are several ways to deal with locked doors "
"(lockpicking and prying being the most common), but right now you don't have "
"the necessary tools at hand.  Instead, you can simply bash it with your "
"<color_light_cyan>baseball bat</color> by pressing <keybind:smash> and then "
"selecting the direction.\n"
"\n"
"Note that not every door can be bashed down.  Some doors will require more "
"strength than you have or a stronger weapon.  If you're not seeing any damage "
"being done after a few swings, an alternative approach might be needed.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please smash the door."
msgstr ""
"Esta puerta está cerrada. Hay varias formas de lidiar con las puertas "
"cerradas en el juego (ganzúas, palancas y algunas otras), pero ahora mismo no "
"tienes las herramientas necesarias a mano. Así que simplemente se golpea con "
"tu <color_light_cyan>bate</color> pulsando <color_yellow>'s'</color> y a "
"continuación seleccionando la dirección.\n"
"Ten en cuenta que no todas las puertas pueden ser tiradas a golpes, y para "
"algunas puertas puede que simplemente no tengas la fuerza o el arma necesaria "
"para lograrlo.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, destroza la puerta."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Bashing things is hard work that will deplete your stamina.  You can see how "
"much stamina you have on the sidebar.  The less stamina you have, the slower "
"your movement and most actions will be.  To restore stamina, you need only to "
"wait.  You can press <keybind:wait> to open the <color_light_cyan>Wait for "
"how long</color> menu and select the amount of time you want to wait.  Select "
"option <color_light_cyan>Wait until you catch your breath</color> to fully "
"restore all lost stamina.\n"
"\n"
"Be careful about doing too many strenuous activities as you will build up "
"your weariness over time, which will stack movement and action penalties on "
"top of your stamina cost.  You can watch your <color_light_cyan>Weary "
"Transition</color> in the sidebar as you are performing longer activities to "
"see their effect on  your weariness.  To reduce your weariness, you just need "
"to rest or do less strenuous activities for a while."
msgstr ""
"Golpear cosas es una tarea árdua y gastará tu vigor. Puedes ver cuánto vigor "
"tienes en la barra lateral. Cuanto menos vigor tengas, más lentos serán tus "
"movimientos y tus acciones. Para recuperar vigor, solamente tienes que dejar "
"pasar el tiempo. Puedes pulsar <keybind:wait> para abrir el menú "
"<color_light_cyan>Cuánto tiempo esperar</color> y selecciona la cantidad de "
"tiempo que quieres dejar pasar. Selecciona la opción "
"<color_light_cyan>Esperar hasta recuperar el aliento</color> para recuperar "
"todo tu vigor.\n"
"\n"
"Ten cuidado si haces muchas actividades extenuantes porque vas juntando "
"fatiga con el tiempo, lo que te hace acumular penalizaciones a tu movimiento "
"y tus acciones además del gasto de vigor. Puedes ver tu "
"<color_light_cyan>Transición de Cansancio</color> en la barra lateral "
"mientras vas realizando actividades para ver el efecto que tienen en tu "
"fatiga. Para reducir la fatiga acumulada, vas a necesitar descansar o hacer "
"actividades menos exigentes durante un tiempo."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You can put the <color_light_cyan>steel spear</color> in the "
"<color_light_cyan>spear strap</color> to free your hands.  Press "
"<keybind:apply> to open the <color_light_cyan>Use item</color> menu, then "
"select the spear strap, then select the spear, and finally press "
"<keybind:CONFIRM> to confirm.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please put the <color_light_cyan>steel "
"spear</color> in the <color_light_cyan>spear strap</color> and move down the "
"corridor."
msgstr ""
"Puedes poner la <color_light_cyan>lanza de acero</color> en la "
"<color_light_cyan>correa para lanza</color> para liberar tus manos. Pulsa "
"<keybind:apply> para abrir el menú <color_light_cyan>Usar objeto</color>, "
"después selecciona la correa para lanza, después selecciona la lanza y "
"finalmente pulsa <keybind:CONFIRM> para confirmar.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, por favor, pon la <color_light_cyan>lanza de "
"acero</color> en la <color_light_cyan>correa para lanza</color> y sigue por "
"el pasillo."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_LOOK"
msgid ""
"You can also use the mouse to see things around you.  The "
"<color_light_cyan>Mouse view</color> window will appear on the sidebar, and "
"you'll be able to get information on the terrain, monsters, and items in the "
"world around you.  Alternatively, you can press <keybind:look> to open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Look Around</color> window."
msgstr ""
"También puedes utilizar el ratón para ver las cosas que te rodean. La "
"ventana<color_light_cyan> Vista de Ratón </color> aparecerá en la barra "
"lateral, y serás capaz de obtener información del terreno, monstruos y "
"objetos del mundo que te rodea. Alternativamente puedes pulsar<keybind:look> "
"para abrir la ventana <color_light_cyan>Mirar Alrededor</color>."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_MOVEMENT_MODES"
msgid ""
"Most of the time your character will be walking when you move.  But sometimes "
"it's useful to change your movement mode to something else.\n"
"\n"
"There are four movement modes:\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Walking</color>: default mode, average movement speed, "
"stamina draining speed, and noise\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Running</color>: <color_light_green>move much "
"faster</color>, but will <color_light_red>drain your stamina quickly</color>\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Crouching</color>: will make your character "
"<color_light_green>less visible to monsters</color> by allowing you to hide "
"behind some obstacles, <color_light_red>decreased movement speed</color> and "
"<color_light_green>noise</color>\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Prone</color>: <color_light_green>even less "
"visibility</color> to monsters, <color_light_red>even less movement "
"speed</color> and <color_light_green>noise</color>\n"
"\n"
"Pressing <keybind:open_movement> will open the <color_light_cyan>Movement "
"Mode</color> menu, which allows you to switch the mode at any time.  There "
"are extra keybindings that can be set to switch to each mode individually for "
"convenience.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please move to the end of the corridor."
msgstr ""
"La mayor parte del tiempo tu personaje caminará al moverse. Pero a veces es "
"útil cambiar el modo de movimiento por otro.\n"
"\n"
"Hay cuatro modos de movimiento:\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Andar</color>: modo por defecto, velocidad media de "
"movimiento,  ruido y perdida de vigor\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Correr</color>: <color_light_green>movimiento más "
"rápido</color>, con <color_light_red>perdida de vigor rápida</color>\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Agachar</color>: hará que tu personaje "
"<color_light_green>sea menos visible para los monstruos</color> permitiéndote "
"esconderte detrás de algunos obstáculos, <color_light_red>velocidad de "
"movimiento </color> y <color_light_green>ruido</color> reducido\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Reptar</color>: <color_light_green>aun menor "
"visibilidad</color> para los monstruos, <color_light_red>y velocidad de "
"movimiento</color> y <color_light_green>ruido</color> más reducidos\n"
"\n"
"Al pulsar <keybind:open_movement> se abrirá el menú de <color_light_cyan>Modo "
"de Movimiento</color>, que te permite cambiar de modo en cualquier momento. "
"Hay atajos de teclado adicionales que se pueden configurar para moverse entre "
"modos más comodamente.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, por favor, muévete hasta el final del pasillo."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_MONSTER_SIGHTED"
msgid ""
"There is a <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> standing before you.  Let's attack "
"it.  To do this, simply move into it.\n"
"\n"
"After you've dealt with it, please move to the door behind it."
msgstr ""
"Hay un <color_light_cyan>maniquí</color> frente a ti. Vamos a atacarlo. Para "
"ello, simplemente muévete hacia él.\n"
"\n"
"Una vez que te hayas ocupado de él, muévete hacia la puerta que hay detrás."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_REACH_ATTACK"
msgid ""
"There is another <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> standing behind the "
"counters.  Most melee weapons require standing directly adjacent to your "
"target in order to hit it.\n"
"\n"
"Fortunately, some long weapons such as spears are able to perform reach "
"attack with a range of 2 or 3, so if you have one, you don't need to climb "
"onto the counters to stand next to the dummy.  The <color_light_cyan>steel "
"spear</color> has a range of 2, so you can hit the dummy right over the "
"counters.  To use the reach attack, press the <keybind:fire> key.  Once you "
"select your target, press <keybind:CONFIRM> to confirm.\n"
"\n"
"After you've dealt with the dummy, please move to the corridor to the south."
msgstr ""
"Hay otro <color_light_cyan>maniquí</color> parado detrás de los mostradores. "
"La mayoría de las armas de cuerpo a cuerpo requieren que estés parado "
"directamente adyacente a tu objetivo para golpearlo.\n"
"\n"
"Por suerte, algunas armas largas como las lanzas pueden hacer un ataque de "
"largo alcance de 2 o 3 espacios, así que si tienes un arma con esa "
"posibilidad, no necesitas subirte a los mostradores para estar al lado del "
"maniquí. La <color_light_cyan>lanza de acero</color> tiene un alcance de 2, "
"así que puedes golpearlo desde detrás de los mostradores. Para hacer un "
"ataque de largo alcance, pulsa la tecla <keybind:fire>. Cuando hayas "
"seleccionado tu objetivo, pulsa <keybind:CONFIRM> para confirmar.\n"
"\n"
"Cuando te hayas encargado del maniquí, por favor, ve hacia el pasillo del sur."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_HOLSTERS_WEAR"
msgid ""
"Always wielding a <color_light_cyan>steel spear</color> in your hands might "
"be inconvenient.  Fortunately, there is a <color_light_cyan>spear "
"strap</color> lying on the rack nearby.  You can wear it by pressing "
"<keybind:wear>.\n"
"To take off any worn item, you can press <keybind:take_off>.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please wear the spear strap."
msgstr ""
"Empuñar siempre una <color_light_cyan>lanza de acero</color> en las manos "
"puede ser un inconveniente. Por suerte, hay una <color_light_cyan>correa para "
"lanza</color> en un estante cercano. Puedes ponértela pulsando "
"<keybind:wear>.\n"
"Para desequipar un objeto, puedes pulsar <keybind:take_off>.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, por favor, equipate la correa para lanza."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_GUN_LOAD"
msgid ""
"In the next room you'll find a row of racks with a gun, a magazine for it, "
"and ammo for it.  To be able to fire a gun, you'll need to insert a magazine "
"with ammo in it.  Press <keybind:reload_item> to open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Reload item</color> menu and put ammo in the magazine, and "
"then press <keybind:reload_item> once again to insert a magazine into a gun.\n"
"\n"
"If you wish to unload your gun, possibly to change ammunition types, press "
"<keybind:unload>."
msgstr ""
"En esta habitación, vas a encontrar una fila de estantes con un arma, un "
"cargador y munición. Para poder disparar un arma vas a necesitar recargar el "
"cargador con munición y recargar el arma. Pulsa <keybind:reload_item> para "
"abrir el menú de <color_light_cyan>Recargar</color> y recarga la munición en "
"el cargador a continuación pulsa <keybind:reload_item> otra vez para insertar "
"el cargador en el arma.\n"
"\n"
"Si quieres descargar tu arma, por ejemplo para cambiar el tipo de munición, "
"pulsa <keybind:unload>."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_INVENTORY"
msgid ""
"Cataclysm uses a container-based inventory.  Putting something into your "
"inventory requires wearing some clothing or container with pockets that are "
"big enough to hold it.  The <color_light_cyan>spear strap</color> is one "
"example of such containers.  Pockets have finite dimensions, so you can't put "
"an item that has more volume or is longer than a pocket.\n"
"\n"
"To view your inventory, press <keybind:inventory>.  You'll see that you have "
"only your worn clothes, of which only your jeans have 4 small pockets.  "
"Select your jeans and press <keybind:CONFIRM> to see their description and "
"amount of pockets.  To scroll through the description, press "
"<keybind:PAGE_UP> and <keybind:PAGE_DOWN>.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, move to the western rack and wear (<keybind:wear>) "
"the <color_light_cyan>backpack</color> to increase the available capacity of "
"your inventory."
msgstr ""
"El juego utiliza un inventario basado en contenedores. Esto significa que "
"para poner algo en tu inventario, tienes que llevar alguna prenda o "
"contenedor con bolsillos que te tengan espacio para los objetos. La "
"<color_light_cyan>correa de la lanza</color> es un ejemplo de este tipo de "
"contenedores. Los bolsillos tienen dimensiones finitas, por lo que no puedes "
"poner un objeto que tenga mayor volumen o longitud que el propio bolsillo.\n"
"Para ver tu inventario, pulsa <color_yellow>'i'</color>. Verás que sólo "
"tienes lo que llevas puesto, y sólo tus vaqueros tienen 4 bolsillos pequeños. "
"Selecciona tus vaqueros y pulsa <color_yellow>Enter</color> para ver su "
"descripción y la cantidad de bolsillos. Para desplazarte por la descripción, "
"pulsa <color_yellow>'<'</color> y <color_yellow>'>'</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, acércate al estante y equipate con "
"(<color_yellow>'W'</color>) la <color_light_cyan>mochila</color> para "
"aumentar la capacidad de tu inventario."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_FLASHLIGHT"
msgid ""
"There is a <color_light_cyan>flashlight</color> and a "
"<color_light_cyan>medium battery</color> lying on the rack.  Flashlights are "
"very useful tools as they allow you to see in the dark.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please reload the flashlight by pressing "
"<keybind:reload_item>.  Take it with you and move to the stairs."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_INTERACT"
msgid ""
"There is a <color_light_cyan>water dispenser</color> around the corner.  Pick "
"up the <color_light_cyan>plastic bottle</color> from the rack and proceed to "
"the dispenser."
msgstr ""
"Hay un <color_light_cyan>dispensador de agua</color> a la vuelta de la "
"esquina. Recoge la <color_light_cyan>botella de plástico</color> del estante "
"y dirígete al dispensador."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_REMOTE_USE"
msgid ""
"A <color_light_cyan>flashlight</color> is a good thing to have, but it drains "
"its battery quickly, so it won't last very long.  A much better solution for "
"long-lasting lighting is a <color_light_cyan>gasoline lantern</color>.  "
"Reload the lantern with <color_light_cyan>gasoline</color> "
"(<keybind:reload_item>) and then activate it (<keybind:apply>) while standing "
"nearby.  A <color_light_cyan>lighter</color> will help you to fire the "
"lantern.\n"
"\n"
"Some tools (such as lamps, dehydrators, bathroom scales etc) don't need to be "
"picked up before activating and allow remote use.\n"
"\n"
"After you light the lantern, you can safely turn off your flashlight to "
"conserve its energy; the lit lantern will give you enough light for any "
"actions and will last much longer.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please light the lantern and then move to the "
"corridor to the east."
msgstr ""
"Es útil tener una <color_light_cyan>linterna</color> , pero su batería se "
"agota rápidamente, por lo que no durará mucho tiempo. Una solución mucho mas "
"duradera para iluminar es una <color_light_cyan>linterna de gasolina</color>. "
"Recarga la linterna con<color_light_cyan> gasolina</color> "
"(<color_yellow>'r'</color>) y luego actívala (<color_yellow>'a'</color>) "
"estando cerca. Un <color_light_cyan>mechero</color> te ayudará a encender la "
"linterna. Algunas objetos (como las lámparas, los deshidratadores, las "
"básculas de baño, etc.) no necesitan ser recogidas antes de activarse y "
"permiten su uso a distancia.\n"
"Después de encender la linterna de gasolina puedes apagar la linterna de "
"batería con seguridad para conservar su energía, la linterna encendida te "
"proporcionará suficiente luz para cualquier acción y durará mucho tiempo.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, enciende la linterna de gasolina y luego "
"dirígete al corredor del este."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_CRAFTING_FOOD"
msgid ""
"Looks like you're hungry!  The hunger status is indicated on the sidebar.  "
"Let's make a <color_light_cyan>peanut butter sandwich</color> from "
"<color_light_cyan>peanut butter</color> and "
"<color_light_cyan>crackers</color> on the counter next to the wall.\n"
"\n"
"To make food, you need to use the <color_light_cyan>Crafting</color> menu.  "
"Press <keybind:craft> to open the menu.  Press <keybind:NEXT_TAB> and "
"<keybind:PREV_TAB> to toggle crafting categories and select the "
"<color_light_cyan>FOOD</color> category.  From there, select peanut butter "
"sandwich and press <keybind:CONFIRM> to start crafting.\n"
"\n"
"Note that you don't need to stand directly near the counter to be able to "
"craft.  The <color_light_cyan>crafting radius</color> is 6 tiles, so while "
"you're standing no farther than 6 tiles from any crafting components and "
"tools, your character is able to still get them in order to use them.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please craft the peanut butter sandwich and then "
"eat it by pressing <keybind:eat>."
msgstr ""
"¡Parece que tienes hambre! El hambre se indica en la barra lateral. Vamos a "
"hacer un <color_light_cyan>sandwich de mantequilla de cacahuete</color> con "
"la <color_light_cyan>mantequilla de cacahuete</color> y las "
"<color_light_cyan>galletitas saladas</color> que hay en el mostrador junto a "
"la pared.\n"
"Para hacer la comida tienes que usar el <color_light_cyan>Menú de "
"Fabricación</color>. Pulsa <color_yellow>'&' (et)</color> para abrir el menú. "
"Pulsa <color_yellow>Tab</color> y <color_yellow>Backtab (Shift + Tab)</color> "
"para moverte entre las categorías de fabricación y selecciona la categoría "
"<color_light_cyan>COMIDA</color>. Selecciona el sandwich de mantequilla de "
"cacahuete y pulsa <color_yellow>Enter</color> para empezar a hacerlo.\n"
"Ten en cuenta que no necesitas estar cerca del mostrador para poder "
"fabricarlo. El <color_light_cyan>radio de fabricación</color> es de 6, así "
"que mientras estés parado a no más de 6 espacios de componentes y "
"herramientas de fabricación, tu personaje será capaz de obtenerlos por sí "
"mismo.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, fabrica el sandwich de mantequilla de "
"cacahuete y cómetelo pulsando <color_yellow>'E'</color>."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_CONSTRUCTION"
msgid ""
"In the next room, you can find a <color_light_cyan>paint brush</color> and "
"several cans of <color_light_cyan>paint</color>.  You can use them to paint "
"the wall in your preferred color.  To do this, open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Construction</color> menu by pressing <keybind:construct> "
"and toggling the categories with <keybind:LEFT> and <keybind:RIGHT>.  Find "
"the <color_light_cyan>Decorative</color> category and select one of the "
"options to paint the wall.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please paint some walls and move further south."
msgstr ""
"En la siguiente habitación puedes encontrar una "
"<color_light_cyan>brocha</color> y varios botes de "
"<color_light_cyan>pintura</color>. Puedes usarlos para pintar la pared del "
"color que quieras. Para hacer esto, abre el <color_light_cyan>Menú de "
"construcción</color> pulsando <color_yellow>'*'</color> (asterisco) y muévete "
"entre las categorías con las <color_yellow>teclas de dirección</color>. Busca "
"la categoría <color_light_cyan>Decorativo</color> y selecciona una de las "
"opciones para pintar la pared.\n"
"\n"
"Para continuar con el tutorial, pinta algunas paredes y avanza hacia el sur."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_THROWING"
msgid ""
"There are 10 <color_light_cyan>baseballs</color> lying on the floor.  You "
"might not need all 10, or you might not have enough space in your pockets.  "
"To pick up a specific amount of items, press <keybind:pickup>, select the "
"stack of items, and type a number on the keyboard (Multiple numbers can be "
"used for large stacks).  Finish the selection with "
"<keybind:INVENTORY:TOGGLE_ENTRY>.  The cursor should change to a "
"<color_light_cyan>#</color> symbol.\n"
"\n"
"You can throw a baseball at the <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> in the end of "
"the corridor by pressing <keybind:throw>.\n"
"\n"
"To complete the tutorial, throw some baseballs at the dummy and then move to "
"the end of the corridor to the north."
msgstr ""
"Hay 10 pelotas de <color_light_cyan>béisbol</color> en el suelo. Puede que no "
"necesites las 10, o que no tengas suficiente espacio en tus bolsillos. Para "
"recoger una cantidad específica de objetos, pulsa <keybind:pickup>, "
"selecciona la pila de objetos y pulsa el número en el teclado (Se pueden "
"utilizar varios números para pilas grandes). Termina la selección con "
"<keybind:INVENTORY:TOGGLE_ENTRY>.El cursor debería cambiar al símbolo "
"<color_light_cyan># </color>.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes lanzar una pelota de béisbol al <color_light_cyan>maniquí</color> del "
"final del pasillo pulsando <keybind:throw>.\n"
"\n"
"Para completar el tutorial, lanza algunas pelotas de béisbol al maniquí y "
"luego dirígete al final del corredor hacia el norte."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_FINALE"
msgid ""
"Congratulations!  You have completed the tutorial.  Here is some last-minute "
"advice.\n"
"\n"
"You can press <keybind:action_menu> to open the <color_light_cyan>Action "
"menu</color>.  It provides a convenient way to access various actions.\n"
"\n"
"Not sure what keys you can press in a given menu?  Press the "
"<keybind:HELP_KEYBINDINGS> to open the <color_light_cyan>Keybindings</color> "
"menu.  It allows you to view the existing keybindings and modify them to your "
"liking.  Sometimes there will be lesser used or convenience actions without a "
"default keybinding, which you can also set.\n"
"\n"
"You can continue exploring the tutorial rooms, or you can exit the tutorial "
"by pressing <keybind:save>.  This will save your game and exit to the main "
"menu."
msgstr ""
"¡Felicitaciones! Completaste el tutorial. Por último, te dejo unos consejos.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes pulsar <keybind:action_menu> para abrir el menú de "
"<color_light_cyan>Acción</color>. Es una manera conveniente de acceder a "
"diversas acciones.\n"
"\n"
"¿No estás seguro qué teclas tienes que usar en un menú? Pulsa "
"<keybind:HELP_KEYBINDINGS> para abrir el menú de <color_light_cyan>Atajos de "
"teclado</color>. Te permite ver los atajos que ya existen y modificarlos como "
"quieras. A veces, hay acciones que usas menos o acciones interesantes sin una "
"tecla asociada, aquí puedes configurarlas.\n"
"\n"
"Puedes continuar explorando las habitaciones del tutorial o puedes salir "
"pulsando <keybind:save>.  Esto salvará el juego y te llevará al menú "
"principal."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Antivirals Before You Die!"
msgstr "¡Conseguí Antivirales Antes de Morir!"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid "You take an antiviral."
msgstr "Te tomaste un antiviral."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in false effect in EoC
#. "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid "You seem to be feeling a little better, but the prickling sensation remains."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in false effect in EoC
#. "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid ""
"You no longer feel uncomfortably itchy, but your skin is still concerningly "
"pale."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in false effect in EoC
#. "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid ""
"Some of the lesions on your skin have begun to heal, but the itchiness "
"remains."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "zombie_virus"
msgid "Pallor"
msgstr "Palidez"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "zombie_virus"
msgid "Itchy pale skin"
msgstr "Piel pálida y con picazón"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "zombie_virus"
msgid "Necrotic skin"
msgstr "Piel necrótica"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Pallor"
msgid "Your skin is pale and there are dark spots around your eyes."
msgstr "Tu piel está pálida y hay unas manchas oscuras alrededor de tus ojos."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Itchy pale skin"
msgid ""
"Your skin is pale and there are dark spots around your eyes.  You feel a "
"constant itching sensation, like your skin could fall off at any moment."
msgstr ""
"Tu piel está pálida y hay unas manchas oscuras alrededor de tus ojos. Sientes "
"una picazón constante, como si tu piel se pudiera salir en cualquier momento."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Necrotic skin"
msgid ""
"Your skin is pale and covered in gross sores.  It's like your skin is rotting "
"right off your body."
msgstr ""
"Tu piel está pálida y cubierta de unas llagas repugnantes. Es como si tu piel "
"se estuviera pudriendo en tu cuerpo."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Apply message of effect type "Pallor, Itchy pale skin, Necrotic skin"
msgid "An ominous prickling feeling reverberates through your body."
msgstr "Una sensación siniestra de hormigueo reverbera por todo tu cuerpo."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "antivirals"
msgid_plural "antivirals"
msgstr[0] "antivirales"
msgstr[1] "antivirales"
msgstr[2] "antivirales"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/items.json
#. ~ Description of "antivirals"
msgid ""
"An anti-viral medication that inhibits the development of certain viruses.  "
"One dose lasts 16 hours.  Could this, by some miracle, work against whatever "
"the zombies are carrying?"
msgstr ""
"Un medicamento antiviral que inhibe el desarrollo de ciertos virus. Una dosis "
"dura 16 horas. ¿Podría esto, por algún milagro, funcionar contra lo que sea "
"que lleven los zombis?"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/items.json
#. ~ "description" action message of item "antivirals"
msgid "Reduces the effect of certain viral infections."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/modinfo.json
#. ~ MOD name
msgid "Deadly Zombie Virus"
msgstr "Virus Zombi Mortal"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "Deadly Zombie Virus"
msgid ""
"Bites from zombies have a chance to inflict a permanent fatal illness.  Find "
"and consume antivirals to stave off the disease."
msgstr ""
"Las mordeduras de los zombis pueden causar una enfermedad mortal permanente. "
"Encuentra y consume antivirales para evitar la enfermedad."

#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "hook kangaroo"
msgid_plural "hook kangaroos"
msgstr[0] "canguro de gancho"
msgstr[1] "canguros de gancho"
msgstr[2] "canguros de gancho"

#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "hook kangaroo"
msgid ""
"Grotesque and deformed kangaroo body that has black goo seeping from its "
"orifices.  The most unnerving is its forearms have reformed into a raptorial "
"shape, like that of a praying mantis."
msgstr ""
"Grotesco y deforme cuerpo de canguro que tiene una sustancia viscosa negra "
"que se filtra por sus orificios. Lo más desconcertante es que sus antebrazos "
"se han reformado en una forma de rapaz, como la de una mantis religiosa."

#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Gila monster"
msgid_plural "Gila monsters"
msgstr[0] "Monstruo de Gila"
msgstr[1] "Monstruos de Gila"
msgstr[2] "Monstruos de Gila"

#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Gila monster"
msgid ""
"A reptile with aposematic coloration of black and orange that is renowned for "
"an extremely painful venom when it bites."
msgstr ""
"Un reptil con coloración aposemática de negro y naranja que es conocido por "
"un veneno extremadamente doloroso cuando muerde."

#: data/mods/desert_region/modinfo.json
#. ~ MOD name
msgid "Desert Region"
msgstr "Región Desértica"

#: data/mods/desert_region/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "Desert Region"
msgid "A testbed/WIP mod to showcase regional_map_settings JSON changes."
msgstr ""
"Un mod de prueba/WIP para mostrar los cambios en el JSON de "
"regional_map_settings."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_furniture.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "tumbleweed"
msgstr "cardo ruso"

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "tumbleweed"
msgid "Tumbleweed."
msgstr "Es un cardo ruso."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "outcrop"
msgid ""
"An assortment of various large, sharp rocks that jut out from the surrounding "
"terrain.  Could be as a surface for a number of things or climbed on if worn "
"with proper footwear."
msgstr ""
"Un surtido de varias rocas grandes y afiladas que sobresalen del terreno "
"circundante. Puede ser como superficie para varias cosas o para escalar si se "
"usa con el calzado adecuado."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "mudcrack"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "mudcrack"
msgid ""
"Large continuous cracks mark what once was a bottom of a body of water.  With "
"the proper tools, you could extract clay from here."
msgstr ""
"Grandes grietas continuas marcan lo que una vez fue el fondo de una masa de "
"agua. Con las herramientas adecuadas, podrías extraer arcilla de aquí."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/overmap/desert_overmap_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "sandstone"
msgstr "arenisca"

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sandstone"
msgid "A wall of yellowish brown sandstone."
msgstr "Una pared de piedra de arena marrón amarillenta."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "artificial grass"
msgstr "césped artificial"

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "artificial grass"
msgid "A carpet of synthetic fibers made to resemble natural grass."
msgstr "Una alfombra de fibra sintética que parece pasto natural."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "white artificial grass"
msgstr "césped artificial blanco"

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "white artificial grass"
msgid ""
"A carpet of synthetic fibers made to resemble natural grass.  Covered in "
"white latex-based paint, it is used to mark lines in recreational sports."
msgstr ""
"Una alfombra de fibras sintéticas parecida a la hierba natural. Cubierta con "
"pintura blanca basada en latex, que se suele usar para marcar lineas en "
"deportes de entretenimiento."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "withered shrub"
msgstr "arbusto marchito"

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "withered shrub"
msgid "A small shrub that has withered away."
msgstr "Es un pequeño arbusto que se marchitó."

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "buckhorn cholla"
msgstr "choya espinosa"

#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "buckhorn cholla"
msgid ""
"A shrub-like cactus belonging to the 'Cylindropuntia' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the deserts of North America.  If you look closely, you can see "
"some unharvested cholla buds hiding behind clusters of stiff spines."
msgstr ""
"Es un cactus con forma de arbusto que pertenece al género 'Cylindropuntia', "
"comúnmente encontrado en los desiertos de América del Norte. Si lo examinas "
